gd-1009697597550,glassdoor,https://www.glassdoor.co.in/job-listing/j?jl=1009697597550,,Project Manager - Cybersecurity,ProArch,Bengaluru,2025-04-04,,491750.0,900000.0,INR,False,"At ProArch Cybersecurity, our customers are our lifeblood, and our service delivery revolves around enhancing our customers' businesses by providing tailored defense strategies, proactive offensive testing, and strategic risk measurement, all supported by the latest automation technology. We are dedicated to creating an innovative environment that exceeds service reliability, efficiency, and trustworthiness expectations while delighting customers along the way. We aim to predict and reduce threats intelligently, ensuring ongoing protection for our clients and leveraging their insights to offer world class ""Advanced Resilience"" cybersecurity protection. Internally, we prioritize efficient processes, automation, service reliability, proactive vigilance, and providing the utmost value to our clients.


The Project Manager \- Cybersecurity Services is tasked with planning, executing, and delivering cybersecurity projects. Additionally, they ensure the timely provision of managed services within a service delivery environment that focuses on Microsoft security solutions. This role ensures that cybersecurity projects are completed on time, within scope, and within budget, all while meeting the quality and security standards required by the organization and its clients. The Project Manager coordinates cross\-functional teams – including cybersecurity engineers, consultants, and client stakeholders – to drive project success. While a strong understanding of cybersecurity (especially Microsoft’s security technologies) is important, this position emphasizes core project management duties: project planning, execution tracking, stakeholder management, and service delivery coordination to support our service delivery organization

**Key Responsibilities**

* **Project Planning \& Initiation:** Define project scope, objectives, and deliverables in collaboration with clients and technical leads. Develop project plans outlining timelines, tasks, and resource requirements. Ensure each project aligns with customer outcomes.
* **Project Execution \& Coordination:** Lead the day\-to\-day management of cybersecurity project delivery. Coordinate cross\-functional teams (e.g. Security Consultants, Specialists, Analysts) to execute against the plan, ensuring everyone understands their tasks and deadlines. Manage project schedules, track progress, and adjust plans as necessary to account for changes or new requirements, keeping the project on track.
* **Stakeholder Management:** Serve as the primary liaison for project stakeholders, including clients, internal teams, and leadership. Facilitate regular status meetings and reports to communicate progress, milestones, risks, and issues. Manage stakeholder expectations and ensure alignment between technical teams and business/client needs throughout the project lifecycle.
* **Risk Management \& Compliance Coordination:** Proactively identify and document project risks and issues (including security\-related risks). Work with our internal team and customer stakeholders to assess and prioritize these risks. Develop and implement mitigation plans or contingency strategies to address risks.
* **Budget \& Resource Management:** Manage project budgets and resources to ensure efficient delivery. Track project expenditures and labor against estimates, and report on budget status. Coordinate with resource managers to secure necessary staffing (e.g. security analysts, engineers) and adjust resource plans if project scope or timelines change.
* **Service Delivery Coordination:** Ensure a smooth delivery of cybersecurity services as projects transition from implementation to operational support. Work closely with the service delivery and operations teams to hand over completed solutions, making sure that all documentation, training, and support processes are in place. Verify that delivered security solutions (for example, Microsoft 365 security implementations, Azure Sentinel deployments, etc.) meet the agreed\-upon service levels and client expectations.
* **Quality Assurance:** Uphold quality standards for project deliverables. Coordinate testing and validation of cybersecurity solutions in partnership with technical leads – for instance, confirming that security configurations or controls are implemented as designed. Address any quality issues by facilitating reviews or audits by subject matter experts, rather than deep technical troubleshooting by the Project Manager.
* **Change Control:** Manage project scope and changes through change control processes. When new security requirements or technical changes arise, evaluate their impact on timeline and budget, obtain necessary approvals, and communicate changes to all stakeholders.
* **Documentation \& Reporting:** Maintain thorough project documentation including work plans, risk logs, decision registers, and status reports. Provide clear and concise reports on project progress, key metrics, and post\-project results to both internal stakeholders and clients.
* **Continuous Improvement:** After project completion, lead or participate in post\-project reviews/retrospectives. Identify lessons learned and best practices specific to delivering cybersecurity services. Work on improving project management processes and templates for future security projects, contributing to the overall maturity of the cybersecurity service delivery practice.

**Requirements**


**Education:** Bachelor’s / Master's degree in Information Technology, Cybersecurity, Business Administration, or a related field. Master’s degree preferred.

* **Experience:** Minimum of 5\+ years of project management experience. Experience with agile as well as waterfall and other project management methodologies.
* **Certifications:** ITIL, PMP/Prince 2, Lean Six Sigma, PgMP, CISM, CISSP, or relevant certifications are highly desirable.
* **Cybersecurity Domain Knowledge:** Familiarity with core cybersecurity concepts and practices. Experience in projects involving Microsoft cybersecurity solutions (such as Microsoft 365 security suite, Entra ID, Microsoft Defender, Azure Sentinel, or similar) is an advantage. While hands\-on technical skills are not the primary focus, the Project Manager should be comfortable discussing security topics and understanding technical team inputs at a high level.
* **Communication \& Stakeholder Engagement:** Excellent communication skills, both written and verbal. Demonstrated experience in managing stakeholder relationships and expectations, ideally including client\-facing project management. Ability to translate technical information into business terms and ensure mutual understanding among technical teams and non\-technical stakeholders.
* **Organizational Skills:** Exceptional organizational and time management abilities, self\-starter. Capable of juggling multiple priorities and projects in a fast\-paced, service\-driven environment. Detail\-oriented in tracking tasks, issues, and project details, ensuring nothing falls through the cracks.
* **Problem Solving \& Risk Management:** Strong analytical and problem\-solving skills. Adept at identifying potential obstacles or risks early and facilitating collaborative solutions. Experience with risk management techniques and the ability to drive issue resolution by engaging the right resources.
* **Team Collaboration:** A team player who can lead by influence. Experience coordinating cross\-functional teams and encouraging a cooperative working atmosphere. Ability to work with remote or distributed teams, including vendors or third\-party service providers, to achieve project objectives.
* **Adaptability:** Flexibility to adapt to changing project requirements or shifts in client priorities. Comfortable working within agile, waterfall, or hybrid delivery models as required by the project.
* **Service Delivery Mindset:** Prior exposure to a service delivery or managed services environment is beneficial. Understanding of service level agreements (SLAs) and operational handover processes (e.g., following ITIL practices) is a plus. Commitment to delivering value and positive outcomes for clients as well as internal stakeholders.

**How Your Success Will Be Measured**

* Project Success: Completion of projects on time, within budget, and to the satisfaction of stakeholders.
* Client Satisfaction: Positive feedback from clients regarding the delivery and outcomes of security services.
* Innovation: Successful identification and implementation of innovative solutions and process improvements. Provide these through demonstrable improvements in processes and methodologies based on feedback and performance metrics.
* Risk Mitigation: Maintain, communicate and keep updated and active risk register of individual and project portfolio risks and mitigation strategies and communicate that with stakeholders and needed.
* Strategic Alignment: Alignment of Cybersecurity projects with organizational goals and strategic objectives.",,https://www.glassdoor.co.in/Overview/W-EI_IE425101.htm,Cyber Security
gd-1009696933950,glassdoor,https://www.glassdoor.co.in/job-listing/j?jl=1009696933950,,Penetration Test Engagement Coordinator,LSEG (London Stock Exchange Group),Bengaluru,2025-04-04,,396240.0,769500.0,INR,False,"Role profile:
The main function is to improve efficiency between the LSEG business teams and the Cyber Security functions by devising and implementing automation, process, procedures and reporting that improve how the business engages with Cyber strategic plans, standards and policies.
This particular role is focusing on the penetration testing process to manage the scheduling of testing activities within Group. This role requires an in\-depth understanding of the full penetration testing process, with a strong focus on coordination, tracking, and reporting.  

ROLE SUMMARY:
The Team is a highly transparent, adaptable, and effective team within Technology function. We enable the organization to deliver against its strategic aims by reducing cyber risk of significant security incidents and data breaches by continually working to improve the security posture of the organization.
You will join the Cyber Engagement team, which is a function within Cyber Security team to enrich and streamline the communication between Business and Cyber Teams to meet the group's strategic requirements.  

WHAT YOU'LL BE DOING:
Coordination of Penetration Testing Schedule:* Develop and maintain a comprehensive schedule for all penetration testing activities.
* Coordinate with internal teams and external vendors, utilizing a deep understanding of the penetration testing process to align efforts with business and security needs.
* Ensure penetration testing engagement is following the Cyber team standard engagement and quality processes.

Project Management and Tracking:* Monitor the progress of all penetration testing projects, applying insights from previous hands\-on experience to anticipate and address potential challenges.
* Ensure that testing activities are conducted within agreed timelines and budgets, applying a thorough understanding of the complexities involved in penetration testing.

Reporting and Documentation:* Prepare and present detailed reports on the status, findings, and outcomes of penetration tests, leveraging knowledge of penetration testing methodologies.
* Maintain meticulous records of testing activities, ensuring comprehensive documentation of scopes, methodologies, and vulnerabilities identified.

Quality Assurance:* Support the quality of penetration tests to ensure they adhere to internal standards, applying firsthand knowledge of effective testing strategies.
* Facilitate post\-engagement reviews, applying experience in penetration testing to provide valuable insights and recommendations.

Team Leadership:* Mentor team members involved in the coordination of penetration testing, sharing knowledge and experience in penetration testing methodologies.
* Promote a culture of continuous learning and improvement within the team


Vendor Management:* Serving as Point of contact for 3rd party testing vendors
* Coordinate contract discussions, adherence to SLAs and Budgets
* Evaluate vendor performance and collect feedback.

Skills and Qualifications:* Bachelor’s degree in Information Technology, Cyber Security, or a related field.
* Minimum of 5 years of experience in cyber security.
* In\-depth understanding of penetration testing methodologies
* Experience maintaining and developing automation using JIRA and Azure Dev Ops.
* Strong interpersonal and project management skills, with the ability to oversee multiple projects simultaneously.
* Excellent communication skills, capable of engaging with both technical and non\-technical collaborators.
* Proficient in documentation, reporting, and compliance with cyber security regulations.
* Relevant certifications in penetration testing or cyber security management are desirable.
* PMP, Agile, PRINCE2, or other project management are a plus.
  

WHAT YOU’LL GET IN RETURN:* We enhance each employee’s potential through personal development and through a wide range of learning tools both formal and informal.
* We remunerate our people with competitive salaries and offer a range of attractive benefits.
* We also recognize that to attract the best talent, we need to be flexible, and we are open to discussing hybrid work arrangements with you

LSEG is a leading global financial markets infrastructure and data provider. Our purpose is driving financial stability, empowering economies and enabling customers to create sustainable growth.
Our purpose is the foundation on which our culture is built. Our values of Integrity, Partnership, Excellence and Change underpin our purpose and set the standard for everything we do, every day. They go to the heart of who we are and guide our decision making and everyday actions.
Working with us means that you will be part of a dynamic organisation of 25,000 people across 65 countries. However, we will value your individuality and enable you to bring your true self to work so you can help enrich our diverse workforce. You will be part of a collaborative and creative culture where we encourage new ideas and are committed to sustainability across our global business. You will experience the critical role we have in helping to re\-engineer the financial ecosystem to support and drive sustainable economic growth. Together, we are aiming to achieve this growth by accelerating the just transition to net zero, enabling growth of the green economy and creating inclusive economic opportunity.
LSEG offers a range of tailored benefits and support, including healthcare, retirement planning, paid volunteering days and wellbeing initiatives.
