gd-1009693793617,glassdoor,https://www.glassdoor.co.in/job-listing/j?jl=1009693793617,,Senior Audit Manager India,Standard Chartered,Mumbai,2025-04-02,,134850.0,204750.0,INR,False,"Job ID: 24049
 

Location: Mumbai, IN
 

Area of interest: Audit, Accounting \& Finance
 

Job type: Regular Employee
 

Work style: Office Working
 

Opening date: 22 Mar 2025



**Job Summary**

Group Internal Audit (GIA) is looking for an experienced and dynamic audit professional with a solid background and strong knowledge around the key risks and controls to be an integral part of the Global Wealth and Retail Banking (WRB) Audit team. The team provides independent assessments of risk management and internal control environment globally across lending and non\-lending WRB products that are offered to Personal Banking, Small and Medium Enterprise (SME), Affluent and Private Banking client segments. The role holder will also lead the India WRB audit team.


We pride ourselves in being auditors of the future, forward\-looking and agile with a keen focus on smarter auditing. When you join us, you will enter a role that challenges the status quo and moves mindsets and be a part of the future of banking.


This role currently reports to Head of Audit, India and matrix to Group Head of Audit, Personal and SME Banking.


**Key Responsibilities**
* Lead high quality audit engagements across planning, fieldwork and reporting for assigned WRB audits with particular focus on audits on Personal and SME Banking segments. This would involve drafting of audit issues and reports, obtaining agreement with Senior Management on action plans and ensuring all audit work by self and team members be delivered within budgets and timelines, and be in full adherence to GIA methodology standards.
* Keep abreast of existing and emerging internal and external risk trends, industry business practices and technology developments to drive best\-in\-class risk assessments, continuous monitoring, training, and audit planning. Support heads of audits to formulate audit plans focussed on key risks, client outcomes and regulatory requirements and ensure the plan always remains relevant.
* Develop and independently manage relationships with Senior Management in India and globally (for Personal and SME segments) to ensure comprehensive understanding of business strategy and plans and to get agreements on audit issues and results.
* Lead and drive effective use of advanced analytics in all audits, continuous monitoring, and risk assessments and to support various GIA audit transformation related initiatives.
* Be a subject matter expert in risk and auditing in an assigned area within Personal and SME Banking; prepare and continuously update training and audit programs that are used for up\-skilling auditors and performing audits globally in the assigned area.
* Prepare presentations, risk reports and dashboards for GIA’s reporting in in India / Global / Regional senior risk and governance committees. The reports should focus on join\-the\-dot themes and existing and emerging risk areas.
* Support Head of Audit India in local regulatory matters and ensure GIA’s credibility and trust is always maintained with the regulator.


**People Leadership**


* Lead the India WRB Audit team and be responsible from recruitment, coaching, performance management, compensation, and training and professional development.
* Continuously engage, motivate, and drive team members to deliver highest quality audit and non\-audit work. Foster a collaborative and positive work environment.
* Support heads of audits to proactively spot talent for GIA.


**Regulatory \& Business Conduct**


* Display exemplary conduct and live by the Group’s Values and Code of Conduct.
* Take personal responsibility for embedding the highest standards of ethics, including regulatory and business conduct, across Standard Chartered Bank. This includes understanding and ensuring compliance with, in letter and spirit, all applicable laws, regulations, guidelines and the Group Code of Conduct.
* Contribute to the audit team in achieving the outcomes set out in the Bank’s Conduct Principles: Financial Crime Prevention and The Right Environment
**Qualifications**
* Experienced internal auditor or risk professional with minimum 12 years of experience and progressive career growth. A significant part of the career should be around WRB including SME businesses in a bank.
* In\-depth expertise in key risks including credit risk and preferably financial crime risk, operational risk and compliance / conduct risk. Have a good understanding of technology and cyber security risks to be able to drive integrated front\-to\-back audit assignments.
* Demonstrate sound professional judgment to balance risk and reward, think client and understand the latest developments in financial services (like generative Artificial Intelligence, Digital Assets) to be able to both use and audit these.
* Excellent interpersonal skills to be able to influence change, obtain buy\-ins from senior management and interact with regulators independently to drive GIA’s agenda.
* Proactive, self\-directed, and able to drive self and team to innovate and build best practices. Able to operate independently with minimum supervision.
* Able to work within a global team and adapt and learn from people of different cultures and working styles.
* Professional accounting or audit qualification is strongly preferred (for example CA, ACCA, CIA);
* Proven leadership skills and demonstrated ability to motivate and guide audit teams. Prior people leadership experience is strongly preferable.
* Highly evolved communication skills, both written and verbal, is essential.
* Exposure to Indian banking industry is essential and exposure to other regional or global markets is strongly preferable.
* Ability to commit to limited business travel within and outside India.
**About Standard Chartered**

We're an international bank, nimble enough to act, big enough for impact. For more than 170 years, we've worked to make a positive difference for our clients, communities, and each other. We question the status quo, love a challenge and enjoy finding new opportunities to grow and do better than before. If you're looking for a career with purpose and you want to work for a bank making a difference, we want to hear from you. You can count on us to celebrate your unique talents and we can't wait to see the talents you can bring us.
Our purpose, to drive commerce and prosperity through our unique diversity, together with our brand promise, to be here for good are achieved by how we each live our valued behaviours. When you work with us, you'll see how we value difference and advocate inclusion.
Together we:
* **Do the right thing** and are assertive, challenge one another, and live with integrity, while putting the client at the heart of what we do
* **Never settle,** continuously striving to improve and innovate, keeping things simple and learning from doing well, and not so well
* **Are better together,** we can be ourselves, be inclusive, see more good in others, and work collectively to build for the long term
**What we offer**
**In line with our Fair Pay Charter,** we offer a competitive salary and benefits to support your mental, physical, financial and social wellbeing.
* **Core bank funding for retirement savings, medical and life insurance,** with flexible and voluntary benefits available in some locations.
* **Time\-off** including annual leave, parental/maternity (20 weeks), sabbatical (12 months maximum) and volunteering leave (3 days), along with minimum global standards for annual and public holiday, which is combined to 30 days minimum.
* **Flexible working** options based around home and office locations, with flexible working patterns.
* **Proactive wellbeing support** through Unmind, a market\-leading digital wellbeing platform, development courses for resilience and other human skills, global Employee Assistance Programme, sick leave, mental health first\-aiders and all sorts of self\-help toolkits
* **A continuous learning culture** to support your growth, with opportunities to reskill and upskill and access to physical, virtual and digital learning.
* **Being part of an inclusive and values driven organisation,** one that embraces and celebrates our unique diversity, across our teams, business functions and geographies \- everyone feels respected and can realise their full potential.

