in-f977ea54909366bf,indeed,https://in.indeed.com/viewjob?jk=f977ea54909366bf,https://careers.ey.com/ey/job/Bengaluru-Vulnerability-Management-Service-Line-Support-Analyst-Supervising-Associate-KA-560048/1180702001/?feedId=338701&utm_source=Indeed&utm_campaign=EY_indeed,Vulnerability Management Service Line Support-Analyst-Supervising Associate,EY,"KA, IN",2025-04-11,,,,,False,"At EY, you’ll have the chance to build a career as unique as you are, with the global scale, support, inclusive culture and technology to become the best version of you. And we’re counting on your unique voice and perspective to help EY become even better, too. Join us and build an exceptional experience for yourself, and a better working world for all.

 **Service Line Support Analyst, Vulnerability Management**  

Today’s world is fueled by vast amounts of information. Data is more valuable than ever before. Protecting data and information systems is central to doing business, and everyone in EY Information Security has a critical role to play. Join a global team of almost 950 people who collaborate to support the business of EY by protecting EY and client information assets! Our Information Security professionals enable EY to work securely and deliver secure products and services, as well as detect and quickly respond to security events as they happen. Together, the efforts of our dedicated team help protect the EY brand and build client trust.

  

Within Information Security we blend risk strategy, digital identity, cyber defense, application security and technology solutions as we consider the entire security lifecycle. You will join a team of hardworking, security\-focused individuals dedicated to supporting, protecting and enabling the business through innovative, secure solutions that provide speed to market and business value.

 **The opportunity**  

The analyst will support the Vulnerability Management program by engaging with EY service lines to assess and address their vulnerability hygiene. The analyst will assist in integrating robust vulnerability management practices into daily operations, contributing to the enhancement of EY's overall security posture. This role offers a unique chance to learn from senior leaders, develop technical and interpersonal skills, and play a key role in both tactical and strategic security initiatives.

 **Your key responsibilities**  

The Service Line Support Analyst will collaborate closely with the business to understand and communicate their vulnerability hygiene and devise strategic remediation plans through targeted analysis and communication. In this role, the analyst will distil complex security data into actionable insights and communicate these effectively to both technical and non\-technical stakeholders. The analyst will play a pivotal role in building the business’ confidence and collaboration with the Vulnerability Management program by fostering strong partnerships across the organization. Contributions will be instrumental in advancing our security posture and protecting the integrity of our services.

 **Skills and attributes for success**

* Basic understanding of information security and cybersecurity principles.
* Strong communication skills with the ability to convey technical information in a clear manner.
* Eagerness to learn and build relationships within the organization.
* Ability to work in a team environment and support senior team members.
* A proactive approach to problem\-solving and the ability to prioritize tasks.

 **To qualify for the role you must have**

* 4\+ years of experience in an information security role, with exposure to vulnerability management
* Familiarity with security control functionality and threat landscapes
* A willingness to engage with stakeholders and contribute to a collaborative work environment
* Basic experience in data analytics and reporting
* Strong knowledge of identifying and remediating vulnerabilities in an enterprise environment
* Demonstrated experience assessing and communication risk to all levels within an organization
* A fundamental understanding of security control functionality
* Experience working in a collaborative environment

 **Ideally, you’ll also have**

* Analytics background
* Vulnerability management experience

 **What we look for**  

We are looking for an experienced, self\-driven, analyst that can identify vulnerability trends and associated solutions and convey them to a business audience. The ideal candidate will seek to improve others while continuously learning and identifying ways to strengthen the organization. This role will require an analyst that enjoys complex problem sets and developing solutions.

 **What working at EY offers**  

As part of this role, you will work in a highly coordinated, globally diverse team with the opportunity and tools to grow, develop and drive your career forward. Here, you can combine global opportunity with flexible working. The EY benefits package goes above and beyond too, focusing on your physical, emotional, financial and social well\-being. Your recruiter can talk to you about the benefits available in your country. Here’s a snapshot of what we offer:

* **Continuous learning:** You will develop the mindset and skills to navigate whatever comes next.
* **Success as defined by you:** We will provide the tools and flexibility, so you can make a significant impact, your way.
* **Transformative leadership**: We will give you the insights, coaching and confidence to be the leader the world needs.
* **Diverse and inclusive culture:** You will be accepted for who you are and empowered to use your voice to help others find theirs.

 **EY \| Building a better working world**

  

  

EY exists to build a better working world, helping to create long\-term value for clients, people and society and build trust in the capital markets.

  

  

Enabled by data and technology, diverse EY teams in over 150 countries provide trust through assurance and help clients grow, transform and operate.

  

  

