in-83305fc2991cbd40,indeed,https://in.indeed.com/viewjob?jk=83305fc2991cbd40,http://in.indeed.com/job/security-operation-centre-analyst-83305fc2991cbd40,Security Operation Centre Analyst,Netstratum Technologies,"KL, IN",2025-04-10,fulltime,,,,False,"**Location :** Kochi, Kerala

**Experience:** 3\+ years

**Salary:** As per Industry Standards

**Job Description:**  
Netstratum is looking for a motivated and experienced Security Operation Centre Analyst who will be responsible for monitoring security technologies, triaging and analyzing security alerts, and responding to incidents in real time. Your role involves investigating threats, identifying attack vectors, scoping out incidents, performing forensic analysis, and coordinating efforts to contain and mitigate security breaches. The person will be responsible for providing ongoing recommendations to improve security protocols and tools, working closely with other members of the SOC team and collaborating with external security partners when necessary.

**Responsibilities:**

* Monitor security tools (FortiSIEM, FortiEDR, DarkTrace NDR) and network traffic for security events and anomalies.
* Quickly triage, analyze, and respond to security incidents, investigating network anomalies and escalating issues as necessary.
* Perform correlation and trend analysis of security logs, network traffic, and security alerts to detect and investigate suspicious activity.
* Work with the security team to tune security tools to reduce false positives while enhancing detection capabilities.
* Analyze malware, attack vectors, and attacker tactics to strengthen detection capabilities and improve incident response procedures.
* Share threat intelligence and advisories with external partners or government agencies and contribute to cybersecurity initiatives.
* Create detailed reports and provide incident documentation. Maintain shift reports and client communication logs.
* Support the development, tuning, and review of SIEM content to ensure optimal performance of the security infrastructure.

**Requirements:**

* Bachelor's degree in Computer Science, Information Systems, or a related field.
* At least 1\-2 years of experience in a Security Operations Center (SOC), Network Operations Center (NOC), or Computer Incident Response Team (CIRT).
* Experience in detecting, analyzing, and responding to cyber threats. Familiarity with intrusion detection systems and incident response protocols.
* Working knowledge of FortiSIEM, FortiEDR, DarkTrace NDR, and related security tools.
* Proficiency in network devices, operating systems, protocols, and WAN/LAN technologies.
* Experience in system log analysis, network traffic analysis, and correlating security.
* Strong written and verbal communication abilities for documenting incidents and preparing reports.
* Analytical mindset with a passion for solving complex security problems and investigating security incidents.
* Familiarity with Fortinet tools (FortiSIEM, FortiEDR) and experience in packet analysis (HTTP, SMTP, FTP traffic).
* Understanding of ITIL/ITSM processes and advanced security protocols.

To Apply\- Visit our careers page (netstratum.com)

Job Type: Full\-time

Benefits:

* Health insurance
* Provident Fund

Schedule:

* Monday to Friday

