in-900bc7ff56b215b4,indeed,https://in.indeed.com/viewjob?jk=900bc7ff56b215b4,https://www.orioninc.com/careers/job/?gh_jid=4451072006,Global Compliance – Risk and Compliance officer,Orion Systems Integrators Inc,"TN, IN",2025-04-03,,,,,False,"Orion Innovation is a premier, award\-winning, global business and technology services firm. Orion delivers game\-changing business transformation and product development rooted in digital strategy, experience design, and engineering, with a unique combination of agility, scale, and maturity. We work with a wide range of clients across many industries including financial services, professional services, telecommunications and media, consumer products, automotive, industrial automation, professional sports and entertainment, life sciences, ecommerce, and education.

**Job Overview:**



We are seeking a dynamic leader with strong communication skills to manage and align global compliance initiatives with organizational objectives. The ideal candidate will have expertise in industry certifications, internal audits, and process improvements, while ensuring compliance with evolving global regulatory requirements.


**Key Responsibilities:**


* Demonstrate strong leadership qualities and excellent communication skills to influence direct reports. Ensure alignment of global compliance objectives with the company's organizational goals.
* Manage the implementation and adherence to industry\-standard certifications and attestations, including ISO\-27001, SOC1/SOC2, and PCI\-DSS.
* Conduct and oversee internal audits, including SQA, project audits, department audits, and individual process awareness audits, ensuring compliance with internal and external regulations.
* Provide guidance on process improvements based on industry standards, and establish a clear framework to address gaps between the current and desired states.
* Ensure compliance with evolving global regulatory requirements, including GDPR and privacy regulations in the UK and Switzerland, and enforce their enforcement across relevant departments.


**Key Skills:**


* Compliance Expertise (ISO\-27001, SOC1/SOC2, PCI\-DSS)
* Internal Auditing (Project, Department, Process Audits)
* Regulatory Knowledge (GDPR, UK, Swiss Privacy Laws)
* Process Improvement \& Gap Analysis


**Preferred Qualifications:**


* Bachelor’s or Master’s Degree in Business Administration, Information Security, Cybersecurity, or a related field.
* Professional Certifications such as CISSP, CISA, CISM, or similar.
* Knowledge of ESG Governance and frameworks
* Cloud Security and compliance audit experience

Orion is an equal opportunity employer, and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, creed, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, pregnancy, age, national origin, citizenship status, disability status, genetic information, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law.



Candidate Privacy Policy



Orion Systems Integrators, LLC and its subsidiaries and its affiliates (collectively, “Orion,” “we” or “us”) are committed to protecting your privacy. This **Candidate Privacy Policy (orioninc.com)** (“Notice”) explains:


* What information we collect during our application and recruitment process and why we collect it;
* How we handle that information; and
* How to access and update that information.


Your use of Orion services is governed by any applicable terms in this notice and our general **Privacy Policy**.",,https://in.indeed.com/cmp/Orion-Systems-Integrators-Inc,Cyber Security
in-fdca7b5688ebd40a,indeed,https://in.indeed.com/viewjob?jk=fdca7b5688ebd40a,https://apply.workable.com/j/CD837B402E,Project Manager - Cybersecurity,ProArch,"KA, IN",2025-04-03,fulltime,,,,True,"At ProArch Cybersecurity, our customers are our lifeblood, and our service delivery revolves around enhancing our customers' businesses by providing tailored defense strategies, proactive offensive testing, and strategic risk measurement, all supported by the latest automation technology. We are dedicated to creating an innovative environment that exceeds service reliability, efficiency, and trustworthiness expectations while delighting customers along the way. We aim to predict and reduce threats intelligently, ensuring ongoing protection for our clients and leveraging their insights to offer world class ""Advanced Resilience"" cybersecurity protection. Internally, we prioritize efficient processes, automation, service reliability, proactive vigilance, and providing the utmost value to our clients.


The Project Manager \- Cybersecurity Services is tasked with planning, executing, and delivering cybersecurity projects. Additionally, they ensure the timely provision of managed services within a service delivery environment that focuses on Microsoft security solutions. This role ensures that cybersecurity projects are completed on time, within scope, and within budget, all while meeting the quality and security standards required by the organization and its clients. The Project Manager coordinates cross\-functional teams – including cybersecurity engineers, consultants, and client stakeholders – to drive project success. While a strong understanding of cybersecurity (especially Microsoft’s security technologies) is important, this position emphasizes core project management duties: project planning, execution tracking, stakeholder management, and service delivery coordination to support our service delivery organization

**Key Responsibilities**

* **Project Planning \& Initiation:** Define project scope, objectives, and deliverables in collaboration with clients and technical leads. Develop project plans outlining timelines, tasks, and resource requirements. Ensure each project aligns with customer outcomes.
* **Project Execution \& Coordination:** Lead the day\-to\-day management of cybersecurity project delivery. Coordinate cross\-functional teams (e.g. Security Consultants, Specialists, Analysts) to execute against the plan, ensuring everyone understands their tasks and deadlines. Manage project schedules, track progress, and adjust plans as necessary to account for changes or new requirements, keeping the project on track.
* **Stakeholder Management:** Serve as the primary liaison for project stakeholders, including clients, internal teams, and leadership. Facilitate regular status meetings and reports to communicate progress, milestones, risks, and issues. Manage stakeholder expectations and ensure alignment between technical teams and business/client needs throughout the project lifecycle.
* **Risk Management \& Compliance Coordination:** Proactively identify and document project risks and issues (including security\-related risks). Work with our internal team and customer stakeholders to assess and prioritize these risks. Develop and implement mitigation plans or contingency strategies to address risks.
* **Budget \& Resource Management:** Manage project budgets and resources to ensure efficient delivery. Track project expenditures and labor against estimates, and report on budget status. Coordinate with resource managers to secure necessary staffing (e.g. security analysts, engineers) and adjust resource plans if project scope or timelines change.
* **Service Delivery Coordination:** Ensure a smooth delivery of cybersecurity services as projects transition from implementation to operational support. Work closely with the service delivery and operations teams to hand over completed solutions, making sure that all documentation, training, and support processes are in place. Verify that delivered security solutions (for example, Microsoft 365 security implementations, Azure Sentinel deployments, etc.) meet the agreed\-upon service levels and client expectations.
* **Quality Assurance:** Uphold quality standards for project deliverables. Coordinate testing and validation of cybersecurity solutions in partnership with technical leads – for instance, confirming that security configurations or controls are implemented as designed. Address any quality issues by facilitating reviews or audits by subject matter experts, rather than deep technical troubleshooting by the Project Manager.
* **Change Control:** Manage project scope and changes through change control processes. When new security requirements or technical changes arise, evaluate their impact on timeline and budget, obtain necessary approvals, and communicate changes to all stakeholders.
* **Documentation \& Reporting:** Maintain thorough project documentation including work plans, risk logs, decision registers, and status reports. Provide clear and concise reports on project progress, key metrics, and post\-project results to both internal stakeholders and clients.
* **Continuous Improvement:** After project completion, lead or participate in post\-project reviews/retrospectives. Identify lessons learned and best practices specific to delivering cybersecurity services. Work on improving project management processes and templates for future security projects, contributing to the overall maturity of the cybersecurity service delivery practice.

**Requirements**


**Education:** Bachelor’s / Master's degree in Information Technology, Cybersecurity, Business Administration, or a related field. Master’s degree preferred.

* **Experience:** Minimum of 5\+ years of project management experience. Experience with agile as well as waterfall and other project management methodologies.
* **Certifications:** ITIL, PMP/Prince 2, Lean Six Sigma, PgMP, CISM, CISSP, or relevant certifications are highly desirable.
* **Cybersecurity Domain Knowledge:** Familiarity with core cybersecurity concepts and practices. Experience in projects involving Microsoft cybersecurity solutions (such as Microsoft 365 security suite, Entra ID, Microsoft Defender, Azure Sentinel, or similar) is an advantage. While hands\-on technical skills are not the primary focus, the Project Manager should be comfortable discussing security topics and understanding technical team inputs at a high level.
* **Communication \& Stakeholder Engagement:** Excellent communication skills, both written and verbal. Demonstrated experience in managing stakeholder relationships and expectations, ideally including client\-facing project management. Ability to translate technical information into business terms and ensure mutual understanding among technical teams and non\-technical stakeholders.
* **Organizational Skills:** Exceptional organizational and time management abilities, self\-starter. Capable of juggling multiple priorities and projects in a fast\-paced, service\-driven environment. Detail\-oriented in tracking tasks, issues, and project details, ensuring nothing falls through the cracks.
* **Problem Solving \& Risk Management:** Strong analytical and problem\-solving skills. Adept at identifying potential obstacles or risks early and facilitating collaborative solutions. Experience with risk management techniques and the ability to drive issue resolution by engaging the right resources.
* **Team Collaboration:** A team player who can lead by influence. Experience coordinating cross\-functional teams and encouraging a cooperative working atmosphere. Ability to work with remote or distributed teams, including vendors or third\-party service providers, to achieve project objectives.
* **Adaptability:** Flexibility to adapt to changing project requirements or shifts in client priorities. Comfortable working within agile, waterfall, or hybrid delivery models as required by the project.
* **Service Delivery Mindset:** Prior exposure to a service delivery or managed services environment is beneficial. Understanding of service level agreements (SLAs) and operational handover processes (e.g., following ITIL practices) is a plus. Commitment to delivering value and positive outcomes for clients as well as internal stakeholders.

**How Your Success Will Be Measured**

* Project Success: Completion of projects on time, within budget, and to the satisfaction of stakeholders.
* Client Satisfaction: Positive feedback from clients regarding the delivery and outcomes of security services.
* Innovation: Successful identification and implementation of innovative solutions and process improvements. Provide these through demonstrable improvements in processes and methodologies based on feedback and performance metrics.
* Risk Mitigation: Maintain, communicate and keep updated and active risk register of individual and project portfolio risks and mitigation strategies and communicate that with stakeholders and needed.
* Strategic Alignment: Alignment of Cybersecurity projects with organizational goals and strategic objectives.",,https://in.indeed.com/cmp/Proarch,Cyber Security
in-bd586afb372745f6,indeed,https://in.indeed.com/viewjob?jk=bd586afb372745f6,https://www.att.jobs/job/-/lead-cybersecurity-api-security/117/79597493760?utm_source=indeed.com_organic&utm_medium=organic&utm_campaign=organic&utm_content=job_aggregator&utm_term=130398638,Lead Cybersecurity - API Security,AT&T,"TS, IN",2025-04-03,fulltime,,,,False,"**Job Description:**

**About the Company:**


At AT\&T, we’re connecting the world through the latest tech, top\-of\-the\-line communications and the best in entertainment. Our groundbreaking digital solutions provide intuitive and integrated experiences for millions of customers across online, retail and care channels. Join our mission to deliver compelling communication and entertainment experiences to customers around the world as we continue to evolve as a technology\-powered, human\-centered organization. As part of our team, you’ll transform the way we deliver a seamless customer experience with digital at the center of all you do. In our world, digital is much larger than just an eCommerce channel, we are transforming all channels to digitally perform as one team to create a better customer experience. As we move into 2024, the digital transformation will revolutionize the digital space and you can build a career that will propel your future.

**About the Job:**


We are seeking a dedicated Vulnerability Management Specialist with a focus on API security to join our cybersecurity team. The ideal candidate will be responsible for identifying, evaluating, and mitigating security vulnerabilities within our API ecosystem. This role requires a proactive approach to security and a strong understanding of API architecture and security best practices.


This professional must be highly organized and able to manage various stakeholder requests as they arise with strong multitasking skills and technical acumen. In addition, the professional must also be able to assist mentor team members in the designated areas of responsibility.

**Experience Level:** 12\+ years

**Location:** Hyderabad / Bengaluru

**Responsibilities Include:**

* Conduct regular security assessments and monitor real\-time alerts generated from API endpoint monitoring tools.
* Develop and maintain a comprehensive vulnerability management program for APIs.
* Collaborate with development teams to ensure secure coding practices are followed.
* Implement and manage API security tools to monitor and protect against threats.
* Keep abreast of the latest security trends, threats, and mitigation techniques in API security.

**Required skills:**

* 12 years minimum experience in a Application Security
* 5 plus years of experience in API security.
* Hands\-on experience with API security tools and frameworks.
* Strong understanding of RESTful and SOAP web services.
* Knowledge of authentication mechanisms like OAuth, JWT, and API keys.
* Experience in developing secure coding practices for APIs.
* Experience in implementing API security tools.
* Experience with cloud services and their native API security features is desirable.
* Familiarity with the NoName API security tool is a plus.

**Desirable skills:**

* Bachelors or Masters in Computer Sciences Engineering.
* Relevant security certifications (e.g., CISSP, CEH, OSCP) are preferred.
* Excellent problem\-solving and analytical skills.
* Effective communication skills, both written and verbal.
* Ability to work independently and as part of a team.

**Technical Skills:** Vulnerability management**,** API Security, Noname etc.,

**Additional information (if any):** Flexible to provide coverage in US morning hours.

**Certification**: CISSP, CEH, OSCP and/or other relevant certifications.

**Weekly Hours:**


40**Time Type:**


Regular**Location:**


Hyderabad, Andhra Pradesh, India
It is the policy of AT\&T to provide equal employment opportunity (EEO) to all persons regardless of age, color, national origin, citizenship status, physical or mental disability, race, religion, creed, gender, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity and/or expression, genetic information, marital status, status with regard to public assistance, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state or local law. In addition, AT\&T will provide reasonable accommodations for qualified individuals with disabilities. AT\&T is a fair chance employer and does not initiate a background check until an offer is made.",,https://in.indeed.com/cmp/AT&T,Cyber Security
in-b322710f491c1329,indeed,https://in.indeed.com/viewjob?jk=b322710f491c1329,https://careers.wipro.com/job/Hyderabad-Cyber-Security-Analyst-L4-500032/1149721155/?feedId=420455&utm_source=Indeed,Cyber Security Analyst - L4,Wipro,"TS, IN",2025-04-03,,,,,False,"Wipro Limited (NYSE: WIT, BSE: 507685, NSE: WIPRO) is a leading technology services and consulting company focused on building innovative solutions that address clients’ most complex digital transformation needs. Leveraging our holistic portfolio of capabilities in consulting, design, engineering, and operations, we help clients realize their boldest ambitions and build future\-ready, sustainable businesses. With over 230,000 employees and business partners across 65 countries, we deliver on the promise of helping our customers, colleagues, and communities thrive in an ever\-changing world. For additional information, visit us at www.wipro.com.**Job Description**
-------------------

**Role Purpose**

  

The purpose of this role is to analyse, identify, rectify \& recommend specific improvement measures that help in the security posture of the organization by protecting the sensitive information

**͏**
-----

**Do**
======

* **Ensuring customer centricity by providing apt cybersecurity**
---------------------------------------------------------------
* Monitoring and safeguarding the log sources and security access
* Planning for disaster recovery in the event of any security breaches
* Monitor for attacks, intrusions and unusual, unauthorized or illegal activity
* Performs moderately complex log reviews and forensic analysis to identify unauthorized or unacceptable access to data or systems
* Conduct security assessments, risk analysis and root cause analysis of security incidents
* Handling incidents escalated by the L1 team in 24x7 rotational shifts
* Use advanced analytics tools to determine emerging threat patterns and vulnerabilities
* Completing all tactical security operations tasks associated with this engagement.
* Analyses all the attacks and come up with remedial attack analysis
* Conduct detailed analysis of incidents and create reports and dashboards
* **Stakeholder coordination \& audit assistance**
------------------------------------------------
* Liaise with stakeholders in relation to cyber security issues and provide future recommendations
* Maintain an information security risk register and assist with internal and external audits relating to information security
* Assist with the creation, maintenance and delivery of cyber security awareness training for colleagues
* Advice and guidance to employees on issues such as spam and unwanted or malicious emails
**͏**
