in-82576986c64ad9a4,indeed,https://in.indeed.com/viewjob?jk=82576986c64ad9a4,http://in.indeed.com/job/senior-penetration-tester-82576986c64ad9a4,Senior Penetration Tester,SSquad Global,"KA, IN",2025-04-02,fulltime,,,,True,"**Job Description: Senior Penetration Tester**

**Position:** Senior Penetration Tester**Location:** Bangalore**Employment Type:** Full\-time**Reports To:** Security Operations Manager / CISO

**Job Summary:**We are seeking an experienced and highly skilled Senior Penetration Tester to lead and execute comprehensive security assessments for our organization's IT infrastructure, applications, and systems. The ideal candidate will possess strong technical expertise in ethical hacking, vulnerability assessment, and security auditing, along with a proactive approach to identifying and mitigating security threats.

**Key Responsibilities:**

· Conduct advanced penetration tests on networks, web applications, APIs, cloud environments, and mobile applications.

· Identify vulnerabilities and provide detailed risk assessments with actionable recommendations.

· Simulate real\-world attacks to assess security posture and incident response capabilities.

· Develop and execute red team exercises and adversary simulation scenarios.

· Collaborate with IT and development teams to remediate security issues effectively.

· Document findings, create detailed technical reports, and present to technical and non\-technical stakeholders.

· Stay up\-to\-date with emerging threats, vulnerabilities, and security technologies.

· Mentor junior penetration testers and contribute to the development of security best practices.

**Required Skills and Qualifications:**

· Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Information Security, or related field (or equivalent experience).

· 5\+ years of hands\-on experience in penetration testing, ethical hacking, and security assessments.

· Strong knowledge of security frameworks (OWASP, NIST, MITRE ATT\&CK) and common vulnerabilities (CVE, CVSS).

· Proficiency with penetration testing tools (e.g., Burp Suite, Tenable, Cyfirma Metasploit, Nmap, Wireshark, Nessus, Kali Linux).

· Deep understanding of network protocols, operating systems (Windows, Linux), and cloud environments (AWS, Azure, GCP).

· Experience with scripting languages (Python, PowerShell, Bash) for automation and custom exploits.

· Strong analytical, problem\-solving, and communication skills.

**Certifications (Preferred):**

· Offensive Security Certified Professional (OSCP)

· Certified Ethical Hacker (CEH)

· Offensive Security Certified Expert (OSCE)

· GIAC Penetration Tester (GPEN)

· CREST or similar advanced security certifications

**Desirable Attributes:**

· Experience with red teaming and threat emulation exercises.

· Background in incident response and forensic analysis.

· Ability to work independently and manage multiple projects simultaneously.

· Strong attention to detail with a passion for cybersecurity.

Job Type: Full\-time

Pay: ₹1,000,000\.00 \- ₹1,500,000\.00 per year

Benefits:

* Work from home

Work Location: In person",,https://in.indeed.com/cmp/Ssquad-Global-1,Cyber Security
in-af7f4cd64b2a0ddc,indeed,https://in.indeed.com/viewjob?jk=af7f4cd64b2a0ddc,http://in.indeed.com/job/cybersecurity-associate-freshers-af7f4cd64b2a0ddc,Cybersecurity Associate - Freshers,SATTRIX Information Security Pvt Ltd,"GJ, IN",2025-04-02,fulltime,,,,False,"Greetings from Sattrix Group!

This email is in regard to opening of freshers for cybersecurity domain at our organization.

I am glad to introduce you to Sattrix Group\- a trusted name in the IT space. We started our journey by offering Professional and Managed Services in the cybersecurity industry and have added a slew of services along the way of our 10\-year long journey. A brief about the Sattrix Group of companies is given below.

Sattrix Group currently has two companies under its expanding umbrella:

1\) Sattrix Information Security:

An end\-to\-end cybersecurity solutions provider for all your security needs. Sattrix InfoSec caters to the entire lifecycle from consulting, implementation, and management of various cybersecurity solutions. Our expertise starts with implementation and management of Security Analytics, SIEM and extends into areas like Endpoint Security, Network Security, Managed Security and Cloud Security Consulting. We offer both standard and customized solutions with reputable clientele across the globe (US, UAE, Africa, Southeast Asia etc.) and industry verticals (BFSI, Govt., Pharma, ITES, Retail, Telco etc.).

Please visit our website for more information.

2\) Sattrix Software Solutions:

The software wing of Sattrix is not your usual software development partner but aces at providing customized software solutions around advanced technologies like Artificial Intelligence, Machine Learning, Big Data analytics and Business Process Automation. And with the vast experience in cybersecurity, we can integrate your software requirements seamlessly with your security infrastructure while ensuring that the applications and solutions are safe and secure within themselves.

Please visit our website for more information.

**Job Opening \- Details**

* Position: Cybersecurity Associate
* Location: Ahmedabad for inhouse training and later will be placed at project location anywhere in India
* Department: Managed Security Services
* The Cybersecurity Associate is responsible for designing, developing, or recommending integrated security system and physical control solutions that will ensure proprietary/confidential data and systems are protected. Participates with the client in the strategic design process to translate security and business requirements into technical designs. Configures and validates secure systems and physical controls, and tests security products and systems to detect security weakness.

**Detailed Job Description:**

* Understand a variety of network protocols including TCP/IP, UDP, DHCP, FTP, SFTP, ATM, SNMP, SMTP, SSH, SSL, VPN, RDP, HTTP and HTTPS.
* Operate SIEM consoles in order to monitor the environment threat and incidents.
* Understand cyber\-attack methods.
* Perform analysis of security logs in an attempt to detect unauthorized behavior.
* Document and contain security incidents detected on the network.
* Execute incident response process when a security incident has been declared.
* Plan, coordinate, and implement network security measures in order to protect data, software, and hardware on government networks.
* Maintain logs related to network functions, as well as maintenance and repair records.
* Document and present findings to management suitable for customer.
* Work in rotational shifts including weekends \& holidays.
* Monitor IT systems and report technical issues as per process defined.
* Coordinate with customers to solve issues.
* Provide daily reports to Team Leader.
* Carry out analysis of security events and report problems.
* Meet SLA requirements.
* Ready to commit to work for 2 year 3 months.

**Education and skills:**

* Bachelor's degree or equivalent.
* Have strong knowledge of IT networking Concepts.
* Must skills – Excellent command over verbal and written English.

**Employment Conditions:**

**Please note interested candidates must be ready for the following:**

* Interested candidates needs to consider this as earn and learn opportunity for a period of 1 years, as getting break into cyber security for fresher is very rare opportunity and now the future boom will be Cyber security professional as majority services, products are taking this route. They would also get access to industry developed on job training.
* This training will include but not limited to hands on experience on dedicated demo environment \& live like environment with shadowing under cybersecurity expert, Use cases and multiple log / incident management tools.
* Ready to relocate at Ahmedabad (Gujarat) location for training and later will be deployed anywhere PAN India / Overseas as per the project location.
* Upon joining, immediately Technical Training will be initiated which will be for period of approximately 3 to 4 months. The total cost for this training is Rs. 2,00,000\. Company do not charge employee for this training, but employee will be required to sign **Training Agreement** of Rs. 2 Lakh and for two (2\) year 3 months with the company.
* Cheque of Rs. 2,00,000 to be given by employee towards security at the time of joining. This cheque will not be encashed but kept with the company and same cheque will be handed over back to the respective employee after completion of two (2\) year 3 months with us. The cheque will only be utilized upon breaching of Training Agreement of two year three months.
* Employee is required to submit Original LC, HSC Marksheet, HSC Passing Certificate, and last highest university educational marksheet \& passing certificate to the company on the day of joining – The same will be returned by the company post completion of continuous two (2\) year 3 months of services from the date of joining.
* Selected candidate is required to join Ahmedabad Office of Sattrix Information Security within 10 days of receipt of job offer.
* Work in rotational shifts, weekends, holidays (appropriate comp\-off will be provided as per company’s policy)
* Have ready passport or at least have done passport application.
* Ready to learn new technologies and take the ownership of the responsibility given.

**Perks and Benefits:**

**Total Annual Compensation Range:**

* Rs.**2,45,827** (Monthly Rs. 19,762\), Net Take Home Salary: Rs. 18,650\)
* Rs.**3,08,683**(Monthly Rs. 25,000\), Net Take Home Salary: Rs. 24,600\)
* Rs.**4,28,712** (Monthly Rs.35,000 ), Net Take Home Salary: Rs. 34,600\).

**Note:** The annual compensation will be determined based on interview feedback.

(also on job training worth INR 2,00,000, as explained above in point number 1,2,4,5\)

· In case the student has additional / advance knowledge of any tool into cybersecurity and no training need required, in that case the salary of the student will be higher than the fresher level and this salary base will be decided in accordance with the individual's technical interview feedback and ‘ready to put on job’ ability.

· Deployment Allowance: Post Training completion, if physically deployed at Project location, which is different than base location (Ahmedabad) and actual home location of candidate. Project deployment allowance as per the city category will be given in line with the company’s policy.

· Fulfillment of required statutory liabilities.

· Additional certification allowances based on project requirement may be granted and paid by the company.

· Mediclaim insurance of 1 Lakh per year.

· No salary will be deposited to new hired until they join Ahmedabad office or project location physically or become billable \- No salary for Training from home.

**Awards \& Recognition:**

· Technical Training certifications both Internal \& External based on business need and individual performance

· Efforts Recognition

Job Type: Full\-time

Pay: ₹237,144\.00 per year

Benefits:

* Paid sick time
* Provident Fund

Schedule:

* Rotational shift

Supplemental Pay:

* Shift allowance

Work Location: In person",,https://in.indeed.com/cmp/Sattrix-Information-Security-Pvt-Ltd,Cyber Security
