 **The Opportunity**


Are you a passionate cloud security engineer and manager with expertise in securing cloud environments? If so, you'll want to join the Product Security team at Nutanix, where you'll have the opportunity to be a thought leader, develop creative solutions, and work alongside cross\-functional teams to integrate security best practices into our cutting\-edge products and services.


We seek an experienced manager to lead a cloud security team in India. Reporting to the Director, Cloud Security Engineering, the Manager, Cloud Security Engineering will be part of a dynamic and collaborative team of security professionals at Nutanix. The team is dedicated to ensuring the security and integrity of our cloud infrastructure and applications, working closely with cross\-functional teams to identify and address security gaps, develop and implement security configurations, automate workflows, and provide guidance on integrating security best practices. This team is passionate about cybersecurity, innovative solutions, and continuous improvement, and they thrive in a fast\-paced and challenging environment.


The Product Security team at Nutanix is a global team that focuses on ensuring the security of our products. We have a proven track record of success and have been recognized as one of the top teams to work for within Nutanix. Our team is dedicated to staying ahead of the latest security threats and maintaining the integrity of our products. What sets us apart is our commitment to innovation and collaboration, as well as our strong emphasis on continuous learning and growth. Join us if you want to make a real impact on the products that serve thousands of our customers.

 **About the Team**


At Nutanix, you will be joining the Product Security team, a dynamic and innovative group comprised of talented professionals located across the US and India. Our team culture is built on collaboration and ingenuity, ensuring that we constantly push the boundaries of what's possible in securing our products. We foster an environment where new ideas are celebrated, and each team member is empowered to contribute to the overall success of our security efforts.


You will report to the Director of Engineering, who is dedicated to guiding the team towards achieving its goals while also prioritizing individual growth and professional development. The work setup is hybrid, requiring you to be in the office 2\-3 days a week, which allows for a balanced approach to in\-person collaboration and remote work flexibility.

 **Your Role**

**Core Responsibilities:**

* Monitor and manage supported products and services and consult product teams on integrating security best practices
* Identify security gaps and execute projects to address them
* Analyze and estimate feasibility, costs, and time for technical solutions
* Operate security tools and build response playbooks and design and build automated workflows for security operations
