gd-1009705912414,glassdoor,https://www.glassdoor.co.in/job-listing/j?jl=1009705912414,,Software Engineer - Python (Remote),Pricelabs,Pune,2025-04-11,,,,,False,"Preferable Location(s): Pune, India \| Mumbai, India \| Bengaluru, India \| Chennai, India \| Bengaluru, India \| Panaji, India \| Delhi, India \| Hyderabad, India
Work Type: Full Time
  
About the Role:
We are looking for a Python Engineer to help us take our data visualization products (see examples here and here!) through the following several enhancements. The role will be responsible for creating and improving front\-end visualizations, understanding what the data means, and contributing to designing, building, and improving the data pipelines that feed those products.
We use Dash/Plotly for data visualization on our customer\-facing products. Dash is a very powerful platform that is quickly developing, and we want to keep up with what's possible and make the best use of it! While visualizations are the primary focus, to take ownership of some of the products, you will also be working on some backend systems (to do with business logic, scaling systems, caching, etc.). Understanding the domain (new visualizations and features) is also critical!
Visualizations:
Help the rest of the data science team productize features by developing a UI that presents the data and recommendations and lets customers play around.
Work with the customer\-facing teams (and join in their calls!) to understand customer's pain points.
Work with the design team to understand what design improvements can help.
Build and enhance internal and customer\-facing dashboards to track metrics and trends that help customers use PriceLabs more effectively.
Data \& Infrastructure:
Maintain and improve the framework that helps us embed the Dash/Plotly visualizations into our product.
Help us speed up the visualization products by improving the backend code (e.g., more efficient code or implementing systems to cache data)
About You:
Strong understanding of data visualization principles, algorithms, and data structures.
At least 3 years of programming experience in Python. Familiarity and experience with Dash/Plotly are a big plus!
Experience in front\-end web technologies (CSS, HTML, bootstrap, etc.)
Strong communication skills, including the ability and willingness to explain complicated ideas in simple terms.
Experience with relational databases and strong knowledge of SQL.
Prior experience working in a fast\-paced environment.
Desire to wear many hats.
Preferred:
Experience writing product code at a SaaS company
How to apply for this position?
Please fill out the form with the required details. If your profile is shortlisted, our team will reach out to you via email. If you don't find the emails in your inbox, please check your spam folder.
Tip: Avoid using AI\-generated responses. We want to hear from you!
About PriceLabs:
PriceLabs is a revenue management solution for the short\-term rental and hospitality industry, founded in 2014 and headquartered in Chicago, IL. Our platform helps individual hosts and hospitality professionals optimize their pricing and revenue management, adapting to changing market trends and occupancy levels.
With dynamic pricing, automation rules, and customizations, we manage pricing and minimum\-stay restrictions for any portfolio size, with prices automatically uploaded to preferred channels.
Every day, we price over 450,000\+ listings globally across 150\+ countries, offering world\-class tools like the Base Price Help and Minimum Stay Recommendation Engine.
In 2024, we scaled to;
450K\+ properties syncing daily
55K\+ customers worldwide
220\+ globally remote team
36% diversity
Industry awards won:
SaasBoomi 2021
The Shortyz 2020
The Shortyz 2023
We continue to grow exponentially backed by a strong team to take us to the next level.
Why join PriceLabs?
Work with an industry\-leading product that has thousands of customers worldwide, and our customers love the product! (NPS in the 70s, )
Work with a global team (15 countries and counting) of passionate individuals that accept open communication, empowerment, and a shared focus on customer success.
We are a freemium product, so marketing leads the charge on customer acquisition.
We are a remote\-first organization and accept work from home as the norm.
PriceLabs is an equal opportunity employer. We are committed to providing equal opportunity in all aspects of employment. We do not discriminate on the basis of race, colour, religious creed, national origin, ancestry, sex, age, veteran status, marital status or physical challenges.",,https://www.glassdoor.co.in/Overview/W-EI_IE3242222.htm,Software Engineering
