gd-1009706428897,glassdoor,https://www.glassdoor.co.in/job-listing/j?jl=1009706428897,,Software Engineer,ANZ Banking Group,Bengaluru,2025-04-11,,600000.0,990000.0,INR,False,"**Req ID:** 92419
  
**Department:** Tech Institutional Markets Domain
  
**Division:** Technology
  
**Location:** Bengaluru
  
About Us
  
  

At ANZ, we're applying new ways technology and data can be harnessed as we work towards a common goal: to improve the financial wellbeing and sustainability of our millions of customers.
  
  

Our community of over 5,000 engineers is key to making this happen, because technology underpins every part of our business \- from delivering tools, apps and services for our customers, to building a bank for the future.
  
  

About the Role
  
  

As an Automation Engineer you will design, develop, and maintain the automation test script using JavaScript \& validate the regression run in each release cycle, this role involves liaising with Quants and Business teams at early stage to plan and prepare the correct coverage of tests to validate new developments for the Sky platform (ANZ in\-house risk and pricing engine.)
  
  

Banking is changing and we’re changing with it, giving our people great opportunities to try new things, learn and grow. Whatever your role at ANZ, you’ll be building your future, while helping to build ours.
  
  

**Role Type:** Permanent
  
**Role Location:** Bengaluru
  
  

What will your day look like?
  
  

**As an Automation tester, you will:**  

Create, maintain, and execute automated test cases using JavaScript frameworks and tools.
  
  

Test web applications for functionality, performance, and cross\-browser compatibility.
  
  

Design automation frameworks for efficient testing processes
  
  

Collaborate with developers to ensure code quality and proper integration of tests.
  
  

Debug test failures and provide detailed reports on defects and issues.
  
  

Integrate test automation with CI/CD pipelines to maintain build stability.
  
  

Monitor and improve test coverage and automation efficiency.
  
  

What will you bring?
  
  

To grow and be successful in this role, you will ideally bring the following:
  
  

5\-8 years of extensive experience of working on JavaScript and related frameworks (e.g., Node.js).
  
  

5\-8 years of hands\-on experience with automation framework and libraries such as Selenium, Gauge, cucumber.
  
  

Strong understanding of web technologies, including HTML, CSS.
  
  

2\-3 years of relevant experience on API testing.
  
  

Hands\-on experience with version control systems (e.g., Git).
  
  

Must have knowledge of CI/CD pipelines and tools like Jenkins or TeamCity.
  
  

Prior experience of working on any performance testing framework tool like JMeter will be added advantage.
  
  

Nice to have working knowledge of Python.
  
  

Familiarity with cloud platforms like AWS, Azure, or GCP.
  
  

Knowledge of derivatives or capital market domain will be added advantage.
  
  

You’re not expected to have 100% of these skills. At ANZ a growth mindset is at the heart of our culture, so if you have most of these things in your toolbox, we’d love to hear from you.
  
  

So why join us?
  
  

ANZ is a place where big things happen as we work together to provide banking and financial services across more than 30 markets. With more than 7,500 people, our Bengaluru team is the bank's largest technology, data and operations centre outside Australia. In operation for over 33 years, the centre is critical in delivering the bank's strategy and making an impact for our millions of customers around the world. Our Bengaluru team not only drives the transformation initiatives of the bank, it also drives a culture that makes ANZ a great place to be. We're proud that people feel they can be themselves at ANZ and 90 percent of our people feel they belong.
  
  

We know our people need different things to be great in their role, so we offer a range of flexible working options, including hybrid work (where the role allows it). Our people also enjoy a range of benefits including access to health and wellbeing services.
  
  

We want to continue building a diverse workplace and welcome applications from everyone. Please talk to us about any adjustments you may require to our recruitment process or the role itself. If you are a candidate with a disability or access requirements, let us know how we can provide you with additional support.
  
  

/. You can apply for this role by visiting ANZ Careers and searching for reference number 92419\.
  
  

Job Posting End Date
  
  

