gd-1009705069013,glassdoor,https://www.glassdoor.co.in/job-listing/j?jl=1009705069013,,Software Development Engineer - Merchant Experiences,GoDaddy,Pune,2025-04-11,,,,,False,"* R020776
* Pune, Maharashtra, India
* Engineering
* Regular

  
**Location Details:** **Pune, India**



At GoDaddy the future of work looks different for each team. Some teams work in the office full\-time; others have a hybrid arrangement (they work remotely some days and in the office some days) and some work entirely remotely.


This is a hybrid position. You’ll divide your time between working remotely from your home and an office, so you should live within commuting distance. Hybrid teams may work in\-office as much as a few times a week or as little as once a month or quarter, as decided by leadership. The hiring manager can share more about what hybrid work might look like for this team.


**Join Our Team**



Here at GoDaddy, the **Merchant Experiences Team** exists as the cornerstone of our commitment to empowering merchants and enhancing every interaction they have with our platform. This team is tasked with orchestrating an exceptional, seamless, and consistent experience across all touch points where our tools, functionality, and features are offered enabling our customers to complete their jobs to be done (JTBD) efficiently. Through thoughtful design, insightful analytics, and close collaboration across departments, we deliver a cohesive user journey that simplifies, inspires, and supports merchants every step of the way. Our mission is to enable experiences that resonate deeply with our merchants.


**What you'll get to do**



As a Software Development Engineer, you will have the chance to create a significant impact across our various surfaces and contribute to the success of our customers. Your responsibilities will include:


* Develop new customer facing features using ReactJS, TypeScript and other front end technologies.
* Assist in improving our User surfaces by implementing innovative solutions.
* Identifying and tackling opportunities in complex systems, providing incremental business value while simplifying our platform.
* Learn and implement a high standard of software dev practices, including practical coding standards, modern software development approaches, test automation, and a strong focus on security.
* Leading and contributing to release and on\-call activities, ensuring robust support for our platform and code base.
* You will develop cloud\-native solutions to continuously harden our platform and cloud infrastructures at scale.


**Your experience should include**


* 4\+ years of software development experience with NodeJS ecosystem, React, Typescript.
* Strong proficiency in Javascript, HTML and CSS with a solid understanding of modern principles, practices and patterns for front\-end engineering.
* Experience of working with Agile teams.


**You might also have**


* Experience with Amazon Web Services (AWS), Docker, EmberJS, Testing, CICD, Git, Relational and no\-SQL Databases is a big plus.
* Experience with hosting solutions such as Managed Wordpress, WooCommerce, cPanel, Plesk, or other platforms.
* Understanding of Continuous integration (CI) and continuous delivery (CD) models.

  


