gd-1009703813236,glassdoor,https://www.glassdoor.co.in/job-listing/j?jl=1009703813236,,Software Support Engineer - Intern,DataTroops,Mohali,2025-04-10,,,,,False,"Eligibility Criteria

\- **Must pursue or have a BCA degree**  
\- **Must have very good communication skills**  
\- Good to have SQL skills  
\- Good to have any programming language knowledge

The job responsibilities in a support role typically include:

1\. **Troubleshooting**: Diagnosing and resolving technical issues reported by users or customers related to software products. This involves understanding the problem, reproducing it if necessary, and finding a solution.

2\. **Customer Support**: Providing technical assistance and guidance to customers or end\-users through various channels such as email, chat, or phone. This involves answering queries, explaining functionalities, and assisting with technical issues.

3\. **Bug Fixing**: Identifying and fixing software bugs reported by users or discovered during testing. This may involve analyzing code, debugging, and testing fixes to ensure they resolve the issue without introducing new problems.

4\. **Documentation**: Creating and maintaining documentation such as user guides, FAQs, and troubleshooting articles to help users understand and use the software effectively. This can also include updating documentation to reflect changes in software features or fixes.

5\. **Collaboration**: Working closely with other members of the development team, including senior developers and QA engineers, to address complex issues and improve the quality of the software.

6\. **Continuous Learning**: Staying up\-to\-date with new technologies, tools, and methodologies relevant to the software development and support process. This may involve self\-study, attending training sessions, or participating in workshops.

7\. **Quality Assurance**: Assisting in the testing process by conducting regression testing, verifying bug fixes, and ensuring software updates meet quality standards before release.

8\. **Feedback Collection**: Gathering feedback from users or customers about their experience with the software, including any issues encountered or suggestions for improvement. This feedback can help inform future development efforts.

9\. **Escalation Handling**: Escalating complex or critical issues to senior developers or higher\-level support personnel for further investigation and resolution when necessary.

10\. **Ad\-Hoc Tasks**: Assisting with various other tasks as needed, such as software installations, server maintenance, or data migrations, depending on the specific needs of the team or organization.

**Compensation:**

The salary for this internship position will be determined based on the candidate's experience, skills, and performance during the interview process.

Additionally, **DataTroops** offers to sponsor your **MCA (Master of Computer Applications)** degree. In exchange for the sponsorship, you will be required to sign a **3\-year bond**, committing to work with the company for a period of 3 years (including internship).

Ability to commute/relocate:  
**Mohali, Punjab:** Reliably commute or planning to relocate before starting work (Required)

Work Location: In person

Job Types: Full\-time, Fresher, Internship

Pay: ₹1\.00 per hour

Expected hours: No more than 72 per week

Work Days:

* Monday to Friday
* Weekend availability

Work Location: In person",,,Software Engineering
