* Serve as a technical consultant to assist cross\-functionally in the following areas:
	+ Cloud Technologies (AWS) \& Datacenter Architectures
	+ Networking Technologies including MPLS/VPN/SD\-WAN
	+ Voice Technologies including SIP/VoIP/IVR/ASR/TTS/SBCs
	+ Infrastructure Technologies including Physical Systems, Storage, \& Virtualization
	+ Authentication/File Transfer/Database Technologies
	+ Technical Support \& Troubleshooting
	+ Systems Administration \& Integrations
* Participate in client facing correspondence and communications on a regular basis with regards to technical discovery, informational discussions, troubleshooting sessions, and other requests as needed.

 **REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS:**  

* Ability to learn new technologies while remaining dynamic/flexible in a fast paced, changing environment.
* Strong ability to take ownership, solve problems independently, and facilitate the collaboration required to deliver on tasks as necessary.
* Place a high value on integrity, teamwork, and operational excellence.
* Understands concepts of technical integrations such as SIP trunks, SAML authentication, MPLS circuits, VPN tunnels, and other cloud/core technologies.
* Experience \- Minimum 3\-5 years of experience in the information technology field in a client facing role supporting the technical elements of enterprise solutions.
* Experience with large, complex project delivery, preferably in cloud solutions utilizing AWS, Azure, or another major cloud provider.
* Must have previous experience in one or more of the following areas: Systems Administration, Technical Support, Networking, Systems Infrastructure, Project/Operations Management, Cloud Environments, or Systems Security.
* Ability to work Out\-of\-Hours schedule as required.
  


