**About the Role**  

The Software Engineer \- II role at Hinge Health involves hands\-on experience in front\-end development using React Native and some experience in backend technologies, particularly Node.js. The role includes designing and developing front\-end applications, making changes to backend services, and integrating with third\-party technologies. This role requires collaborating with multiple stakeholders such as product managers, product designers and architects across global teams. The role also requires partnerships with staff engineers \& senior engineers to get code \& design reviews completed and also work with team members to implement solutions.

 **What You’ll Accomplish**

* Every day, you’ll work collaboratively with your teammates, product manager and engineering manager
* Every sprint, you’ll will design and run technical DnD’s, and work along with team on implementation
* Every quarter, you’ll support staff \& senior engineers with executing a significant platform\-wide upgrade or innovative change to our workflow or tooling

**Hinge Health Hybrid Model**  

We believe that remote work and in\-person work have their own advantages and disadvantages, and we want to be able to leverage the best of both worlds. Employees in hybrid roles are required to be in the office 3 days per week, for the full 8 hours of a typical business day.

  


Qualificatons:
**Basic Qualifications**

* 3\+ years of non\-internship full time professional software development experience
* 2\+ years of work experience with ReactJS framework
* 2\+ years of work experience with Node JS/ Typescript on the backend

**Preferred Qualifications**

* Bachelor’s Degree (or equivalent) in Computer Science, Engineering or related technical field
* Full stack engineer with exposure to front end technology like react
* Experience on hosting the solution on Cloud like AWS
* Exposure to work with 3rd Party technology is an added advantage

  


Company Information:
