About Us


E2logy is a leading software solutions company dedicated to empowering businesses with innovative technology and exceptional service. We combine our expertise in various domains with cutting\-edge development practices to deliver high\-quality, custom software solutions that cater to your unique needs and goals.  

Visit our website: https://e2logy.com/ to learn more about our services and expertise.  

Job Description


**Job Overview :**  

  

The PHP Associate Software Engineer will assist in developing and maintaining web applications using PHP. This entry\-level position is ideal for a recent graduate or someone with limited experience, eager to build a career in software development. The candidate will work under the guidance of senior developers and have the opportunity to learn and grow in a collaborative environment.  

  

**Responsibility:*** Assist in developing, testing, and maintaining web applications using PHP.
* Collaborate with cross\-functional team members to implement new features and resolve issues.
* Participate in code reviews to learn best practices and improve coding skills.
* Debug and troubleshoot basic technical issues with the support of senior developers.
* Contribute to the optimization of applications for speed and scalability.
* Stay updated on emerging technologies and industry trends to enhance learning and skill development.
* Support the development team in various stages of the software development lifecycle.
* Document\-oriented development process.
* Understanding modular programming techniques.
* Follow our company’s core values: Deliver what was asked, Deliver on time, Deliver in budget, Deliver with quality, Deliver great experience.

  

Requirements

 **Qualifications:**

* Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Information Technology, or a related field (or equivalent experience).
* Basic understanding of PHP and its frameworks (such as Laravel, CodeIgniter).
* Familiarity with front\-end technologies such as HTML, CSS, and JavaScript.
* Exposure to database systems like MySQL or PostgreSQL.
* Willingness to learn version control systems, especially Git.
* Basic problem\-solving skills and a keen attention to detail.
* Strong willingness to learn and adapt in a team environment.

 **Preferred Skills:**

* Understanding of RESTful APIs and third\-party integrations.
* Knowledge of basic web security principles and performance optimization.
* Familiarity with Agile/Scrum methodologies is a plus.

  

Benefits

* Competitive entry\-level salary and performance\-based bonuses.
* Health insurance and other employee benefits.
* Opportunities for professional development and career growth.

**Schedule:**  

* Day shift
* Monday to Friday

**Work Environment:**  

* Collaborative office setting with guidance from senior developers.
* Remote or hybrid work arrangements may be available.
* Occasional additional hours may be required to meet project deadlines.

**Application Process:**  

* Submit your resume, cover letter, and optionally a portfolio of academic projects or personal work to careers@e2logy.com",,https://www.glassdoor.co.in/Overview/W-EI_IE784821.htm,Software Engineering
gd-1009691015903,glassdoor,https://www.glassdoor.co.in/job-listing/j?jl=1009691015903,,Senior HTML-CSS Developer,Tarini Consulting,,2025-04-01,,,,,True,"**About us**

We are Digital Transformation Consultants specializing in Sales Pipeline Automation, Zoho CRM, Helpdesk Setup, Chatbot Setup, and Zoho Creator.

This is a remote position.

**Job Details**

* **Job Title:** Senior HTML/CSS Developer
* **Job Location:** Remote
* **Working Hours:** 4 PM to 1 AM IST (Indian Standard Time)
* **Important Note:** The company will not provide a laptop during the probation period. Candidates must have their own device to perform their duties effectively.

**Who We’re Looking For**

We’re searching for a highly skilled and passionate Senior HTML/CSS Developer with **7\+ years of front\-end development experience**, including extensive expertise in **HTML5, CSS3 and JavaScript**. The ideal candidate will have a strong portfolio showcasing their ability to create responsive, cross\-browser compatible, and accessible web designs. If you thrive in a collaborative, fast\-paced environment and are committed to delivering pixel\-perfect, user\-friendly interfaces, this role is perfect for you!

**Key Responsibilities**

As a Senior HTML/CSS Developer, you’ll be responsible for shaping the front\-end of our web applications and ensuring they meet the highest standards of quality and performance. Your key duties will include:

* Writing clean, semantic, and well\-structured **HTML5,** **CSS3** **and JavaScript** code to build responsive and accessible web pages.
* Ensuring **cross\-browser compatibility** and optimizing web pages for speed, scalability, and SEO best practices.
* Collaborating with designers to translate UI/UX wireframes and mockups into fully functional, pixel\-perfect web interfaces.
* Implementing **responsive design principles** to ensure seamless experiences across devices (desktop, tablet, mobile).
* Working closely with back\-end developers to integrate front\-end code with server\-side logic and APIs.
* Mentoring junior developers and conducting code reviews to maintain high standards of code quality.
* Staying up\-to\-date with the latest front\-end trends, tools, and best practices to continuously improve our development processes.

**Requirements**

To excel in this role, you’ll need a strong technical foundation, leadership capabilities, and a proven track record. We’re looking for candidates with:

* **7\-8 years of front\-end development experience**, with a focus on **HTML5 and CSS3 and JavaScript**.
* Expertise in **responsive design**, including media queries, flexbox, and grid layouts.
* Proficiency with CSS preprocessors such as **SASS** or **LESS**.
* Strong understanding of **cross\-browser compatibility** issues and solutions.
* Experience with **accessibility standards** (WCAG) to ensure inclusive web experiences.
* A **strong portfolio** showcasing your ability to create visually appealing, user\-friendly web interfaces and lead successful projects.
* Proficiency with **JavaScript** and experience with front\-end frameworks such as **React**, **Angular**, or **Vue.js**.
* Familiarity with version control systems like **Git**.
* Excellent **problem\-solving skills** and meticulous attention to detail.
* Proven ability to **mentor and guide junior developers**.
* Ability to work independently and collaboratively in a remote team environment.
* Fluency in English for effective communication in a global setting.

**Preferred Skills (Nice\-to\-Have)**

While not required, the following skills will make you stand out:

* Experience with **CSS\-in\-JS** solutions or CSS modules.
* Familiarity with front\-end build tools like **Webpack**, **Gulp**, or **Parcel**.
* Understanding of **SEO best practices** for front\-end development.
* Exposure to **UI/UX design principles** and tools like Figma or Sketch.
* Experience with **agile methodologies** and project management tools (e.g., Jira, Trello).

**Benefits**

* Competitive salary.
* Opportunities for career growth and skill development.
* A collaborative, dynamic, and supportive work environment.
* Remote and Flexible work timings to support work\-life balance.

