Job Title: Azure Devops engineer/SSE  

Position: Azure Devops engineer/SSE  

Experience: 4\-6 Yrs.  

Category: Software Development/ Engineering  

Main location: India \- Bangalore, Hyderabad, Chennai,
  

Position ID: J0225\-1714  

Employment Type: Full Time  

Work Type: Hybrid  

  

We are seeking a skilled Azure DevOps Engineer with strong experience in Azure Kubernetes Service (AKS) and Kubernetes to join our cloud infrastructure and deployment team. The ideal candidate will be responsible for building and managing scalable, secure, and automated CI/CD pipelines to support the deployment of containerized applications in cloud environments.

**Your future duties and responsibilities**


Key Responsibilities:  

Design and implement CI/CD pipelines using Azure DevOps (YAML pipelines preferred) for microservices\-based applications.  

  

Deploy, manage, and monitor applications in AKS (Azure Kubernetes Service).  

  

Create and maintain Helm charts or Kubernetes manifests for application deployment.  

  

Automate infrastructure provisioning using ARM templates, Bicep, or Terraform.  

  

Collaborate with development and operations teams to ensure smooth deployments and reliable releases.  

  

Configure and manage Kubernetes resources such as pods, deployments, services, ingress, and config maps.  

  

Monitor system health, availability, and performance using Azure Monitor, Log Analytics, or Prometheus/Grafana.  

  

Manage secrets and credentials using Azure Key Vault and Kubernetes secrets.  

  

Ensure security best practices across build, release, and runtime environments.  

  

Troubleshoot and resolve deployment and environment issues quickly and effectively.

**Required qualifications to be successful in this role**


Required Skills \& Experience:  

Proven experience with Azure DevOps (Repos, Pipelines, Artifacts).  

  

Strong hands\-on experience with AKS and Kubernetes (kubectl, Helm, etc.).  

  

Solid understanding of containerization with Docker and microservices architecture.  

  

Proficient in scripting (Bash, PowerShell, or Python).  

  

Experience with Infrastructure as Code (IaC) tools like Terraform or ARM templates.  

  

Good understanding of networking and security in cloud\-native applications.  

  

Familiarity with Git for source control.  

  

Experience with monitoring and logging tools in cloud environments.  

  

Excellent problem\-solving skills and a strong team player.

