**POSITION PURPOSE**
--------------------


LINK is a Performance Management control tool housed within the Performance Management area of Fresh the IT team responsible for Group level Finance systems. It is used for budget actuals monitoring and the generation of invoices / costs based on those actuals and is based on a service\-oriented software architecture (SOA).

* It uses the link between operational activities and budget made in LINK.
* Builds the corresponding WBS for ONE CAPP (Invoicing / approval of invoices)
* It checks whether the item already exists in the ONE CAPP Repository


The team is composed of a business analyst and two Full Stack developers in Paris.


The main role of the developer will be to rewrite the code in java 11 and spring\-boot and integration with the application’s front\-end. Maintain application integrity and update. Manage application obsolescence, HTTPS certificates, migration of environments, Provide technical user support with production and functional with LINK application users.

**Responsibilities**

**DIRECT RESPONSIBILITIES**
---------------------------

* Propose technical solutions adapted to the business needs (Contribute to technical requirements writings)
* Report to steering team on a regular basis (Roadmap follow\-up, incident/bugs tracking, budget consumption.)
* Analyze and interpret requirement specifications received from analyst.
* Liaise with analyst and other stakeholders to ensure correct understanding and implementation of specifications.
* Design and develop IT solutions based on the specifications received.
* Work closely in a “one team” approach with all stakeholders during all phases of the project, jointly providing high quality deliverables.
* Participate in the testing phases (system, user acceptance, regression…) as required while coordinating with BA.
* Provide support to operations from a technical perspective.

**CONTRIBUTING RESPONSIBILITIES**
---------------------------------


Contribute to overall FRESH and ISPL Vision goals as directed by Team and Department Management.

