* Drive the implementation of best practices into the automation to make it highly stable, discovers defects, requires low maintenance and runs swiftly and selectively.
* Manage and participate in hands\-on testing and test automation to identify, document, and resolve system defects.
* Stay up\-to\-date with the latest QA methodologies, tools, and best practices to continually improve the QA function.
* Effectively communicate with project leaders and Engineering management regarding the scope and limits of testing and analysis efforts


What you’ll bring:

* Master's degree in Computer Science, Software Engineering or related field is preferred
* Must have 5\+ yrs. of experience in TOSCA Automation
* Must have 2\+ years experience in any open source tools ( Senilum, Robot Framework,cypress etc)
