in-2692867de889d3bf,indeed,https://in.indeed.com/viewjob?jk=2692867de889d3bf,https://ncratleos.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/en-US/ext_apacatleos/job/MUMBAI-IND/Cloud-Network-Operations-Engineer_R1146524-4,Cloud Network Operations Engineer,NCR Atleos,"MH, IN",2025-04-11,fulltime,,,,False,"About NCR Atleos
NCR Atleos, headquartered in Atlanta, is a leader in expanding financial access. Our dedicated 20,000 employees optimize the branch, improve operational efficiency and maximize self\-service availability for financial institutions and retailers across the globe.
Job Title: Cloud Network Operations Engineer
Location: Mumbai
Grade: 10
Job Overview:
We are seeking a Cloud Network Operations Engineer. The ideal candidate will understand multi\-cloud environments, primarily with AWS and Azure, and have some experience with other cloud providers such as OCI (Oracle Cloud Infrastructure) and Equinix cloud infrastructure as a plus. You will be responsible for managing cloud networking infrastructure, primarily focusing on firewall security, scalability, and network performance. Expertise in Azure services required including Virtual WAN (vWAN), Network Security Groups (NSG) firewalls, and cloud\-based routing, transit gateways and native Load balancing is essential. Experience with virtual firewalls such as Palo Alto or Fortigate a plus.
Key Responsibilities:* Implementation:
	+ Manage cloud solutions primarily on Azure and AWS. Knowledge of Google Cloud, Equinix and OCI platform experience a plus.
	+ Understanding how to connect Cloud infrastructure to legacy on\-prem data centers.
	+ Develop and implement complex cloud environments, focusing on infrastructure as code (IaC) using tools like Terraform, ARM templates, or CloudFormation.
	+ Configure and optimize Azure Virtual WAN (vWAN) for global connectivity.
	+ Understand how to setup and configure Express Routes to on\-Prem and other cloud solutions.
* Security and Compliance:
	+ Implement and manage Network Security Groups (NSG), firewalls, and other security mechanisms to protect cloud environments.
	+ Ensure cloud infrastructure meets compliance and security standards, conducting regular audits and assessments.
	+ Knowledge of Virtual firewalls such as Palo Alto or Fortigate a plus
* Networking and Routing:
	+ Manage cloud networking components, including VPCs, subnets, and routing tables.
	+ Configure and maintain routing protocols and ensure efficient traffic flow between on\-premises and cloud environments.
	+ Understanding cloud native load balancing in Azure, AWS and OCI
	+ Knowledge of Virtual Load Balancers such as F5 a plus
* Collaboration and Support:
	+ Work closely with Network engineering teams and development teams to ensure smooth deployment of applications and services.
	+ Provide ongoing support and troubleshooting for cloud security and infrastructure issues.


Qualifications:* Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Information Technology, or a related field.
* 3\+ years of experience as a Cloud Security Engineer or in a similar role.
* Strong expertise in Azure, including Virtual WAN (vWAN), Network Security Groups (NSG), and other core services.
* Proficiency in Azure, AWS and Equinix, with a solid understanding of cloud networking, load balancing, security, and firewall management.
* Hands\-on experience with cloud routing, firewalls, and VPNs.
* Strong problem\-solving skills, with a focus on cloud network security, performance, and reliability.
* Excellent communication and teamwork abilities.


Offers of employment are conditional upon passage of screening criteria applicable to the job.
