Summary: As a Software Development Lead, you will be responsible for developing and configuring software systems, applying knowledge of technologies, methodologies, and tools to support projects or clients throughout the product lifecycle. Roles \& Responsibilities: \- Test Strategy \& Architecture: Design and implement a comprehensive system test strategy for connected vehicle solutions, covering functional, security, performance, and end\-to\-end validation. \- Test Framework Development: Develop and enhance test automation frameworks, simulation environments, and cloud\-based validation platforms for connected car systems. \- System Validation \& Compliance: Ensure adherence to ISO 26262, ASPICE, ISO 21434 (Cybersecurity), UNECE WP.29, and AUTOSAR for connected vehicle security and safety. \- Connected Car Feature Testing: Lead validation of OTA (Over\-the\-Air) updates, V2X communication, telematics, infotainment, cybersecurity, and data analytics. \- Cloud \& IoT Testing: Validate cloud\-based vehicle connectivity, data streaming, and backend integration with platforms like AWS, Azure, and Google Cloud. \- Cross\-functional Collaboration: Work closely with software, hardware, security, and DevOps teams to align test requirements and resolve system issues. \- Test Execution \& Reporting: Oversee test execution, issue tracking, root cause analysis, and test reporting, ensuring continuous improvement in system validation. \- Supplier \& Toolchain Management: Evaluate and integrate third\-party testing tools, connectivity solutions, and network simulators for comprehensive validation. \- Team Leadership: Mentor and lead a team of system test engineers, fostering a culture of innovation, automation, and best practices in connected car testing. Professional \& Technical Skills: \- Bachelor’s or Master’s degree in Electrical Engineering, Computer Science, Automotive Engineering, or a related field. \- 12\+ years of experience in system testing, validation, and verification of connected vehicle services, telematics, or infotainment systems. \- Strong expertise in V2X, 5G, LTE, Wi\-Fi, Bluetooth, GNSS, and IoT protocols. \- Hands\-on experience with test automation frameworks, cloud\-based validation, and vehicle network simulation. \- Proficiency in Python, C\+\+, or Java for test automation and scripting. \- Knowledge of AUTOSAR, MQTT, REST APIs, CAN, Ethernet, and TCP/IP protocols. \- Experience with cybersecurity testing for connected vehicles and compliance with ISO 21434 \& UNECE WP.29\. \- Familiarity with Over\-the\-Air (OTA) updates, backend integration, and data security protocols. \- Strong problem\-solving and analytical skills with a deep understanding of cloud\-based automotive platforms. Preferred Certifications: \- ISTQB Advanced Level – Test Manager or equivalent certification. \- AWS, Azure, or Google Cloud Certification for cloud\-based validation expertise. Additional Information: \- The candidate should have a minimum of 12 years of experience in Automotive Mobility Services \& Connected Vehicles. \- This position is based at our Bengaluru office. \- A 15 years full time education is required.


  

