### **About Us**


**The Modern Story**  

It has become imperative for enterprises to derive value from their data. Unfortunately, today’s data landscape is increasingly varied and constantly changing. The rise of IoT, unstructured data volume, and need for data analytics from all departments emphasize the need for a composable data management solution.  

The Modern Data Company was founded to radically simplify how organizations manage, access, and interact with data. Modern’s data operating system, DataOS, unifies all data across silos, at scale. The composable layers of DataOS evolve with your existing technology stack to future\-proof all data initiatives.  

### **Job Description**


We are seeking **DevOps Engineers** to be at the forefront of our Cloud \& DevOps practice, driving the deployment and operations of **DataOS**, Modern’s flagship product. As a key member of the DevOps team, you will collaborate closely with **Engineering, Product, and our customers** to ensure seamless deployments, reliability, and scalability. You will play a critical role in troubleshooting, resolving issues, and optimizing **DataOS** upgrades while fostering strong customer relationships.

 **Key Responsibilities**

  

* Work closely with customers and implement solutions/product deployment
* Define and lead cloud strategies while building strong relationships with key technical stakeholders.
* Collaborate with Product and Engineering teams to understand product architecture and deployment methodologies.
* Troubleshoot and resolve complex issues related to cloud infrastructure, networking, and application deployments.
* Ensure high availability, disaster recovery, and backup strategies for cloud\-based applications.
* Design and implement robust monitoring systems using observability tools to track performance, detect anomalies, and proactively resolve potential issues.

### **Requirements**

* At least 3\+ years of strong DevOps and Infrastructure as Code experience.
* Excellent communication skills and ability to drive solutions/products deployment and related activities on customer’s environment
* Multiple cloud platform experience; AWS, Microsoft Azure, and Google.
* Candidate must have very strong experience in Terraform, used modules, locals, worked in various versions of Terraform and knows the latest and greatest features available.
* Hands\-on expertise in **Kubernetes** is essential, including proficiency in using **kubectl** for deployment management, troubleshooting, and debugging.
* Good knowledge of Containerization technologies (Docker with CLI, Kubernetes including setting up of resources such as Services, Pods, ConfigMaps, Secrets, Ingress etc.).
* Have understanding of modern application development practices and tools such CI/CD and related technology.
* Experience in at least one of Puppet, Ansible, or other automation platforms is a preferred
* Expertise in programming languages such as Python or Golang is a plus

### **Benefits**

**Working at Modern**

  

First and foremost, our value system is sacred to us – HEAT: Humility, Empathy, Accountability and Transparency. Beyond this, we are fond of individuals who are curious, love solving problems and can see the larger picture. We love to take a leap of faith on potential. If you believe you haven’t had the chance to do your life’s best work, Modern is the place for you.

  

Modern embraces competition for great talent. We have been able to get great talent onboard owing to the attractive compensation and benefits we provide, in addition to the upside we share with all our employees in the form of ESOPs. Moreover, our ESOP policies are highly employee\-friendly replicating ethos of some of the best Silicon Valley tech startups. We are committed to making sure our employees create significant value for themselves.",,https://in.indeed.com/cmp/The-Modern-Data-Company-1,Software Engineering
