in-a92481f11b1e1d32,indeed,https://in.indeed.com/viewjob?jk=a92481f11b1e1d32,https://you.bamboohr.com/careers/383?source=indeed&src=indeed&postedDate=2025-04-11,Senior DevOps Engineer,You Technologies Group,"TN, IN",2025-04-11,fulltime,,,,False,"**We Are**



YouTrip is at the forefront of Asia's financial revolution, defining the future of digital finance with its leading multi\-currency payment platform. Launched in 2018, YouTrip has swiftly ascended as a powerhouse, orchestrating billions in transactions annually and securing the trust of millions. With innovative solutions like YouTrip for consumers and YouBiz for businesses, we offer unmatched financial ease and cost\-effectiveness. Fresh off a successful US$50 million Series B funding round led by Lightspeed Venture, we're setting new benchmarks in the digital financial services sector.

  

At the heart of our mission is a commitment to eliminate financial borders across Asia, propelling us into the next wave of digital finance.



Job Description: Senior DevOps Engineer



As a DevOps Engineer, you will be responsible for bridging the gap between development and our AWS based infrastructure, ensuring the seamless integration of these two critical functions. Your role is pivotal in enhancing our software delivery processes and maintaining a reliable infrastructure. You will work at the intersection of technology, collaborating with development teams to streamline the deployment, delivery, and management of software products. Your contributions will directly impact our ability to deliver high\-quality software to our users efficiently.



Responsibilities:


* Design, implement, and maintain cloud infrastructure solutions on AWS, leveraging best practices for scalability, reliability, and security.
* Lead the adoption and implementation of AWS services and features to optimize infrastructure performance, cost efficiency, and operational excellence.
* Configure and manage AWS services such as EC2, S3, RDS, Lambda, ECS, and EKS to support the deployment and operation of containerized applications and microservices.
* Develop and maintain infrastructure as code (IaC) using tools such Terraform to provision and manage AWS resources in a repeatable and automated manner.
* Implement monitoring, logging, and alerting solutions to ensure the health and performance of cloud\-based applications and services.
* Collaborate with development teams to optimize application architecture and performance for cloud environments, providing guidance on cloud\-native design principles and best practices.
* Lead incident response and troubleshooting efforts for AWS infrastructure and services, identifying root causes and implementing preventive measures to minimize downtime and impact on operations.
* Mentor and coach junior DevOps engineers, sharing knowledge and expertise in AWS technologies, DevOps methodologies, and cloud architecture principles.
* Stay current with AWS services, features, and updates, evaluating new technologies and tools to drive innovation and improve operational efficiency.


Requirements:


* Minimum of 5 years of experience in a DevOps/Cloud Engineering, with at least 3 years of hands on experience designing, deploying and managing AWS based infrastructure
* AWS Certification such as AWS Certified DevOps Engineer, AWS Certified Solutions Architect or AWS Certified SysOps Administrator would be an added advantage
* Experience with CI/CD tools such as Jenkins, CircleCI, or GitLab CI/CD.
* Proficiency in infrastructure provisioning tools like **Terraform**.
* Deep knowledge of AWS services including EC2, S3, RDS, Lambda, ECS, EKS, VPC, IAM, CloudWatch, and CloudTrail.
* Proven track record of leading technical projects, mentoring junior team members, and driving initiatives to successful completion.
* Ability to thrive in a fast\-paced, agile environment, with a passion for learning and staying current with emerging technologies and best practices in cloud computing and DevOps.
* Strong commitment to security best practices and compliance standards, with experience implementing and maintaining security controls in AWS environments.",,https://in.indeed.com/cmp/You-Technologies-Group,Software Engineering
in-26525db6d8f4af25,indeed,https://in.indeed.com/viewjob?jk=26525db6d8f4af25,http://in.indeed.com/job/erp-software-developer-26525db6d8f4af25,ERP Software Developer,Hawkerlab Softech Pvt Ltd.,"UP, IN",2025-04-11,fulltime,,,,False,"**Role : ERP \& Inventory Systems Specialist \& Software Engineer** 

**Key Technologies:** Node.js, Firestore, GCP (Cloud Storage), Inventory \& ERP Systems knowledge

**Experience Required:** 5\+ years

**Food industry knowledge is mandatory.**

**What You’ll Do:**

● Design ERP and inventory management modules tailored to food manufacturers.

● Bring lessons learned from prior experience building ERP/inventory systems to help us avoid common pitfalls.

● Collaborate with the founding team to turn supply chain complexity into intuitive, streamlined digital experiences.

● Help build features like stock management, production forecasting, sales forecasting and traceability.

● Bring clarity and structure to how profitability, COGS, and sustainability metrics interact with real\-world operations.

**What We’re Looking For:**

● Deep understanding of how inventory and ERP systems operate in practice.

● Eager to apply past learnings but curious enough to explore new approaches.

