 **Role Summary**


We are hiring a Frontend Developer to help us in the build our platforms within the Delta Capita which supports top\-tier investment banks and financial services firms.


The future\-state platform build and deploy will be the major part of their role. But we would welcome the Frontend Developer to be involved when clients have incidents expecting this individual to want to be an active part of trouble\-shooting incidents, as much as being a part of the DC developer community.

**Role and Responsibilities:**


As a Frontend Developer, you will be responsible for developing and maintaining our Angular application platforms. You will work closely with our backend developers and designers to create a seamless and engaging user experience.

  

Develop and maintain Angular applications using JavaScript/TypeScript.


Collaborate with backend developers to integrate APIs and services.


Ensure the technical feasibility of UI/UX designs.


Optimize applications for maximum speed and scalability.


Write clean, maintainable, and efficient code.


Participate in code reviews and provide constructive feedback.


Troubleshoot and debug applications.


Stay up\-to\-date with the latest industry trends and technologies.

 **Essential Skills \& Experience:**

 **Proven experience as a Frontend Developer of 5 \+ years**


Strong proficiency in **Angular and JavaScript/TypeScript.**


Strong proficiency with HTML5, CSS3, and responsive design principles.


Understanding of cross\-browser compatibility issues and ways to work around them.


Experience with version control systems (e.g., Git).


Excellent problem\-solving skills and attention to detail.


Ability to work independently and as part of a team.


Strong communication skills.


Secure Coding Practices


Pipeline delivery tools / Continuous Integration frameworks


Agile/Scrum concepts

 **Desirable Skills \& Experience:**

  

AWS experience


AWS Lambda experience


AWS Tooling


S3 experience


Familiarity with any of the following MySQL, Python, Kotlin, and Java.


Experience working in Consulting Businesses


Experience working with Investment Banks

 **How We Work:**


Delta Capita is an equal opportunity employer. We positively encourage applications from suitably qualified and eligible candidates regardless of age, colour, disability, national origin, ancestry, race, religion, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity and/or expression, veteran status, genetic information, or any other status protected by applicable law.  

  

We will ensure that individuals with disabilities are provided reasonable accommodation to participate in the job application or interview process, to perform essential job functions, and to receive other benefits and privileges of employment. If you require any reasonable adjustments through your interview process, please use the designated space within the application questionnaire.


This is a permanent full\-time position located in Pune. As the selection and interview process is ongoing, please submit your application in English as soon as possible, if your profile is selected, a member of our team will contact you within 4 weeks.

 **Who Are We:**


Delta Capita Group (a member of the Prytek Group) is a global managed services, consulting, and solutions provider with a unique combination of experience in Financial Services and technology innovation capability. Our mission is to reinvent the financial services value chain providing technology based mutualized services for financial institutions for non\-differentiating services.

 **Our 3 offerings are:**

* Managed Services
* Consulting \& Solutions
* Technology

  

