At Synopsys, we drive the innovations that shape the way we live and connect. Our technology is central to the Era of Pervasive Intelligence, from self\-driving cars to learning machines. We lead in chip design, verification, and IP integration, empowering the creation of high\-performance silicon chips and software content. Join us to transform the future through continuous technological innovation.

### **You Are:**


You are a highly passionate technical engineer with 2\-3 years of object\-oriented programming experience. You are driven by the desire to innovate and solve complex problems. You possess a strong foundation in programming with expertise in C\#, .NET Framework, and WPF. Your understanding of data structures and algorithms allows you to develop robust and efficient solutions. You have a keen interest in power electronics and are excited about the opportunity to work on high\-precision virtual prototyping tools. You are a team player, capable of working collaboratively with application engineers to enhance and maintain user experiences. Your attention to detail ensures that customer requirements are meticulously addressed, and you are adept at implementing regression test cases to ensure software reliability.

### **What You’ll Be Doing:**

* Developing, implementing, and testing user experiences for high\-precision virtual prototyping tools.
* Collaborating with application engineers to enhance existing user experiences and develop new ones.
* Designing and implementing solutions to address customer requirements and issues.
* Adding regression test cases to ensure software reliability and performance.
* Conducting what\-if studies and generating best and worst\-case results for power electronics simulations.
* Staying up\-to\-date with the latest advancements in power electronics and software development.

### **The Impact You Will Have:**

* Enhancing the user experience of Synopsys' virtual prototyping tools, making them more intuitive and efficient.
* Accelerating the validation of software\-defined vehicles through advanced simulation technologies.
* Contributing to the reduction of project schedules for customers, enhancing their productivity.
* Driving innovation in the field of power electronics through high\-precision simulations.
* Ensuring the reliability and performance of Synopsys' software solutions through rigorous testing.
* Supporting the development of cutting\-edge technologies that shape the future of smart systems.

### **What You’ll Need:**

* Bachelor's degree in Computer Science or a related field.
* Strong programming skills in C\#, .NET Framework, and WPF.
* In\-depth knowledge of data structures and algorithms.
* Experience with object\-oriented programming concepts.
* Interest or knowledge in power electronics.

### **Who You Are:**

* Collaborative team player with excellent communication skills.
* Detail\-oriented with a strong problem\-solving mindset.
* Adaptable and eager to learn new technologies and concepts.
* Proactive in addressing customer requirements and issues.
* Innovative thinker with a passion for technology and development.

### **The Team You’ll Be A Part Of:**


Our Technology and Product Development Group (TPG) is all about enabling our customers to adopt a software\-first approach to building and testing high\-performance embedded systems. We’re the world’s leading provider of solutions to accelerate software\-defined vehicle (SDV) validation through Synopsys virtual prototyping and electronic digital twins technologies, eliminating months off customers’ project schedules.

### **Rewards and Benefits:**


We offer a comprehensive range of health, wellness, and financial benefits to cater to your needs. Our total rewards include both monetary and non\-monetary offerings. Your recruiter will provide more details about the salary range and benefits during the hiring process.",,https://in.indeed.com/cmp/Synopsys,Software Engineering
