The Delivery Head is responsible to lead Awign Staffing division and manage the end\-to\-end recruitment delivery process, ensuring client expectations are met or exceeded, and leading a team of recruiters and account managers. This role requires a strategic mindset to drive operational efficiency, client satisfaction, and profitability within the staffing division. The Delivery Head works closely with clients, vendors, and internal teams to deliver high\-quality staffing solutions across various industries and roles.
  
* Develop and implement delivery strategies that align with company goals and client expectations.
* Forecast recruitment needs based on client pipelines and manage resources accordingly.
* Monitor market trends to adapt delivery processes, ensuring competitiveness and relevance.
* Lead and mentor a team of recruiters, delivery managers, and account managers.
* Set and review KPIs for the team, ensuring high performance and productivity.
* Build and maintain strong relationships with key clients, acting as the primary point of contact for escalations and service reviews.
* Conduct regular client meetings to review progress, address challenges, and identify future needs.
* Ensure client satisfaction by delivering quality candidates within agreed timelines.
* Oversee the full recruitment lifecycle, from sourcing and screening to offer management and onboarding.
* Establish and maintain efficient processes for candidate management, interview coordination, and feedback.
* Ensure adherence to service level agreements (SLAs) and client requirements for every placement.
* Track and report delivery metrics, such as time\-to\-fill, quality of hire, and retention rates.
* Analyze delivery data to identify bottlenecks and areas for improvement.
* Provide regular updates to senior management on delivery performance and client satisfaction.
* Continuously improve recruitment processes to reduce costs, improve efficiency, and enhance candidate quality.
* Work with technology and operations teams to implement recruitment tools and automation solutions.
* Maintain compliance with relevant legal and regulatory standards in staffing.

Manage budgets and P \& L for the delivery team, optimizing resources to meet financial targets.* Collaborate with finance and sales to maximize profitability on each account.
* Identify opportunities for upselling or expanding services within existing accounts.


  
* 10 to 15 years of experience in IT staffing with a proven track record in a leadership role. 5 years of minimum experience in a leadership role.
* Deep understanding of the IT staffing industry, including trends, challenges, and best practices.
* Superior consulting, leadership, management, interpersonal, and mentoring skills
* Strong client management skills, with experience handling complex accounts and escalations.
* Exceptional leadership and team management abilities.
* Analytical mindset, with proficiency in data analysis and performance tracking.
* Process improvement/continuous improvement or project management skills
* Ability to work in complex environments and deal with ambiguity, uncertainty and challenges
* Should have commercial acumen and client focus
* Excellent verbal and written communication skills.
* Bachelor’s degree in business or a related field; MBA or other advanced degree preferred.
* Knowledge of compliance and legal aspects related to staffing and recruitment.
* Proven project management skills with a focus on process improvement.",,https://www.glassdoor.co.in/Overview/W-EI_IE1694424.htm,Information Technology
