gd-1009707346924,glassdoor,https://www.glassdoor.co.in/job-listing/j?jl=1009707346924,,IT Specialist,DSV,Hyderābād,2025-04-12,,1000000.0,1000000.0,INR,False,"If you are a current DSV employee and interested in a position in another country, please contact your Human Resource representative to discuss the process and requirements of applying.


Job Req Number: 92984  

Time Type: Full Time



Are you ready to develop your career in a rapidly growing and successful global company acting in a fast\-paced role?


If you are someone looking for a position that challenges and inspire you in a successful international company, **DSV is your place**.


The DSV group, headquartered in Denmark, is one of the biggest transports and logistics companies in the world, with more than 46,000 dedicated employees, operating in more than 90 countries. You will join a global and determined group driven forward by the desire to grow and will be part of a dynamic group, which is characterized by high level professionalization and constant improvement.

  


**An international team of specialists**


Join Commercial Applications \& Integration team in DSV Global IT Commercial Applications \& Integrations. Your team members, located across the globe, stand ready to assist with any technical challenges that may arise and act as a sounding board in your day\-to\-day work.  



Together, our mission is to build and maintain microservices on Hybrid Computing Platform and to ensure that the current integration platform is stable, robust and that all solutions are of high enterprise quality.  



**Essential Responsibilities:**


* 5\-8 years of experience with Test Management and Automation testing – UI and API automation
* Plan, track and estimate product Test activities.
* Working experience in developing test plans, test metrics, reports, and results in JIRA.
* Passionate about automated testing: Manage / drive testing \- unit tests, system tests, regression.
* Provide technical guidance as well hands on management for all product life cycle.
* Hands\-on on implementing Quality Gates
* Understand user stories/requirements, application, test automation requirements and translate to design and implementation of framework tests.
* Expert in at least one test management tool such as JIRA, Xray, HP ALM, TestRail, Zephyr etc.
* Expert in version control tools such as Git/TFS and CI/CD tools such as Jenkins, Bamboo
* Collaborate with cross\-functional team members business analysts, developers and management to build and refine test cases.
* Experience working in Scrum\-based Agile teams
* Take initiatives to train and mentor associates.
* Ability to ramp up quickly in a new environment and work independently with minimum help.
* Proactively raise, suggest, and discuss improvement areas and issues related to people,


processes, technology, quality and delivery with group manager and higher management.

  


**Technical Skills:**


* Any Programming Language – Java / Python / C\+\+/ .Net
* Automation Testing – Selenium / UiPath / Test Complete
* Database hands on – Oracle / SQL
* Any test management tool such as JIRA, Xray, HP ALM, TestRail, Zephyr
* Version control tools \- Git/TFS and CI/CD tools such as Jenkins, Bamboo


**Behaviour Skills:**


* Effective communication skills in English.
* Must be able to work in a dynamic team environment with minimal supervision and possess good organizational skills
* Excellent team management skills \& collaboration skills.
* Proactive, Good Team player and being able to work independently.
* Strong analytical skills and Self\-motivated and enthusiastic.

  




**Good to have:**


* Experience in the logistics industry and supply chain management
* Well versed in Customer facing experience
* Experience in IT Test Management to ensure practical understanding of approach, issues, and risks

  




**We offer you:**


The opportunity to expand your experience in a truly international, world\-class company whose philosophy is that your everyday work should be both varied and full of professional challenges, with wide opportunities for constant professional and personal development.

  


**Additionally, we offer the following:**


* Medical Insurance including family and Parents up to 10 Lakh INR per year.
* 2\.5 days earned leave per month which is 30 days in a calendar year.
* 10 days sick leave per calendar year.
* 1\-day Work from home per calendar Month.
* Free parking for 4\-wheeler or 2\-wheeler vehicle.
* Flexible working hours between 9:00 AM to 6:30 PM IST Monday to Friday. Employees can choose the work time either 9:00 AM to 5:30 PM or 9:30 AM to 6:00 PM IST.
* Personal Mobile and Internet expenses reimbursed per calendar month subject to maximum cap.

  


**Location:**


* Hyderabad (India)

  




**DSV – Global Transport and Logistics**


DSV is a dynamic workplace that fosters inclusivity and diversity. We conduct our business with integrity, respecting different cultures and the dignity and rights of individuals. When you join DSV, you are working for one of the very best performing companies in the transport and logistics industry. You’ll join a talented team of approximately 75,000 employees in over 80 countries, working passionately to deliver great customer experiences and high\-quality services. DSV aspires to lead the way towards a more sustainable future for our industry and are committed to trading on nature’s terms.


We promote collaboration and transparency and strive to attract, motivate and retain talented people in a culture of respect. If you are driven, talented and wish to be part of a progressive and versatile organisation, we’ll support you and your need to achieve your potential and forward your career.


