gd-1009698665543,glassdoor,https://www.glassdoor.co.in/job-listing/j?jl=1009698665543,,IT Business Analyst,Nestlé IT,Bengaluru,2025-04-05,,1000000.0,1004500.0,INR,False,"**The role**

As a Business Analyst, you will be accountable for SAP \- Controlling module is properly setup to attend the business requirements in line with other work streams. Understand the business requirement and ensure its integration SAP Central Finance system.


This role requires a deep understanding of Management Accounting processes and the ability to drive solution deployment with efficiency and leadership.

 **What you’ll do**

* Collaborate with cross\-functional teams to gather and analyze business requirements related to Management Accounting and Controlling (SAP S4\). Conduct thorough research and analysis to identify potential solutions and recommend best practices.
* Configure and drive functional discussions around Income Statement, Trade expend, Marketing expense and other P\&L lines applying SAP as main platform (Margin Analys and COPA Costing based method).
* Collaborate with IT cross stream to design, configure, and test Cost Center Accounting, Profit Center Accounting, Project System. Ensuring data consistency, figures reconciliation and smooth PEC execution.
* Stay up to date with complementary solutions customized to attend Nestlé’s business requirements related to Balance sheet accounting, BS allocation, reconciliation, trial balance and its integration with Central finance.
* Provide guidance and support the regional product teams during the implementation phase, ensuring adherence to global solution template, guidelines and standards. Conduct regular system audits and performance assessments to identify areas for improvement and optimization.

 **We offer you**

We offer more than just a job. We put people first and inspire you to become the best version of yourself.

* **Great benefits** including competitive salary and a comprehensive social benefits package. We have one of the most competitive pension plans on the market, as well as flexible remuneration with tax advantages: health insurance, restaurant card, mobility plan, etc**.**
* **Personal and professional growth** through ongoing training and constant career opportunities reflecting our conviction that people are our most important asset.
* **Hybrid working environment with flexible working scheme.** Our state\-of\-the\-art campus is dog friendly and equipped with a medical center, canteen and areas to co\-create network and chill!

 **Minimum qualifications:**

* Minimum bachelor’s degree required, bachelor’s degree in computer science, Business Administration, Economy or related field.
* Proven experience in S/4 HANA, specifically in Controlling module and its integration with Central Finance and data replication processes.
* Solid understanding of SAP FICO, COPA Costing Based, Margin Analysis, including Cost Center Account, Project System, configuration and troubleshooting in S4 Hana and analytics technologies.
* Solid understand of reporting tools in SAP and its configurations such as Report Painter, Sap Analytics cloud (SAC), CDS queries etc.
* Strong knowledge on Profit Center Account, SAP splitting document experience, preparation of trial balance and balance sheet allocations.
* Strong communication and presentation skills explaining complex functional concepts.
* Proficient in project management within SAP implementation, including planning, execution, and coordination with team members.
* Fluency in English (written and spoken), additional languages are a plus.

  



**Bonus Points If You:**

* Proven experience on cFIN technical integration and configurations (SLT, AIF).
* Proficiency in ABAP programming language and SAP integration technologies (e.g., IDocs, BAPIs, RFCs).
* Good understanding of Snowflake in the context of reporting and interfaces

 **About the IT Hub**

At Nestlé IT, we are a diverse, global team of IT professionals in the biggest health, nutrition and wellness company of the world. We strive to create an environment where people are valued for who they are. We innovate every day through future ready technologies to create opportunities for Nestlé to delight consumers, customers, and employees alike. We collaborate with partners around the world to deliver tangible value at global scale. We continuously work to develop our people to be future ready.

 **About Nestlé**

We are Nestlé, the largest food and beverage company in the world, with a presence in more than 185 countries. With net sales of CHF 94\.4 billion in 2022, the company has over 291,000 employees and 418 factories in 85 countries. Our values are based on respect: respect for ourselves, respect for others, respect for diversity, and respect for our future. Nestlé is dedicated to offering high\-quality food and beverage products and services that contribute to the nutrition, health, and well\-being of people, pets, and the planet. Additionally, it is committed to being a leading company in sustainability and achieving net zero greenhouse gas emissions by 2050\. Want to learn more? Visit us at: www.nestle.com

 *We encourage the diversity of applicants across gender, age, ethnicity, nationality, sexual orientation, social background, religion or belief and disability.*


