gd-1009692946431,glassdoor,https://www.glassdoor.co.in/job-listing/j?jl=1009692946431,,IT Change and Problem Coordinator,Brennan IT,Mumbai,2025-04-01,,626000.0,851000.0,INR,False,"**Brennan. Where true performance thrives.**  

At Brennan, we believe that *how* technology is delivered is every bit as important as *what* the technology is. We focus on creating real and relevant value for customers with solutions that fit their specific needs and always reflect their true interests.  

It’s a claim backed by our **True Performance System** – a way of working engineered to get us closer, and deliver better, for our customers and their actual experience of technology.  

  

**Why join Brennan**  

True performance for our customers starts with a true belief in our people.  

It’s why we’ve structured our business to help our teams, and their talents, shine bright. It's why we’ve created a workplace where people of all backgrounds, beliefs and experiences are welcomed and empowered. And it’s why we’ve built an organisation where real innovation makes a genuine impact and generates true rewards for our team members.  

  

**True rewards**  

In addition to competitive remuneration, Brennan offers extensive benefits, including:  

* Training and certification bonuses
* Culture Awards that recognise excellence
* Brennan Daredevils – our annual, all\-expenses paid trip awarded to our top performers and outstanding contributors
* Vibrant, fun social activities
* Discounted hardware and software
* An environment that embraces learning and development

**The Role:**  

In the IT Change Coordinator part of this role, you will be responsible for managing the lifecycle of IT changes within the organization.  

This role ensures that changes to IT services are conducted efficiently, with minimal risk to the business, and that all changes are appropriately documented and communicated.  

The IT Change Coordinator works closely with the IT Change and Problem Manager, various IT teams, project managers, and business stakeholders to ensure seamless integration and implementation of changes.  

The IT Problem Manager part of this role is responsible for managing the lifecycle of all problems within the IT infrastructure and services.  

This includes identifying, analysing, and resolving problems to minimize the impact on business operations, as well as preventing the recurrence of incidents.  

  

**Key Responsibility:**  

  

* Change management process – coordinate and manage the change management process, ensuring adherence to policies, coordinate with project managers and delivery teams to plan, schedule and oversee changes.
* Change management process – coordinate and manage the change management process, ensuring adherence to policies, coordinate with project managers and delivery teams to plan, schedule and oversee changes.
* Change assessment and approval – evaluate the impact, risk and benefit of proposed changes, participate in the CAB meetings, ensure all changes comply with policies and regulatory requirements, follow up on change approvals.
* Ensure all changes are properly documented and approved.
* Communicate change plans and impacts to stakeholders, ensure the appropriate testing, validation and backout plans are in place for all changes.
* Work closely with the incident management and other IT teams to ensure the timely resolution of problems and communicate status updates to the relevant stakeholders.
* Develop and implement action plans for problem resolution and ensure that problem records are maintained and updated.
* Assist in the generation of problem management reports and document RCA results and resolutions for future reference.

  

**What skills you will bring to the team:**  

  

* Proven experience as an IT Change Coordinator and Problem Coordinator or in a similar role within IT Service Delivery.
* Strong understanding of IT systems, infrastructure, and applications.
* Excellent communication, organizational, and problem\-solving skills.
* Ability to work collaboratively with cross\-functional teams.
* Experience with service delivery tools and software.
* ITIL certification
* Attention to Detail: Strong attention to detail to ensure accurate change documentation and reporting.
* Adaptability: Ability to adapt to changing priorities and manage multiple tasks simultaneously.
* Analytical Skills: Proficient in analysing data and metrics to drive informed decision\-making.
* Customer Focus: strong dedication to customer service and satisfaction

  

**Brennan** is an equal opportunity employer.",,https://www.glassdoor.co.in/Overview/W-EI_IE256439.htm,Information Technology
