3\. Configure / Implement Network Devices as per the hardening Guidelines \& as per particular Project requirement.

4\. Troubleshoot Network \& Security related problems in a particular Project based on the Project scope defined.

5\. Implementation of Network Infrastructure for new Offshore Development Centres (ODC) with appropriate security levels and redundancy as per the ODC requirements.

6\. Implementation of Network Infrastructure for new Enterprise Projects with appropriate security levels and redundancy.

7\. Implement ODC setups with connectivity varying from MPLS Connectivity, Client to site VPN, Site to Site VPN (Router based).

8\. Handle implementations in project movements, Point to point link establishment, Network infra for new project locations including LAN/WAN/Internet Architecture etc.

9\. Coordination with ISP, clients and onsite technical teams for P2P, MPLS, VPN and other links for new implementations and troubleshooting connectivity issues.

10\. Validating the technical feasibility of the network design plans for customer/Enterprise networks submitted by the design team and provide appropriate suggestions as required.

11\. Knowledge \& exposure on (not limited to) NMS Tools, Routing Protocols such as OSPF, BGP, etc., MPLS Configuration (VRF Config), Switching Protocols, STP, QoS, etc.

12\. CCNP Equivalent Certifications with around 5 years’ experience.

13\. Should be able to Multitask \& involve in multiple projects at a time.

14\. Take lead and participate in S0 calls and Outages till resolution.

15\. Knowledge About L3 Switches.

