in-27aebf1c14786d04,indeed,https://in.indeed.com/viewjob?jk=27aebf1c14786d04,https://pepsicojobs.com/jobs/373786/job?utm_source=indeed_integration&iis=Job%20Board&iisn=Indeed&indeed-apply-token=73a2d2b2a8d6d5c0a62696875eaebd669103652d3f0c2cd5445d3e66b1592b0f,"Associate Director - Senior Solution Architect – Data, Analytics & AI",PepsiCo,"TS, IN",2025-04-09,,,,,True,"Overview:
**We are PepsiCo**


PepsiCo is one of the world's leading food and beverage companies with more than $79 Billion in Net Revenue and a global portfolio of diverse and beloved brands. We have a complementary food and beverage portfolio that includes 22 brands that each generate more than $1 Billion in annual retail sales. PepsiCo's products are sold in more than 200 countries and territories around the world. PepsiCo's strength is its people. We are over 250,000 game changers, mountain movers and history makers, located around the world, and united by a shared set of values and goals.

  

We believe that acting ethically and responsibly is not only the right thing to do, but also the right thing to do for our business. At PepsiCo, we aim to deliver top\-tier financial performance over the long term by integrating sustainability into our business strategy, leaving a positive imprint on society and the environment. We call this **Winning with Purpose**. For more information on PepsiCo and the opportunities it holds, visit www.pepsico.com.

  

We are seeking an experienced and highly skilled Senior Solution Architect with a strong background in data architecture, governance, Azure Cloud services, and AI\-driven solutions. The ideal candidate will have 15\+ years of experience in IT and software architecture, with a significant focus on designing scalable, secure, and high\-performance data and AI solutions in a cloud environment. The successful candidate will play a pivotal role in shaping the enterprise data architecture strategy, fostering AI/ML adoption, and collaborating across teams to drive the implementation of data governance frameworks and AI capabilities.


This role will also involve working on global programs such as Integrated Business Planning (IBP) and collaborating with cross\-functional teams to deliver innovative, scalable, and practical solutions.


Responsibilities:
**Architecture Design \& Implementation:**

* Lead the design and implementation of cloud\-native solutions on Azure, ensuring alignment with business objectives, security standards, and scalability requirements.
* Architect end\-to\-end data solutions and AI\-driven architectures, enabling seamless integration of data sources, processing systems, and AI/ML platforms.
* Provide guidance on building and maintaining robust data pipelines, real\-time data processing, and ETL/ELT workflows, integrating AI capabilities where applicable.
* Create comprehensive product specifications with a focus on system integration and practicality, ensuring alignment with business needs and technical feasibility.
* Define coding standards, workflows, and development processes to ensure consistency and quality across projects.

 **Data Governance \& Security:**

* Implement and enforce data governance frameworks, policies, and industry best practices, leveraging tools like Informatica Axon and EDC.
* Develop data security strategies, ensuring compliance with privacy regulations and corporate security standards while supporting AI/ML applications.
* Oversee data quality, consistency, and integrity across multiple platforms, ensuring effective stewardship of enterprise data assets.

 **Cloud \& AI Strategy:**

* Architect solutions leveraging Azure Data Services (Azure Data Lake, Azure Synapse, Azure Databricks, Azure Data Factory) to support data\-driven decision\-making processes, with a focus on enabling AI and machine learning workflows.
* Design AI/ML architectures for model development, training, and deployment, including integration with Azure AI/ML services (Azure Machine Learning, Cognitive Services, etc.).
* Collaborate with data science and AI teams to define and implement end\-to\-end AI pipelines, from data preparation and model training to deployment and monitoring.

 **AI/ML Adoption \& Integration:**

* Lead efforts to implement AI\-driven analytics, insights, and automation solutions across business functions.
* Drive AI/ML strategy and adoption, ensuring data is appropriately prepared and aligned for machine learning applications.
* Evaluate and integrate emerging AI technologies and tools, such as natural language processing (NLP), computer vision, and predictive analytics, into business processes.

 **Stakeholder Collaboration:**

* Collaborate with business and technical teams to understand requirements and translate them into innovative, scalable architectural solutions, ensuring alignment with AI and data strategies.
* Act as a thought leader for AI and cloud architecture, engaging with senior leadership to influence the direction of AI adoption and data\-driven initiatives.
* Lead cross\-functional teams in solution delivery, acting as a liaison between architecture, development, data science, and operations teams.
* Work on global programs such as Integrated Business Planning (IBP) and collaborate with virtual teams across different time zones.

 **Mentorship \& Leadership:**

* Mentor and guide junior architects, data engineers, and technical staff, fostering a culture of innovation and continuous improvement.
* Promote best practices for AI/ML architecture and governance across teams, ensuring alignment with business goals and industry standards.
* Influence and drive the architectural vision across teams and stakeholders, ensuring consistency in architecture and design standards.
* Provide technical guidance and coaching to developers and engineers, fostering a culture of continuous learning and improvement.


Qualifications:
* 15\+ years of experience in IT, with at least 8 years in a solution architecture or data architecture role.
* A Master’s degree in computer science or a related field would be an asset
* Proven expertise in designing and implementing cloud\-based solutions on Azure, with deep knowledge of Azure Data Services (Azure Data Lake, Azure Synapse, Azure Databricks, Azure Data Factory, etc.).
* Strong experience in data architecture and data governance, including frameworks, policies, and tools such as Informatica Axon, EDC, and related technologies.
* In\-depth knowledge of AI/ML architectures, including experience with Azure AI/ML services (Azure Machine Learning, Cognitive Services, etc.).
* Strong expertise in data modeling, ETL/ELT processes, data integration, and big data technologies.
* Hands\-on experience integrating AI/ML capabilities into business processes, including predictive analytics, natural language processing, and recommendation systems.
* Experience with Microsoft Power Platform (Power BI, Power Apps, Power Automate) for data visualization and automation.
* Experience with distributed system development using Web Services (SOAP or RESTful), HTTPs, and JSON.
* Strong leadership skills with experience managing cross\-functional teams and guiding senior stakeholders in the adoption of architectural solutions.
* In\-depth knowledge of enterprise architecture frameworks, such as TOGAF or Zachman, is highly desirable.
* Master’s degree in computer science or a related field is a plus.


\-

**Desired Skills:**

* Certifications: Azure Solution Architect Expert, Azure AI Engineer, Azure Data Engineer, or similar certifications.
* Experience with data cataloging and business glossary tools.
* Expertise in integrating AI/ML frameworks with data governance and data\-driven decision\-making.
* Strong understanding of AI ethics, explainability, and fairness considerations in AI model design.
* Understanding of software quality assurance principles to ensure robust and reliable solutions.
* Experience with mobile application development using Native or JavaScript Native Script frameworks is a plus.


\-

**Soft Skills:**

* Strategic Thinking: Ability to translate business needs into scalable, sustainable, and innovative architectural solutions.
* Collaboration \& Teamwork: Strong interpersonal skills to work effectively with business stakeholders, technical teams, and external partners.
* Problem\-Solving: Creative and analytical mindset to solve complex architecture and integration challenges, especially around AI and data.
* Communication: Exceptional verbal and written communication skills, able to simplify complex technical concepts for diverse audiences, including executive leadership.
* Leadership \& Mentorship: Proven ability to lead teams, mentor junior staff, and foster a culture of knowledge sharing and continuous learning.
* Adaptability: Comfortable working in a fast\-paced, evolving environment and willing to adapt to emerging technologies and changing business needs.
* Attention to Detail: Strong attention to detail to ensure high\-quality architectural designs and implementations.
* Managing Competing Priorities: Proven ability to manage multiple, competing priorities simultaneously in a fast\-paced environment.
* Virtual Team Collaboration: Ability to work effectively in virtual teams across different time zones, ensuring seamless communication and collaboration.


\-

**Why Join Us:**

* Opportunity to work on cutting\-edge cloud, data, and AI technologies in a collaborative and innovative environment.
* Play a pivotal role in shaping the organization's data architecture, governance, and AI strategy.
* Work on global programs and collaborate with teams across different time zones.",,https://in.indeed.com/cmp/PepsiCo,Information Technology
in-7ec5dc8d0bfd1846,indeed,https://in.indeed.com/viewjob?jk=7ec5dc8d0bfd1846,https://medtronic.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/en-US/MedtronicCareers/job/Pune-Maharashtra-India/IT-Architect--Data-Engineer-_R26847,IT Architect (Data Engineer),Medtronic,"MH, IN",2025-04-09,fulltime,,,,False,"At Medtronic you can begin a life\-long career of exploration and innovation, while helping champion healthcare access and equity for all. You’ll lead with purpose, breaking down barriers to innovation in a more connected, compassionate world.


**A Day in the Life**
=====================

We’re a mission\-driven leader in medical technology and solutions with a legacy of integrity and innovation, join our new Minimed India Hub as Digital Engineer. We are working to improve how healthcare addresses the needs of more people, in more ways and in more places around the world. As a PySpark Data Engineer, you will be responsible for designing, developing, and maintaining data pipelines using PySpark. You will work closely with data scientists, analysts, and other stakeholders to ensure the efficient processing and analysis of large datasets, while handling complex transformations and aggregations.
**Responsibilities may include the following and other duties may be assigned:**

* Design, develop, and maintain scalable and efficient ETL pipelines using PySpark.
* Work with structured and unstructured data from various sources.
* Optimize and tune PySpark applications for performance and scalability.
* Collaborate with data scientists and analysts to understand data requirements, review Business Requirement documents and deliver high\-quality datasets.
* Implement data quality checks and ensure data integrity.
* Monitor and troubleshoot data pipeline issues and ensure timely resolution.
* Document technical specifications and maintain comprehensive documentation for data pipelines.
* Stay up to date with the latest trends and technologies in big data and distributed computing.

**Required Knowledge and Experience:**

* Bachelor’s degree in computer science, Engineering, or a related field.
* 4\-5 years of experience in data engineering, with a focus on PySpark.
* Proficiency in Python and Spark, with strong coding and debugging skills.
* Strong knowledge of SQL and experience with relational databases (e.g., PostgreSQL, MySQL, SQL Server).
* Hands\-on experience with cloud platforms such as AWS, Azure, or Google Cloud Platform (GCP).
* Experience with data warehousing solutions like Redshift, Snowflake, Databricks or Google BigQuery.
* Familiarity with data lake architectures and data storage solutions.
* Experience with big data technologies such as Hadoop, Hive, and Kafka.
* Excellent problem\-solving skills and the ability to troubleshoot complex issues.
* Strong communication and collaboration skills, with the ability to work effectively in a team environment.

**Preferred Skills:**

* Experience with Databricks.
* Experience with orchestration tools like Apache Airflow or AWS Step Functions.
* Knowledge of machine learning workflows and experience working with data scientists.
* Understanding of data security and governance best practices.
* Familiarity with streaming data platforms and real\-time data processing.
* Knowledge of CI/CD pipelines and version control systems (e.g., Git).

**Physical Job Requirements**  

  

The above statements are intended to describe the general nature and level of work being performed by employees assigned to this position, but they are not an exhaustive list of all the required responsibilities and skills of this position.


**Benefits \& Compensation**
============================

**Medtronic offers a competitive Salary and flexible Benefits Package**  

A commitment to our employees lives at the core of our values. We recognize their contributions. They share in the success they help to create. We offer a wide range of benefits, resources, and competitive compensation plans designed to support you at every career and life stage.  

  



This position is eligible for a short\-term incentive called the Medtronic Incentive Plan (MIP).
