e proper setup and alignment of cameras, network settings, and DVRs/NVRs.Perform routine maintenance and troubleshooting on installed systems.**System Troubleshooting:**Diagnose and resolve hardware, software, and connectivity issues in CCTV systems.Provide technical solutions for system failures, poor image quality, or network connection issues.Ensure the optimal performance of CCTV systems.**Product Knowledge \& Training:**Stay updated with the latest CCTV technology, software, and hardware developments.Provide training and guidance to customers and staff regarding CCTV system usage and best practices.Documentation:Document all technical support activities, including customer queries, solutions provided, and system setups.Prepare detailed reports on recurring issues or potential improvements to the product.Collaboration \& Coordination:Coordinate with field engineers and other internal teams to ensure timely resolution of issues.Collaborate with product teams to suggest improvements based on customer feedback.Required Qualifications \& Skills:Experience: 2\-4 years of experience in technical support or a similar role, particularly within CCTV or surveillance systems.Technical Skills:Strong knowledge of CCTV systems, cameras, NVR/DVR setups, IP cameras, and video analytics.Familiarity with networking concepts (TCP/IP, LAN/WAN, VPN).Experience with CCTV\-related software, configuration tools, and troubleshooting.Knowledge of security protocols and data protection methods.Ability to work with video management systems (VMS) and integration with other security systems.**Job Title : Technical Support Engineer** 

