At first glance, you’ll see that for more than 80 years we’ve been dedicated to advancing and optimizing the laboratory to move science and healthcare forward. Join a team where you can be heard, be supported, and always be yourself. We’re building a culture that celebrates backgrounds, experiences, and perspectives of all our associates. Look again and you’ll see we are invested in you, providing the opportunity to build a meaningful career, be creative, and try new things with the support you need to be successful.


Beckman Coulter Diagnostics is proud to work alongside a community of six fellow Diagnostics Companies at Danaher. Together, we’re working at the pace of change to improve patient lives with diagnostic tools that address the world’s biggest health challenges.


The *IT Site Support Engineer* for Beckman Coulter Diagnostics is responsible *for* *providing IT support to associates in Bangalore (IDC) Sites. This includes PC hardware and software support, infrastructure support and maintenance, network monitoring and maintenance, application support and local telecommunication support. Assists with the overall planning of changes or upgrades and is responsible for their implementation. Will be asked to help with support and work on projects for other sites and/or on regional level.*


This position is part of the *Global IT Organization* located in *Bangalore* and will be *On\-site.* At Beckman Coulter, our vision is to relentlessly reimagine healthcare, one diagnosis at a time.

**In this role, you will have the opportunity to:**

* *Install, configure, deploy and maintain PC hardware, MS operating systems and software. Provide support for O365 platform (SharePoint, OneDrive, Power BI, etc.).*
* *Provide phone, e\-mail/instant messaging and hands\-on support to associates and on other sites if required. Maintain records of incidents and request in ticketing systems.*
* *Troubleshoot incidents with computer systems, including hardware and software, messaging, network, printers, telephony, peripheral equipment and accessories; make repair and correction where necessary.*
* *Work with infrastructure support teams and external contactors to install, configure and deploy servers, network hardware and other infrastructure equipment. Provide hands\-on support when required.*
* *Maintain asset inventory of computers, infrastructure equipment, communication lines, applications, etc. Vendor and contract management. Assist with formulating of IT budget, plan IT expenses throughout the year and coordinate procurement of IT hardware and accessories.*
* *Participate on local, regional and global projects and process improvement activities, occasionally leading them. Act as a relationship manager between local business representatives and IT organization, translates business needs into IT project offerings.*
* *Provide support for global and local applications, participate on application deployment, testing and validation. Follow corporate IT standards and help develop site specific policies and standards as needed, including creating relevant quality documentation*

**The essential requirements of the job include:**

* *Bachelor's degree in Computer Science or Computer Engineering or related field.*
* *Experience in working with Medical, Healthcare Organizations*
* *Continuous improvement mindset, with the ability to adapt to changing organizational landscapes*

**It would be a plus if you also possess previous experience in:**

* *Experience in IT Ticketing system is a must*
* *Server and networking advanced knowledge are a plus*


Join our winning team today. Together, we’ll accelerate the real\-life impact of tomorrow’s science and technology. We partner with customers across the globe to help them solve their most complex challenges, architecting solutions that bring the power of science to life.


For more information, visit www.danaher.com.


