The IT Systems Administrator is responsible for managing and maintaining IT infrastructure, including Office 365, Windows, Linux, and Cloud environments. This role also includes overseeing IT asset management, ensuring efficient tracking, maintenance, and lifecycle management of IT assets. The administrator will work to optimize system performance, security, and compliance. This role requires collaboration with various IT teams to support business operations, enhance system efficiency, and ensure robust cybersecurity measures.


