in-acfa4dd266730437,indeed,https://in.indeed.com/viewjob?jk=acfa4dd266730437,https://mycareer.hsbc.com/en_GB/external/PipelineDetail/Linux-Administrator-Senior-Systems-Administrator/263851,Linux Administrator/Senior Systems Administrator,HSBC,"TS, IN",2025-04-08,fulltime,,,,False,"Job description
Some careers shine brighter than others.


If you’re looking for a career that will help you stand out, join HSBC and fulfil your potential. Whether you want a career that could take you to the top, or simply take you in an exciting new direction, HSBC offers opportunities, support and rewards that will take you further.


HSBC is one of the largest banking and financial services organisations in the world, with operations in 64 countries and territories. We aim to be where the growth is, enabling businesses to thrive and economies to prosper, and, ultimately, helping people to fulfil their hopes and realise their ambitions.


Department\-Enterprise Infrastructure, CTO


In this role, you will:


* Monitor and deploy patches and updates for operating systems and applications to ensure security and functionality are maintained.
* Work with respective security teams to identify and assess vulnerabilities in the system. Prioritize patching activities based on risk, security exposure, and business needs.
* Maintain detailed records of patching activities, including what patches were applied, the systems affected, and any issues encountered. Provide regular reports on patching status and compliance.
* Implement automated patching processes and tools to improve efficiency and reduce manual intervention. Identify opportunities to reduce toil and raise remand for respective engineering / automation teams.
* Work cross\-functionally with other IT teams (e.g., Systems, Security, Network, etc.) to coordinate patching efforts and minimize service disruptions.
* Assist with troubleshooting and remediation of issues arising from patching, ensuring minimal downtime and service interruption.
* Ensure patching processes align with internal policies, industry standards, and regulatory requirements. Support auditing activities related to patch management.
* Stay current with the latest security vulnerabilities, patches, and industry best practices, making recommendations for improvements to patching strategies and tools
* The role requires flexible working via shifts and out of hours / weekend coverage on rotation basis to align with respective maintenance windows of the services.
Requirements
To be successful in this role, you should meet the following requirements:


* Hands on administration experience of Unix/Linux / Windows operating systems.
* Experience on scripting languages (e.g., PowerShell, Bash) for automation.
* Experience on IT Service Management i.e. Change Management, Incident Management, Problem Management and understanding of OLAs and SLAs.
* Experience on DevOps processes and Agile methodologies – Scrum, Kanban
* Knowledge of cryptography (SSL/TLS) security.
* Good analytical and troubleshooting skills.
* The ability to manage self\-workload, set and meet customer expectations.
* Excellent communication skills, both written and verbal.
* Strong attention to detail and a proactive approach to managing patching activities.

You’ll achieve more when you join HSBC.


www.hsbc.com/careers


HSBC is committed to building a culture where all employees are valued, respected and opinions count. We take pride in providing a workplace that fosters continuous professional development, flexible working and opportunities to grow within an inclusive and diverse environment. Personal data held by the Bank relating to employment applications will be used in accordance with our Privacy Statement, which is available on our website.


Issued by – HSBC Software Development India",,https://in.indeed.com/cmp/HSBC,Information Technology
