in-9efe6dde5441ffdb,indeed,https://in.indeed.com/viewjob?jk=9efe6dde5441ffdb,https://careers3-powerschool.icims.com/jobs/49938/job?utm_source=indeed_integration&iis=Job%20Board&iisn=Indeed&indeed-apply-token=73a2d2b2a8d6d5c0a62696875eaebd669103652d3f0c2cd5445d3e66b1592b0f,"Senior System Administrator, NetSuite",PowerSchool Group,"KA, IN",2025-04-07,fulltime,,,,False,"Overview:

At PowerSchool, we are a dedicated team of innovators guided by our shared purpose of powering personalized education for students around the world. From the central office to the classroom to the home, PowerSchool supports the entire educational ecosystem as the global leader of cloud\-based software for K\-12 education. Our employees make it all possible, and a career with us means you’re joining a successful team committed to engaging, empowering, and improving the K\-12 education experience everywhere.### **Team Overview**


Our Information Technology (IT) team leads all aspects of IT systems and processes across the enterprise, including data services, security, compliance, applications, automation, and end\-user services. Through innovative and streamlined technology solutions, this dynamic team enables company growth, protects data, and serves as a critical partner to all departments of PowerSchool.### **Role Overview**


The **Senior System Administrator, NetSuite** will support the ongoing maintenance and customization of PowerSchool’s instance of NetSuite to ensure the continued delivery of innovative, high\-quality solutions that enable PowerSchool to accomplish its company and financial business objectives. This role will work cross\-functionally with a variety of PowerSchool departments to maximize the value NetSuite provides to PowerSchool. This includes managing the day\-to\-day incoming requests from business users, understanding requirements and determining complexity, defining solution functionality, designing solutions, developing and maintaining solutions over time. The Senior System Administrator \- NetSuite will be hands\-on and be involved in the support of managing NetSuite in a diverse working environment. This individual will apply proven communication, analytical, and problem\-solving skills to help maximize the benefit of IT system investments.
Responsibilities:
### **Description**


The Enterprise Applications team is responsible for establishing and configuring enterprise software applications, providing training to IT staff and employees, supporting users, and troubleshooting issues.
Your day\-to\-day job will consist of:  

Essential duties and responsibilities include the following. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions.* Customization of PowerSchool’s NetSuite instance using SuiteScript in support of key business initiatives inclusive of maintaining and creating new scripts
* Support integration of NetSuite with other platforms, including Salesforce.com
* Analyze business needs and facilitate design, review \& training sessions with technical and business stakeholders
* Prepare and deliver saved searches, reports, recommendations, or alternatives that address existing and potential trouble areas in operating NetSuite across the organization
* Manage system enhancement projects in accordance with established SDLC and agile methodologies
* Create systems documentation including, business requirements documents, functional designs, user manuals, test scripts, test plans and training materials
* Work collaboratively across teams and/or independently to design and build solutions on the NetSuite, SuiteScript, and SuiteBuilder platform using progressively complex capabilities
* Administration of new enhancements: creation of custom functions, processes, forms, reports, workflows
* Develop reports, dashboards, and processes to continuously monitor data quality and integrity
* Manage security, users, roles, profiles, groups, queues and other NetSuite setup options as necessary
* Serve as a subject matter expert on items related to NetSuite and SuiteApps
* Coordinate and perform in\-depth tests, including end\-user reviews, for modified and new systems, and other post\-implementation support
* Identify opportunities for automation to increase quality and speed of processes.
* Prioritize tasks, manage time effectively and work on projects in parallel.
* Other duties as assigned.


Qualifications:
### **Qualifications**


To be considered for and to perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential duty and responsibility satisfactorily. The requirements listed below are representative of the knowledge, skill and/or ability required.
Qualifications include:* Bachelor's Degree in Computer Science, Engineering or related technical field preferred
* 4\+ years of experience as a NetSuite Developer or NetSuite Administrator required
* NetSuite SuiteFoundation, Administrator and SuiteCloud Developer Certifications desired
* Track record of multiple successful NetSuite and similar ERP full\-lifecycle implementation
* Hands on knowledge and proven competency coding in SuiteScript
* Deep knowledge of NetSuite functionality, and the coding that brings about this functionality
* Highly skilled at coding in HTML, CSS, JavaScript
* Experience with revenue\-based functionality such as Advanced Revenue Management and Fixed Asset Management
* Experience working with the Electronic Bank Payments SuiteApp
* Knowledge of the NetSuite Dunning module
* Experienced in SuiteAnalytics and SuiteAnalytics Connect
* Hands on knowledge of Salesforce, Coupa, Boomi a plus
* Has a professional image and builds strong relationships across functions
* Excellent analytical, mathematical, and creative problem\-solving skills
* Excellent written and verbal communication skills while maintaining objectivity and proper understanding of a problem or situation when placed under stressful conditions
* Excellent listening and interpersonal skills with ability to communicate and explain complex concepts across functions and levels of the organization
* Must have the ability to make recommendations to effectively resolve problems or issues using judgement that is consistent with standards, practices, policies, procedures, regulation or government law
* Ability to conduct research into NetSuite issues and related products as required
* Ability to communicate ideas in both technical and user\-friendly language
* Highly self\-motivated and directed and work well as with a team while learning software capabilities hands\-on and willingness to be self\-driven in ongoing skills development
* Ability to effectively prioritize and execute tasks in a high\-pressure environment
* Ability to research and analyze information from a variety of sources to determine best go forward path
* Familiarity with integrated application platforms and the impact of data quality on the successful transformation of information between systems


EEO Commitment:
### **EEO Commitment**

*PowerSchool celebrates a diverse and inclusive workplace. PowerSchool is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, national origin, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, protected veteran status, disability, age, or other legally protected status. Our inclusive culture empowers PowerSchoolers to deliver the best results for our customers. We not only celebrate the diversity of our workforce, we celebrate the diverse ways we work. If you have a disability and need an accommodation regarding our recruiting process, please let us know by emailing accomodations@powerschool.com.* *\#LI\-NB1*",,https://in.indeed.com/cmp/Powerschool,Information Technology
in-ee7f814e89f62026,indeed,https://in.indeed.com/viewjob?jk=ee7f814e89f62026,https://careers.orica.com/job/Hyderabad-Global-IT-Architect-Core-Technology-TG-500081/1280123100/,Global IT Architect - Core Technology,Orica,"TS, IN",2025-04-07,fulltime,,,,True,"**Date:** 7 Apr 2025


**Location:** Hyderabad, TG, IN, 500081


**Company:** Orica


**About Orica**  

At Orica, it’s the power of our people that leads change and shapes our futures. Every day, all around the world, our people help mobilise vital resources essential to progress. Established in 1874, we have grown to become the world leader in mining and civil blasting with a diverse of team of more than 13,000 across the world.  

  

It’s an exciting time to join us – we are shaping the future of mining through digital and automated technologies, embracing new ways of thinking, pioneering innovation and reimagining the way we work.
**About the role**  

Orica is seeking a highly skilled Global IT Architect – Core Technology to join our global IT team. The role will be based in Hyderabad, India. This position is pivotal in shaping the strategic direction of our IT infrastructure, cloud, and network domains across 400 global sites in over 60 countries.  

  

The Global IT Architect – Core Technology will drive the full use of cloud services and software\-defined networking, ensuring the availability, integrity, and security of Orica’s IT infrastructure. This role offers the opportunity to influence and guide architecture development, simplify IT operations, and support business growth and innovation.  

  

Join Orica and be part of a team that drives innovation and excellence in IT infrastructure, cloud, and network architecture. to make a significant impact on our global operations!
**What you will be doing**  

* Develop and maintain a 3\-year strategy and roadmap.
* Define and maintain the Core Technology architecture vision.
* Align solutions with business strategies and objectives.
* Establish and maintain standards for Core Technology.
* Capture requirements and develop high\-level designs.
* Provide oversight to Engineers and project teams.
* Develop a project roadmap to standardize technology and reduce costs.
* Use Proof of Concepts (PoCs) to validate solutions.
**What you will bring**  

* 3\-5 years in architecture roles for large, global organizations.
* 5\+ years of experience with IT Infrastructure, Networking, and Cloud Technology.
* Experience with multi\-cloud environments (VMWare, Azure, Google Cloud, AWS).
* Knowledge of hardware asset management, Windows Infrastructure services, SQL Server, and backup/recovery solutions.
* Proficiency in network services (WAN, LAN, WLAN), remote access solutions, and cybersecurity principles.
* Strong communication and presentation skills.
* Ability to build trust and foster collaboration.
* Solution and outcome\-focused, with commercial awareness.
* Teamwork and problem\-solving skills.
* Integrity, ethics, and values.
**What we offer**  

As part of a truly global company, you will have the ability to grow and learn in a diverse, collaborative culture. We foster relationships and learning through connected global and local teams, promote flexible and diverse career paths and support the development of your knowledge and skills.  

  

You will be paid a competitive salary, learn from talented individuals across multiple disciplines and be able to thrive in a safe workplace within a collaborative culture. Ignite your career at a place where your distinct potential can find its home.
**We respect and value all**  

Orica promotes and fosters a culture of inclusion and Equal Opportunity Employment everywhere we operate. We treat our people and applicants with fairness, dignity, and respect, getting the best of everyone’s contributions.  

  

All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, religion, sexual orientation, gender perception or identity, nationality, age, military or veteran, marital or disability status.",Agriculture And Extraction,https://in.indeed.com/cmp/Orica,Information Technology
