### **Role description**


### **Role Overview:**



As an L2 Desktop Support Engineer, you will be a key member of the Global Desktop Engineering team, focusing on engineering and escalations related to **Windows Desktop Operating Systems** across both **physical and virtual desktops**. This role emphasizes support, maintenance, and optimization of desktop platforms, along with driving resolutions for escalations and collaborating on global technology initiatives.


### **Key Responsibilities:**


* Support and maintain the desktop platform and related infrastructure.
* Participate in global OS patch management and deployment efforts.
* Create and manage deployment packages and custom applications in an enterprise environment.
* Act as the escalation point for APAC end\-user service issues, driving resolution and bridging Desktop Engineering with regional EUS support.
* Ensure regional (APAC) nuances are considered while implementing global desktop standards.
* Coach EUS and service desk teams on both new and routine desktop\-related tasks.
* Recommend and evaluate new end\-user technologies to enhance security, reliability, and user experience.
* Provide engineering guidance in global technology projects involving end\-user computing.
* Collaborate closely with Wintel, Network Engineers, and third\-party support organizations.
* Generate reports to track department productivity and support efforts.
* Develop and maintain global workstation standards, processes, and documentation.
* Stay up\-to\-date with next\-generation desktop platforms and automation technologies.

### **General Skills:**


* Client\-focused and service\-oriented mindset.
* Experience in mission\-critical and fast\-paced environments.
* Background in financial services or similarly regulated industries (preferred).
* Strong documentation skills for desktop platforms and procedures.
* Hands\-on experience in managing large\-scale desktop environments, especially **VDI (Virtual Desktop Infrastructure)**.
* Involvement in complex desktop transformation projects.
* Experience with profile management, Citrix policy optimization, and application/OS deployment.
* Familiarity with patch management, desktop troubleshooting (physical and virtual), and Windows client migrations.
* Flexibility to work in shifts or participate in weekend activities as required.

### **Technical Skills:**


**Citrix:**


* XenDesktop / XenApp 7\.15\+

**Microsoft Technologies:**


* Windows OS (7, 10, Server)
* Group Policy Management
* PowerShell scripting and automation
* SCCM 2012 R2\+
* Microsoft App\-V
* Office365
* Microsoft Azure
* Troubleshooting memory and application dumps

**User Environment Management:**


* AppSense (Environment Manager, Performance Manager, Application Manager)

**Other Technologies:**


* Thin Client platforms
* VMware vSphere
* Skype for Business
* Sophos, Lumension
* Monitoring and ITSM tools: ServiceNow, LogicMonitor, Systrack

### **Personal Attributes:**


* Positive, solution\-driven mindset under pressure.
* Strong communicator and global team collaborator.
* Self\-driven with a sense of ownership and initiative.
* Ability to challenge the status quo and improve user experience.
* Excellent organizational and time management skills.
* Capable of independently handling complex Level 4 technical issues.
* Detail\-oriented and analytical thinker.

### **Preferred Certifications:**


* **Citrix Certified Expert – Virtualization (CCE\-V)** or **Citrix Certified Professional – Virtualization (CCP\-V)**
* **Microsoft Certified Solutions Expert (MCSE)** / **Microsoft Certified IT Professional (MCITP)**
