* As every BMC employee, you will be given the opportunity to learn, be included in global projects, challenge yourself and be the innovator when it comes to solving everyday problems.

**To ensure you’re set up for success, you will bring the following skillset \& experience:*** You can embrace, live, and breathe our BMC values every day!
* You have 3\-5 years of hands\-on IT experience, with a minimum of 3 years in a technical support role for software products.
* You have strong troubleshooting expertise across Unix/Linux operating systems, with basic knowledge of Windows, application/production servers, and networking concepts.
* You bring experience in supporting BMC Discovery/ADDM (10\.x, 11\.x, 12\.x), including integration with CMDB and/or ServiceNow.
* You have hands\-on experience with TPL programming and application modeling.
* You are skilled in shell scripting and comfortable working with global enterprise customers.
* You have excellent communication and analytical skills with a customer\-centric mindset.
* You are flexible with work hours and open to working in rotational shifts, including periodic weekend work if required.
* You hold a full\-time bachelor’s degree in Engineering (BE/B.Tech), Computer Applications (BCA/MCA), or Science (B.Sc).
**Whilst these are nice to have, our team can help you develop in the following skills:*** Certifications in Linux/Unix and/or ITIL Foundation
* Experience in PL/SQL, database log analysis, and system activity reporting
* Familiarity with Windows administration including Active Directory and Domain Controllers
* Exposure to cloud technologies, Docker, Kubernetes
* Knowledge of virtualization platforms (VM Hypervisors, VM Admin, Hyper\-V, LDOM)
Understanding of PowerShell and Kerberos Authentication  
