gd-1009706455711,glassdoor,https://www.glassdoor.co.in/job-listing/j?jl=1009706455711,,Product Owner,Experian,Hyderābād,2025-04-12,,450000.0,685000.0,INR,False,"**Company Description**  

Experian is a global data and technology company, powering opportunities for people and businesses around the world. We help to redefine lending practices, uncover and prevent fraud, simplify healthcare, create marketing solutions, all using our unique combination of data, analytics and software. We also assist millions of people to realize their financial goals and help them save time and money.


We operate across a range of markets, from financial services to healthcare, automotive, agribusiness, insurance, and many more industry segments.


We invest in people and new advanced technologies to unlock the power of data. As a FTSE 100 Index company listed on the London Stock Exchange (EXPN), we have a team of 22,500 people across 32 countries. Our corporate headquarters are in Dublin, Ireland. Learn more at experianplc.com

 **Job Description**  

As a Product Owner, you will work within the Financial Crime Compliance division. You will be \#LI\-hybrid based in Hyderabad reporting to the Product Director, Financial Crime Compliance. The team focuses on providing customers with a perpetual KYC/KYB solution, enabling them to efficiently manage compliance requirements and mitigate financial crime risks on an ongoing basis. This role will concentrate on enhancing our KYC/KYB solution to ensure it meets regulatory standards and customer needs.

**Key Responsibilities**

* Collaborate with the Product Manager and Technology team to deliver the product vision and strategy.
* Perform the role of Product Owner within an Agile Scrum team, including defining user stories and prioritizing the product backlog.
* Manage the product delivery roadmap, ensuring alignment with business goals and customer needs.
* Act as the primary liaison between stakeholders and the development team, ensuring communication and understanding of product requirements.
* Gather and analyze customer feedback to continuously improve the product.
* Ensure the product meets regulatory requirements and industry standards, particularly in the context of financial crime compliance.
* Provide guidance and support to the development team, helping to resolve any issues that arise during the development process.
* Leverage experience with agile methodologies to maintain regular customer contact, drive experimentation, and lead with insights that resonate across various market verticals.
* You will engage in both technical and commercial discussions, bridging the gap between different stakeholders to ensure alignment and understanding.
* Utilise background in financial crime compliance solutions to enhance product offerings and ensure regulatory adherence, providing customers with robust and compliant solutions.
* Apply understanding of product metrics to maximize the effectiveness of the product and drive continuous improvement.

  

**Qualifications**  

* 5\+ years of experience in product ownership, preferably within the business information services industry.
* Proven experience with Agile methodologies and working within Scrum teams.
* Understanding of SaaS solutions and their development lifecycle.
* Experience in financial crime compliance and regulatory adherence.
* Gather and interpret customer feedback and product metrics.
* Manage and prioritize a product backlog effectively.
* Experience in facilitating Agile ceremonies such as sprint planning, reviews, and retrospectives.
* Guide and support development teams.

  

**Additional Information**  

Our uniqueness is that we celebrate yours. Experian's culture and people are important differentiators. We take our people agenda very seriously and focus on what matters; DEI, work/life balance, development, authenticity, collaboration, wellness, reward \& recognition, volunteering... the list goes on. Experian's people first approach is award\-winning; World's Best Workplaces™ 2024 (Fortune Global Top 25\), Great Place To Work™ in 24 countries, and Glassdoor Best Places to Work 2024 to name a few. Check out Experian Life on social or our Careers Site and Glassdoor to understand why.

  

Experian is proud to be an Equal Opportunity and Affirmative Action employer. Innovation is a critical part of Experian's DNA and practices, and our diverse workforce drives our success. Everyone can succeed at Experian and bring their whole self to work, irrespective of their gender, ethnicity, religion, color, sexuality, physical ability or age. If you have a disability or special need that requires accommodation, please let us know at the earliest opportunity.

  

Benefits


Experian care for employee's work life balance, health, safety and wellbeing. In support of this endeavor, we offer best\-in\-class family well\-being benefits, enhanced medical benefits and paid time off.


Experian Careers \- Creating a better tomorrow together


Find out what its like to work for Experian by clicking here",,https://www.glassdoor.co.in/Overview/W-EI_IE42406.htm,Product Management
gd-1009706610127,glassdoor,https://www.glassdoor.co.in/job-listing/j?jl=1009706610127,,Product Manager - Growth,GoTo Group,Bengaluru,2025-04-12,,370000.0,830000.0,INR,False,"**About the Role**  

As a Product Manager—Growth at Gojek, you will play a pivotal role in shaping and driving the product vision and roadmap with a clear focus on optimizing promotional spend to maximize efficiency and ROI. You’ll work cross\-functionally with Business, Data Science, Design, and Engineering teams, while also coordinating closely with Product Managers from other teams. This role requires both strategic thinking and hands\-on execution—balancing high\-level problem solving with deep attention to detail in implementation.
### **What You Will Do**

* + Own the end\-to\-end product lifecycle, from ideation to launch, ensuring timely delivery of high\-quality features that drive growth and improve promotional efficiency.
	+ Gather product ideas and stakeholder feedback, define clear product requirements, write specs, create wireframes/workflows, and iterate based on continuous feedback.
	+ Design configurable, adaptable solutions that cater to diverse business needs across multiple markets and product lines.
	+ Act as the key point of clarity for development teams and stakeholders—communicating feature requirements, expected impact, and go\-to\-market strategies to drive effective adoption.
	+ Analyze feature performance using data\-driven insights to understand adoption and impact, continuously refining features to better solve user and merchant pain points.
	+ Build strong partnerships across teams to understand their goals and convert them into product solutions that drive business impact.
	+ Define, prioritize, and manage the product roadmap in alignment with business priorities, balancing short\-term wins with long\-term scalability.
	+ Foster a culture of experimentation, learning, and iteration to ensure our growth strategies are continually optimized for impact.

### **What You Will Need**

* + At least 6 years of product management experience, with a strong track record of delivering impactful products. Prior experience working with Data Products or Data Science teams is highly preferred.
	+ Excellent critical thinking and analytical skills—able to break down complex problems into actionable steps and data\-driven decisions.
	+ Experience working within an Objectives and Key Results (OKR) framework to set clear goals and track progress.
	+ Data\-driven mindset with proven experience analyzing product performance, defining success metrics, and driving experimentation (e.g., A/B testing).
	+ Strong strategic and organizational skills—able to manage multiple priorities while aligning stakeholders around a clear product vision.
	+ Excellent verbal and written communication skills to foster effective collaboration across diverse teams.
	+ Familiarity with agile development processes and experience driving productivity within distributed teams is a plus.

**About the Team**  

At Gojek, our Product Management team thrives at the intersection of innovation and collaboration. We take pride in solving complex problems at scale, creating seamless experiences for millions of users every day. The Growth team focuses on customer activation and retention, building personalized journeys that onboard users smoothly and keep them engaged through meaningful experiences. We’re a team that values creativity, experimentation, and impact—and we’re looking for passionate product leaders who are eager to build the future of growth at Gojek. If you enjoy tackling tough challenges, collaborating with sharp minds, and using technology to drive tangible results, we’d love to have you on board. **About GoTo Group**
GoTo Group is the largest digital ecosystem in Indonesia with its mission to “Empower Progress’ by offering technological infrastructure and solutions for everyone to access and thrive in the digital economy. The GoTo ecosystem consists of on\-demand transportation services, food and grocery delivery, logistics and fulfillment, as well as financial and payment services through the Gojek and GoTo Financial platforms.It is the first platform in Southeast Asia that hosts these crucial cases in a single ecosystem, capturing the majority of Indonesia’s vast consumer household. **About Gojek**
Gojek is Southeast Asia’s leading on\-demand platform and pioneer of the multi\-service ecosystem with over 2\.5 million driver partners across the regions offering a wide range of services such as transportation, food delivery, logistics and more. With its mission to create impact at scale, Gojek is committed to resolving consumer problems and raising standards of living by connecting consumers to the best providers of goods and services in the market. **About GoTo Financial**
GoTo Financial accelerates financial inclusion through its leading financial services and merchants solutions. Its consumer services include GoPay and GoPayLater and serve businesses of all sizes through Midtrans, Moka, GoBiz Plus, GoBiz, and Selly. With its trusted and inclusive ecosystem of products, GoTo Financial is open to new growth opportunities and aims to empower everyone to Make It Happen, Make It Together, Make It Last. *GoTo and its business units, including Gojek and GoToFinancial (""GoTo"") only post job opportunities on our official channels on our respective company websites and on LinkedIn. GoTo is not liable for any job postings or job offers that did not originate from us. You should conduct your own due diligence to prevent being victims of any fake job scams, if they did not originate from GoTo's official recruitment channels.* *\#LI\-HYBRID*",,https://www.glassdoor.co.in/Overview/W-EI_IE2478392.htm,Product Management
