gd-1009706825632,glassdoor,https://www.glassdoor.co.in/job-listing/j?jl=1009706825632,,News Product Manager - Metrics and Social Media,LSEG (London Stock Exchange Group),Bengaluru,2025-04-12,,198000.0,879829.0,INR,False,"Junior Product Manager  

Role Summary
Financial news is at the core of the LSEG Data \& Feeds value proposition to clients. The News Product Team is looking for a highly motivated Product Manager to join the team. The Product Manager will play a meaningful role in bringing to bear usage data to advise product decisions and drive growth. The analysis tasks revolve around understanding user behaviours, translating that into actionable insights, and working cross\-functionally to optimize product performance. This role will also lead all aspects of the social media news content in Workspace, including current relationships and any future partners.  

Responsibilities* Produce regular Management Information reports and summaries to provide insights into news usage and consumption that will help advise investment decisions.
* Provide adhoc reports as needed by news leadership team
* Supervise the accuracy and reliability of collected data, ensuring that tracking setups are consistent and collect all relevant events
* Collaborate with data engineers and analysts to implement and maintain the analytics tools (Microsoft PowerBI, Amplitude, and Enterprise Data Warehouse)
* Identify new Key Performance Indicators for tracking news production, consumption, and product usage that align with the overall business and product objectives
* Analyze usage patterns to understand how users interact with the product, which features are most popular, which sources are most/least popular, cost per click analysis, and identifying where users may be encountering issues
* Segment users by different attributes (e.g., demographics, behavior, job role/channels) to identify trends and make insights more actionable
* Build and maintain dashboards to present key usage metrics to partners (executives, marketing, sales, etc.) and provide actionable insights
* Translate sophisticated analytics into clear and concise reports for decision\-makers, highlighting trends, opportunities, and areas for improvement
* Management of Social Media feed, adding content, competitor analysis
  

Required Skills \& Qualifications* Bachelor's degree or equivalent experience in Business, Finance, Data Science, or an equivalent field
* Experience in product management, preferably within the news or finance industry
* Strong analytical abilities with experience in data analysis and interpretation
* Proficiency with analytics tools such as Microsoft PowerBI, Amplitude, and Enterprise Data Warehouse
* Excellent communication and collaboration skills to work effectively with cross\-functional global teams
* Ability to translate data insights into actionable product strategies
* Experience with social media management and partnerships is a plus
* Candidate to demonstrate they are both a great teammate and are self\-motivated
  

LSEG is a leading global financial markets infrastructure and data provider. Our purpose is driving financial stability, empowering economies and enabling customers to create sustainable growth.
Our purpose is the foundation on which our culture is built. Our values of Integrity, Partnership, Excellence and Change underpin our purpose and set the standard for everything we do, every day. They go to the heart of who we are and guide our decision making and everyday actions.
Working with us means that you will be part of a dynamic organisation of 25,000 people across 65 countries. However, we will value your individuality and enable you to bring your true self to work so you can help enrich our diverse workforce. You will be part of a collaborative and creative culture where we encourage new ideas and are committed to sustainability across our global business. You will experience the critical role we have in helping to re\-engineer the financial ecosystem to support and drive sustainable economic growth. Together, we are aiming to achieve this growth by accelerating the just transition to net zero, enabling growth of the green economy and creating inclusive economic opportunity.
LSEG offers a range of tailored benefits and support, including healthcare, retirement planning, paid volunteering days and wellbeing initiatives.
We are proud to be an equal opportunities employer. This means that we do not discriminate on the basis of anyone’s race, religion, colour, national origin, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, age, marital status, veteran status, pregnancy or disability, or any other basis protected under applicable law. Conforming with applicable law, we can reasonably accommodate applicants' and employees' religious practices and beliefs, as well as mental health or physical disability needs.
Please take a moment to read this privacy notice carefully, as it describes what personal information London Stock Exchange Group (LSEG) (we) may hold about you, what it’s used for, and how it’s obtained, your rights and how to contact us as a data subject.
If you are submitting as a Recruitment Agency Partner, it is essential and your responsibility to ensure that candidates applying to LSEG are aware of this privacy notice.",,https://www.glassdoor.co.in/Overview/W-EI_IE11860.htm,Product Management
