Want to make a significant business impact and build a platform from ground up? If so, here is an opportunity tailored for you. It’s no secret that Amazon relies on its technology to deliver millions of packages every day to its customers – on time, with low cost. We, Transportation Engineering Systems \-Tech Innovation (TITANS), build the software solutions to automate our network change management workflows and enable optimization of the network plan. Our mission is to build the most efficient and optimal transportation system on the planet, using our engineering muscle as our biggest advantage. Our team, TITANS, builds the technology that enables configuration and planning automation to reduce operational overhead and increasing velocity for network plan generation.
Key job responsibilities
You will lead the transportation network planning automation product roadmap, business requirements/user story definition and Go To Market rollout. This role is inherently cross\-functional; you will work closely with software developers, supply chain planners, UI design, and finance to enhance the customer experience and deliver on product ROI. We are looking for a highly analytical, resourceful, customer focused, team\-oriented individual who has the ability to work independently under time constraints to meet deadlines. He or she will have a proven track record in taking on end\-to\-end ownership and successfully delivering results in a fast\-paced and dynamic business environment.
A day in the life
Lead high\-visibility, cross\-team initiatives including scoping, requirement gathering, technical design, implementation, and launch phases. This includes evaluating and recommending technical solutions to meet customer requirements, ensuring long\-term scalability, and meeting project timelines
Identify system and process deficiencies and lead the charge to drive meaningful change. This includes writing effective narratives and presenting them to Directors and VP's
About the team
TESS manages transportation network configuration by working with different internal stakeholders and systems, to deliver desired business outcomes. The North America Transportation Systems engineering team (TITANS) is a sub org within TESS and owns the development of software products for config and transportation planning automation.
  

