### **Job Description**


**Job Title** \- Technical Product Manager
  

**Function** \- Uttar Pradesh Building or Other Construction Workers Welfare Board  

**Location** \- Lucknow, Uttar Pradesh  

**Qualifications** \- Bachelors/Masters with relevant work experience **About Indus Action**  

At Indus Action, we seek empathetic, driven, and action\-oriented team members who share our mission of making welfare access sustainable and frictionless for vulnerable citizens. We collaborate with both the state (Sarkar) and communities (Samaaj) to drive meaningful change.  


We prioritize an inclusive, equitable work environment with transparent policies and a supportive culture. As a Deliberately Developmental Organization (DDO), we foster growth through cross functional learning and a no\-door policy, promoting open collaboration across all levels.  


If you're passionate about building impact at scale, experimenting, and learning joyfully, Indus Action is the place for you! **Position Summary**  

The North Zone operations team is at an exciting stage of launching new projects in Uttar Pradesh. Indus Action has signed an MoU with The Government of Uttar Pradesh (GoUP) to transform the delivery of social security benefits to millions of construction and unorganized sector workers across the state. This partnership marks a significant step toward digital governance and enhanced social  


protection. Through this collaboration, Indus Action will support the GoUP in modernizing the state’s worker welfare system by implementing digital solutions and streamlined processes. The initiative will focus on benefits delivered through the Building and Other Construction Workers (BoCW) Board and the Unorganized Workers (UoW) Social Security Board.  


Indus Action is looking for a professional who can take ownership of critical technological aspects of these projects and support the state lead in driving towards crucial outputs and outcomes. The Technical Product Manager will be working with the technology vendor and the technical team of the board to work on different technical products owned by the board for workers registration, claims access and Access collection.The role may also involve supporting operations in other states in the North zone as per project requirements. **Role and Responsibilities**  

The primary responsibilities would include:  

* Manage and oversee projects from time, scope, budget, and risk perspective
* Create, review and monitor project plans and track deliverables
* Work closely and actively with different teams to understand their requirements
* Hold regular technical team meetings with the vendor to determine progress and address any questions or challenges regarding projects
* Prepare and present progress reports for senior management and other stakeholders in the government department
* As an individual coordinator \- take up some technical tasks for delivery and completion

### **Requirements**

**Requirements**  

**Skills and Qualifications**  

* The applicant must be a graduate (BE in CS or IT preferred) with at least 5 years of work experience preferably in the social sector, with at least 2\+ years of project management and end\-to\-end delivery experience
* Excellent leadership abilities, interpersonal and communications skills
* Attention to detail with the ability to problem\-solve under pressure
* An individual who is a go\-getter and who can strategize and implement large\-scale programs
* Able to work across teams and translating government briefs to tech team deliverables
* Candidates who have partnered with the government and built relations to drive large\-scale projects for 1\+ year shall be preferred
* Should be well versed with principles of designing thinking, planning and execution, budget management, quality control, and monitoring and evaluation
* Capable of understanding technology to set up MIS systems and envisioning the scope that technology can play to make the implementation smoother
* A strong local understanding \- of language (Hindi), culture, terrain
* Experience in working with technologies such as HTML, PHP, ASP.Net, MVC, Java Script, jQuery, SQL SERVER 2012, and RESTful web API (at least a few of these)

 **Behavioral Competencies and Values*** **Citizen\-Focused Mindset:** Upholding the principle of placing the vulnerable citizen at the center of every initiative
* **Entrepreneurial Energy:** Showcasing ownership of time and resources to yield solutions
* **Dealing with Ambiguity**: Maintaining grace under pressure and showcasing a progressive approach
* **Growth Mindset:** Perceiving every experience as a learning curve and an opportunity for growth
* **Collaboration:** Cultivating productive partnerships internally and externally.

 **Language** \- Ability to read and speak Hindi fluently is essential### **Benefits**

**Compensation**  

The compensation will be based on Indus Action's compensation bench marking rubric. The  


compensation range will depend on the qualifications, experience, and fit for the role.  

The candidate would need to use his/her own laptop and the organization will bear the annual  


maintenance cost up to INR 12,000 per year as per actuals.",,https://www.glassdoor.co.in/Overview/W-EI_IE1362877.htm,Product Management
