gd-1009706189415,glassdoor,https://www.glassdoor.co.in/job-listing/j?jl=1009706189415,,Technology Product Manager - Vice President - Technical Product Owner,Morgan Stanley,Bengaluru,2025-04-11,,360000.0,755000.0,INR,False,"**Job Description**
-------------------

#### **Employment Type**


Full time#### **Job Level**


Vice President#### **Posted Date**


Apr 10, 2025**Technology Product Manager \- Vice President \- Technical Product Owner**

**Profile Description**


We’re seeking someone to join our team as (Vice President) as a Product Manager for our Cloud, Platform Security and Developer Enablement team in Cyber. Our Product team ensures we deliver meaningful security outcomes, and partner successfully across the Morgan Stanley Enterprise Technology organizations.

**CDRR Technology**


The Cybersecurity organization's mission is to create an agile, adaptable organization with the skills and expertise needed to defend against increasingly sophisticated adversaries. This will be achieved by maintaining sound capabilities to identify and protect our assets, proactively assessing threats and vulnerabilities and detecting events, ensuring resiliency through our ability to respond to and recover from incidents and building awareness and increase vigilance while continually developing our cyber workforce.

**Technical Product Owner/Manager**


This is a Vice President position that defines the product vision, prioritizing features, and ensuring the successful delivery of high\-quality technical solutions.


Morgan Stanley is an industry leader in financial services, known for mobilizing capital to help governments, corporations, institutions, and individuals around the world achieve their financial goals.  

  

At Morgan Stanley India, we support the Firm’s global businesses, with critical presence across Institutional Securities, Wealth Management, and Investment management, as well as in the Firm’s infrastructure functions of Technology, Operations, Finance, Risk Management, Legal and Corporate \& Enterprise Services. Morgan Stanley has been rooted in India since 1993, with campuses in both Mumbai and Bengaluru. We empower our multi\-faceted and talented teams to advance their careers and make a global impact on the business. For those who show passion and grit in their work, there’s ample opportunity to move across the businesses for those who show passion and grit in their work.  

  

Interested in joining a team that’s eager to create, innovate and make an impact on the world? Read on…

**What you’ll do in the role:**


This role requires an outgoing individual who can collaborate with empathy and communicate with clarity across a matrixed organization of technical staff, risk professionals and senior leaders. The role reports to the Head of Product for Cloud \& Platform Security and Developer Enablement.

**Responsibilities:**

* Lead customer and stakeholder discovery, and partnership.
* Drive the management, socialization, and evolution of the product roadmap.
* Enable the engineering team to work in an agile manner, with clear direction and feedback on priorities and deliverables.
* Ensure the end\-to\-end delivery of the product roadmap with collaboration across teams, including the identification and communication of dependencies and risks.
* Ensure the individual product strategy is aligned and integrated within our wider organization strategy.
* Understand the industry and market your product is in and apply that knowledge to customer interactions and the product roadmap.
* Build and maintain customer community and engagement for the product.
* Champion the team’s customer successes.

**What you’ll bring to the role:**

**Required:**

* Experience within Product Management.
* A technical background that enables probing conversations with customers and discussion with the product engineering team.
* Experienced within a modern software engineering environment and the software development lifecycle.
* Experience in building relationships and partnerships with key stakeholders.
* Experience in delivering outcomes in matrix organizations, influencing partners and stakeholders.
* Ability to facilitate collaboration across teams and roles.
* Strong attention to detail and quality, with excellent written and verbal communication skills.
* Experience in delivering within an agile development environment.

**Desired:**

* Experienced working with Key Management and Cryptographic Services
* Experienced in delivering products/solutions/services within the developer ecosystem.
* Experienced working in large complex organizations within a highly regulated industry.
* Experienced in delivering products/solutions/services in Public / Private Cloud environments.

**WHAT YOU CAN EXPECT FROM MORGAN STANLEY:**


We are committed to maintaining the first\-class service and high standard of excellence that have defined Morgan Stanley for over 89 years. Our values \- putting clients first, doing the right thing, leading with exceptional ideas, committing to diversity and inclusion, and giving back \- aren’t just beliefs, they guide the decisions we make every day to do what's best for our clients, communities and more than 80,000 employees in 1,200 offices across 42 countries. At Morgan Stanley, you’ll find an opportunity to work alongside the best and the brightest, in an environment where you are supported and empowered. Our teams are relentless collaborators and creative thinkers, fueled by their diverse backgrounds and experiences. We are proud to support our employees and their families at every point along their work\-life journey, offering some of the most attractive and comprehensive employee benefits and perks in the industry. There’s also ample opportunity to move about the business for those who show passion and grit in their work.


Morgan Stanley is an equal opportunities employer. We work to provide a supportive and inclusive environment where all individuals can maximize their full potential. Our skilled and creative workforce is comprised of individuals drawn from a broad cross section of the global communities in which we operate and who reflect a variety of backgrounds, talents, perspectives, and experiences. Our strong commitment to a culture of inclusion is evident through our constant focus on recruiting, developing, and advancing individuals based on their skills and talents.",,https://www.glassdoor.co.in/Overview/W-EI_IE2282.htm,Product Management
gd-1009705796654,glassdoor,https://www.glassdoor.co.in/job-listing/j?jl=1009705796654,,Technical Product Manager,Equifax,Pune,2025-04-11,,288000.0,680000.0,INR,False,"Equifax is seeking a Global Technical Product Manager who has experience with both Business and Technical responsibilities on large platforms, bridging the gaps between business stakeholders and software development teams by writing business requirements, understanding technical impacts, and focusing on global scale capabilities.


As a Global Product Manager of InterConnect® Platforms, you will help to drive the product strategy and roadmaps, while executing on the Initiatives for the platform for various regions around the globe. InterConnect® is Equifax’s flagship online decision platform that automates the orchestration of data, analytical models and decision policies for lending institutions. It is supported by several applications, many of which this role will be responsible for managing. The right candidate will have a technical background with strong experience managing UI applications and workflow services, with at least some exposure to MLOps and data modeling (AI/ML). The right candidate must also be experienced in gathering business requirements from markets and internal user groups remotely, with the ability to tie these requirements to the platform.


### **What You’ll Do**

**Product Strategy:**

* Understand the overall market for the InterConnect platform, working closely with internal stakeholders and external customers
* Demonstrate deep understanding of customer needs through market research and analysis
* Lead market validation through review and testing of concepts with existing and prospective customers (voice of customer, customer advisory boards, etc.)
* Contribute to business cases and budget planning activities
* Collaborate with business unit product leaders to tie product deliverables to GTM efforts

**Product Roadmaps and Requirements:**

* Drive prioritization of strategic platform initiatives
* Lead requirements definition for product development, understanding product trade\-offs and driving alignment
* Manage market feedback efforts to drive product direction
* Assess and plan the product’s future lifecycle, to include enhancement and sunsetting
* Collaborate with product owners to break down strategic initiatives into epics and features for the platform
* Facilitate ideation and brainstorming sessions/workshops with stakeholders and your team to solve problems

**Execution:**

* Foster innovation by bringing up new problems and encouraging new ways to solve existing problems
