· Client Relationship Management:

i. Build, develop, and maintain long\-term relationships with new and existing clients.

ii. Understand clients' requirements, provide product recommendations, and create tailored quotations.

· Exhibition Representation:

i. Represent the company at leading national and international plastic exhibitions such as Plastindia, Plastivision, Plastfocus, Indplas, Hiplex, Kplex, and others.

ii. Promote the company’s products and services, generate leads, and network with potential clients and partners at exhibitions.

· Client Meetings \& Business Travel:

i. Travel as required to meet with clients and potential customers, both domestically and internationally.

ii. Conduct face\-to\-face meetings to understand client needs, offer solutions, and close business deals.

· Machine Trials \& Demonstrations:

i. Provide detailed information about machinery during client trials or demonstrations, ensuring all technical and operational queries are addressed.

ii. Support customers during the machine trial phase, helping to ensure smooth operation and satisfaction.

· Client Visits \& Company Tours:

i. Organize and facilitate plant visits for customers or potential clients, offering them an in\-depth understanding of the company’s manufacturing process, product quality, and capabilities.

· Documentation \& Reporting:

i. Maintain detailed records of all client interactions, including inquiries, quotations, and communications.

ii. Prepare regular reports on sales activities, lead generation, and market trends.

· Communication \& Market Intelligence:

i. Act as a key point of contact between the company and its clients, ensuring effective communication and resolution of any concerns.

ii. Provide regular updates and insights into market trends and customer feedback to help refine product offerings and marketing strategies

**Requirements and skills**

· Plastic graduated or Post graduate with MBA.

· SKILL REQUIRED Communication skill (English/Hindi/Any other language).

· MS Office (Specially Excel, PPT).

· CRM Software.

· Demonstrable experience in marketing together with the potential and attitude required to learn

· Proven experience in identifying target audiences and in creatively devising and leading across channels marketing campaigns that engage, educate and motivate

· Solid knowledge of website analytics tools.

· Experience in setting up and optimizing Google Adwords campaigns

· Numerically literate, comfortable working with numbers, making sense of metrics and processing figures with spreadsheets

· A sense of aesthetics and a love for great copy and witty communication

· Up\-to\-date with the latest trends and best practices in online marketing and measurement

**What We Offer:**

· Competitive salary and yearly performance appraisal

· Friendly and supportive work environment

· Opportunities for growth and career development

· Training and continuous learning program

Job Type: Full\-time

