gd-1009703812204,glassdoor,https://www.glassdoor.co.in/job-listing/j?jl=1009703812204,,Senior BA/Product Manager,SourceFuse,,2025-04-10,,,,,True,"**Job Information:**
--------------------



Work Experience: 5\+ years  

Industry: IT Services  

Job Type: FULL TIME  

Location: Remote, India


**Key Responsibilities:**
-------------------------


**Strategic Navigator: Chart the Course of Product Innovation**

  


* Pioneer solutions by crafting razor\-sharp user stories and requirements that align with our overall PARIS product vision, ensuring every feature solves real problems for our of vessels and seafarers.
* Decode stakeholder needs —transform vague requests into crystal\-clear requirements using critical thinking, separating “wants” from mission\-critical objectives and needs.
* Shape the future : Partner with Product Managers to evolve the product roadmap, balancing ambition with feasibility while challenging assumptions to future\-proof our PARIS ecosystem.
* Anticipate storms before they hit : Proactively identify risks, gaps, and opportunities to steer projects clear of icebergs and toward seamless execution.

  


**Collaborative Architect: Build Bridges Between Vision and Reality**

  


* Orchestrate cross\-functional crews : Lead dynamic partnerships with tech, operations, and external stakeholders to map needs, negotiate priorities, and align solutions with strategic North Star.
* Champion change : Design and steer rollout strategies for new products, ensuring smooth adoption through training, communication, and stakeholder engagement—because innovation only matters if it’s embraced.
* Engineer efficiency : Spot bottlenecks in workflows and processes, then implement upgrades that keep our product development engine running like a well\-oiled ship’s engine room.

  


**Agile Problem\-Solver: Turn Data into Decisive Action**

  


* Master the art of triage : Juggle multiple high\-stakes projects with finesse, prioritising tasks like a captain navigating through shifting tides—always keeping the end goal in sight.
* Unlock insights : Dive into user feedback and UX analytics to dissect what’s working, what’s not, and why , turning raw data into actionable strategies that elevate product performance.
* Mentor the next wave : Guide other Business Analysts with your expertise, fostering a culture of excellence where clear thinking, rapid iteration, and collaboration are the compass for success.

**Experience \& Qualifications:**
---------------------------------


* 5\+ years of experience working in a Business Analysis role in developing repeatable, scalable IT products.
* Effective and confident communication in written and spoken English – getting messages across clearly and concisely.
* Strong mindset on understanding the use of data to help drive prioritisation – demonstrated through the use of either:
* Advanced Excel skills, or.
* Use of database skills such as SQL and ElasticSearch or Google Analytics for UX analytics.
* Led change management initiatives across a large department / company to land new capability smoothly and effectively.
* Demonstration of influencing senior stakeholders (Director level including C\-Level).
* Evidence of mentoring other Business Analysts to help them grow and reach their potential Experience of independent working – ability to drive an initiative forward with limited guidance.

**Desirable:**
--------------


* Qualification in process mapping (such as Lean Six Sigma).
* Maritime / Shipping industry experience would be a huge plus – or similar industries such as Aviation.
* Proficient problem\-solving skills including ability to resolve complex problems using data or tools like Google Analytics.

**Competencies:**
-----------------


* **Analysis and Problem Solving (Level 3\):** Uses a systematic approach to root cause analysis on complex problems to identify underlying trends and put forward well\-thought\-out solutions to address the causes and reduce risk.
* **Listening and Communicating (Level 3\):** Is effective in communicating his vision with a wider audience. A good communicator knows when to use which channel, and which tone of voice in order to drive maximum impact.
* **Collaboration, Inclusion \& Teamwork (Level 2\):** A good team player that is personable, friendly, polite and takes the time to know people. Helps new colleagues and visitors feel welcome. Mentors and encourages junior members.
* **Customer Focus (Level 3\):** Proactive in maintaining relationships and managing customer expectations effectively. Takes a partnership approach to solve problems and improve service standards using data to define continuous improvement.
* **Planning \& Organising (Level 2\):** Uses the supplied tools for structured planning for optimal time use. Balances competing priorities. Promptly updates people when plans change and keep updated on progress. Adjusts own plans based on FML strategies and plans.
* **Initiative (Level 3\):** Always looks for opportunities to improve efficiency and effectiveness in their own and other peoples work backed by clear rationale and benefits to the business. Role models desired change behaviour and uses external best practice as reference.
* **Accountability (Level 2\):** Responsible for delivering own work without unnecessary supervision. Always demonstrates integrity and ethical behaviour being a role model for others. Invites constructive feedback adjusting actions accordingly. Thinks through mistakes made and finds ways to prevent reoccurrence.
* **Resilience and managing wellbeing (Level 1\):** Is willing to take on additional unplanned urgent tasks when required without sacrificing performance standards. Knows how to priories and break down tasks, and when to escalate to his managed to manage pressure.
* **Adaptability (Level 2\):** Seeks to understand the rationale for changes looking for different perspectives to facilitate and positively contribute to the initiatives within the team and themselves.
**Interview Process**
---------------------


* Technical Assessment
* Technical Round",,https://www.glassdoor.co.in/Overview/W-EI_IE378538.htm,Product Management
gd-1009704290890,glassdoor,https://www.glassdoor.co.in/job-listing/j?jl=1009704290890,,Manager Product Management,UKG,Noida,2025-04-10,,271667.0,765000.0,INR,False,"Job Description

#### **Job ID**


MANAG012468#### **Employment Type**


Regular#### **Work Style**


hybrid#### **Location**


Noida,UP,India#### **Travel**


Up to 25%#### **Role**


Manager Product Management
Company Overview



With 80,000 customers across 150 countries, UKG is the largest U.S.\-based private software company in the world. And we’re only getting started. Ready to bring your bold ideas and collaborative mindset to an organization that still has so much more to build and achieve? Read on.

  



At UKG, you get more than just a job. You get to work with purpose. Our team of U Krewers are on a mission to inspire every organization to become a great place to work through our award\-winning HR technology built for all.

  



Here, we know that you’re more than your work. That’s why our benefits help you thrive personally and professionally, from wellness programs and tuition reimbursement to U Choose — a customizable expense reimbursement program that can be used for more than 200\+ needs that best suit you and your family, from student loan repayment, to childcare, to pet insurance. Our inclusive culture, active and engaged employee resource groups, and caring leaders value every voice and support you in doing the best work of your career. If you’re passionate about our purpose — people —then we can’t wait to support whatever gives you purpose. We’re united by purpose, inspired by you.



We have a great opportunity for a Manager, Product Management to lead a team focused on product infrastructure within our Pro WFM Suite. Specifically, this Manager, Product Management will lead a team of Product Managers, coaching and developing the team to identify, design, deliver and optimize solutions for an existing product that’s used by millions of global employees each month within our human capital management and workforce management applications.  

This will include ongoing collaboration with partners in all their forms: external customers such as Buyers, Admin users, HR users, employees along with internal customers who implement and deliver the products that this team will develop and launch. The role will balance between coach and contributor: coaching developing and managing an existing team of Product Managers while contributing as a product lead for cross\-functional development teams as needed on a mature global product.  

As a Manager, Product Management, your focus is on working with teams, people issues, and alignment. To succeed at this, you will have to take a step back and look at the bigger picture to optimize processes and improve team performance. Communication, leadership, and collaboration skills are necessary to succeed in this role as you are tasked to constantly communicate with customers (internal and external) and team members to identify previously unseen challenges and possible opportunities. It is a Manager, Product Management’s role to create consensus locally with impacted teams and around the larger company.  

This individual will be responsible to help shape and execute the overall vision of the product to incrementally deliver value to our customers, while learning from, and along with, our customers, partners and the Product teams that you will support. You will manage this product and ensure each product release is successful by fostering team collaboration, continuous improvement and representing the voice of the customer. You will own the direction of features and clearly define the product metric goals and the right mechanisms to collect, track, report and react to the data, demonstrating a balance of qualitative and quantitative observations to fuel ongoing learning and customer centricity.  

  

* Strong discipline in the use and positioning of AI technologies

  

5\+ years experience leading product management teams with track record of developing and coaching Product Managers through ambiguous problems  

* 5\+ years experience as a Senior Product Manager or Product Manager on a scaling SaaS application in an Agile development environment
* Demonstrated experience in developing customer centricity and outcomes delivery through matrixed cross\-functional Product Development teams
* Ability to create and embody a culture of “customer first” in approaching user and business problems
* Strong use of analytics, user research and business cases to drive decisions and improve products in an enterprise SaaS setting
* Comfortable and experienced presenting to various audiences and levels
* Track record of balancing between discovering new product opportunities and delivering world\-class product experiences

  

PREFERRED  

* Experience working with globally distributed teams
* Demonstrated experience in enterprise SAAS product launches

  

* Deep knowledge of SAAS infrastructure and Component Applications
* Ability to use data to help inform and prioritize product decisions and priorities
* Functional and technical knowledge of Workforce Management and Human Capital Management software
* Experience working with both technical and business user communities
* Comfort with the ambiguity that comes with building new products from zero to mature adoption
  



Where we’re going

  



UKG is on the cusp of something truly special. Worldwide, we already hold the \#1 market share position for workforce management and the \#2 position for human capital management. Tens of millions of frontline workers start and end their days with our software, with billions of shifts managed annually through UKG solutions today. Yet it’s our AI\-powered product portfolio designed to support customers of all sizes, industries, and geographies that will propel us into an even brighter tomorrow!

  



UKG is proud to be an equal opportunity employer and is committed to promoting diversity and inclusion in the workplace, including the recruitment process.

  



Disability Accommodation in the Application and Interview Process



For individuals with disabilities that need additional assistance at any point in the application and interview process, please email UKGCareers@ukg.com",,https://www.glassdoor.co.in/Overview/W-EI_IE7900.htm,Product Management
