* Work closely with developers and designers to translate business requirements into technical
* solutions and ensure flawless execution.
* Plan and execute initiatives, balancing business objectives with technical feasibility
* Analyze data metrics, user behavior, and technical KPIs to identify optimization opportunities.
* Act as the bridge between technical teams and business stakeholders, ensuring clear
* communication and alignment.

  

Who you are?


* 4\+ years of experience in product management.
* Hands\-on experience in performance marketing and website optimization is an advantage.
* Strong ability and comfort in working with engineering teams.
* Proven track record of managing projects and delivering measurable results.
* Strong analytical skills and the ability to leverage data to inform decisions.
* Excellent communication and collaboration skills to work effectively across cross\-functional
* teams
* A background in website marketing or performance marketing is highly preferred.

Note:


* At Whatfix, we thrive on the power of collaboration, innovation, and human connection. We strongly believe that working together in our office (five days a week) fosters open communication, builds a sense of community, fuels innovation, and enables us to achieve our collective goals effectively.
* We strive to live and breathe our Cultural Principles and encourage employees to demonstrate some of these core values \- Customer First; Empathy; Transparency; Fail Fast and scale Fast; No Hierarchies for Communication; Deep Dive and innovate; Trust, Do it as you own it;

