gd-1009704001186,glassdoor,https://www.glassdoor.co.in/job-listing/j?jl=1009704001186,,Sr. Product UX Designer,Codecademy,Hyderābād,2025-04-10,,475000.0,870000.0,INR,False,"**We are NYC based, but remote friendly unless specified.**



Hello, World! Codecademy is on a mission to build inspiring careers in technology through engaging, accessible, and interactive online coding education.



Our learners have gone on to start new jobs, launch new companies, and lead new lives thanks to their work with Codecademy, and our platform has transformed the way businesses develop and retain their teams.



Since 2011, our team has grown to over 200 employees serving 50\+ million learners from 190\+ countries. We’ve raised over $82M in venture capital funding from top investors including Prosus, Owl Ventures, Union Square Ventures, Y Combinator, and more\-which gives us the capital to get stuff done in an impactful way.



Join us to help build a business that empowers tens of millions of people to lead better lives!

  

**This role is for India specific hiring, only candidates from India region should apply.**


**Role Overview:**



As a Senior Product Designer at Codecademy, you’ll take ownership of an entire product area or business unit, leading design solutions that impact our learners globally. You will play a key role in crafting intuitive, engaging, and user\-centered designs that elevate our platform. You will collaborate with cross\-functional teams to define and solve complex challenges, contribute to design strategy, and help shape the overall product direction. This is an exciting opportunity to use your expertise to shape the future of online education for individuals, small groups and business clients.

  



**Key Responsibilities:**

  



**Product Design Leadership \& Ownership:**



* Lead the design of a major product area or business unit, taking full ownership of user experiences and ensuring consistency across touchpoints.
* Define scope and success criteria for the product areas you own, with little to no oversight.
* Own design files for large portions of the user experience, ensuring a seamless and cohesive flow throughout the product.
* Regularly solve complex, high\-impact problems and refine user flows to ensure the best possible experience for learners.
**Collaboration \& Strategy:**



* Work closely with Product Managers, Engineers, and other stakeholders to ensure your designs align with the team’s goals, business objectives, and user needs.
* Ability to collaborate with stakeholders in US time zones
* Contribute to shaping projects based on predefined strategies, selecting appropriate tactics to ensure alignment with overarching business goals.
* Co\-lead large teams and drive design decisions that influence the direction of the product and business.
* Participate proactively in cross\-functional meetings and contribute to the overall design strategy.
* Collaborate closely with our local team in India and other remote teams in the US, ensuring a strong and unified approach to product design.
**Design Process \& Execution:**



* Contribute to the refinement and evolution of Codecademy’s design processes, ensuring consistency and innovation across the product team.
* Leverage high technical proficiency to create detailed, high\-fidelity prototypes and assets, while managing design specifications.
* Ensure that the user experience is not only visually compelling but also intuitive, accessible, and aligned with business objectives.
**Mentorship \& Growth:**



* Assist junior designers with developing their craft, guiding them through design challenges, and promoting best practices in design process.
* Contribute to the culture of experimentation, critique, and continuous learning within the design team.
* Actively share knowledge, advocate for user\-centered design practices, and help elevate the craft across the team.
* Manage up by contributing insights into strategy, design, and process improvements to senior leadership.
**Qualifications:**



* 5–8 years of experience in product design, with a proven track record of leading successful design projects from concept to launch.
* Expertise in UX/UI design, interaction design, and information architecture.
* Strong portfolio that showcases your design process, problem\-solving abilities, and at least several shipped projects.
* Solid experience in SaaS, EdTech, or similar industries, with a deep understanding of business and user needs.
* Proficient in design and research tools such as Figma and UserTesting.
* Experience collaborating with cross\-functional teams, including PMs and Engineers, and leading projects in a collaborative environment.
* Excellent communication skills with the ability to clearly articulate design decisions and rationale to various stakeholders.
* Experience working remotely and managing teams or collaborating across time zones, particularly with global teams (India and US).
* Strong understanding of accessibility principles, user testing, and iterative design.
* Ability to balance design excellence with business and technical constraints.
**Desired Traits:**



* A strong sense of ownership, with the ability to make decisions and drive designs to completion autonomously.
* Passion for mentoring and helping others develop their design skills.
* Highly collaborative and empathetic, with a focus on building strong relationships across teams.
* Strong problem\-solving abilities, with the ability to think critically and creatively in a fast\-paced environment.
* A deep commitment to delivering high\-quality design that is user\-centered and business\-driven.
* Willingness to experiment, challenge norms, and push the boundaries of what’s possible in online learning experiences.
**Why Join Us:**



* Work on meaningful projects that help empower learners and change the future of online education.
* Be part of a diverse, mission\-driven team that values creativity, innovation, and collaboration.
* Flexible, fully remote work environment with a global team.
* Opportunities for career growth and development, with mentorship from senior leaders.
* Competitive compensation and benefits package.
If you are a design leader with a passion for shaping the future of online learning, we would love to hear from you! Apply today to join Codecademy and help us create the next generation of learning tools.



**Equal Employment Opportunity**
--------------------------------



At Codecademy, we are committed to teaching people the skills they need to upgrade their careers. Codecademy aims to educate a richly diverse demographic of learners with our product and in order to accomplish this, we believe our team should reflect that rich diversity. Our company celebrates diversity in all of its forms\- race, gender, color, national origin, marital status, sexuality, religion, veteran status, age, ability, disability status\- and works to create an inclusive workplace where people of all backgrounds and beliefs are empowered to better their futures.",,https://www.glassdoor.co.in/Overview/W-EI_IE792111.htm,Product Management
gd-1009703927354,glassdoor,https://www.glassdoor.co.in/job-listing/j?jl=1009703927354,,Account Manager View Jobs,Swiggy,Mumbai,2025-04-10,,,,,False,"**Way of working: Field/Office :** **Employees will work fulltime from their base location.**

 **About the team:**


Swiggy Dineout is building India’s largest dining out platform that processes more than 100M diners for its partner restaurants across its network for 21000 restaurants in 34 cities and growing. We are striving to augment our consumer promise of enabling unparalleled convenience by helping diners explore restaurants across all categories \- from QSRs, cafes, casual dining, premium, fine dining and more and offer the widest range of offers on restaurant bills through easy payments on the app. We are on a mission to change the way India dines out. If you are a foodie and equally passionate to redefine the experience of dining out, join our team to be a part of the Swiggy ride!


Dineout is present in 34 cities across India and we have partnerships with more than 21,000 restaurant partners where users can save upto 40% on their dining bills when they pay their restaurant bills using the dineout feature on the Swiggy app


Using the Dineout feature on the Swiggy app, users can discover and avail the best deals and discounts at restaurants, cafes, bars, and pubs in their city.


Users can search for their favourite restaurants based on various parameters such as cuisine, location, price range, and availability.


For customers, our vision is to become their default app for all their dining\-out occasions. We intend to do so by building a full stack solution for them to discover restaurants they might like, make a table reservation, make payment, and avail the best discounts/value across restaurants.


For restaurants, our vision is to become their de facto platform of choice to grow their dine\-in business. We aspire to do so by becoming the most cost\-efficient marketing channel for them to build their brand, drive demand and acquire \& engage customers.

**Job Responsibilities:**

* Drive restaurant onboarding for your designated area, Act as a consultant to restaurant partners to manage and mutually grow business,
* You should have a keen interest in the food and beverage industry with a desire to sign up for the best local and national restaurants,
* Be the local market expert: gather restaurant feedback, monitor competitor activity, and provide recommendations for improvements to management and
* Ability to conduct cold calls and walk\-ins, schedule in\-person meetings, and sell the Dineout product portfolio to restaurants.

**Desired Skill:**

* The candidate has to have successfully completed a Bachelor’s degree,
* Freshers with internship or min 6 months of sales experience in consulting, e\-commerce or start\-ups are encouraged to apply,
* The candidate has to be flexible, restaurant owners do not operate on 9\-to\-5 schedules,
* The candidate has to be outgoing and confident in their appearance,
* We are looking for self\-motivated individuals with the ability to work remotely and under pressure and
* The candidate has to be an ‘out\-of\-the\-box thinker and should want to always challenge the status quo.

