gd-1009702273032,glassdoor,https://www.glassdoor.co.in/job-listing/j?jl=1009702273032,,AVP - FP&A Product Manager,NASDAQ,Bengaluru,2025-04-09,,525000.0,1000000.0,INR,False,"Nasdaq Technology is looking for a passionate AVP, to join the Bangalore technology center in India. If Innovation and effectiveness drive you forward this is the place for you!  

  

Nasdaq is continuously revolutionizing markets and undergoing transformations while we adopt new technologies to develop innovative solutions, constantly aiming to rewrite tomorrow. As AVP, FP\&A , you own the portfolio of products offered within Finance and drive cohesiveness across the portfolio. You define the product vision and roadmap with the business.  

  

We are looking for candidates who share those values along with a genuine desire and drive to deliver top technology solutions to today's markets.
Your role and responsibilities:
As FP\&A Product Manager, you are the product visionary for the tools and processes supporting our global FP\&A teams. You ensure that Nasdaq delivers valuable products to our internal stakeholders using agile methodologies to ensure alignment with the business strategy, maximizing value delivery and continuously evaluating and adjusting priorities. You will have responsibility for the products that support both our Corporate and Divisional FP\&A teams, and will be a key part of the Finance Transformation efforts currently underway. You help to define the product vision and roadmap with the business, and efficiently invest in and develop a suite of capabilities that help Nasdaq quickly respond to rapidly changing demands in strategic planning, while fostering a culture of openness and transparency.
In this role, you will partner with a global team to manage the strategy, development, and delivery for Strategic Planning, as well as take part in the execution of several transformation efforts currently underway, balancing stakeholder needs, financial viability, and technical feasibility throughout the product lifecycle.
The Team
Our FP\&A Product Manager reports to our overall Head of Product for Finance \& Workplace who also leads Nasdaq’s Financial Planning \& Analysis function. You will manage the FP\&A products, as well as product delivery leads and business analysts supporting these efforts.
Furthermore, you will:* Ensure Strategic Alignment: Ensure our FP\&A products and processes align with strategic objectives. Develops and drives the products’ long \-term vision, value proposition and thematic goals to create a long\-term vision. Is responsible for understanding client needs, product requirements, and the overall market and translating them to measurable outcomes.
* Execute the Vision: Translate the product strategy into a clear product roadmap, metrics and desired functionality for all stakeholders. Strategically drive the development, launch, and continual support and product improvement while interpreting market trends to identify new opportunities. Effectively influences a global team as part of their daily work and achieves set objectives by executing the product strategy and roadmap.
* Measure Success: Lead the creation and review of key metrics, outcomes, and reporting related to milestones and objectives. Monitor metrics to ensure product remains viable, desirable, feasible to develop. Prepares comprehensive overview of the progress against strategic goals, analyzing key performance metrics, identifying potential risks and opportunities, facilitating discussions to adjust priorities and collaborates with stakeholders to develop actionable plans. Ensures alignment for the direction and overall strategy by conducting quarterly business revies.
* Manage the ecosystem: Collaborate with key external and internal stakeholders, actively engaging them throughout the product lifecycle, managing relationships across the stakeholder base. Coordinates product features or offerings with other Finance pillars where relevant and focus on innovation. Ensure that the appropriate stakeholders are engaged in risk identification and mitigation. Manages risks and impact of the product strategy and roadmap.
* Develop talent: Focus on creating a self\-organizing, autonomous, cross functional team with a shared understanding of the product goals and strategy, empowering them to make decisions and adapt to changing priorities. Create and maintain client visibility for the entire product team. Encourage experimentation, foster continued learning, and tight feedback loops. Leads and mentors the product management team working across the product suite. Leverages agile principles like continuous improvement and iterative feedback loops to optimize talent development within the portfolio of products.
* Direct priorities: Lead all planning, prioritization, improvement, and management activities for the products to provide clients with the best value for their investment. Reevaluate the business value delivered and reprioritize work as appropriate. Manage funding and align capacity with demand to optimize resources across products.
* Lead by example: Champion the team, partners, and external stakeholders to ensure alignment around overall strategy and direction of the product. Attend team demos and team ceremonies (as invited) and model strong leadership behaviours.


We expect you to have:* Experience: At least 18\+ years of experience developing products or managing FP\&A processes.
* Experience: At least 5 plus years working as an Agile Product leader and implementing agile ways of working.
* Financial services experience a plus and financial system product knowledge a plus
* Anaplan Model building experience strongly preferred.
* Education: Degree qualified in Computer Science, Business / Finance or related discipline, or equivalent work experience


Come as You Are
Nasdaq is an equal opportunity employer. We positively encourage applications from suitably qualified and eligible candidates regardless of age, color, disability, national origin, ancestry, race, religion, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity and/or expression, veteran status, genetic information, or any other status protected by applicable law.
We will ensure that individuals with disabilities are provided reasonable accommodation to participate in the job application or interview process, to perform essential job functions, and to receive other benefits and privileges of employment. Please contact us to request an accommodation.",,https://www.glassdoor.co.in/Overview/W-EI_IE12152.htm,Product Management
gd-1009702843351,glassdoor,https://www.glassdoor.co.in/job-listing/j?jl=1009702843351,,Operation Manager Head,TFarm Pvt. Ltd.,Bhubaneshwar,2025-04-09,,25000.0,70000.0,INR,False,"**Job Summary:**

We are looking for an experienced and highly organized Operations Manager to oversee and optimize the day\-to\-day operations of our agricultural business. The ideal candidate will be responsible for managing the logistics, supply chain, production processes, and operational workflows, ensuring that they are efficient, cost\-effective, and aligned with the company’s goals. The Operations Manager will also work closely with various teams to ensure smooth execution and maximize productivity in the agriculture sector.

**Key Responsibilities:**

**Production Management:**

* Operating solvent extraction machineries using skilled operations with high efficiency.
* Supervise the production process, ensuring that agricultural products are produced on time and meet quality standards.
* Work closely with production teams to forecast demand, adjust production schedules, and optimize output.
* Implement effective production planning to meet seasonal fluctuations in demand while ensuring consistent product quality.

**Operations Oversight and Process Improvement:**

* Oversee and manage the day\-to\-day operations of the agricultural business, including production, distribution, and logistics.
* Develop, implement, and continuously improve operational procedures to increase efficiency, reduce waste, and enhance productivity.
* Ensure optimal utilization of resources, including labor, equipment, and materials.
* Monitor key operational metrics and performance indicators to identify areas for improvement.
* Ensure that operations comply with all regulatory requirements, safety standards, and environmental guidelines.

**Supply Chain and Inventory Management:**

* Manage and optimize the supply chain to ensure the timely delivery of raw materials, equipment, and agricultural products.
* Oversee inventory management, ensuring accurate stock levels and minimizing overstocking or stockouts.
* Work with suppliers and vendors to negotiate prices, terms, and delivery schedules to ensure cost\-effective sourcing.
* Monitor and maintain the quality of incoming goods and products, ensuring that they meet industry standards.

**Team Management and Development:**

* Manage and lead a team of operations staff, ensuring clear communication and a collaborative work environment.
* Hire, train, and provide continuous support and development opportunities for team members.
* Set performance goals for the team, monitor progress, and provide constructive feedback to drive improvements.
* Ensure that all team members adhere to operational procedures and safety protocols.

**Budgeting and Financial Management:**

* Assist in preparing and managing operational budgets, ensuring efficient use of resources and adherence to financial targets.
* Monitor operational costs and implement cost\-saving initiatives where possible without compromising quality.
* Evaluate the financial impact of operations strategies and suggest improvements to enhance profitability.

**Health, Safety, and Compliance:**

* Ensure that all operational activities meet safety and environmental standards set by the company and regulatory authorities.
* Develop and implement safety protocols for production and fieldwork to minimize accidents and ensure a safe working environment.
* Conduct regular audits and inspections to ensure compliance with industry standards and regulations.

**Reporting and Data Analysis:**

* Generate and present regular reports on operational performance, production status, inventory levels, and financial metrics to senior management.
* Use data analysis tools to identify trends, predict future operational needs, and recommend strategies for process optimization.
* Track and report on key performance indicators (KPIs) related to operational efficiency, product quality, and cost management.

**Sustainability and Innovation:**

* Work with the management team to implement sustainable agricultural practices and processes.
* Explore new technologies, farming practices, or operational methods to improve efficiency and reduce environmental impact.

**Qualifications:**

* Bachelor’s degree in Agriculture, Business Administration, Operations Management, or a related field.
* 5\+ years of experience in operations management, preferably in the solvent extraction plants and spice industry.
* 5\+ years of sales experience, preferably in the spice or food processing sector.
* Proven leadership skills with the ability to manage and develop sales teams.
* Strong knowledge of the spice industry and market dynamics.
* Excellent communication, negotiation, and interpersonal skills.
* Proficient in Microsoft Office Suite and operational management software.

**Desired Skills:**

* Experience in managing agricultural operations at scale (e.g., large farms, production plants).
* Familiarity with lean manufacturing principles, process optimization, and quality control.
* Ability to implement and manage sustainability initiatives within agricultural operations.
* Knowledge of agricultural equipment, machinery, and technology applications in farming.

