**Phenom Intro:**


Our purpose is to help a billion people find the right work! Phenom is an AI\-Powered talent experience platform that is redefining the HR tech space. We have grown into a global organization with offices in 6 countries and over 1,500 employees. As an HR tech unicorn organization, innovation and creativity is within our DNA. Come help us make every talent moment Phenomenal!

**What you'll do**


Phenom is looking for an experienced **Product Manager** to join our dynamic team and lead the development and enhancement of our SaaS products. The ideal candidate will have a proven track record of managing SaaS products, collaborating with cross\-functional teams, and driving product strategies that align with business goals. You will be responsible for the entire product lifecycle, from ideation to execution, while ensuring seamless stakeholder and customer engagement.

**Key Responsibilities:**

* **Product Strategy \& Roadmap:** Define, develop, and execute product strategies that align with the company’s vision and market needs.
* **Stakeholder Management:** Collaborate with internal and external stakeholders, including executives, customers, and development teams, to gather requirements and prioritize features.
* **Customer Interaction:** Work closely with clients to understand their pain points, gather feedback, and translate their needs into actionable product enhancements.
* **Cross\-functional Collaboration:** Partner with engineering, marketing, sales, and support teams to drive product initiatives and ensure smooth execution. Standard aspects of inbound product management – planning / prioritizing sprints, maintaining and grooming the product backlog with UX and engineering in an agile fashion.
* **Agile Product Development:** Lead agile development cycles, define user stories, and work closely with engineering teams to deliver high\-quality software.
* **Market \& Competitive Analysis:** Stay updated on industry trends, competitor products, and emerging technologies to make data\-driven product decisions.
* **Metrics \& Performance Tracking:** Report on key performance indicators (KPIs) to measure product success and drive continuous improvements as a part of weekly business reviews.
* **Team Leadership \& Management:** Mentor and guide cross\-functional teams, fostering a culture of innovation and accountability.

  

**Work Experience**  

**Qualifications \& Skills:**

* **Experience:** 5\+ years in product management, preferably in a SaaS environment.
* **Customer\-Centric Approach:** Passion for delivering exceptional user experiences and solving customer pain points.
* **Problem\-Solving:** Ability to analyze complex issues and propose effective solutions.
* **Stakeholder Management:** Strong ability to engage with senior stakeholders, clients, and cross\-functional teams.
* **Technical Acumen:** Understanding software development processes, cloud technologies, and Proven track record in managing API and integration\-based product development from concept to launch.
* **Communication Skills:** Excellent verbal and written communication skills with the ability to convey technical concepts to non\-technical audiences.
* **Project Management:** Experience with Agile, Scrum, or Kanban methodologies.
* **Data\-Driven Mindset:** Proficiency in using data analytics tools and techniques to drive product decisions.


**Preferred Qualifications:**

* Experience working in B2B SaaS products.
* Familiarity with tools like Jira, Confluence, Figma, or similar.
* Previous experience in a startup or fast\-paced environment.

**Education:** Full time graduation

**Why Join Us?**

* Opportunity to work on cutting\-edge SaaS products.
* Collaborative and innovative work environment.
* Competitive salary and benefits package.
* Professional growth and career advancement opportunities.


If you are passionate about product management and have a knack for leading SaaS products to success, we’d love to hear from you!

 **Benefits**  

We want you to be your best self and to pursue your passions!

* Health and wellness benefits/programs to support holistic employee health
* Growing organization with career pathing and development opportunities
* Tons of perks and extras in every location for all Phenoms!

**Diversity, Equity, \& Inclusion:**


Our commitment to diversity runs deep! Diversity is essential to building phenomenal teams, products, and customer experiences. Phenom is proud to be an equal opportunity employer taking collective action to build a more inclusive environment where every candidate and employee feels welcomed. We recognize there is more to be done. Our teams are committed to continuous improvement until these powerful ideas are ingrained in our culture for Phenom and employers everywhere!",,https://www.glassdoor.co.in/Overview/W-EI_IE263893.htm,Product Management
