### **About Us**


**The Modern Story**  

It has become imperative for enterprises to derive value from their data. Unfortunately, today’s data landscape is increasingly varied and constantly changing. The rise of IoT, unstructured data volume, and need for data analytics from all departments emphasize the need for a composable data management solution.  

The Modern Data Company was founded to radically simplify how organizations manage, access, and interact with data. Modern’s data operating system, DataOS, unifies all data across silos, at scale. The composable layers of DataOS evolve with your existing technology stack to future\-proof all data initiatives.  

### **Job Description**


### **About the Role**

  

We’re looking for a **Technical Product Manager** to lead the evolution of **DataOS APIs** into first\-class products. You will bring an **API product mindset**—focusing on long\-term value, ease of developer consumption, extensibility, and alignment with business goals. Your work will be critical in shaping how APIs are designed, delivered, documented, and evolved over time across the DataOS platform.

### **Responsibilities**

* **Own the end\-to\-end lifecycle** of DataOS APIs—from strategy and roadmap to delivery and adoption.
* Work closely with API engineers to **design consistent, secure, and scalable APIs** that are easy to consume.
* Collaborate with internal stakeholders and end users to **translate business needs into API product requirements**.
* Define and manage the API product roadmap, ensuring alignment with broader platform and business objectives.
* Promote **best practices in API usability**, including clear documentation, versioning, authentication (OAuth), and developer experience.
* Use API management tools to gain insights into usage patterns, customer adoption, and operational performance.
* Ensure APIs are designed with **future extensibility** in mind—without overengineering or locking into narrow use cases.
* Evangelize the API\-first approach within the organization, fostering a culture of **modularity, reuse, and composability**

### **Requirements**

* **4\+ years** of experience as a **Technical Product Manager**, preferably in platform or API\-focused roles.
* **2\+ years** of hands\-on **API engineering or backend development experience**.
* Strong understanding of REST APIs, authentication protocols (e.g., OAuth), API gateways, and API design principles.
* Track record of **shipping developer\-facing products** with measurable adoption.
* Excellent communication and documentation skills, with a user\-centric and outcome\-driven mindset.
* Experience with API monitoring, analytics, and lifecycle management tools is a plus.

### **Benefits**

**Working at Modern**

  

First and foremost, our value system is sacred to us – HEAT: Humility, Empathy, Accountability and Transparency. Beyond this, we are fond of individuals who are curious, love solving problems and can see the larger picture. We love to take a leap of faith on potential. If you believe you haven’t had the chance to do your life’s best work, Modern is the place for you.

  

Modern embraces competition for great talent. We have been able to get great talent onboard owing to the attractive compensation and benefits we provide, in addition to the upside we share with all our employees in the form of ESOPs. Moreover, our ESOP policies are highly employee\-friendly replicating ethos of some of the best Silicon Valley tech startups. We are committed to making sure our employees create significant value for themselves.",,https://www.glassdoor.co.in/Overview/W-EI_IE5466547.htm,Product Management
