gd-1009702318995,glassdoor,https://www.glassdoor.co.in/job-listing/j?jl=1009702318995,,Product Designer- II,MindTickle,Bengaluru,2025-04-09,,170000.0,210000.0,INR,False,"**Who we are**  

Mindtickle is the market\-leading revenue productivity platform that combines on\-the\-job learning and deal execution to get more revenue per rep. Mindtickle is recognized as a market leader by top industry analysts and is ranked by G2 as the \#1 sales onboarding and training product. We’re honoured to be recognized as a Leader in the first\-ever Forrester Wave™: Revenue Enablement Platforms, Q3 2024! **Job Snapshot**  

As a Product Designer at Mindtickle, you will work on the next generation of sales enablement solutions and solve big problems for companies of all sizes. In this role, you will work actively on our AI initiatives across the platform and drive the UX of key cutting\-edge solutions with product and engineering stakeholders.
### **What’s in it for you?**

* + Design intuitive, AI\-powered sales enablement tools and experiences that empower our sales team
	+ Collaborate with key stakeholders to build consensus and deliver best\-in\-class user experiences
	+ Partner with the research team to discover user needs and validate your design solutions
	+ Deliver high\-quality design consistently, and be an expert in feedback processes
	+ Apply core visual design principles (typography, color theory, composition, hierarchy) to create compelling and effective interfaces
	+ Evangelize design best practices, including impactful presentation skills and effectively articulating cohesive design decisions to non\-design audiences
	+ Create high\-fidelity Figma prototypes to demonstrate ideas and get stakeholder buy\-in
	+ Effectively manage time, work proactively, prioritize tasks, all to meet deadlines

### **What we are looking for**

* + Strong portfolio featuring product design work demonstrating complex problem\-solving and solid design fundamentals
	+ 4\+ years of experience in designing web applications (preferably B2B SaaS)
	+ Bachelor’s degree in Product Design, Graphic Design, Human\-Computer Interaction, or a related field
	+ Proficient in user\-centered design processes
	+ Skilled in high\-fidelity pixel\-perfect UI and interaction design in Figma
	+ Actively seeks customer insights and deeper problem understanding,
	+ Experienced thinking strategically about product vision, and partners effectively with product managers
	+ Strong understanding of design processes and the full development cycle for web applications
	+ Knowledge of HTML, CSS \& JavaScript fundamentals (Preferred)
	+ Background in designing conversational interfaces or AI assistants (Preferred)
	+ A link to your portfolio is mandatory to be considered for this role.

### **What we offer**

* + Opportunity to shape Design the integrated experience layer across the platform.
	+ Collaborative environment with a direct impact on product strategy
	+ Work alongside top design professionals, sharpening your skills and expanding your design acumen.
	+ Hybrid work arrangements
	+ Competitive compensation
  

**Our culture \& accolades**  

As an organization, it’s our priority to create a highly engaging and rewarding workplace. We offer tons of awesome perks and many opportunities for growth.  

Our culture reflects our employee's globally diverse backgrounds along with our commitment to our customers, and each other, and a passion for excellence. We live up to our values, DAB, Delight your customers, Act as a Founder, and Better Together.  

Mindtickle is proud to be an Equal Opportunity Employer.  

All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, colour, religion, sex, national origin, disability, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law.  

Your Right to Work \- In compliance with applicable laws, all persons hired will be required to verify identity and eligibility to work in the respective work locations and to complete the required employment eligibility verification document form upon hire.",,https://www.glassdoor.co.in/Overview/W-EI_IE543637.htm,Product Management
gd-1009703030785,glassdoor,https://www.glassdoor.co.in/job-listing/j?jl=1009703030785,,Senior Product Designer,YipitData (Alternative),Bengaluru,2025-04-09,,624000.0,999678.0,INR,False,"**About YipitData:**



YipitData is the market\-leading data and analytics firm. We analyze billions of data points every day to provide accurate, detailed insights across industries, including consumer brands, technology, software, and healthcare.



Our insights team uses proprietary technology to identify, license, clean, and analyze the data that many of the world's largest investment funds and corporations depend on. We raised $475M from The Carlyle Group at a valuation over $1B, further accelerating our growth and market impact.



We have been recognized multiple times as one of Inc's Best Workplaces. As a fast\-growing company backed by The Carlyle Group and Norwest Venture Partners, YipitData is driven by a people\-first culture rooted in mastery, ownership, and transparency.



With offices in New York, Austin, Miami, Denver, Mountain View, Seattle, Hong Kong, Shanghai, Beijing, Guangzhou, and Singapore, we continue to expand our reach and impact across global markets.


**About The Role:**



We are looking for a Senior Product Designer to join our Product Experience team. As a Senior Product Designer, you will lead our product through its most complex UX challenges and discover how to delight our customers with intuitive, actionable experiences that fit seamlessly into their workflows. You will deeply orient yourself around actual customers, become an expert in their user journeys, and mold our product's experience based on that expertise. This is a role that combines aspects of research \& design. You will own projects from start to finish while being tightly coupled with Product \& Engineering to ensure your work gets deployed with tangible impact.


**Work Hour Expectations:** This is a fully remote based in India. We expect hires to work between 12:30pm \- 9:30pm IST at least 3 days per week; work hours on other days are flexible (e.g., \~11am \- 8pm IST).


**As Our Senior Product Designer, You Will:**


* **UX Design:** Own the end\-to\-end design process from discovery to production. This process may include research proposals, information architecture, interactive prototypes, and high\-fidelity artifacts that Engineering can deliver.
* **Prototyping and Testing:** Plan and conduct tests to validate the usability and value of your solutions as quickly as possible. Iteratively improve the user experience until we're confident it will delight our customers.
* **User Research:** Conduct research to deepen our understanding of our user personas, discover opportunities to solve problems that matter, and propose solutions that will generate value for our customers.
* **UX Strategy:** Influence the vision and strategy of our product's experience by analyzing, consolidating, and synthesizing what is known about the needs of our customers.
* **Cross\-functional Collaboration:** Collaborate with product managers, engineers, and other stakeholders to refine product strategy and create user\-centric solutions to the most important customer problems.
* **Continuous Improvement:** Seek out and experiment with user\-centered design and research methodologies. Encourage growth, innovation, and creativity within the design org.


**You Are Likely To Succeed If You Have:**


* 5\+ years of experience **designing data applications** that provide analytics and insights in simple and actionable ways.
* Experience designing data analytics applications, including dashboards and data visualizations (this requirement is a high priority!).
* Excellent communication and presentation skills, with the ability to articulate design decisions clearly to a diverse audience.
* Proficiency in design and prototyping tools such as Figma as well as cutting\-edge AI tools to empower you to go faster.
* Excellent user research skills and the ability to translate research findings into tangible design solutions.
* Comfort working in a fast\-paced startup environment.


**What We Offer:**


* Our compensation package includes comprehensive benefits, perks, and a competitive salary.
* We care about your personal life and we mean it. We offer vacation time, parental leave, team events, learning reimbursement, and more!
* Your growth at YipitData is determined by the impact that you are making, not by tenure, unnecessary facetime, or office politics. Everyone at YipitData is empowered to learn, self\-improve, and master their skills in an environment focused on ownership, respect, and trust.


*We are committed to equal employment opportunity regardless of race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, age, marital status, disability, gender, gender identity or expression, or veteran status. We are proud to be an equal\-opportunity employer.*



Job Applicant Privacy Notice



