gd-1009702908631,glassdoor,https://www.glassdoor.co.in/job-listing/j?jl=1009702908631,,Ad Operations Coordinator,Wiley,Noida,2025-04-09,,407500.0,840000.0,INR,False,"**Location: Noida, U.P., India (Hybrid work model \- 8 days at the office a month)**

Our mission is to unlock human potential. We welcome you for who you are and the background you bring, and we embrace individuals who get excited about learning. Bring your experiences, your perspectives, and your passion; it's in our differences that we empower the way the world learns.  



**About the role:**

We are currently seeking a curious and ambitious coordinator to join our team and contribute to a fast\-paced team, offering support and administrative coordination across the digital advertising operations. The perfect candidate will have an understanding of the global advertising ecosystem and the basics in digital display advertising on Google Ad Manager (GAM), plus other ad servers, alongside the ability to carry out reporting of house campaigns. The right candidate will also have a desire to learn more about the business and immerse themselves within the teams to become the 'go\-to' for supporting on larger\-scale projects in a support role.  



**How will you make an impact?**

* Demonstrate willingness to learn all aspects of the advertising business at Wiley.
* Offer support across the business, including reporting, troubleshooting, etc.
* Continually develop market knowledge, insights, and user focus for product development.
* Learn and develop knowledge in relation to the competition, industry standards, best practices, expected outcomes, and other key considerations in advertising technology.
* Work closely with the Product and Technology team/site engineers to QA/troubleshoot ad tech integrations/deployments and platform releases.
* Support with process and workflow improvements for Ad Tech and connected teams \- Sales, Sales support, and Ad Operations.
* Support with the management of technical escalation for troubleshooting to support Ad Ops and Ad Tech coordinators.
Be flexible and accommodating in your approach to administrative tasks across the advertising business.  
* 

**What we are looking for:**

* Must have experience in the digital display advertising industry.
  

Experience within a corporate business (ideally publishing or digital marketing space).
* Knowledge of the publishing industry, research environments, or information services.
* Knowledge of Google Ad Manager (GAM) plus other ad servers is essential.
  

Awareness/experience of Adobe Workfront is desired.
* Solves complex, multidisciplinary problems; uses in\-depth analytical or creative thinking to identify innovative solutions.
* Willingness to learn, achieve, develop, and make an impact in a fast\-paced team.
* Bachelor's Degree (or equivalent) or 2\+ years of experience in ad technology, digital ad operations, or other relevant media/advertising/technology field
* An awareness or understanding of digital ad products, ad measurement, and programmatic advertising
* Experience in analytics, reporting, and the ability to manage reporting tools.

**Why should you join Wiley?**

* The team! You'll be joining a talented group of professionals who are truly passionate about the work we do.
* We embrace you for you! Wiley is committed to attracting and retaining a talented and diverse workforce and fostering a work environment in which all colleagues are valued and can enjoy professional success.
Fantastic well\-being initiatives such as 'Happy Fridays' with the afternoon off during part of the year, flexibility to work from home, fun events and activities throughout the year to get colleagues together, free access to Headspace, and much more!  
* 

**About Wiley:**

Enabling Discovery, Powering Education, Shaping Workforces.


We clear the way for seekers of knowledge, illuminating the path forward for research and education, tearing down barriers to society's advancement, and giving seekers the help they need to turn their steps into strides.


Wiley may have been founded over two centuries ago, but our secret to success remains the same: our people. We are willing to challenge the status quo, move the needle, and innovate. Wiley's headquarters are located in Hoboken, New Jersey, with operations across the globe in more than 40 countries.  



**\*When applying, please attach your updated resume/CV to be considered.**

