The **Flour Mill Purchase Manager** will be responsible for overseeing and managing the procurement processes for all materials needed for flour production, including raw grains, packaging materials, and other supplies. This role requires strong negotiation skills, a keen understanding of the supply chain, and the ability to manage vendor relationships to ensure consistent, cost\-effective supply management.

**Key Responsibilities:**

* **Procurement Management:** Oversee the purchase of raw materials (wheat, grain, additives) and other supplies necessary for mill operations. Ensure materials are available in the right quantity, at the right quality, and on time.
* **Vendor Relations:** Develop and maintain strong relationships with suppliers and vendors. Negotiate prices, terms, and contracts to ensure the best value for the company.
* **Inventory Control:** Monitor and manage inventory levels of raw materials, packaging materials, and spare parts. Ensure that stock levels align with production requirements while avoiding overstocking.
* **Cost Optimization:** Identify and implement cost\-saving initiatives through strategic sourcing, bulk purchasing, and negotiating better terms with suppliers.
* **Supplier Evaluation:** Continuously evaluate supplier performance, including delivery times, quality, and reliability. Address and resolve any issues related to procurement.
* **Quality Assurance:** Work closely with the quality control team to ensure that purchased materials meet company and industry quality standards.
* **Budget Management:** Manage the procurement budget, ensuring that purchasing activities stay within the allocated budget while meeting production needs.
* **Supply Chain Coordination:** Collaborate with other departments, including production and logistics, to ensure smooth flow of materials from suppliers to the production line.
* **Market Research:** Stay updated on market trends, including commodity prices and supply chain challenges. Provide strategic insights to help plan purchasing strategies.
* **Compliance:** Ensure compliance with all relevant regulations, including those related to food safety, sustainability, and industry standards.

