gd-1009700129007,glassdoor,https://www.glassdoor.co.in/job-listing/j?jl=1009700129007,,Lead Product Manager,Cloud Software Group,Bengaluru,2025-04-06,,447000.0,990000.0,INR,False,"**About the Role**  

Citrix is seeking a **Lead Product Manager** to drive the **product roadmap and strategy for the Citrix Workspace app on ChromeOS and HTML5**, with a strong focus on engaging and aligning roadmap priorities with **Google in the CVAD (Citrix Virtual Apps and Desktops) team**. This role is critical in shaping the next\-generation user experience for modern endpoints, enabling secure, seamless, and high\-performance access to virtualized apps and desktops across **cloud, on\-premises, and hybrid infrastructure configurations**.


As the product lead for Workspace on these platforms, you will define the vision and lead cross\-functional collaboration with engineering, UX, customers, partners (notably Google), and field teams to deliver high\-impact solutions that align with enterprise requirements and future trends in cloud and workspace delivery.

 **Job Description/Responsibilities:**

* Lead the product roadmap and strategy for Citrix Workspace app on **ChromeOS and HTML5**, enabling consistent user experiences across **cloud, on\-premises, and hybrid deployments**.
* Drive the **joint roadmap with Google**, representing Citrix’s vision and priorities in cross\-company planning, execution, and partnership forums.
* Work closely with engineering, design, and quality teams to define requirements, manage prioritization, and ensure timely execution.
* Collaborate with customer success, sales engineering, and marketing to drive adoption, evangelize capabilities, and capture feedback.
* Track market developments, conduct competitive analysis, and incorporate insights into strategic planning.
* Influence platform adoption and innovation across enterprise and education segments by aligning with ChromeOS and browser\-based trends.
* Define and track product success metrics; leverage telemetry, customer feedback, and support data for continuous improvement

**Qualifications \& Experience:**

* 7\+ years of experience in Product Management (or equivalent) in enterprise software, virtualization, or cloud workspace platforms.
* A University degree is mandatory (Engineering preferred) and minimum 8 years of prior relevant experience; or Master’s degree (MBA) with 6 years; or PhD with 3 years of experience.
* Experience working with **ChromeOS, browser\-based (HTML5\) applications**, or Google ecosystem products is highly desirable.
* Strong understanding of Citrix Virtual Apps and Desktops (CVAD), Citrix DaaS, and client\-side technologies across **cloud, on\-premises, and hybrid environments**.
* Knowledge of any endpoint platforms like Windows, macOS, Linux, iOS, Android, ChromeOS, and browser technologies.
* Proven ability to lead cross\-functional teams and manage complex stakeholder relationships.
* Strong analytical mindset with experience in data\-driven decision\-making.
* Excellent communication and stakeholder management skills.

**Preferred Skills:**

* Prior experience working with Google, VMware, Microsoft, or similar ecosystem partners.
* Familiarity with web technologies, remote display protocols, and cloud\-delivered applications.
* Deep customer empathy and the ability to translate insights into strategic product decisions.
* Experience launching high\-quality software at scale in B2B enterprise environments.

**Why Join Us?**

* Lead the evolution of workspace delivery on **ChromeOS and HTML5** in a market\-leading virtualization company.
* Shape a key area of innovation and partner engagement with **Google**.
* Define experiences that span **cloud, on\-premises, and hybrid infrastructure**, impacting users globally.
* Be part of a high\-impact, collaborative team driving the future of work experiences across platforms.

**About Us:**


Cloud Software Group is one of the world’s largest cloud solution providers, serving more than 100 million users around the globe. When you join Cloud Software Group, you are making a difference for real people, each of whom count on our suite of cloud\-based products to get work done — from anywhere. Members of our team will tell you that we value passion for technology and the courage to take risks. Everyone is empowered to learn, dream, and build the future of work. We are on the brink of another Cambrian leap \- a moment of immense evolution and growth. And we need your expertise and experience to do it. Now is the perfect time to move your skills to the cloud.


Cloud Software Group is firmly committed to Equal Employment Opportunity (EEO) and to compliance with all federal, state and local laws that prohibit employment discrimination. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, race, color, creed, sex or gender, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, ethnicity, national origin, ancestry, citizenship, religion, genetic carrier status, disability, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions (including lactation status), marital status, military service, protected veteran status, political activity or affiliation, taking or requesting statutorily protected leave and other protected classifications.


