* Collaborate with stakeholders across cross\-functional teams and ensure clear communication of product goals, timelines, and milestones
* Participate and assist in ensuring healthy product backlog and develop detailed product roadmaps, considering resource allocation, timelines, and dependencies. Ensure customer focus by gathering and analysing customer journeys, feature performance, user testing, data\-driven decision\-making, reviewing customer feedback and incorporating insights into product improvements via optimizations.
* Be the subject matter expert on digital for single/multiple payment flow.
* Manage products ensuring proper alignment and approvals are obtained from Legal, Compliance, Privacy and Infosec.
* Experience in Analytics for ascertaining the product performance (any tool like Google Analytics, Amplitude etc).

**Role Requirements**

* 7\-12 years of product management experience in the digital space.
* Consumer product management experience, with a deep understanding of the technical ecosystems.
* Excellent analytical skills and ability to constantly deep dive and take decisions based on data.
* Experience creating wireframes, workflow diagrams, product features \& stories
* Ability to break down complex experiences into simple documents, stories, and flows. Experience in developing user flows and collaboration Diagrams.
* Experience with customer research and usability testing methodologies.
* Experience working with multiple stakeholders/teams in different countries with different cultural backgrounds.
* Hands on experience in product development, optimization and new product initiatives process and product life\-cycle management.
* Strong business writing, presentation, verbal communication and interpersonal skills, with the ability to translate complex technical concepts to a broad range of audiences.
* Great attention to detail coupled with experience seeing the bigger picture, prioritizing competing needs and providing extreme clarity to your team
* Undergraduate degree in business, engineering, or equivalent relevant experience.

**What will make you stand out:**

* Master’s degree in business.
* Experience in web and mobile marketing and analytics
* Experience in FinTech industry in digital space \- mainly in payments – cards, D2B etc.
* Experience working in a large corporate environment
* Experience in global money movement or financial services
* Ability to effectively use – AB test tools, Analytics tools and other front\-end tools is an advantage

 **We make financial services accessible to humans everywhere. Join us for what’s next.**


Western Union is positioned to become the world’s most accessible financial services company —transforming lives and communities. We’re a diverse and passionate customer\-centric team of over 8,000 employees serving 200 countries and territories, reaching customers and receivers around the globe. More than moving money, we design easy\-to\-use products and services for our digital and physical financial ecosystem that help our customers move forward.


Just as we help our global customers prosper, we support our employees in achieving their professional aspirations. You’ll have plenty of opportunities to learn new skills and build a career, as well as receive a great compensation package. If you’re ready to help drive the future of financial services, it’s time for Western Union. Learn more about our purpose and people at https://careers.westernunion.com/.

