gd-1009698796464,glassdoor,https://www.glassdoor.co.in/job-listing/j?jl=1009698796464,,Staff Technical Product Manager,GE Vernova,Chennai,2025-04-05,,814923.0,969420.0,INR,False,"**Job Description Summary**
===========================


Technical Product Manager Role will:
  

  

Act as liaison between process owners and solution stakeholders and become the official solution advocates where required. Key person in determining when, how a solution needs to be developed, upgraded, or dropped.  

Guides project teams and customers for planning of sprints and Iterations of delivery of solutions.  

A Product manager will have to deal with “Systems of Systems” scenarios, must be concerned not just with how the solution will operate in its own context, but how it will function in the context of the larger IT ecosystem. A successful candidate is expected to question assumptions and drive change to mitigate potential risks, envision or evaluate new technology or solutions and to move towards it.  

  

The successful candidate will gain and understand business process relevant to the problem, defining the AS\-IS process, identify gaps that needs to be addressed, define the To\-Be Process and convert them into IT requirements, solutions. This position will give you an opportunity to be part of an innovation team in a greenfield area to help define new process improvements, solutions in automation, data challenges to help GE Power Conversion to continuously drive innovation and maximize businesses outcomes along with user experience.**Job Description**
===================

**Essential Responsibilities**

**1\. Business Analyst**

Meets with business and IT stakeholders to translate business challenges into a business case for automation.


Writes business case documentation, which includes documentation of as\-is process, business process modelling, identification of automation areas, and return on investment (ROI) benefits analysis.


Writes the Business Requirements document which includes a detailed overview of the as\-is process and outlines the challenges that could be solved through an IT and/or automation solution.


Actively engages with key stakeholders and goes to the place of work to observe the business processes in actions to effectively provide ideas for automation.


Maintains strong relationships with key stakeholders by gaining trust of stakeholders and respect through technical leadership.

**2\. Technical Solution Architect**


Looks at business processes to identify potential automation solutions that can be automated using RPA, AI, or similar technologies.


Partners with business and application solution architects to understand how processes are implemented in IT systems and provides automation solutions to drive productivity and simplification.


Writes Solution Design document and holds session with business and IT stakeholders to ensure full understanding of technical approach for solution delivery.


Evaluate and design RPA Solutions that could provide better value when combined with GenAI/Agentic AI


Technical Experience in managing RPA (Robotics Process Automation) platform.

**3\. Product Management**


Manages the full lifecycle of the solution, including initial problem definition, solution design, development, postproduction support, and eventual solution retirement.


Evaluates the active solution portfolio and upgrade and improve existing solutions as required based on evolving business needs.


Works with business functional subject matter experts and IT owners to identify automation opportunities.


Writes and maintains product specifications, which includes the solution configuration guide and operations guide.


**4\. Vendor Management**


Manages vendor relationship to drive delivery, including providing effort estimation, evaluation of proposals, and overseeing delivery of third\-party resources.


Manages Development \&Testing, Deployment and Maintenance.

**Qualifications / Requirements**

* At least 8 years related experience in IT Industry as Business Analyst, Solution Architect, or equivalent role.
* Provided solutions for cross functional IT Systems, with a significant part of the experience in Business Applications and/or ERP solutions.
* At least 3 years of experience in RPA(Robotics Process Automation) /Automations.
* At least 3 years of experience in a Business Analyst role in at least one of the business domains.
* Experience with UIPath, Agentic Automation will be an advantage.
* GenAI / AI experience is an added advantage.

**Desired Characteristics**

* Quick learner of functional process and how it influences IT applications and solutions with Problem Solving mind set.
* Ability to work with cross\-functional teams to drive outcomes
* Thinker with focus on big picture, root cause while driving discussions, solution design and tools required to solve the problems.
* Technical Experience: ERP in one of more modules, RPA, Chat\-BoT Automation and or BI/Data Analytics experience.
* Good presentation and Communication skills
* Have had experience in evaluation of tools and s/w
* Six Sigma or Lean Certified.
* Experience working in remote / global teams.

**Additional Information**
==========================

**Relocation Assistance Provided:** No",,https://www.glassdoor.co.in/Overview/W-EI_IE740889.htm,Product Management
gd-1009698842691,glassdoor,https://www.glassdoor.co.in/job-listing/j?jl=1009698842691,,Sr. Product Manager/Sr.DevOps Manager,Sanglob Business Services,Pune,2025-04-05,,3000000.0,4000000.0,INR,False,"**Job Title:** Head of DevOps / Director of DevOps / Principal DevOps Engineer / Senior DevOps Manager / Product Manager

**Location:** Pune/Remote

**Experience:** 15\+ Years

**Availability:** Immediate joiners required (0\-7 days)

**Note:** Minimum10\+ experience is required, kindly do not apply if you are less experienced

**About the Role:**

We are seeking a **highly experienced and technically strong DevOps leader** to drive the organization's **DevOps strategy, cloud infrastructure, automation, and CI/CD pipelines**. As a **Head of DevOps / Director of DevOps**, you will be responsible for **scaling and optimizing deployment processes, enhancing security, and ensuring high availability of systems.**

This role requires **expertise in cloud platforms (AWS, Azure, GCP), container orchestration (Kubernetes, Docker), infrastructure as code (Terraform, CloudFormation), and strong leadership capabilities** to mentor teams and collaborate across engineering departments.

**Key Responsibilities:**

**DevOps Strategy \& Leadership:**

* Define and implement the **DevOps roadmap, best practices, and automation strategies** to streamline development and deployment.
* Lead and mentor **cross\-functional teams** including DevOps engineers, SREs, and developers.
* Establish and enforce **SLA/SLOs, high availability, and scalability strategies** for infrastructure.

**CI/CD \& Automation:**

* Design, implement, and maintain **end\-to\-end CI/CD pipelines** using Jenkins, GitHub Actions, GitLab CI/CD, or ArgoCD.
* Automate provisioning, configuration management, and deployments with **Terraform, Ansible, Chef, or Puppet**.
* Optimize **release management, monitoring, and rollback strategies** for smooth software delivery.

**Cloud \& Infrastructure Management:**

* Architect and manage **cloud\-native infrastructures** on AWS, Azure, or GCP.
* Implement **high\-performance, cost\-optimized, and scalable cloud solutions** using Kubernetes, Docker, and serverless computing.
* Drive **multi\-cloud and hybrid cloud strategies** for large\-scale environments.

**Security \& Compliance:**

* Enforce **DevSecOps principles**, integrating security practices into CI/CD pipelines.
* Implement **IAM, RBAC, and security best practices** for cloud and on\-prem environments.
* Ensure compliance with **SOC 2, ISO 27001, GDPR, and other security frameworks**.

**Monitoring, Logging, and Performance Optimization:**

* Set up **end\-to\-end monitoring, observability, and logging solutions** using Prometheus, Grafana, ELK, or Datadog.
* Optimize **application performance, incident response, and system reliability**.
* Establish **disaster recovery (DR) and business continuity planning (BCP)**.

**Collaboration \& Stakeholder Management:**

* Work closely with **development, QA, security, and product teams** to align DevOps initiatives with business goals.
* Drive **cost efficiency in cloud infrastructure and DevOps operations**.
* Advocate for **DevOps culture, CI/CD adoption, and automation\-first mindset** across the organization.

**Key Skills \& Qualifications:**

* **15\+ years of experience** in DevOps, SRE, or cloud infrastructure roles.
* Strong expertise in **AWS, Azure, GCP, Kubernetes, Terraform, Docker, Helm, and CI/CD tools**.
* Proficiency in **Python, Go, Bash, or any scripting language** for automation.
* Deep understanding of **networking, security, observability, and performance tuning**.
* Experience in **multi\-cloud, hybrid cloud, microservices, and Kubernetes clusters at scale**.
* Strong leadership, mentoring, and stakeholder management skills.
* Excellent communication and ability to work in **fast\-paced, enterprise environments**.

**Preferred Qualifications:**

* Certifications like **AWS Certified DevOps Engineer, Kubernetes CKAD/CKA, or Terraform Associate**.
* Experience with **FinOps (cost optimization), AI\-driven DevOps, or GitOps practices**.
* Hands\-on experience in **edge computing, service mesh (Istio, Linkerd), and AIOps**.

**Why Join Us?**

* Work with **cutting\-edge cloud, automation, and DevOps technologies**.
* Lead **highly skilled engineering teams** and drive DevOps transformation.
* Competitive salary, perks, and a dynamic work culture.

**If you're a strategic thinker, DevOps expert, and a problem\-solver, we'd love to hear from you, Send resume to ankita.parbat@sanglob.in** 

