gd-1009699012972,glassdoor,https://www.glassdoor.co.in/job-listing/j?jl=1009699012972,,Product Owner - Resiliency Services,Cowbell Cyber Inc.,Pune,2025-04-05,,600000.0,915000.0,INR,False,"Cowbell is signaling a new era in cyber insurance by harnessing technology and data to provide small and medium\-sized enterprises (SMEs) with advanced warning of cyber risk exposures bundled with cyber insurance coverage adaptable to the threats of today and tomorrow. Championing adaptive insurance, Cowbell follows policyholders' cyber risk exposures as they evolve through continuous risk assessment and continuous underwriting. In its unique AI\-based approach to risk selection and pricing, Cowbell's underwriting platform, powered by Cowbell Factors, compresses the insurance process from submission to issue to less than 5 minutes.



Founded in 2019 and based in the San Francisco Bay Area, Cowbell has rapidly grown, now operating across the U.S., Canada, U.K., and India. This growth was recently bolstered by a successful Series C fundraising round of $60 million from Zurich Insurance. This investment not only underscores the confidence in Cowbell's mission but also accelerates our capacity to revolutionize cyber insurance on a global scale. With the backing of over 25 prominent reinsurance partners, Cowbell is poised to redefine how SMEs navigate the evolving landscape of cyber threats.

  


**Objective**



Seeking a dynamic and experienced Product Owner with a strong background in software development within the cyber security or cyber insurance industry, with proficiency in Scrum methodologies. The ideal candidate will participate in cross\-functional teams to deliver innovative, customer\-centric solutions, driving product vision and strategy. This role demands a deep understanding of market trends, user needs, and competitive landscapes to ensure the successful execution of product roadmaps and continuous improvement in product delivery.


**What you will do**


* Be a key member of the Product Team, and create the right digital experiences to delight our users (Policyholders, internal users).
* Groom and prioritize backlog; develop user stories and acceptance criteria.
* Execute cyber security product roadmaps through technology platform solutions within the Cowbell ecosystem
* Collaborate with our design team to create and validate solutions for the customer's requirements.
* Gather requirements and feedback through frequent process observation, surveys, analysis, research and testing.
* Be a department liaison for business divisions; performing the role of the primary communicator and link between user stakeholders and engineering teams
* Coordinate User Acceptance testing and manage inner\-departmental dependencies surrounding project release tasks


**What Cowbell needs from you**


* 5\+ years of experience with agile scrum methodologies, of which 3\+ years are in a Product Manager or Product Owner role
* Sense of urgency and mission driven
* Core understanding of the system development life cycle for custom built software
* Experience with cyber security tools, terminology, process and industry needs
* Experience working with product roadmaps, prioritization, sprints, stand\-ups
* Experience with the Atlassian suite of tools preferred (JIRA, Confluence, etc.)
* Experience negotiating priorities
* Experience writing user stories
* Flexible and open to change and new information


**What Cowbell brings to the table:**


* Employee equity plan for all and wealth enablement plan for select customer facing roles
* Comprehensive wellness program, meditation app subscriptions, lunch and learn, book club, happy hours and much more
* Professional development and the opportunity to learn the ins and outs of cyber insurance, cyber security as well as continuing to build your professional skills in a team environment


**Equal Employment Opportunity:**  

  

We are committed to equal opportunity in the terms and conditions of employment for all employees and job applicants without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, age, gender identity or gender expression, national origin, disability, or veteran status.  

Cowbell is a leading innovator in cyber insurance, dedicated to empowering businesses to always deliver their intended outcomes as the cyber threat landscape evolves. Guided by our core values of TRUE—Transparency, Resiliency, Urgency, and Empowerment—we are on a mission to be the gold standard for businesses to understand, manage, and transfer cyber risk.



At Cowbell, we foster a collaborative and dynamic work environment where every employee is empowered to contribute and grow. We pride ourselves on our commitment to transparency and resilience, ensuring that we not only meet but exceed industry standards.  

We are proud to be an equal opportunity employer, promoting a diverse and inclusive workplace where all voices are heard and valued. Our employees enjoy competitive compensation, comprehensive benefits, and continuous opportunities for professional development.



