Are you looking for an exciting opportunity to join a dynamic and growing team in a fast paced and challenging area? This is a unique opportunity for you to work in the Wealth Management team to partner with the Business.


As a Lending \& Treasury Manager within the Global Lending/Treasury team, you will play a crucial role in supporting the Product Manager and promoting initiatives within the Treasury and Lending space.

**Job Responsibilities:**

* Develop, maintain and implement strategies to improve treasury and lending functions within the Wealth Management space.
* Prepare and present reports and updates to senior management, demonstrating a clear understanding of financial trends and insights.
* Manage projects from conception to execution, ensuring alignment with strategic goals.
* Collaborate with global teams to gather insights and drive initiatives that enhance our Treasury/Lending solutions.
* Understand regulatory frameworks and analytical skills to assess and challenge existing processes, ensuring compliance while driving innovation and efficiency.

**Required qualifications, capabilities, and skills**


* 7\+ years of experience within financial services, supporting the Banking business.
* Financial services/lending \& treasury background in Wealth Management.
* Strong project management skills with a proven track record of driving business objectives.
* Excellent communication skills, with the ability to convey complex information clearly and effectively.
* Proficiency in financial analysis tools and a willingness to learn and utilize new technologies, including LLMs.
* Strong analytical skills with the ability to understand and interpret regulatory frameworks related to lending and treasury operations.
* Experience in assessing and challenging existing processes to drive innovation and efficiency.




**Preferred qualifications, capabilities, and skills**

* Experience in treasury or lending is a plus.
* Knowledge of Wealth Management lending is preferred.
* Demonstrated ability to work independently and take ownership of projects.
* Strong integrity and the ability to speak up and advocate for ideas, even in challenging situations.
* Experience working in a global or multicultural environment.
* A strategic thinker with a strong sense of ownership and accountability.
* A willingness to learn and adapt to new challenges and opportunities


**ABOUT US**  

JPMorganChase, one of the oldest financial institutions, offers innovative financial solutions to millions of consumers, small businesses and many of the world’s most prominent corporate, institutional and government clients under the J.P. Morgan and Chase brands. Our history spans over 200 years and today we are a leader in investment banking, consumer and small business banking, commercial banking, financial transaction processing and asset management.  

  

We recognize that our people are our strength and the diverse talents they bring to our global workforce are directly linked to our success. We are an equal opportunity employer and place a high value on diversity and inclusion at our company. We do not discriminate on the basis of any protected attribute, including race, religion, color, national origin, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, age, marital or veteran status, pregnancy or disability, or any other basis protected under applicable law. We also make reasonable accommodations for applicants’ and employees’ religious practices and beliefs, as well as mental health or physical disability needs. Visit our FAQs for more information about requesting an accommodation.

  

  

  

**ABOUT THE TEAM**  

  

J.P. Morgan Asset \& Wealth Management delivers industry\-leading investment management and private banking solutions. Asset Management provides individuals, advisors and institutions with strategies and expertise that span the full spectrum of asset classes through our global network of investment professionals. Wealth Management helps individuals, families and foundations take a more intentional approach to their wealth or finances to better define, focus and realize their goals.",,https://www.glassdoor.co.in/Overview/W-EI_IE5224839.htm,Product Management
gd-1009699187059,glassdoor,https://www.glassdoor.co.in/job-listing/j?jl=1009699187059,,Consultant-Product Management,Verizon,Chennai,2025-04-05,,,,,False,"### **When you join Verizon**


You want more out of a career. A place to share your ideas freely — even if they’re daring or different. Where the true you can learn, grow, and thrive. At Verizon, we power and empower how people live, work and play by connecting them to what brings them joy. We do what we love — driving innovation, creativity, and impact in the world. Our V Team is a community of people who anticipate, lead, and believe that listening is where learning begins. In crisis and in celebration, we come together — lifting our communities and building trust in how we show up, everywhere \& always. Want in? Join the V Team Life.

**What you’ll be doing...**


We’re looking for you to bring the latest and greatest features to our customers\-—and to help us tell the marketplace about what’s new and why they need to have it. This role combines deep technical knowledge of AI accelerator technologies with strategic product management to deliver solutions that enable faster, more efficient AI deployment. Collaborating with others, you’ll build the roadmap and drive the process from ideation through design and roll\-out—and build compelling value messages along the way. Your focus will be on AI products, features, and services that solve customer challenges and help make people’s lives better. This role requires a clear understanding of AI with a strong B2B acumen, committed to driving key business outcomes through data.

* Understanding and anticipating market needs.
* Define and communicate the product vision and strategy for AI features in our products, ensuring alignment with the company’s overall goals and objectives
* Stay informed about the latest AI trends and identify potential applications for the business
* Defining requirements and leading the team through design and development.
* Building the business case, getting internal consensus, and defining product roadmaps.
* Forging strong relationships across the organization to get it all done.
* Tracking success metrics and communicating results to management.

**What we’re looking for…**


Understanding what customers will want next is your driver. You are creative but balance that with your practical business side. You can juggle several projects with tight deadlines and not drop any balls—while also keeping your eye on the big picture. An environment with lots of competing priorities and new challenges every day is where you thrive. With a knack for working with different types of people, you inspire others to do their best work and carry out your vision.


You'll need to have:

* Bachelor’s degree or four or more years of work experience.
* Four or more years of relevant work experience.
* Good understanding of AI concepts, ML model architectures and computational requirements
* Excellent analytical, problem\-solving, and decision\-making skills specifically regarding large but undefined problem space
* Experience using data to drive product decisions and measure success.
* Experience in improving customer experience.
* Experience in enterprise digital analytics, with a strong preference for B2B industry experience.
* Demonstrated ability to work independently as a self\-starter and lead cross\-functional teams.
* Strong communication skills with the aptitude to convey complex data concepts in business terms.

**Even better if you have one or more of the following:**

* Ecommerce or online experience
* Extensive experience with data modeling, statistical analysis, and predictive analytics.
* A strategic thinker with a proven record of leveraging analytics for business growth and transformation.
* Knowledge of design thinking.
* Digital experience, digital marketing and digital product management either in a business, agency or consulting organization.
* Managed complex projects with shifting priorities, demands, and stakeholders. Ideally, with cross\-functional teams and agencies.
* Passion for innovation and a commitment to driving business value through technology.


If Verizon and this role sound like a fit for you, we encourage you to apply even if you don’t meet every “even better” qualification listed above.

### **Where you’ll be working**


In this hybrid role, you'll have a defined work location that includes work from home and assigned office days set by your manager.### **Scheduled Weekly Hours**


40### **Equal Employment Opportunity**


Verizon is an equal opportunity employer. We evaluate qualified applicants without regard to race, gender, disability or any other legally protected characteristics.",,https://www.glassdoor.co.in/Overview/W-EI_IE89.htm,Product Management
