gd-1009697330204,glassdoor,https://www.glassdoor.co.in/job-listing/j?jl=1009697330204,,Product Manager,Movius Interactive Corporation,Bengaluru,2025-04-04,,,,,False,"**About Movius**
Movius is the leading global provider in cloud\-based secure mobile communications software, helping enterprises deliver better engagement for their clients. Enterprises around the world use the company’s all\-in\-one mobility platform to connect with their customers in more convenient, cost\-effective, and compliant ways. The platform offers an easy way to extend and integrate voice, text, and messaging services into CRM systems, collaboration tools and other enterprise systems and take advantage of our built\-in AI capabilities to drive conversational analytics.
Movius supports remote working with our people located across USA, India, Australia, Asia and Europe.
**The Role**
Are you ready to take on your next challenge in this fast\-paced tech company? We are currently looking for experienced Product Manager who can help drive the product vision and evolution of the Movius product portfolio.
Working closely with other product managers, engineering, service, sales, and customer success teams, the product manager will collaborate to define a strategy and an implementation plan to deliver on the roadmap.
The Product Manager is responsible for the setting of strategic product direction, collating and maintaining product requirements and ensuring successful realization of product strategy across the portfolio within our chosen market categories and customer segment domains.
As a product manager, you will:
* Own and drive the evolution of the Movius Platform including the Movius APIs, and integration of AI capabilities.
* Document product requirements in detail and drive delivery through the engineering team.
* Engage and interface with large strategic customers and play the role of product evangelist in the market to support Sales and gather Voice of the Customer feedback.
* Track overall market dynamics and competitive landscape.
* Drive optimization, efficiency and scalability for current platform.
* Lead the product planning from concept through to product approval and launch. This includes the resource planning to execute Product evolution.
* Be a hands\-on person in terms of grooming product stories with architecture, engineering, testing and DevOps teams.
* Support the sales and marketing teams with product questions and customer presentations.
* Develop presentations, whitepapers, and RFP responses to support technical and non\-technical customer requirements and presentations for sales and executive leadership team members.
* Manage time schedules and overall product delivery.
* Report on both the business and operational performance of your products and customers on a regular basis.

**Who are you:**
* Minimum 5 years’ experience in product management in a fast\-paced company.
* Must have a bachelor’s degree in information technology or engineering. An advanced degree such as a master’s degree or MBA is a plus
* You are a strategic thinker and technically savvy in enterprise software, communications stack, APIs, cloud, and mobile devices.
* Experience with Software Development Life Cycle and Agile methodology.
* You are structured in your daily work with attention to detail and proven ability to prioritize and complete multiple projects concurrently and meet committed deadlines.
* The ability to solicit customer requirements from many sources, prioritize, and work with engineering and design to deliver
* Exceptional verbal and written communication to effectively collaborate and communicate with geographically dispersed cross\-functional teams to drive business outcomes.
* Experience creating and contributing to a software product lifecycle evolution management, evangelizing the product vision, and grooming stories.

**Advantage:**
* Knowledge of telecommunications networks, SIP stack, VoIP.
* 2\-3 years of experience working is a similar position in a Communication Platform as a Service (CPaaS) provider.
* Experience in addressing enterprise customers requirements related to communications platforms is highly beneficial.
* Experience managing products in enterprise end\-user technology team.
* Experience in regulated environments such as financial services/healthcare or related industries.",,https://www.glassdoor.co.in/Overview/W-EI_IE29205.htm,Product Management
gd-1009698406477,glassdoor,https://www.glassdoor.co.in/job-listing/j?jl=1009698406477,,Senior Product Manager - Freshworks’ Platform (Enterprise Communication and Collaboration),Freshworks,Bengaluru,2025-04-04,,505000.0,742500.0,INR,False,"**Company Description** **About Freshworks**


Freshworks makes it fast and easy for businesses to delight their customers and employees. Our fresh approach to software is affordable, quick to implement, and designed for the end user—empowering businesses of all sizes to create better customer (CRM, CX) and employee (ITSM) experiences.


Headquartered in San Mateo, California, Freshworks operates across 13 global locations, serving 65,000\+ companies—from startups to public enterprises. Our cloud\-based product suite includes Freshdesk (omni\-channel support), Freshsales (sales automation), Freshmarketer (marketing automation), Freshservice (IT service desk), and Freshchat (AI\-powered bots)—all powered by Freshworks Platforms, our unified platform of shared services.


Recognized by CNBC, Forbes, Fortune, and Bloomberg, and honored as a Best Place to Work in San Francisco and Denver, Freshworks consistently earns top ratings on G2 and TrustRadius for its industry\-leading products.

 **Job Description** **The Opportunity: Build the Future of Enterprise Communication \& Collaboration**


As a **Senior Product Manager** on the **Freshworks Platform Team**, you’ll play a pivotal role in shaping the future of the communication and collaboration ecosystem for businesses worldwide. This is an opportunity to own, innovate, and scale high\-impact product modules that drive differentiation and customer delight.


We are looking for a strategic thinker, customer advocate, and execution powerhouse who thrives in a fast\-paced SaaS environment. If you’re passionate about building seamless, intuitive, and scalable communication experiences, we’d love to hear from you!

**What You’ll Do**


**Own \& Build for Growth**

* Take full ownership of key product modules, driving sustained differentiation and impact.
* Develop deep domain expertise and stay ahead of industry trends in communication \& collaboration.
* Define, build, release, and measure success for end\-to\-end product experiences.


**Be a Customer Champion**

* Develop a deep understanding of customer pain points, needs, and workflows.
* Bridge the gap between customers, engineering, design, and business teams—ensuring customer\-centric product development.
* Continuously gather insights, test hypotheses, and iterate to drive meaningful outcomes.


✨ **Deliver Exceptional User Experiences**

* Create intuitive, elegant, and powerful solutions that balance customer needs with technical feasibility.
* Work with design and engineering teams to bring best\-in\-class usability to every product interaction.
* Champion an iterative MVP\-first approach—shipping fast, learning continuously, and improving rapidly.

**Collaborate \& Lead**

* Partner with engineering, marketing, sales, and leadership teams to align product strategy with business goals.
* Communicate clear, compelling product visions to stakeholders, ensuring seamless execution and adoption.
* Foster a culture of innovation, ownership, and agility within the product team.
* **Act with Speed \& Impact**
* Break down complex problems into phases, enabling incremental progress while keeping the big picture in focus.
* Leverage data\-driven decision\-making to prioritize and iterate effectively.
* Drive structured experimentation and learning loops to optimize product outcomes.

 **Qualifications** **What You Bring**

**✅** 8\+ years of experience in global/cross\-functional software teams in a SaaS/product company.


✅ Knowledge of Distributed Systems


✅ Platforms mindset


✅ 5\+ years of core product management experience, building features for internet\-scale software products.  

✅ Customer\-first mindset with a strong ability to listen, empathize, and problem\-solve.  

✅ Ability to simplify complex technical concepts and communicate effectively with internal \& external stakeholders.  

✅ A proven track record of making data\-driven decisions while balancing long\-term vision and fast\-paced execution.  

✅ Experience working in an agile, iterative environment, leveraging structured experimentation to drive impact.

 **Additional Information**  

**Impact at Scale:** Shape the future of collaboration for thousands of businesses worldwide.  

**High\-Growth Environment:** Work with a team of passionate, world\-class professionals in a rapidly scaling company.  

**Innovative Product Culture:** We prioritize craftsmanship, continuous learning, and customer delight.  

**Recognized Excellence:** Join a company that’s trusted, award\-winning, and loved by users.


If you’re excited about building world\-class communication \& collaboration experiences, apply today and let’s create something amazing together!


At Freshworks, we are creating a global workplace that enables everyone to find their true potential, purpose, and passion irrespective of their background, gender, race, sexual orientation, religion and ethnicity. We are committed to providing equal opportunity for all and believe that diversity in the workplace creates a more vibrant, richer work environment that advances the goals of our employees, communities and the business.",,https://www.glassdoor.co.in/Overview/W-EI_IE1680273.htm,Product Management
gd-1009697166286,glassdoor,https://www.glassdoor.co.in/job-listing/j?jl=1009697166286,,Lead Product Manager-Payment Services,Careers at Tide,Bengaluru,2025-04-04,,,,,False,"### **ABOUT TIDE**



At Tide, we are building a finance platform designed to save small businesses time and money. We provide our members with business accounts and related banking services, but also a comprehensive set of connected administrative solutions from invoicing to accounting.



Launched in 2017, Tide is now used by over **1 million small businesses** across the world and is available to UK, Indian and German SMEs. Headquartered in central London, with offices in Sofia, Hyderabad, Delhi, Berlin and Belgrade, Tide employs over 2000 employees.



Tide is rapidly growing, expanding into new markets and always looking for passionate and driven people. Join us in our mission to empower small businesses and help them save time and money.

**ABOUT THE TEAM**



You'll be part of a dynamic, cross\-functional team of experienced product managers, engineers, data scientists, designers, and marketers. Together, we build and refine Tide's global partner credit and digital payments solutions. Our team thrives on collaboration, customer obsession, and data\-driven decision\-making to empower small businesses with seamless access to financial services


**ABOUT THE ROLE**



As a Lead Product Manager for Tide's global payment services, you will drive strategy and execution for digital payments across Europe and India. You will lead, innovate and drive the roadmap, collaborate with cross\-functional stakeholders, and leverage data\-driven insights to enhance our market position. Your role focuses on reducing friction in digital payments, improving customer experience, and enabling small businesses to access competitive business loans..


**As a Lead product manager you'll:**


* Develop and drive the product vision \& strategy within our product portfolio, aligned with the company's overall objectives and targets.
* Conduct market research to identify trends, competitive landscape, and customer needs to inform product decisions.
* Drive the product\-led cross\-functional teams through the product development lifecycle, from concept to launch and eventual value realisation, while ensuring timely delivery and quality.
* Prioritise product features and enhancements based on market requirements, customer feedback, and business goals.
* Create and maintain a product roadmap, ensuring alignment with near\- \& medium\-term business objectives and long\-term vision.
* Collaborate closely with internal stakeholders, including engineering, operations, risk, marketing and other product teams, to ensure a coordinated product strategy and successful launches.
* Lead by example: you will be hands on, take ownership for business metrics and product KPIs and play a pivotal role in bringing all stakeholders onboard.
* Define and scope new product ideas leveraging internal technology and external vendor solutions.
* Cultivate a seamless customer experience by ensuring the smooth functioning of automated and manual processes.
* Manage \& coach a team of experienced product managers to own and drive the impact of the product in line with objectives \& targets.

**WHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR**
---------------------------


* You have 5\+ years of relevant PM experience and 10 years overall experience with proven experience working with agile/scrum delivery teams.
* Deep expertise in payments and connectivity, particularly bank payments, with extensive experience in fintechs or banks across global markets.
* Strong understanding of fund flows, transaction settlement, and reconciliation involving multiple parties.
* Should have a strong Product sense of user experience and design, with the ability to create state\-of\-the\-art experiences that drive adoption and engagement.
* You're a product evangelist: obsessed with the end user, well\-versed in best in class product research and development practices and are willing to share your knowledge with other product owners
* Leadership acumen and a desire to mentor and manage fellow PMs
* Comfort in a fast\-paced environment, adapting to shifting priorities and pioneering new processes.
* You have Technical knowledge and experience with API\-based products.
* A proactive ""can\-do"" attitude, adept at multitasking and achieving results.

**WHAT YOU'LL GET IN RETURN:**
------------------------------


* Self \& Family Health Insurance
* Term \& Life Insurance
* OPD Benefits
* Mental wellbeing through Plumm
* Learning \& Development Budget
* WFH Setup allowance
* 15 days of Privilege leaves
* 12 days of Casual leaves
* 12 days of Sick leaves
* 3 paid days off for volunteering or L\&D activities
* Stock Options

**TIDEAN WAYS OF WORKING:**
---------------------------



At Tide, we champion a **flexible workplace** model that supports both in\-person and remote work to cater to the specific needs of our different teams.



While remote work is supported, we believe in the power of face\-to\-face interactions to foster team spirit and collaboration. Our offices are designed as hubs for innovation and team\-building, where we encourage regular in\-person gatherings to foster a strong sense of community.

### **TIDE IS A PLACE FOR EVERYONE**



At Tide, we believe that we can only succeed if we let our differences enrich our culture. Our Tideans come from a variety of backgrounds and experience levels. We consider everyone irrespective of their ethnicity, religion, sexual orientation, gender identity, family or parental status, national origin, veteran, neurodiversity or differently\-abled status. We celebrate diversity in our workforce as a cornerstone of our success. Our commitment to a broad spectrum of ideas and backgrounds is what enables us to build products that resonate with our members' diverse needs and lives.



We are One Team and foster a transparent and inclusive environment, where everyone's voice is heard.

  


*At Tide, we thrive on diversity, embracing various backgrounds and experiences. We welcome all individuals regardless of ethnicity, religion, sexual orientation, gender identity, or disability. Our inclusive culture is key to our success, helping us build products that meet our members' diverse needs. We are One Team, committed to transparency and ensuring everyone's voice is heard.*

  


*You personal data will be processed by Tide for recruitment purposes and in accordance with* *Tide's Recruitment Privacy Notice**.*",,https://www.glassdoor.co.in/Overview/W-EI_IE2058934.htm,Product Management
