gd-1009697419846,glassdoor,https://www.glassdoor.co.in/job-listing/j?jl=1009697419846,,Lead Digital Marketing Manager (WFH),Outsource Bigdata,,2025-04-04,,,,,True,"Apr 3, 2025

  

#### **Aimleap**


#### **India (Remote)**


#### **Posted on Apr 03, 2025**

**AIMLEAP is Hiring:**
----------------------

##### **Lead Digital Marketing Manager** **(WFH)**


Experience: 5\+ years  

Location: Remote/Bengaluru  

Mode of Engagement: Full time  

No of Positions: 1  

Educational Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree  

Industry: IT/Software/ITES (B2B/SaaS)  

Notice Period: Immediate

**Job Description:**
--------------------

**What we are looking for**

* Proven experience in B2B/SaaS product marketing with a strong track record in digital marketing leadership.
* Expertise in leading and managing a team of digital marketers, content creators, and SEO specialists.
* Strong knowledge and hands\-on experience in both **on\-page and off\-page SEO** strategies.
* Experience in technical content writing, including crafting whitepapers, case studies, blogs, and website content.
* Experience leveraging AI for SEO optimization, including AI\-driven keyword research, trend analysis, and search intent predictions.

**RESPONSIBILITIES:**

* Develop and execute digital marketing strategies to drive demand generation and lead acquisition for B2B/SaaS products.
* Lead and mentor a team of SEO, content, and marketing specialists to ensure successful campaign execution.
* Oversee **on\-page SEO** efforts, including website optimization, keyword research, and content strategy.
* Manage **off\-page SEO**, including link\-building, PR outreach, and backlinking strategies to improve search rankings.
* Develop and execute **technical content marketing** initiatives, ensuring alignment with brand voice and industry trends.
* Collaborate with product, sales, and engineering teams to create compelling marketing collateral, landing pages, and thought leadership content.
* Utilize web analytics tools (Google Analytics, GA4, Tag Manager, Search Console) to track performance and generate insights for continuous improvement.
* Stay updated with SEO trends, Google algorithm changes, and digital marketing best practices to maintain competitive advantage.

**QUALIFICATIONS:**

* Bachelor’s degree in marketing, Business, Communications, or a related field.
* 5\+ years of experience in digital marketing, preferably within a **B2B/SaaS environment.**
* Proven experience in **SEO strategy, technical content marketing, and demand generation**.
* Experience with AI\-driven marketing tools and automation platform.
* Strong understanding of digital marketing channels, including organic, paid, email, and social media.
* Familiarity with CRM tools for lead management and customer engagement.
* Proficiency in SEO and analytics tools (Google Analytics, Ahrefs, SEMrush, Moz, etc.).
* Strong analytical and problem\-solving skills with a data\-driven approach to decision\-making.
* Exceptional leadership, communication, and project management skills.
* Ability to analyze data, optimize campaigns, and drive continuous improvement in marketing performance.
**About Us:**
-------------


AIMLEAP is an ISO 9001:2015 and ISO/IEC 27001:2013 certified global technology consulting and service provider offering Digital IT, AI\-augmented Data Solutions, Automation, and Research \& Analytics Services.


AIMLEAP has been recognized as ‘The Great Place to Work®’. With focus on AI and automation\-first approach, our services include end\-to\-end IT application management, Mobile App Development, Data Management, Data Mining Services, Web Data Scraping, Self\-serving BI reporting solutions, Digital Marketing, and Analytics solutions.


We started in 2012 and successfully delivered projects in IT \& digital transformation, automation driven data solutions, and digital marketing for more than 750 fast\-growing companies in the USA, Europe, New Zealand, Australia, Canada; and more.


– An ISO 9001:2015 and ISO/IEC 27001:2013 certified  

– Served 750\+ customers  

– 12\+ Years of industry experience  

– 98% Client Retention  

– Great Place to Work® Certified  

– Global Delivery Centers in the USA, Canada, India \& Australia.

