gd-1009695563240,glassdoor,https://www.glassdoor.co.in/job-listing/j?jl=1009695563240,,Technical Product Delivery Specialist,Paul Mason Consulting India,Vadodara,2025-04-03,,,,,False,"**Summary of the position**


PMC is a specialist, independent, and highly regarded consultancy, delivering retail solutions to clients across the high street. They are a growing organization, team\-focused, powered by the people and unequalled in support and testing services to clients.


They have the opportunity for an enthusiastic Tools Analyst to join their Managed Services Support team based In Vadodara, India.


The tools and systems utilised within Managed Services and across PMC’s delivery teams are critical to the successful delivery of services, ensuring alignment to business strategy of both PMC and our customers.


The Tools Analyst role is critical to the governance and quality of the Managed Services team as it ensures the operational integrity of the key tools and systems used to support the delivery of our services.


The Tools Analyst will be accountable for ensuring the day\-to\-day operational integrity of the tools \& systems used to support our services, our customers, associated processes and the data across the delivery functions.


They will be responsible for proactively managing the service availability levels of the infrastructure and application(s). Collaborating with the delivery teams to define the metrics for operational performance reporting, new configuration, and continuous improvement initiatives.


**Key Accountabilities**

* Act as a Subject Matter Expert for the tools and systems currently in use across the Managed Services department which support the delivery of our support services. Ensuring ongoing alignment between business/delivery processes and tooling.
* Act as a primary point of advice, support and guidance to Support Teams, Project and Service Delivery Managers on the use of the tools and systems, ensuring compliancy and consistency of use.
* Maintain end to end data in management information systems, tracking databases and reporting tools to deliver timely and accurate reports in line with the baseline reporting routine.
* Drive and influence data quality, proactively identifying any issues and solutions.
* Ensure accurate information is shared between relevant interfaces.
* Assure service integrity and change control for routine updates and changes, coordinating with users and support teams as necessary.
* Work with technical support teams and 3rd party teams in the support of the operational stability of the tools and systems, maintaining the service availability KPI's.
* Support the ongoing development of the tools \& systems and partake in technical workshops to define and coordinate implementation of future changes.
* Promote and nurture a consistent use policy on the standard toolset.
* Support with on boarding of new starters.
* Proactively seek to address any skills and knowledge gaps that would be critical to undertaking the role by engaging with colleagues and customers.


**Skills and Experience \| Essential**


* Advanced user of RMM and/or ITSM Solutions, preferably within a support environment.
* Proficient in the use of Microsoft Office365 Applications, Word, Outlook, Excel, PowerPoint, SharePoint
* Experience in providing analysis reporting, ideally working with reporting suites such as Splunk or Datadog.
* Good oral and written communication skills
* The ability to work effectively in a team environment and collaborate with a wide variety of people
* A clear understanding of industry tools, lifecycles, methodologies (Agile/Waterfall/Release Management) and demonstrable ability to deliver a broad range of the activities required supporting the wider managed services capability.
* Have experience in a similar role within a technical environment.
* Have relevant experience supporting tools and systems which underpin a managed services or support service in a similar function.
* Champion of ITIL Support processes and their implementation
* Technical Skills (must have at least some of these)
	+ Splunk
	+ Interface / API coding \& experience
	+ Business Intelligence – Visualization of Data
	+ SQL
	+ PowerShell Scripting
	+ BAT File scripting
	+ Kaseya VSA Experience
	+ Service Desk ITSM Tool Experience
	+ Microsoft Office 365 Product Suite

**Personal Attributes**

**Communication Skills**


* For this person to be successful in this role, PMC will expect a high communication level with our customer, internal departments, and direct reports.


**Honesty**


* Our business works based on honesty, even if we are delivering bad news, which makes bad news more palatable is the delivery of a thought\-through action plan.


**Work Ethic**


* This role will be demanding for the successful person; we strive to maintain and deliver excellence, always. Particularly during a critical time, whether that be having a project or during peak trading times.


**Self\-Motivation**


* Self\-motivation is essential, and you will need the energy to deliver excellence through microanalysis, innovation, influencing change and driving its implementation.


**Professionalism**


* However challenging a task or a situation becomes you must be relaxed, calm and collected, managing any problem that you may face with a high level of professionalism.",,https://www.glassdoor.co.in/Overview/W-EI_IE518262.htm,Product Management
