gd-1009693623386,glassdoor,https://www.glassdoor.co.in/job-listing/j?jl=1009693623386,,Product Manager - Data & Privacy Products,Leegality,India,2025-04-02,,,,,False,"This is a remote position.


Company Mission:

  

  

Leegality has transformed how businesses handle documentation, offering a seamless, digital\-first solution for agreements, forms, and document workflows. Our platform has powered the paperwork of 2000\+ enterprises, including HDFC, SBI Cards, ICICI Bank and Federal Bank—streamlining their document infrastructure at scale.

  

Now, we’re tackling the next big challenge for businesses: handling user data and ensuring compliance with evolving data protection laws like the Digital Personal Data Protection Act (DPDP). We’re building cutting\-edge data and privacy products to help companies navigate these complexities with confidence and ease.

  

Find out more about our privacy products here: https://www.leegality.com/dpdp\-consent

  

  

Job Brief:

  

  

Leegality’s product team is built for speed, innovation, and solving high\-impact problems. With our new privacy\-focused product, we’re entering a 0\-to\-1 phase, and we need a sharp, driven Product Manager to help shape its future.

  

This role isn’t just about managing a product—it’s about building something transformative from the ground up. You’ll work directly with the company’s founders and product leaders, iterating rapidly, executing a high\-velocity GTM plan, and driving outcomes with energy, creativity, and hustle. This is a hands\-on role where your ability to execute, problem\-solve, and adapt quickly will be key to success in creating a category\-defining solution in privacy tech.

  

Experience with privacy/data products, self\-hosted solutions, or a background in data and engineering is highly preferred and will help you hit the ground running.

  

If you thrive in ambiguity, love solving hard problems, and want to be part of an early\-stage team building something groundbreaking—this is your chance.

  

  

  

Responsibilities:

  

  

* Work closely with founders, product leaders, designers, engineers, and business stakeholders to bring the company’s data privacy product vision to life by managing the product lifecycle from concept to launch.
  
* Support designers and engineers by creating extremely high\-quality PRDs, user stories, and wireframes.
  
* Utilize strong design instincts to guide the product's user interface and experience.
  
* Leverage data analytics tools, including SQL and dashboarding, to make data\-driven decisions.
  
* Work with marketing and business teams to launch go\-to\-market initiatives and drive adoption and business outcomes.
  
* Develop a deeply researched and nuanced understanding of our customers’ needs, our business model, and the overall market dynamic, and leverage this understanding in building high\-quality products.
  

  

Requirements:

  

  

* 2 to 5 years of experience in SaaS/tech product companies working as a product manager.
  
* Quick learning ability and adaptability to tackle new challenges in a fast\-paced startup environment.
  
* Strong analytical and quantitative skills, comfortable using tools like Excel/Google Sheets/MySQL.
  
* Excellent written and verbal communication skills with strong interpersonal skills.
  
* Strong understanding of design principles and the ability to create wireframes using modern tools like Figma.
  
* Good conceptual understanding of technical concepts and ability to work effectively with developers.
  
* Hustler mentality—willingness to roll up your sleeves and contribute to various aspects of the product lifecycle, including design, testing, documentation, and data analysis.
  

  

**Good to have (not mandatory, but highly preferred if you have one or more):**

  

  

* Experience with privacy/data products.
  
* Experience with on\-prem or self\-hosted products.
  
* Preference for a data/engineering background.
  
* Privacy qualifications or certifications.
  

  

This role is perfect for someone who thrives in ambiguity, loves problem\-solving, and wants to be at the forefront of building innovative data privacy solutions for Indian businesses.

  

  

Recruitment Process:

  

* To effectively evaluate your application, it is important that we get to know you better. It is necessary that you complete the job\-based assessment.
  
* Please answer all questions in the assessment thoroughly.
  
* You will be shortlisted based on your profile and answers to the job\-based assessment.
  
* On being shortlisted, you would be contacted for the interview process.
  
* We further have 3 rounds of interviews.
  
* Your final CTC would be decided on the basis of your skills, experience, and final assessment.
  

  

Apply directly through our career page: https://careers.leegality.com/jobs/Careers

  

For more information about us, please visit our:

  

Our Company and Culture: https://bit.ly/3Iqm5SB

  

Our Website: https://www.leegality.com/

  

Our LinkedIn Page: https://www.linkedin.com/company/leegality/


  
