gd-1009693650404,glassdoor,https://www.glassdoor.co.in/job-listing/j?jl=1009693650404,,Senior Product Manager,Atlassian,Bengaluru,2025-04-02,,360000.0,425000.0,INR,False,"Overview:
**Working at Atlassian**


Atlassians can choose where they work – whether in an office, from home, or a combination of the two. That way, Atlassians have more control over supporting their family, personal goals, and other priorities. We can hire people in any country where we have a legal entity. Interviews and onboarding are conducted virtually, a part of being a distributed\-first company.


The Cloud Transition team at Atlassian is creating the capabilities that allow the largest companies in the world to adopt Jira, Confluence, Bitbucket, Trello, and more. We solve the data management needs of thousands of enterprise customers. By unlocking their ability to rely on our products, we help them to unleash the potential of their teams.


We're hiring a Senior Product Manager reporting to the Group Product Manager. We are looking for an someone with a solid background in Product Management. You will independently create strategies and influence/ align multiple teams both internally and externally. You will partner with leadership on long\-term planning and team development.


You will guide a team to work with every function in the company, from engineering and design to sales, partnerships, ecosystem, legal, risk \& compliance and support to identify opportunities, develop processes and features, take them to market, and improve them over time.


Responsibilities:
* Gather, prioritise and translate customer and business requirements into product strategies
* Develop the vision, strategy and roadmap for Cloud data management capabilities
* Own the scope, rollout and roadmap for our Cloud data management capabilities across Atlassian's customers, multiple products, thousands of micro\-services
* Work across the Strategy, Security, Risk \& Compliance, Apps \& Marketplace, Cloud Infrastructure and product (e.g. Jira, Confluence) teams
* Build a leadership squad with other crafts and work with dedicated engineering teams, program management and designers
* Become Atlassian's expert on the Cloud Data management landscape


Qualifications:
* 5\+ years of Product Management experience building enterprise software products and/ or tech services and/ or platforms
* Have led or guided PMs and engineers in building complex products or platform
* Have worked in large\-scale collaborative companies across timezones
* Experience working directly with customers in collaboration with sales/systems engineering teams for large deployments or deals.
* Strong technical background, comfortable understanding/ sparring/ challenging technical approaches with experienced architects, senior engineering leadership and customers
* Experience building product for large and complex enterprises, balancing competing needs across customers and markets
* A proven track record for defining, building and delivering high impact products that create business and customer value in fast\-growth or large\-scale companies
* Strong stakeholder management skills that help you to communicate and manage relationships across the organisation \- from customers, developers, to senior executives.

**Our perks \& benefits**


Atlassian offers a variety of perks and benefits to support you, your family and to help you engage with your local community. Our offerings include health coverage, paid volunteer days, wellness resources, and so much more. Visit **go.atlassian.com/perksandbenefits**to learn more.

**About Atlassian**


At Atlassian, we're motivated by a common goal: to unleash the potential of every team. Our software products help teams all over the planet and our solutions are designed for all types of work. Team collaboration through our tools makes what may be impossible alone, possible together.


We believe that the unique contributions of all Atlassians create our success. To ensure that our products and culture continue to incorporate everyone's perspectives and experience, we never discriminate based on race, religion, national origin, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, age, or marital, veteran, or disability status. All your information will be kept confidential according to EEO guidelines.


To provide you the best experience, we can support with accommodations or adjustments at any stage of the recruitment process. Simply inform our Recruitment team during your conversation with them.


To learn more about our culture and hiring process, visit **go.atlassian.com/crh****.**",,https://www.glassdoor.co.in/Overview/W-EI_IE115699.htm,Product Management
