gd-1009692431333,glassdoor,https://www.glassdoor.co.in/job-listing/j?jl=1009692431333,,Senior Associate Product Manager,Principal Global Services,Hyderābād,2025-04-01,,885000.0,975000.0,INR,False,"Responsibilities:

At Principal, products provide value to customers, users, and partners, and help solve their needs as we work to enable a world where financial security is accessible to all. The Senior Associate Product Manager is responsible for supporting Product Managers as part of a product management team; however, they are not the accountable Product Manager for a product. They develop knowledge, experience, and skills by working side\-by\-side experienced product managers. They lead the discovery sessions, maintaining product health and operations metrics, and aiding in insights gathering. They support a highly complex product or family of products; gaining exposure and building relationships with key product disciplines. While building the skills required to operate as an independent product manager, they contribute to an efficient and effective product practice. They demonstrate curiosity, open\-mindedness, and motivation to gain exposure and experience in all phases of the product lifecycle.  

Essential Functions Lists major actions performed in the job. Describes what occurs and the reason the action is taken. Provides impact of each action by indicating percentage of time spent performing the functions. Regular and predictable attendance is a required function of this position.
Description
Product Discovery: 45%* Understand and execute strategic intent, problems to solve, and outcome hypotheses from PM or Senior PM
* Listens and anticipates customer needs and conveys needs to PM or Senior PM and product teams
* Turn business and domain knowledge into product knowledge in partnership with PM or Senior PM
* Support and demonstrate experprtize with the product team (design, engineering, and various business roles) in ideating and running experiments.
* Reports on measurable performance against outcome hypotheses and success criteria. Leads in documenting and sharing insights and learnings with key partners and stakeholders.

  

Product Delivery: 40%* Collaborate with PM or Senior PM and product teams to identify, understand, and track resolution of impediments to progress and dependencies with other teams
* Demonstrate expertize with procure, package, and distribute the business, customer, user, and stakeholder context and information required to solve problems effectively and efficiently.
* Collaborates with team to help administer key team practices and team enablement technologies
* Expected to play the role of product owner for SCRUM teams, collaborating on story creation and refinement, definition and success criteria, and acceptance that work is done
* Participate in team/agile ceremonies
* Communicates product releases to stakeholders \& partners.

  

Product Assessment: 15%* Assist PM and Senior PM to ensure every goal\-aligned unit of value created by the team(s) is measurable and can show progress towards product goals.
* Monitors and communicates product health, impact of product releases, and progress against product objectives.


Qualifications
Describes the minimum education and experience, certifications, licenses, physical demands, working conditions and skill sets needed to perform the job. Provide prompt, courteous, and excellent service at an acceptable cost to all customers; operate in an ethical manner in accordance with all applicable laws and regulations, the company's Corporate Code of Ethics, employee handbook, applicable compliance and operations policies and procedures, and other policies of the company. Possess a high degree of integrity and actively cooperate and interact with all entities of the Principal Financial Group.* 5\+ year of experience either through direct work experience supporting product, technology, business or demonstrated through equivalent military experience.
* Demonstrated experience with strategic thinking and decision making in a professional context.
* Basic experience with managing multiple workloads and/or competing priorities in a professional context.
* Demonstrated experience with synthesizing, summarizing, and aggregating information and building visuals.
* Demonstrated experience solving problems and operating in uncertainty.
