gd-1009692784310,glassdoor,https://www.glassdoor.co.in/job-listing/j?jl=1009692784310,,Global Product Manager Device Platforms,GE HEALTHCARE,Bengaluru,2025-04-01,,262000.0,312000.0,INR,False,"**Job Description Summary**
===========================


The Global Product Manager for GE Healthcare’s Device Platforms will conceive, define, accept, deliver, monitor, and refine device platform components including operating systems, processing components, and visual toolkits. This individual will work with key stakeholders (including business leaders, finance, marketing, and IT) and the other members of the Digital Solutions team to develop and convey a product vision. The candidate will also work closely with the product teams to accelerate their product development using shared platform components.  

  

The Digital Solutions Platform team is working on GE HealthCare’s next generation ecosystem of distributed data platform and related components. It will provide mission critical real\-time data about patients and medical devices in acute care settings where patients can be the most vulnerable. The Global Product Manager is a critical and highly visible role within the Digital Solutions organization and will play a key role in developing device components and unifying them with the overall platform strategy.**Job Description**
===================

**Role Summary / Purpose:**
---------------------------


The Global Product Manager for GE Healthcare’s Device Platforms will conceive, define, accept, deliver, monitor, and refine device platform components including operating systems, processing components, and visual toolkits. This individual will work with key stakeholders (including business leaders, finance, marketing, and IT) and the other members of the Digital Solutions team to develop and convey a product vision. The candidate will also work closely with the product teams to accelerate their product development using shared platform components.


The Digital Solutions Platform team is working on GE HealthCare’s next generation ecosystem of distributed data platform and related components. It will provide mission critical real\-time data about patients and medical devices in acute care settings where patients can be the most vulnerable. The Global Product Manager is a critical and highly visible role within the Digital Solutions organization and will play a key role in developing device components and unifying them with the overall platform strategy.

**Essential Qualifications:**
-----------------------------


As the Global Product Manager, you will be responsible for:

* **Owning the d****evice platform****product** **vision and roadmap:** Defining the long\-term product vision and strategic direction for the platform, aligned with evolving industry trends and customer needs. Developing a deep understanding of the business goals and processes to inform device platform priorities and enablers. Establishing platform roadmaps and release plans that satisfy requirements and support the device product portfolio.
* **Deep understanding of the clinical healthcare landscape:** Possessing a strong understanding of healthcare medical device regulations (FDA, HIPAA, GDPR, etc..), compliance requirements, and the unique challenges faced by healthcare providers and stakeholders.
* **Technical expertise:** Demonstrating a solid understanding of embedded system \& architecture (e.g., IoT hardware and software technologies), modern software engineering and IoT cybersecurity best practices. Medical device technology trends and competitive intelligence to inform product strategy and proactively propose new solutions.
**Product Leadership:**
-----------------------

* Managing platform investment decision making and the overall financial performance of the device platform, taking a return\-on\-investment approach to increasing the value while minimizing costs.
* Leading the platform lifecycle, from ideation and requirements gathering to release, post\-release monitoring, and iteration.
* Ensure that the needs of product teams are met and communicated across teams and the organization.
 **Communication and advocacy:**

* Effectively communicating and socializing the value proposition of the Device Platform to internal and external stakeholders, including customers, partners, and industry leaders.
* Leverage your role to improve device platform utilization across the organization, reducing costs and increasing security for devices.
**Cross\-functional collaboration:** Building \& maintaining strong relationships with engineering, data science, finance, sales, and marketing teams to ensure seamless product development and go\-to\-market strategies.

**Data\-driven decision making:** Utilizing data insights to inform platform decisions, measure success, and track key performance indicators (KPIs).

**Desired Qualifications:**
---------------------------

* 5\+ years of experience as a Product Manager, with most of those years specifically in HealthCare and medical device technology.
* Strong understanding of IoT, medical device development, IoT cybersecurity, embedded hardware/compute technologies and embedded operating systems.
* Proven track record of successfully launching and managing medical device products in the healthcare or life sciences industry.
* Excellent interpersonal and communication skills with the ability to collaborate effectively across diverse teams.
* Strategic thinker with the ability to analyze market trends, user needs, and business requirements to drive product innovation.
* Experience with Agile methodologies and product management tools.
* Strong analytical and problem\-solving skills, combined with a passion for improving patient care and clinical research.
* Experience with design thinking principles and customer experience design.
* A high degree of empathy: An ability to align and relate to customers.
* Highly curious and able to deal with uncertainty.
* Excellent problem\-solving and analytical skills, including experience leveraging data to inform decision making and assist in solving engineering problems.

Join our passionate team at GE Healthcare and make a meaningful impact on healthcare and research through the advancement of our Platforms. We offer competitive compensation, benefits, and the opportunity to shape the future of clinical data solutions.

**Inclusion and Diversity**
---------------------------


GE Healthcare is an Equal Opportunity Employer where inclusion matters. Employment decisions are made without regard to race, color, religion, national or ethnic origin, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, age, disability, protected veteran status or other characteristics protected by law. We expect all employees to live and breathe our behaviors: to act with humility and build trust; lead with transparency; deliver with focus, and drive ownership – always with unyielding integrity. Our total rewards are designed to unlock your ambition by giving you the boost and flexibility you need to turn your ideas into world\-changing realities. Our salary and benefits are everything you’d expect from an organization with global strength and scale, and you’ll be surrounded by career opportunities in a culture that fosters care, collaboration and support

**Additional Information**
==========================

**Relocation Assistance Provided:** No",,https://www.glassdoor.co.in/Overview/W-EI_IE4112.htm,Product Management
gd-1009691273048,glassdoor,https://www.glassdoor.co.in/job-listing/j?jl=1009691273048,,VP - Relationship Manager - Business Banking,HSBC,Gurgaon,2025-04-01,,,,,False,"Job description
**Some careers open more doors than others.**


If you’re looking to unlock new job opportunities, take a look at the possibilities right on your doorstep here at HSBC.


**Business Banking**
Through Business Banking our global network offers comprehensive support and services to businesses in the SME market. From expanding overseas to managing the cash and trade flows of an established enterprise, the Business Banking team of Relationship Managers and Product Specialists provides a range of end\-to end solutions designed to help small and large businesses reach their potential.


We are currently seeking an experienced professional to join the Business Banking team.


**Job Introduction**


The role holder will work closely with the RM supporting delivery of a professional relationship management service to customers, prospective customers and professionals. The job holder is required to provide high quality service to his/her internal and external customers; taking ownership and completing all tasks in a timely manner This supports the bank’s long\-term strategy to lead business by establishing and maintaining long term relationships with businesses, treating customers fairly, identifying their needs, delivering solutions to meet those needs and providing an excellent customer service.
**Principal Responsibilities**


* Actively source New to Bank customers for Asset as well as Liability business to build a new portfolio adhering to the parameters related to minimum revenue threshold from the NTB relationship.
* Maximize HSBC share of wallet through cross selling transaction banking products.
* Ensure all sales processes are properly followed and activity data is updated in the system within stipulated timelines.
* Maintaining quality of portfolio for Asset customers and Liability customers by regular visiting and interacting and monitoring business activities .
* Develop proficiency in job related skills through exposure to training programs.
* Minimize customer complaints received. Handle customer inquiries and complaints in a way that demonstrates excellent service.
* Maintain and ensure due observance of HSBC Internal Control Standards, including the timely implementation of recommendations made by internal/external auditors and external regulators. Ensure awareness of compliance requirements and implementation of Group Compliance Policy.
* Maintain awareness of operational risk including its identification, assessment, mitigation and control, loss identification and reporting in accordance with section 4 of the Group Operations FIM.
* Foster a compliance culture and implement Group Compliance Policy by managing compliance risk in liaison with the Head of Group Compliance, Regional Compliance Officer, Area Compliance Officer or Local Compliance Officer, ensuring adequate compliance resources are in place and training is provided, and optimizing relations with regulators
Requirements
**Essential**
* Minimum Bachelor’s degree / Graduation or as required for the role, whichever is higher
* Understanding of risk management
* Some understanding of credit
* Analytical and financial skills.
* Ability to work without constant direction
* Good organizational and time management skills.
* Ability to interact with all levels of commercial customers
* Good interpersonal skills
* Good communication skills, both oral and written
* Qualifications and/or training courses

**Desirable**
* Commercial awareness, including economic, cultural, procedural and regulatory issues.
* Relevant experience working in a relationship management role
* Working knowledge of CMB’s international proposition / product capabilities
* Working knowledge of HSBC Group capabilities

**Additional Information**


* *Mandatory* *to successfully complete Anti\-Money Laundering and Sanctions training and post\-course assessment, as required*

You’ll achieve more when you join HSBC.


HSBC is committed to building a culture where all employees are valued, respected and opinions count. We take pride in providing a workplace that fosters continuous professional development, flexible working and opportunities to grow within an inclusive and diverse environment.


Personal data held by the Bank relating to employment applications will be used in accordance with our Privacy Statement, which is available on our website.


*Issued by The Hongkong and Shanghai Banking Corporation Limited, India*",,https://www.glassdoor.co.in/Overview/W-EI_IE3482.htm,Product Management
gd-1009691014696,glassdoor,https://www.glassdoor.co.in/job-listing/j?jl=1009691014696,,Deputy General Manager,KALA GENSET,Pune,2025-04-01,,,,,False,"Job Description: **General Manager – Diesel Generator (DG) Division** \| Defense Manufacturing Company

**Position Title**: General Manager – Diesel Generator (DG) Division

**Department**: Operations / Engineering / Productio

The **General Manager – Diesel Generator (DG) Division** will lead and manage all aspects of the Diesel Generator (DG) division within a defense manufacturing company. This includes overseeing the design, production, maintenance, and service of diesel generators (DG) used for critical defense applications. The role will require a strategic leader to drive product development, improve operational efficiency, ensure compliance with industry and defense regulations, and manage cross\-functional teams to meet production, safety, and financial targets. The GM will also be responsible for driving profitability, fostering innovation, and ensuring the timely delivery of DG systems for defense operations.

**Key Responsibilities:**

* **Strategic Leadership \& Planning**:
* Develop and implement the strategic vision for the DG division in alignment with company goals and objectives.
* Lead the overall growth of the DG division, ensuring the successful design, manufacturing, and servicing of high\-performance diesel generators for defense applications.
* Drive innovation and explore new technologies and systems to improve the performance, efficiency, and reliability of DG systems used in defense environments.
* Work closely with senior management to ensure the division’s strategy aligns with the company’s long\-term growth plans.
* **Operations Management**:
* Oversee the entire lifecycle of the DG division, from product design and prototyping to full\-scale production and post\-sale services.
* Manage production schedules, resource allocation, and facility operations to ensure timely and cost\-effective delivery of products.
* Ensure the DG division is adequately staffed with skilled engineers, technicians, and support staff to meet production demands.
* Optimize the operational efficiency of the division, identifying opportunities for automation, lean manufacturing, and cost reduction.
* **Team Leadership \& Development**:
* Lead, mentor, and develop a team of engineers, production staff, and managers in the DG division, promoting a culture of excellence, collaboration, and continuous improvement.
* Establish clear performance objectives and KPIs for the team, providing guidance and regular feedback to foster a high\-performance culture.
* Encourage employee development through training programs, workshops, and certifications relevant to DG manufacturing and defense industry standards.
* **Project Management \& Execution**:
* Lead the project management of new DG system designs, ensuring all projects are executed according to schedule, budget, and technical specifications.
* Coordinate with R\&D, engineering, and production teams to ensure the successful integration of new technology into DG systems for defense use.
* Oversee quality assurance processes and resolve any issues that arise during the manufacturing, assembly, and testing phases of DG products.
* Provide regular updates to senior management on the status of DG projects, including progress reports, risks, and mitigation strategies.
* **Regulatory Compliance \& Safety**:
* Ensure that all diesel generators manufactured comply with relevant defense industry standards and regulations, including ITAR, MIL\-SPEC, ISO, and other applicable guidelines.
* Implement and monitor safety protocols during production, installation, and maintenance phases to ensure a safe working environment for all personnel.
* Oversee the compliance of DG products with local, regional, and international environmental and safety standards, including emission standards for diesel generators.
* Ensure that DG products and services meet military specifications for reliability and performance under extreme conditions.
* **Customer Relations \& Support**:
* Build and maintain strong relationships with key customers, including government defense agencies, military organizations, and other defense contractors.
* Provide high\-level technical support for customer inquiries, ensuring that any issues related to DG products are addressed promptly and efficiently.
* Ensure customer satisfaction by overseeing the timely delivery, installation, and commissioning of DG systems and providing ongoing maintenance and technical support.
* Collaborate with sales teams to develop solutions that meet customer needs and specifications for DG systems.
* **Financial Management**:
* Develop and manage the budget for the DG division, ensuring financial targets are met and costs are controlled.
* Monitor key financial performance indicators (KPIs) related to cost, production, revenue, and profit margins.
* Lead pricing strategies for DG systems, considering both cost structures and market competitiveness in the defense sector.
* Identify opportunities for cost optimization and resource allocation without compromising product quality or operational efficiency.
* **Supply Chain \& Vendor Management**:
* Manage the sourcing and procurement of raw materials, components, and sub\-systems for the production of DG systems.
* Build strong relationships with key suppliers and vendors to ensure the timely delivery of high\-quality materials and components.
* Oversee logistics, ensuring that components and finished products are delivered on time to meet production schedules and customer expectations.
* Monitor supplier performance and implement corrective actions in case of supply chain disruptions or quality issues.
* **Risk Management \& Problem Solving**:
* Proactively identify potential risks in product design, manufacturing, or delivery timelines, and implement mitigation strategies.
* Troubleshoot any complex technical or operational problems related to the design, production, or servicing of DG systems.
* Work closely with other departments (engineering, quality control, customer service) to resolve issues and prevent recurrence.

Job Type: Permanent

Pay: ₹10\.00 \- ₹12\.00 per year

Benefits:

* Cell phone reimbursement
* Food provided
* Health insurance
* Provident Fund

Schedule:

* Day shift

Supplemental Pay:

* Yearly bonus

Education:

* Diploma (Preferred)

Work Location: In person",,,Product Management
