in-f14dbc56bc8b1661,indeed,https://in.indeed.com/viewjob?jk=f14dbc56bc8b1661,https://franklintempleton.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/en-US/Primary-External-1/job/Hyderabad-Telangana-India/Senior-Digital-Consultant_862037,Senior Digital Consultant,Franklin Templeton,"TS, IN",2025-04-11,fulltime,,,,False,"Fiduciary Trust International is a premier investment and wealth management firm with a commitment to growing and protecting wealth across generations. We offer a dynamic and collaborative approach to managing wealth for high\-net\-worth and ultra high\-net\-worth individuals and families, family offices, endowments, foundations, and institutions. Unlike other firms, our investment managers, tax and estate planning professionals work together to develop holistic strategies to optimize clients’ portfolios while mitigating the impact of taxes on their wealth. As a fiduciary, the guidance we provide is always in the best interests of our clients, without conflict or competing benefits. We offer boutique customization and deep expertise in specialized investment, tax and planning strategies alongside sophisticated technology and custody platforms.
Fiduciary Trust International is owned by Franklin Templeton, a diversified firm that spans asset management, wealth management, and fintech, giving us many ways to help investors make progress toward their goals. With clients in over 150 countries and offices on six continents, you’ll get exposed to different cultures, people, and business development happening around the world.
What is the Sr. Digital Consultant group responsible for?* Responsible for work on projects or parts of programs with moderate to high scope and complexity. Provides support to at least one value stream or product (business capability). Partners with project teams and business/technical partners to deliver value and achieve business strategies and objectives \#MID\_SENIOR\_LEVEL


What is the Sr. Digital Consultant responsible for?* Leads the collection of stakeholder business requirements and translates into detailed functional and technical requirements. Works directly with Product Owners, UX/UI, and technical/vendor teams to prioritize project execution based on Alpha, Beta, or MVP phase releases. Works on large\-scale, high impact, and complex initiatives involving multiple business divisions and Digital Team partners. Acts as a mentor for junior Digital Consultant resources, sharing best practices for sprint planning and execution, and release demonstrations and training.


What ideal qualifications, skills and experience would help someone to be successful?* Financial Industry: Experience in the financial industry, preferably in Wealth Management.
* Agile Expertise: Proficiency in agile methodology, including user story creation, backlog grooming and prioritization, and As\-Is/To\-Be workflow documentation and mapping. Disciplined Agile Delivery or SAFe certifications are preferred but not required.
* Communication: Strong communication, critical thinking, and problem\-solving skills. Ability to lead sprint grooming and planning meetings with technology and vendor resources, and report on backlog status and sprint planning outcomes.
* Relationship Management: Approachable and personable when interacting with team members and stakeholders.
* Critical Thinking: Ability to analyze complex problems and develop effective solutions.
* Strategic Planning: Proactive and adaptable in a fast\-paced environment. Capable of developing long\-term strategies based on workload. Proficient in product demonstrations and end\-user training.
* Tools: Expertise in JIRA, Confluence, SharePoint, and Microsoft Office suite. Proficiency in CRM, PowerBI/Power Apps, and ServiceNow preferred.


Work Shift Timings \- 2:00 PM \- 11:00 PM IST
