The Media Ant is an 12\-year\-old platform for media discovery, planning, and execution of marketing campaigns. We aim to disrupt the traditional process of executing ad campaigns through a physical media agency and replace it with a self\-serve advertising platform. The platform works equally well for both online and offline media.


This platform will empower any advertiser, irrespective of their budget and level of marketing understanding, to be able to plan and launch a campaign.


The Media Ant is the winner of various startup awards and is used by more than a million users every year. Please visit our website (www.TheMediaAnt.com) to learn more.  



  

**Job Description:**

As a Manager for Influencer Marketing, you will be responsible for creating and executing influencer marketing campaigns to promote our brand, products, or services. Your role will involve partnering with influencers, understanding and communicating the brief, overlook the


entire campaign execution and measuring the impact of campaigns to achieve the campaign marketing objectives.  



  

**Education/Job Experience Required:**

* MBA/Master Degree in marketing, communications, or a related field (or equivalent work
* experience).
* 2 \- 4 years of proven experience in influencer marketing or digital marketing, with a
* strong portfolio of successful influencer campaigns.
* Excellent communication and negotiation skills.
* Strong understanding of social media platforms and influencer marketing trends.
* Proficiency in data analytics tools to track and measure campaign performance.
* Creative thinking and the ability to develop engaging content ideas.
* Attention to detail and project management skills.
Ability to work collaboratively within a team and with external influencers.  
* 

  

  

**Location:** Bengaluru **.**

  

**Day\-to\-Day Work:**

**Content Collaboration** :


* Work closely with influencers to conceptualize and create engaging and authentic content that resonates with their audience and our brand message.
* Provide creative direction and guidelines to ensure content quality and brand consistency.

**Compliance Management:**

* Ensure influencers adhere to contractual obligations and deadlines.
Ensure that influencers follow industry regulations and guidelines regarding disclosures and endorsements.  
* 

  

**Campaign Execution:**

* Monitor and manage influencer content across various social media platforms and other relevant channels.
Engage with influencers to maintain a positive and productive relationship throughout the campaign.  
* 

  

**Performance Measurement:**

* Track and analyze the performance of influencer campaigns using key metrics (engagement rates, reach, conversion, etc.).
Provide regular reports and insights to assess campaign effectiveness and make data\- driven recommendations for improvement.  
* 

  

**Stay Updated:**

Stay current with industry trends, emerging platforms, and new influencer opportunities to keep our influencer marketing strategies innovative and effective.  

* 

  

  

**Must\-Have:**

**In\-depth Knowledge of Social Media Platforms:**

Proficiency in various social media platforms such as Instagram, TikTok, YouTube,Twitter, etc., including understanding their algorithms, user demographics, and best practices.  

* 

  

**Familiarity with Influencer Ecosystem:**

Knowledge of the influencer landscape, including different types of influencers, their niches, engagement rates, and audience demographics.  

* 

  

  

**Communication Skills**

 Strong verbal and written communication skills to effectively liaise with influencers, clients, and internal teams, as well as to craft compelling campaign briefs and reports.  



  

**Budgeting and Resource Management:**

 Experience in allocating budgets effectively, optimizing resources, and maximizing ROI for influencer marketing campaigns.  



  

**Good to have:**

  

**Attention to Detail:**

 Being detail\-oriented is important for managing multiple campaigns simultaneously, ensuring all elements are executed correctly, and measuring campaign performance accurately.  



  

**Creativity:**

 The ability to come up with creative campaign ideas that resonate with the target audience and align with the brand \& objectives.  



  

**Team Collaboration:**

 Ability to work collaboratively with other marketing team members, social media managers, and creative teams to align influencer campaigns with overall marketing strategies.",,https://in.indeed.com/cmp/The-Media-Ant-1,Product Management
in-81d03999215c731c,indeed,https://in.indeed.com/viewjob?jk=81d03999215c731c,https://www.okta.com/company/careers/product/senior-director-of-product-management-okta-isv-6201138/,"Senior Director of Product Management, Okta ISV",Okta,"KA, IN",2025-04-11,fulltime,,,,False,"**Get to know Okta**  

  

Okta is The World’s Identity Company. We free everyone to safely use any technology—anywhere, on any device or app. Our Workforce and Customer Identity Clouds enable secure yet flexible access, authentication, and automation that transforms how people move through the digital world, putting Identity at the heart of business security and growth.  

  

At Okta, we celebrate a variety of perspectives and experiences. We are not looking for someone who checks every single box \- we’re looking for lifelong learners and people who can make us better with their unique experiences.  

  

Join our team! We’re building a world where Identity belongs to you.


Companies all over the world and across every industry trust Okta for elegant and secure identity management. Okta relies on its partner ISVs for not only the Okta Integration Network (OIN) ecosystem, but also the success of our largest customers due to the security and trust our partners reinforce through our joint offerings.



We are looking for a driven, curious, and empathetic product management leader to push the envelope of Okta’s market footprint by growing our ISV ecosystem. As Director of Product Management for Okta ISV Ecosystem, this manager will be responsible for product strategy, and managing a PM team dedicated to evolving the ISV touchpoints (digital properties, environments, app dev/test/submit/publish, API surface area) across the entirety of the partner’s journey with Okta. If you have a passion for custom/partner collaboration, ecosystems, and a belief that ISV success is core to an enterprise software company’s expansion, we are looking for you!


**Responsibilities**


* Own the growth of Okta’s ISV ecosystem through product vision.
* Connect with key ISV partners and customers to distill down feature asks and pain points into true requirements that deliver broad customer value
* Develop roadmaps that make hard tradeoffs and prioritize the highest value work first
* Build compelling hypotheses and find ways to validate assumptions at low cost
* Collaborate with global cross\-functional teams, including engineering, ISV program, tech partnerships, and marketing, to ensure the successful launch and adoption of ISV experience enhancements.
* Work with India\-based development scrum teams (PM, UX, Dev) to deliver valuable new ISV targeted features and product improvements to customers.
* Conduct research and analysis to identify ISV partner needs, and use this information to inform strategic vision, innovation, product decisions, prioritization and roadmap.
* Define and communicate product requirements, including features, user experience, and technical specifications, to engineering teams.
* Leverage product data to continually get smarter about how to improve our existing products, and work across the business to drive adoption and success
* Track industry trends and think strategically to develop solutions that are differentiated from the competition
* Be the subject matter expert for your product area and help enable your counterparts in the ISV Program, Marketing, and tech partnerships teams.

**Required:**


* 13\+ years of Product Management experience in enterprise scale SaaS products or comparable relevant experience.
* Experience building or product managing the user experience of a partner joining, engaging, and building upon a core enterprise software platform.
* Strong communication (presentation, verbal and written) and collaboration skills. You easily work with customers and colleagues across different functions and backgrounds.
* Demonstrated business results from products, features or capabilities you have shipped.
* Strong analytical, problem\-solving, and decision\-making skills. You can produce solid action plans from often incomplete, conflicting or ambiguous inputs.
