What to expect at BizBox:

  

* A workplace is driven by non\-negotiable and ‘Culture First’ organizational values
  
* A 9\-hour workday and a 5\-day workweek.
  
* Best in class Health Insurance
  

About us:

  

We are a best\-in\-class creative services company. We serve and partner with top brands in the wedding, fashion, beauty, media, and entertainment industries worldwide. We're a team of fast\-paced, hard\-working, forward thinkers who are dedicated to succeeding on behalf of one another and on behalf of our customers, at scale.

  

  

What we do:

  

BizBox clients make up a variety of market leaders in the following areas: Small \& Medium\-Sized Entrepreneurship, Photography, Sales, Marketing, Social Media. Our clients require creative content that is inspirational, motivational, narrative\-driven, and also technical.

  

  

Our vision is to create products and services that radically improve the success of our customers. We are also a modern content communication company committed to creating and designing relevant and valuable content that will create amazement, ignite inspiration, educate, promote entrepreneurial gusto, and motivate our community of customers to succeed.

  

  

What we’re looking for:

  

  

We are seeking a talented and experienced Mid\-Senior Salesforce Developer to join our remote team. In this role, you will take ownership of our Salesforce environment, contributing actively to solution architecture and integration while ensuring continuous improvement and innovation. You will work closely with cross\-functional teams, including the web team and various stakeholders, to design, develop, and optimize Salesforce solutions that drive business success.

  

Successful candidates at Bizbox are draft picks from the marketplace and professional peer group. They bring consistent intellectual energy and acumen to their position and increase value to our teammates AND our customers.

  

They demonstrate a strong alignment with our values. At Bizbox, we stay 'True North’ by practicing:

  

* An Open mind to always improving through coaching.
  
* On\-time and accurate delivery.
  
* Kindness.
  
* Transparency; Accountable and humble, yet has the strength to communicate with their upline with conviction.
  
* Always willing to go the extra mile for our colleagues and our customers. We bring a 'solutions' mindset to the table.
  
* Inspecting what we expect; Planning what we do, doing what we plan.
  

KEY RESPONSIBILITIES:

  

  

* Comprehensive Development: Design, develop, and maintain custom Salesforce applications and integrations using Apex, Visualforce, Lightning Web Components, and Flows.
  
* Peer Code Reviews \& Best Practices: Lead and participate in peer code reviews to ensure adherence to coding standards and best practices, fostering a culture of technical excellence and collaboration.
  
* Stakeholder Communication: Collaborate with business analysts, project managers, the web team, and stakeholders to translate complex business requirements into scalable, robust solutions.
  
* Continuous Improvement: Identify opportunities for system enhancements, actively contribute to revamping our Salesforce architecture and processes, and stay updated with the latest Salesforce technologies and trends.
  
* Integration \& Support: Integrate Salesforce with other systems using APIs and middleware, manage deployment processes with CI/CD tools, and provide technical support and guidance across teams.
  

  

KPIs:

  

PERFORMANCE GOALS / KPIs

  

  

* Complete 100% of assigned sprint items by the deadline
  
* Complete all assigned advanced level of Salesforce Flows or Apex work by the assigned deadline.
  
* 100% quality of code review
  
* Additional KPIs will be incorporated at the time of onboarding
  

  

Required Qualifications

  

  

* 4–6 years of experience in Salesforce development.
  
* Proficiency in Apex, Visualforce, Lightning Web Components, and Salesforce Flows.
  
* Strong experience with Salesforce integrations and API development.
  
* Solid understanding of Salesforce data modeling, security, and administration best practices.
  
* Demonstrated ability to conduct peer code reviews and mentor team members.
  
* Proven aptitude for collaborating in a remote, fast\-paced environment.
  

  

  

  

  

  

Preferred Qualifications

  

  

* Salesforce certifications (e.g., Platform Developer I \& II, Administrator).
  
* Familiarity with Agile Scrum methodologies.
  
* Experience with third\-party applications and integration tools.
  
* Exposure to CI/CD practices within Salesforce development environments.
  
* Industry\-specific knowledge, such as experience with Pardot or similar marketing automation tools.
  

  

  

  

  

  

What We Value

  

  

* A passion for Salesforce development, innovation, and continuous learning.
  
* A collaborative mindset with strong communication skills to work effectively with both technical and non\-technical stakeholders.
  
* Initiative and leadership in driving peer code reviews and best practices across the team.
  
* A commitment to contributing to our evolving Salesforce architecture and delivering creative, scalable solutions.
  

  

  

  

  

  

Career Growth and Benefits

  

  

* Opportunity to actively shape solution architecture and integration strategies while continuously upskilling with the latest Salesforce technologies.
  
* Involvement in revamping Salesforce architecture and processes, offering a mix of ongoing maintenance and new feature development.
  
* Competitive salary and benefits package, including health, dental, and vision coverage.
  
* A monthly remote work allowance to support your home office setup and a fully remote work environment.
  

  

  

  

  

  

Inclusivity and Work Environment

  

  

* We are a remote\-based organization that believes in collaboration, teamwork, and growing together.
  
* Our culture is built on innovation, inclusivity, and continuous improvement, welcoming candidates from diverse backgrounds and experiences.",,https://in.indeed.com/cmp/Bizbox-Publishing,Product Management
in-4d88fd6d267cf304,indeed,https://in.indeed.com/viewjob?jk=4d88fd6d267cf304,https://careers.rapid7.com/jobs/software-engineering-manager-pune-india-6a88707f-f17f-4d74-8b30-4bf6fbdae23e?source=indeed,Software Engineering Manager,Rapid7,"Remote, IN",2025-04-11,fulltime,,,,True,"Rapid7 is a publicly traded Cybersecurity company headquartered in Boston, MA with 17 offices around the world. We are excited to be expanding our Global footprint into India and as we build out our Product \& Engineering teams, we are looking for an experienced Software Engineering Manager. You will lead a team of software engineers, set the prioritization and direction for your team and be passionate about helping them grow and develop through mentorship and coaching. This is an exciting opportunity to be one of the first hires for Rapid7 in India supporting our growth strategy in a culture that supports trying new approaches and continuous learning.

**About the Team**


Our Product and Engineering team works with our award\-winning products to help us create a single experience to help customers assess risk, detect threats and automate their security programs at over 10,000 organizations. These teams use best\-in\-class technology, leading\-edge research, and broad, strategic expertise to develop new products and features, and enhance existing features, in order to create value for customers across the world.


The stakes for creating a safer digital world are greater than ever. At Rapid7 we believe it’s our responsibility to show up every day and give our best for our customers and the entire security community. Our global engineering teams are at the centre of this mission and are dedicated to building a complete suite of industry\-leading products which provide a cohesive platform for our customers. Our range of solutions spans vulnerability management, detection, automation, cloud security, and penetration testing; in order to build these products our teams work with an array of technologies including Java, Python, AWS and Go, just to name a few.


Join our engineering team to help us build and innovate great products on our Insight platform using the latest technologies to make the world a safer digital space.

**About the Role**


As a Software Engineering Manager you will be responsible for managing the day\-to\-day operations. First and foremost, you will coach and grow the individuals on your team so they feel supported and engaged.


You will also be responsible for keeping track of the projects the teams are working on, facilitating cross\-team discussions when necessary and deciding on the future direction of the team (what projects they will focus on next). You will collaborate with UX, Product and other development teams to deliver best\-in\-class solutions for our customers.


In this role, you will:

* Directly manage a team of Software Engineers, coaching and mentoring team members, including scoping work and prioritising tasks
* Mentor engineers and help grow their skills, identify growth areas, set expectations and provide feedback
* Manage projects and socialising progress across engineering teams and leadership
* Keep a keen eye on quality, and continue to drive improvements to testing, monitoring and alerting
* Work cross functionally with PM, UX and Engineering to address specific customer pain points and to think strategically about the future direction of the product
* Work closely with other managers and teams across the InsightVM product to align efforts and initiatives
* Kickstart new ideas, build proof of concepts and jumpstart newly funded projects
* Work closely with other managers and teams across the InsightVM product to align efforts and initiatives


The skills you’ll bring include:

* 10\+ years of experience working within Software Engineering including 3\+ years experience in managing engaged and high performing software engineering teams with a track record in developing and mentoring software engineers at all levels
* A demonstrable passion for all things software engineering with a solid understanding of the software development lifecycle and the ability to read code
* A solid pulse on the security landscape
* A customer centric approach with the ability to drive that throughout your teams, understanding the customers needs and drivers and putting the customer at the forefront of all decision making
* Strong cross\-functional skills, with the ability and desire to build relationships with other teams including Product Management, UX and engineering teams to achieve broader company objectives
* Experience with managing multiple, high\-impact projects
* Capable of managing through high\-intensity situations when they arise
* BEng, BSc or related technical field or equivalent practical experience


We know that the best ideas and solutions come from multi\-dimensional teams. Teams reflecting a variety of backgrounds and professional experiences. If you are excited about this role and feel your experience can make an impact, please don’t be shy \- apply today.

**About Rapid7**


At Rapid7, we are on a mission to create a secure digital world for our customers, our industry, and our communities. We do this by embracing tenacity, passion, and collaboration to challenge what’s possible and drive extraordinary impact.


Here, we’re building a dynamic workplace where everyone can have the career experience of a lifetime. We challenge ourselves to grow to our full potential. We learn from our missteps and celebrate our victories. We come to work every day to push boundaries in cybersecurity and keep our 10,000 global customers ahead of whatever’s next.

  

Join us and bring your unique experiences and perspectives to tackle some of the world’s biggest security challenges.

  

\#LI\-MM10",,https://in.indeed.com/cmp/Rapid7,Product Management
