in-f2fbd4606bb6d589,indeed,https://in.indeed.com/viewjob?jk=f2fbd4606bb6d589,http://in.indeed.com/job/general-manager-sales-f2fbd4606bb6d589,General Manager Sales,ankit pulps and board,"MH, IN",2025-04-11,fulltime,,,,False,"Contact Person No:7666900213

**Job Description Of General Manager Sales**

**Key Job Responsibilities**

\- Create and implement strategic sales and marketing plans to successfully achieve business objectives

\- Monitor competitor products with relevant sales and marketing data

\- Use and monitor available data to accurately forecast sales and set appropriate sales performance goals

\- Identifying key clients and develop and maintain positive relationships with key clients.

\- Plan visits, Price Negotiation and close Key client contracts.

\- Develop complete plan along with budgets for marketing activities for team

\- Monitor daily communications via CRM, Outlook emails and take appropriate steps where ever necessary.

\- Maintain the average selling price

\- Keeping the outstanding at bare minimum. Proactively monitors account receivables from directs accounts to maintain a healthy credit control scenario

\- Develop sales monitoring system for team members for daily, weekly, monthly visible targets vs achievements along with incentive schemes

**Other Vital Accountabilities**

\- Manage teams with focus on excelling business targets \& sales metrics.

\- Responsible for handing existing customers in import \& export market

\- Focusing more on special grade/value products for achieving the average price.

\- Developing new business across the globe for Microcrystalline Cellulose Powder, Spirulina Powder and other products.

\- Responsible for appointing new distributors or end customers.

\- Coordinate with other heads of departments, integrating objectives and ideas for organizational growth

\- Allocate resources to various centres and regions; all aimed at achieving results

\- Responsible for training and mentoring staff; motivating them all for effective performance for the growth of the company

**Product Profile**

\- MCC is used in Pharma industry: as excipient, bulking agent and as binder to increase tablet hardness. It acts as disintegrating agent, stabiliser, adsorbent, anti\-sticking agent and capsule diluent.

\- MCC has wide applications in food industry. Used as Hot and Cold stabiliser, fat substitute and emulsifier in Ice Cream industry, Frozen foods, desserts \& canned meat for improved stability.

\- Used as gelling agent, stabilizer, anti\-caking agent and suspending agent in beverages \& Fruit Juices.

\- It's anti\-caking properties in Bakery industry helps improving crispiness, to improve water retention, to reduce calories \& breakages.

\- Spirulina is blue\-green algae consumed by humans and animals. It is used as dietary supplement.

\- Spirulina is available in Powder, Tablet and Capsule formats.

**Job Specification**

\- Qualification \- B. Tech / MSc / M. Pharm/B. Pharm \+ MBA

\- Experience \- 5 to 20 Years in similar API/Capsules/excipient/ Food industries with at least 5 years as Sales Head / Leadership role

Job Type: Full\-time

Pay: ₹1,000,000\.00 \- ₹1,500,000\.00 per year

Benefits:

* Cell phone reimbursement
* Health insurance
* Provident Fund

Schedule:

* Day shift

Supplemental Pay:

* Performance bonus
* Yearly bonus

Work Location: In person",,https://in.indeed.com/cmp/Ankit-Pulps-and-Board,Product Management
in-38e56b1401e0b935,indeed,https://in.indeed.com/viewjob?jk=38e56b1401e0b935,https://app.jobvite.com/CompanyJobs/Job.aspx?j=oHCNvfwl&loc=CoLoWfwd&s=Indeed,Member of Technical Staff 2 (Backend),Nutanix,"MH, IN",2025-04-11,fulltime,,,,False,"**Hungry, Humble, Honest, with Heart.**  

  

**The Opportunity**  

Are you a flexible and adaptable software engineer with a strong problem\-solving attitude and a passion for engaging with customers? If so, you’ll thrive in our collaborative and supportive environment, where you’ll have the opportunity to learn new technologies, solve real customer challenges, and contribute to innovative cloud solutions at Nutanix.  

  

**About the Team**  

The MTS1 role is part of the NC2 Core Team located in . This team embraces a culture centered around humility and support, ensuring that every member feels valued and comfortable. The mission of the NC2 Core Team at Nutanix is to continuously innovate and deliver high\-quality cloud solutions that effectively address customer needs, fostering a collaborative environment where team members can grow together and develop their technical skills. The team is dedicated to learning and adapting to new technologies, ensuring they remain at the forefront of cloud infrastructure solutions.  

You will report to a Senior Engineering Manager, who emphasizes a strong work\-life balance and prioritizes the well\-being of team members. The manager encourages an open and adaptive leadership style, focusing on mentorship and support to help team members thrive. The position is hybrid, requiring the hire to work from the office two days a week initially, with plans to adjust to three days in the near future.  

There are no anticipated travel requirements for this role, allowing the new hire to focus on their responsibilities without the added burden of travel constraints. The position is designed to facilitate strong communication and collaboration within the team while engaging directly with customers on\-site as needed.**About the Team: Nutanix Clusters**  

Nutanix Clusters provides a single platform that can span private and public clouds but operates as a single cloud using Prism Central enabling true hybrid cloud architecture.  

Using the same platform on both clouds, Nutanix Clusters reduces the operational complexity of extending, bursting, or migrating your applications and data between clouds. Because Nutanix Clusters runs Nutanix AOS and AHV with the same CLI, UI, and APIs, existing IT processes or third\-party integrations that work on\-premises continue to work regardless of where they are running.**Your Role*** Architect, design and develop storage software for a converged computing and storage platform for the software\-defined data center.
* Develop a deep understanding of complex distributed systems, and design innovative solutions for customer requirements.
* Work on performance, scaling out and resiliency of distributed storage systems.
* Work closely with development, test, documentation and product management teams to deliver high\-quality products in a fast\-paced environment.
* Engage with customers and support when needed to solve production issues.


**What You Will Bring*** Experience in designing, building and supporting large\-scale distributed systems software and fault\-tolerant services.
* Excellent understanding of low\-level operating system concepts, including multi\-threading, concurrency, memory management, networking and storage, performance and scale.
* Strong systems programming skills
* Strong CS fundamentals include high\-performance data structures, algorithms, and distributed systems.
* Love of programming and rock\-solid in one or more languages: Go, C\+\+, Python, ideally for enterprise\-quality software.
* Development experience in distributed system management, Cloud native services, and orchestration engines.
* Familiarity with Docker, Kubernetes, Envoy, Istio, a plus.
* Optional: Familiarity with any popular cloud platforms such as AWS/GCP and cloud architecture (multi\-tenancy, IAM, components and abstractions, object store fundamentals, REST API development) preferred
* Bachelor’s/Master’s (required), or PhD (preferred) in Computer Science
* Exp: 2–3 Years",Internet And Software,https://in.indeed.com/cmp/Nutanix,Product Management
