in-fef10e124afc64cc,indeed,https://in.indeed.com/viewjob?jk=fef10e124afc64cc,http://in.indeed.com/job/blockchain-developer-fef10e124afc64cc,Blockchain Developer,MasterTech  WebApplications,"Thane, MH, IN",2025-04-11,fulltime,,,,False,"**Job Title:** Senior Blockchain \& Golang Developer

**Job Location:** Thane, Maharashtra

**Job Type:** Full\-Time (Work from Office

**Salary:** Competitive, based on experience

**Job Description:**

We are seeking an experienced Blockchain Developer with a strong command of the Go programming language (Golang) to join our team and contribute to the development of a next\-generation privacy\-focused blockchain solution.

You will work on reviving and scaling a sophisticated open\-source blockchain infrastructure, which includes components for private transactions, cross\-chain interoperability, a privacy\-first DEX (pDEX), staking mechanisms, and a native token economy.

**Key Responsibilities:**

* Analyze, troubleshoot, and optimize an existing Go\-based privacy blockchain codebase to align with modern standards.
* Create and maintain clear technical documentation to ensure scalability, maintainability, and knowledge transfer.
* Improve the core protocol with privacy\-preserving features (e.g., stealth addresses, ring signatures, private staking).
* Implement mechanisms to facilitate private transactions across major blockchains like Bitcoin and Ethereum.
* Conduct security audits and integrate advanced cryptographic techniques to secure the network.
* Build and enhance features for a privacy\-focused decentralized exchange, including AMM models, atomic swaps, and liquidity pools.
* Write, deploy, and audit smart contracts for CHML token transactions, governance, staking, and DEX functionality.
* Design and maintain staking systems and validator node infrastructure (V\-Nodes \& P\-Nodes) to support decentralized operations
* Create performance monitoring, debugging, and scaling tools for validator and network operation.
* Integrate privacy features into mobile and web wallet apps, supporting shielding, unshielding, staking, and multi\-currency storage.
* Conduct thorough unit, integration, and stress testing across modules to ensure high reliability and efficiency.
* Build APIs and SDKs for external developers and support ecosystem expansion.
* Work closely with product managers, full\-stack engineers, and designers to hit project milestones.

**Requirements:**

* Strong expertise in Golang (Go) – required. Experience building production\-ready Go applications, ideally within blockchain environments.
* Proficiency in blockchain architectures, P2P networking, consensus algorithms, and decentralization principles.
* Familiarity with privacy features like stealth addresses, RingCT, zero\-knowledge proofs, or homomorphic encryption.
* Hands\-on experience with smart contract frameworks like Anchor, Hardhat, or Truffle.
* Experience developing or debugging DEX, staking mechanisms, and cross\-chain bridges.
* Prior experience working with open\-source blockchain codebases, especially privacy\-centric or layer\-1 protocols.
* Comfort working with APIs, SDKs, and Web3\.js, @solana/web3\.js, or similar libraries.
* Strong debugging, reverse engineering, and legacy code modernization experience.
* Effective communication and documentation skills for working in distributed, multi\-disciplinary teams.

**Preferred Qualifications:**

* Experience contributing to or maintaining blockchain protocols written in Go.
* Exposure to decentralized governance models (DAO frameworks).
* Experience with CI/CD, DevOps tooling, or automated testing pipelines.
* Previous work on privacy blockchain or DeFi projects (e.g., Monero, Zcash, Secret Network, etc.).
* Familiarity with sharding, rollups, or other blockchain scaling solutions.

If you're passionate about privacy, decentralization, and building tools that push the boundaries of blockchain innovation—this role is for you.

