Role\- Area Credit Manager  



Job Description:


Candidate shall be a part of credit team in the capacity of Area Credit Head for West (which caters to Maharashtra, Central) for Relationship Banking (RBG) Group and TDF and *will be based at Mumbai* . RBG Business under Commercial Banking at Kotak Mahindra Bank caters to all the working capital requirements of Commercial Vehicles / Construction Equipment (Infrastructure) / Dealer Finance segments. TDF business caters to funding requirements of Auto / Tractor dealers in rural / semi urban regions.  



* To provide sound, independent (unsolicited) credit advice, recommendations and quality feedback on Commercial Vehicles / Construction Equipment (Infrastructure) / Dealer Finance credit proposals.
* Handling all types of working capital facilities (Fund base and Non\-fund based limit)
* Credit appraisal including financial analysis to understand the solvency, liquidity position and repayment capacity of the entity, preparation of appraisal notes, credit checks etc.
* As per Approval Authorizations, presenting the proposal to various sanctioning forums and get it sanctioned from approving authority satisfying all their queries.
* Meeting Customer and making Site visits at factory/office/residence of the client, viewing the working capacities of the business, inventory and working environment of the business.
* To interact with approving authority and provide them with required information for better decision making and engaging in regular discussions to give them an independent view of the credit / economic developments.
* To monitor and manage credit portfolio and other risks on a proactive basis by having an in\-depth knowledge on individual credit\-takers. Engage in discussions with the business to modify account strategy / credit rating, etc. as warranted.
* Manage and ensure timely renewal of accounts and enhancement of portfolio.
* To align decision making with business requirements without compromising on quality of decision making or compromising on laid down policies by engaging in regular discussions with the business teams.
* To contribute in central projects and also interact with vendors and external agencies for providing support in digital business solution \& IT teams to develop scalable reporting/decision support tools
* Maintenance of various MIS / compliance related records and providing it to the authorities from time to time.
* Excellent written and oral communication skills
* Chartered Accountant / MBA with an experience of credit underwriting and also leading credit team with an experience of at least 6\-8 yrs
* *Experience of team management*
* Good analytical skills
* Good understanding of all the working capital products",,https://in.indeed.com/cmp/Kotak-Mahindra-Bank,Product Management
