Job Title: MLOps Engineer \_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_ Job Summary: Machine Learning Operations (MLOps) enable the deployment of AI/ML models from development environments to production environments. At UST, the MLOps team manages both customized MLOps services for clients as well as development of a proprietary MLOps platform called UST xpresso.ai. We are seeking talented and innovative MLOps Engineers for both services and platform divisions. In this role, you will collaborate closely with data scientists, software engineers, and DevOps teams to design, develop, and deploy robust ML models and pipelines. You may also be asked to work on implementing exciting new MLOps features (including Generative AI features) into UST xpresso.ai. We are looking for motivated and enthusiastic engineers for this role. Lack of knowledge of Machine Learning / MLOps is not a limitation to the right candidate. Our team will provide the required training. The right attitude and aptitude is more important for this role. \_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_ Key Responsibilities: • Provide MLOps Services to clients o Model Deployment \& Integration:  Collaborate with data scientists and software engineers to deploy machine learning models into production.  Develop and maintain end\-to\-end ML pipelines from training to deployment. o Infrastructure \& Automation:  Design, implement, and manage CI/CD pipelines to automate model testing, deployment, and monitoring.  Utilize containerization (Docker) and orchestration (Kubernetes) to streamline deployment processes.  Manage cloud\-based infrastructure (AWS, GCP, or Azure) to optimize cost and performance. o Monitoring \& Maintenance:  Implement robust logging, monitoring, and ing solutions to ensure system reliability.  Troubleshoot and resolve issues in production, ensuring minimal downtime and performance degradation. o Collaboration \& Documentation:  Work closely with cross\-functional teams to integrate ML systems with existing software and data pipelines.  Document system architecture, processes, and best practices to support team collaboration and knowledge sharing.  Stay updated with emerging trends and technologies in MLOps, machine learning, and cloud services. • Xpresso.ai Platform Development o Understand the microservices\-based architecture of xpresso.ai o Work closely with the product management team and technical leads to understand new features, or changes to existing ones o Provide detailed designs and effort estimates for implementing new features o Make changes to existing microservices, or create new ones, to implement new features. Thoroughly unit test any changes made o Deploy the changed microservices to the xpresso.ai DEV environment and run integration tests o Work closely with the QA team during the QA cycle to fix any issues found o Follow standard software development processes, including code versioning, unit testing, documentation, etc. \_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_ Required Qualifications: • Education: Bachelor’s or Master’s degree in Computer Science, Engineering, or a related field. • Experience: 2\+ years in roles related to software development, or DevOps. • Collaborative mindset, Willingness to learn • Technical Skills: o Proficiency in Python o Understanding of Object\-Oriented Programming Principles o Experience with at least one database (preferably MongoDB) o Solid grasp of Linux operating systems and shell scripting. \_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_ Preferred Qualifications: • Experience with serverless architectures and microservices. • Hands\-on experience with containerization (Docker) and orchestration (Kubernetes). • Strong understanding of CI/CD tools (e.g., Jenkins, Bamboo, GitLab CI/CD, CircleCI). • Experience with cloud platforms (AWS, GCP, or Azure) and managing scalable infrastructures. • Familiarity with monitoring tools (e.g., Prometheus, Grafana) and logging systems. • Familiarity with ML frameworks (e.g., TensorFlow, PyTorch, scikit\-learn) • Knowledge of Infrastructure as Code (e.g., Terraform, CloudFormation). • Familiarity with data engineering concepts and ETL pipeline development. • Experience with A/B testing frameworks and model performance tracking • Familiarity with model artifact registries • Understanding of security aspects around data ingestion and model deployment
