in-703d29e4fabf415b,indeed,https://in.indeed.com/viewjob?jk=703d29e4fabf415b,http://in.indeed.com/job/marketing-manager-703d29e4fabf415b,Marketing Manager,,"WB, IN",2025-04-11,fulltime,,,,False,"About Us:

The Fashion Secrets is a leading manufacturer and wholesaler of Saree, kurti and blouses, blending traditional craftsmanship with modern design. We are committed to quality, style, and customer satisfaction. With a strong presence on social media, we’re looking for a passionate and creative Marketing Manager to lead our brand's growth across digital platforms.

Job Summary:

The Marketing Manager will be responsible for developing and executing innovative marketing strategies to enhance brand awareness, drive customer engagement, and boost sales. The ideal candidate is a trend\-savvy professional with a deep understanding of digital marketing, social media, and fashion retail.

Key Responsibilities:

Marketing Strategy \& Planning:

Develop and implement effective marketing campaigns for both B2B and B2C segments.

Set marketing goals aligned with business objectives.

Content Creation \& Social Media Management:

Lead content planning and execution for Instagram, Facebook, and YouTube.

Oversee creation of engaging reels, videos, stories, and posts that highlight product features, behind\-the\-scenes, and customer stories.

Brand Management:

Maintain consistent brand messaging across all channels.

Manage collaborations with influencers and fashion bloggers.

Digital Marketing \& Advertising:

Plan and manage paid advertising campaigns across Meta (Facebook \& Instagram) and YouTube.

Monitor campaign performance, analyze ROI, and optimize for best results.

Market Research \& Trends:

Analyze customer insights, market trends, and competitor activity.

Suggest product development or promotional changes based on insights.

Team \& Coordination:

Collaborate with the design, production, and sales teams to align marketing efforts.

Guide junior marketing staff or freelancers as needed.

Requirements:

Bachelor's degree in Marketing, Business, or a related field.

2\+ years of experience in fashion marketing or digital marketing.

Strong knowledge of Instagram, Facebook, YouTube, and paid media tools.

Excellent creative, storytelling, and communication skills.

Experience with Canva, video editing tools, and social media scheduling platforms.

Passion for ethnic fashion and understanding of traditional wear is a plus.

Job Type: Full\-time

Pay: ₹15,000\.00 \- ₹21,000\.00 per month

Supplemental Pay:

* Overtime pay
* Performance bonus
* Yearly bonus

Work Location: In person",,https://in.indeed.comNone,Product Management
in-4e0cb23f89e46287,indeed,https://in.indeed.com/viewjob?jk=4e0cb23f89e46287,https://app.jobvite.com/CompanyJobs/Job.aspx?j=oBBLvfwc&s=Indeed,Coordinator - Ad,Xperi,"KA, IN",2025-04-11,fulltime,,,,False,"Xperi invents, develops and delivers technologies that create extraordinary experiences at home and on the go for millions of people around the world. Powering billions of consumer electronics, connected cars and digital content titles, we make entertainment more immersive, driving more intelligent and every interaction seamlessly personalized through our renowned consumer brands: **DTS®, HD Radio™** and **TiVo®**.

Xperi (NYSE: XPER) is a publicly traded technology company headquartered in San Jose, CA with over 2,000 employees across North America, Europe and Asia. Come join a thriving team where you can play an integral role in shaping the future of entertainment technology.
**About TiVo Advertising**
TiVo brings entertainment together, making it easy to find, watch and enjoy. We serve up the best movies, shows and videos from across live TV, on\-demand, streaming services and countless apps, helping people to watch on their terms. For studios, networks and advertisers, TiVo delivers a passionate group of watchers to increase viewership and engagement across all screens. Our Advertisers are our partners in connecting their brand to audiences they need to reach.
**About the role:**
TiVo is seeking an India\-based Advertising Operations Coordinator to join our team. The ideal candidate is detail oriented and proactive. The position will be responsible for the scheduling, QC, optimization and reporting of advertising campaigns across multiple platforms, both proprietary and third party, and in multiple regions and timezones. This role requires a strong understanding of ad operations, excellent organizational skills, and the ability to work collaboratively with various teams to ensure the successful delivery of ad campaigns.  

**Key Responsibilities****:*** Campaign Execution: Manage the scheduling and trafficking of advertising campaigns using proprietary and third party ad systems. Ensure best practices are adhered to and ad policies are enforced.
* Campaign Optimization: Monitor and optimize campaigns to ensure they meet performance goals and client expectations.
* Collaboration: Work closely with the sales, engineering, and creative teams to gather campaign requirements and ensure accurate and timely execution.
* Troubleshooting: Proactively identify and resolve any issues related to ad delivery, including discrepancies, technical problems, and performance concerns. Take ownership of initial escalations from partner teams.
* Reporting: Generate and analyze reports on campaign performance, providing insights and recommendations for optimization.
* Documentation: Maintain detailed records of campaign schedules, changes, and performance metrics.
* Innovation: Stay up to date on industry trends and provide feedback to product and engineering teams on recommended process and system improvements.Other assignments as needed.


**Qualifications****:*** 1\-2yrs experience in advertising campaign oversight, execution, and technical support across CTV \- display advertising.
* Understanding of direct sold digital display advertising products a plus.
* Ability to grasp technical concepts, work collaboratively and confidently with clients, across internal departments and with senior leadership.
* Customer\-centric mindset and a strong focus on driving business growth.
* Thrives in a dynamic, fast\-paced, high\-growth work environment. Highly organized, with the ability to proactively manage multiple tasks simultaneously.
* Strong proactive communicator, and service\-oriented personality with high interpersonal skills.
* Experience with Google Ad Manager, Salesforce, Adobe Creative Suite and familiarity with common web languages a plus.
* Ability to speak fluent English. Spanish speaking a plus.

**Life @ Xperi:**
At Xperi, we value People, Customers, Performance and Innovation. We are dedicated to creating a workplace where all employees have a voice and sense of belonging, feel safe and valued, and are acknowledged for how their unique differences contribute to organizational culture and business outcomes.
Our employees and their families are important to us, and our comprehensive pay, stock and benefits programs reflect that. Xperi supports personal well\-being, builds financial security and enables employees to share in our collective success.
