in-a6d254b0d83ac28f,indeed,https://in.indeed.com/viewjob?jk=a6d254b0d83ac28f,https://careers.fedex.com/software-developer-senior-i/job/P25-169008-1?utm_domicile=unspecified&utm_persona=unspecified&utm_trackedsource=srm_indeed_org&utm_subco=FECAMEA,Software Developer-Senior I,FedEx,"TS, IN",2025-04-11,fulltime,,,,False,"Under general guidance, the AI Engineer will be responsible for collaborating with the Information Security organization to analyse current\-state business processes and develop automated workflows using Generative AI chatbot technology to increase efficiency and quality. The AI Engineer will develop and support AI\-driven chatbot solutions for cross\-functional teams across our diverse and growing Infosec organization. This role will also demand building AI Agents that can reason and interact with users and other systems. We look for self\-motivated individuals who can function and adapt in an Agile development model with iterative delivery, incorporating feedback rapidly into delivery components.

  

* Lead a team in all aspects of AI and Generative AI chatbot development, including requirements gathering, solution architecture, development, testing, deployment, and continuous improvement using Agile methodology.
* Collaborate with the Information Security organization to analyze and design process workflows, build, test, and implement AI solutions, ensuring system quality.
* Act as a consultant to other Infosec departments, conducting business process analysis and evaluation.
* Assess AI opportunities from a technical standpoint, perform technical feasibility studies, and develop optimal solutions. Own Solution Design Documents (SDD) or Technical Design Documents (TDD) with a focus on reusability.
* Collaborate with other IT teams and architects to identify the right technologies, avoiding redundancy and ensuring the best fit for proposed AI solutions.
* Conduct thorough process analysis to ensure identified AI opportunities provide intended business benefits.
* Maintain a thorough understanding of technology, quality tools, and process design; think creatively when enhancing existing processes and fixing code errors.
* Adapt to changes in the work environment, manage multiple competing demands, and handle frequent changes, delays, or unexpected events calmly and logically.
* Maintain a thorough understanding of state and federal laws and regulations related to information security compliance, including privacy laws.

**Requirement:**

* Preferred bachelor’s degree or equivalent in Computer Science or related discipline.
* Minimum 6\-9 years of relevant work experience in AI development, including Generative AI chatbots, NLP, and related technologies.
* Proficiency in languages such as Python, JavaScript, Java, or C\#
* Experience with NLP libraries and frameworks like NLTK, spaCy, or Stanford NLP, and platforms like Dialogflow, IBM Watson, or Microsoft LUIS
* Understanding of machine learning concepts and frameworks such as TensorFlow, PyTorch, or scikit\-learn for building intelligent chatbots
* Proficient in implementing Retrieval\-Augmented Generation (RAG) and vector\-based search techniques to enhance AI\-driven information retrieval and contextual response generation
* Knowledge of RESTful APIs and experience with integrating chatbots with various platforms
* Familiarity with SQL and NoSQL databases for storing conversation data and user information.
* Proficiency in Agentic AI, including the ability to build AI agents that can autonomously solve complex, multi\-step problems using sophisticated reasoning and iterative planning.
* Basic understanding of front\-end technologies (HTML, CSS, JavaScript) to integrate chatbots into web applications
* Experience with Azure cloud platform for deploying and scaling chatbots
* Strong analytical and problem\-solving abilities to debug issues and improve chatbot performance.
* Ability to work collaboratively and communicate effectively with cross\-functional teams, including designers, product managers, and other developers.
* Ability to work collaboratively and communicate effectively with cross\-functional teams, including designers, product managers, and other developers.
* Experience with end\-to\-end AI management and SDLC cycle using Agile methodology.
* Experience with Microsoft Power Apps Automation, Co\-Pilot AI, including chatbots and conversational AI, OCR tools, and Power BI is an advantage.
* Practical experience in implementing LEAN, AGILE, and Design Thinking is preferred.

  

