in-cc1c692c8acdb36d,indeed,https://in.indeed.com/viewjob?jk=cc1c692c8acdb36d,https://careers.thomsonreuters.com/us/en/job/THTTRUUSJREQ189905EXTERNALENUS/Product-Owner-Salesforce-Forecasting-AI?utm_source=indeed&utm_medium=phenom-feeds,Product Owner Salesforce - Forecasting & AI,Thomson Reuters,"KA, IN",2025-04-10,fulltime,,,,True,"We are seeking a Product Owner Salesforce \- Forecasting \& AI to join our team. You will play a critical role in Leading and executing Salesforce solutions to enhance sales effectiveness and business operations. You will collaborate closely with stakeholders, technology teams, and business leaders to deliver high\-value CRM solutions, ensuring they align with organizational goals and customer needs.

**About the Role:**


In this opportunity as a Product Owner Salesforce, you will:

* Act as the primary liaison between business stakeholders and technical teams, translating business needs into detailed product requirements.
* Define and maintain a comprehensive product roadmap for Salesforce CRM solutions, prioritizing initiatives based on business impact and customer value.
* Work closely with engineering, sales, marketing, and operations teams to deliver high\-quality features and enhancements.
* Lead the product backlog, ensuring clarity in user stories, acceptance criteria, and prioritization based on business objectives.
* Own the end\-to\-end product lifecycle, from ideation and development to deployment and continuous improvement.
* Use data\-driven insights to evaluate product performance, drive key improvements, and measure the success of Salesforce implementations.
* Champion Agile methodologies, facilitating sprint planning, backlog grooming, and daily stand\-ups with cross\-functional teams.
* Stay up to date with Salesforce trends, AI\-driven sales enablement, and emerging technologies to drive innovation.

**About You:**

  

You’re a fit for the role of Product Owner Salesforce if you have:

* Bachelors / Masters degree required.
* 5–7 years of experience as a Product Owner, Product Manager, or in a similar role within Salesforce CRM\-focused initiatives.
* The role requires the candidate to work from 2 PM to 11 PM IST.
* Proven expertise in Salesforce Sales Cloud and other Salesforce products, with experience in system customization, process automation, Forecasting and AI
* Strong understanding of sales processes, pipeline management, and sales performance analytics.
* Ability to work in a fast\-paced environment, managing multiple initiatives and prioritizing effectively.
* Hands\-on experience with Agile frameworks and methodologies such as Scrum and Kanban.
* Excellent communication, stakeholder management, and problem\-solving skills.
