in-2b5b455f20d3c2bc,indeed,https://in.indeed.com/viewjob?jk=2b5b455f20d3c2bc,https://satsure.keka.com/careers/jobdetails/76751,Product Manager,,IN,2025-04-10,fulltime,,,,True,"We are looking for an experienced Product Manager who is passionate about building products that customers love. You will join a dynamic and fast\-paced environment and work with cross\-functional teams to design, build and roll\-out products that deliver the company’s vision and strategy. **About SatSure:**  

SatSure, a Series A\+ startup, operates at the intersection of space technology, remote sensing, and AI/Computer Vision. With a 150\+ strong team, we tackle challenges in financial inclusion for smallholder farmers, climate sustainability, and critical infrastructure monitoring. Our vision is to create a groundbreaking satellite company that redefines how space data benefits people and businesses. While no playbook exists to scale from 50 to 500 enterprise customers, we’re confident we’re writing one for the future. **Responsibilities:**
* Gain a deep understanding of customer experience, identify and fill product gaps and generate new ideas that grow market share, improve customer experience and drive growth
* Create buy\-in for the product vision both internally and with key external partners
* Develop product pricing and positioning strategies
* Translate product strategy into detailed requirements and prototypes
* Scope and prioritize activities based on business and customer impact
* Work closely with engineering teams to deliver with quick time\-tomarket and optimal resources
* Drive product launches including working with public relations team, executives, and other product management team members
* Evaluate promotional plans to ensure that they are consistent with product line strategy and that the message is effectively conveyed
* Act as a product evangelist to build awareness and understanding
* Represent the company by visiting customers to solicit feedback on company products and services
* Create long\- and short\-term product sales forecasts and analysis for management
* Bring new products to market with return\-on\-investment analysis
* Market new products with sales, advertising and production teams Determine product pricing based on market research, production costs and anticipated demand
* Schedule and assign operational requirements to follow up on work results
* Manage the product team, including coaching and disciplinary actions, planning, monitoring and job appraisal
* Continue professional and technical education, attending workshops, seminars, etc.

 **Qualification:**  

* Bachelor's/Master's in Computer Science or related field

 **Must\-have:**  

* 4\-5 years of experience in product management or as an associate product manager
* Proven ability to develop product and marketing strategies and effectively communicate recommendations to executive management
* Skilled at working effectively with cross\-functional teams in a matrix organization
* Proven track record of working with designers, engineers, and various stakeholders to coordinate, plan, execute, and track product releases from beginning to end.
* Excellent written and verbal communication skills
* Outstanding project and time management skills
* Strong problem\-solving skills and willingness to think outside the box and roll up one’s sleeves to get the job done

 **Good\-to\-have:**  

* Familiarity with agile software development methodologies is also a plus.


**Benefits:**  

* Medical Health Cover for you and your family including unlimited online doctor consultations
* Access to mental health experts for you and your family
* Dedicated allowances for learning and skill development
* Comprehensive leave policy with casual leaves, paid leaves, marriage leaves, bereavement leaves
* Twice a year appraisal

 **Interview Process:**  

* Intro call
* Assessment
* Presentation
* Interview rounds (ideally up to 3\-4 rounds)
* Culture Round / HR round",,,Product Management
in-32ec70cda8a26a80,indeed,https://in.indeed.com/viewjob?jk=32ec70cda8a26a80,https://careers.anz.com/job/Bengaluru-Risk-Relationship-Manager/1060663366/,Risk Relationship Manager,ANZ,"KA, IN",2025-04-10,fulltime,,,,False,"**Req ID:** 86793
  
**Department:** Risk Lending Services \- Business Banking
  
**Division:** Risk
  
**Location:** Bengaluru
  
About Us
  
  

At ANZ, we're shaping a world where people and communities thrive, driven by a common goal: to improve the financial wellbeing and sustainability of our millions of customers.
  
  

About the Role
  
  

As an Assistant Manager in Lending Services, you will be providing direct support to the Relationship Managers and Case Managers in Lending Services Business Banking, Corporate Commercial \& Private Banking and Agri business for day\-to\-day management of high\-risk customer portfolios. You will be completing a wide variety of tasks allocated to you via a central email inbox which will need to be completed within the agreed service level agreements. You will be responsible for contacting various teams such as Commercial Services Team (CST) and other back\-office teams such as Asset Finance, Fulfilment teams within ANZ also external parties such as Valuation firms to complete these tasks and timely updates regarding the tasks should be provided to the relevant Relationship Manager or Case Manager. You will be also responsible in completing Annual Reviews and Take on Diary Notes of Lending Services Business Banking customers to meet well managed requirements which will involve assessing and analysing Annual Financial reports also reviewing ANZ security documents. You will be responsible in completing these tasks independently and in a highest quality standard with minimum rework to meet all audit and compliance requirements. You will be expected to meet weekly productivity targets in place for Lending Services Assistant Manager Pool while maintaining high quality work.
  
  

Banking is changing and we’re changing with it, giving our people great opportunities to try new things, learn and grow. Whatever your role at ANZ, you’ll be building your future, while helping to build ours.
  
  

**Role Type:** Full Time, Permanent
  
**Role Location:** Bengaluru
  
  

What will your day look like?
  
  

Provide support to Lending Services Relationship Managers and Case Managers by completing requests such as Lending Services system maintenance, customer account requests, retrieving Bank statements, financial data extraction, requesting valuations, Annual Reviews, Take on Diary notes. These requests need to be completed with minimum rework and with high quality standards to meet all compliance and audit requirements.
  
  

All tasks allocated via the central inbox needs to be completed in a timely manner while SLA Targets being always met. Relationship Managers and Case Managers need to be updated and advised of the progress of the task and at the completion of the task or if there are any delays in completing the tasks.
  
  

Working collaboratively with different stakeholders including internal stakeholders such as Relationship Managers/ Case Managers and other back\-office support functions as well as external stakeholders such as Lending Services customers, Litigation firms, valuation firms etc to successfully complete tasks by the due date/ SLA.
  
  

Ability to work independently to come up with solutions and workarounds for customer and other stakeholder requests by liaising with different teams within ANZ.
  
  

All communications , information requests from Relationship Managers and Case Managers should be clear and concise and within business hours of the onshore team to meet SLA / Due dates.
  
  

Working collaboratively with the onshore Assistant Manager Pool and share ideas within the team about what works and help others to focus on identifying ways to do things differently to create better outcomes .
  
  

Attending all Lending Services Business Banking On Shore meetings/ training sessions via MS Teams where Lending Services Assistant Managers are required to attend.
  
  

Meeting all compliance training requirements such as ACL / FSR and Tier 2 in Financial Advice as well as timely completion of all other Mandatory learning requirements.
  
  

Meeting productivity targets measured via completed tasks each week.
  
  

What will you bring?
  
  

‘Must have’ knowledge, skills and experiences
  
  

Relevant banking experience and relevant tertiary qualification in Business, Finance or Commerce discipline.
  
Strong communication skills including strong English verbal and written skills with the ability to clearly communicate with stakeholders.
  
Expert knowledge of ANZ’s systems including but not limited to CAP, Cache, ACM, Credit Lens
  
Strong financial analysis skills and an understanding of structuring security arrangements.
  
Demonstrated customer service and negotiation skills.
  
Ability to manage conflict and resolve issues in a transparent, respectful, and professional manner.
  
Interpersonal skills – confidence, professionalism, integrity, and strong sense of accountability.
  
Strong organizational skills, attention to detail and problem\-solving skills.
  
  

‘Good to have’ knowledge, skills and experiences
  
  

Customer Focus
  
  

The willingness to focus effort on delivering to customer needs. Customers include both external and internal stakeholders.
  
Ensuring required outcome is achieved to full fill Customer requests by collaborating with few different teams and working through the problems.
  
  

Problem Solving
  
  

The ability to understand problems and situations by systematically breaking down the problem or situation, assessing and interpreting options, weighing up and prioritising alternatives, and thinking through options.
  
  

Influence \& Relationship Building
  
  

Collaborate with internal stakeholders to come up with solutions for customer inquiries.
  
Ability to influence internal stakeholders to ensure that urgent requests are being met and to meet deadlines.
  
Provide support to ensure processes and priorities are adhered to
  
  

Financial \& Business Acumen
  
  

Collation of data and reporting on financial metrics
  
Identify and report on key findings
  
  

Time Management
  
  

Ability to prioritise and reprioritise tasks through the day and ability to effectively manage time through the day to ensure that all deadlines are being met.
  
Timely, appropriate, and efficient response to all stakeholder inquiries and requests.
  
  

People
  
  

The willingness to work in a cooperative and helpful manner with other team members as well as working independently as required
  
  

Qualifications
  
  

Tertiary qualification in Business, Finance or Commerce discipline is required.
  
Banking experience and expert knowledge in ANZ Core systems such as CAP, CACHE, ACM, CCMS
  
So why join us?
  
  

From the moment you join ANZ, you'll be doing meaningful work that will shape a world where people and communities thrive.
  
  

But it's not just our customers who'll feel your impact. you'll feel it too. Because at ANZ, you'll have the resources, opportunities, and support you need to take the next big step in your career.
  
  

We're a diverse bunch at ANZ in different roles, different locations, doing different things. That's why we have a range of flexible working arrangements, so our people can 'make work, work for them'. We also provide a range of benefits including access to health and wellbeing services and discounts on selected products and services from ANZ and more.
  
  

At ANZ, you'll be part of an organisation where the different backgrounds, perspectives and life experiences of our people are celebrated. That's because we're committed to building a workplace that reflects the diversity of the communities we serve. We welcome applications from everyone and encourage you to talk to us about any adjustments you may require to our recruitment process or the role itself. If you are a candidate with a disability or access requirement, let us know how we can provide you with additional support.
  
  

. You can apply for this role by visiting ANZ Careers and searching for reference number 86793\.
  
  

Job Posting End Date
  
  

