in-a2b36ddca117e701,indeed,https://in.indeed.com/viewjob?jk=a2b36ddca117e701,https://eeho.fa.us2.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/286997,Software Developer 3 - Identity Governance,Oracle,"KA, IN",2025-04-10,fulltime,,,,False,"***About Oracle Managed Cloud Services***

Oracle Managed Cloud Services plays a critical role in delivering and supporting best\-of\-breed cloud solutions to Oracle customers.


Oracle Cloud is the industry’s broadest and most integrated public cloud. It offers best\-in\-class services across software as a service (SaaS), platform as a service (PaaS), infrastructure as a service (IaaS), and even lets you put Oracle Cloud in your own Data Center. Oracle Cloud helps organizations drive innovation and business transformation by increasing business agility, lowering costs, and reducing IT complexity.


The Oracle Cloud has shown strong adoption, supporting 70\+ million users and more than 30\+ billion transactions each day. OCI currently live on 42 regions and growing strongly.


***About Service Engineering team***

Service Engineering team is an engineering arm that creates significant impact on the success of Managed Cloud Services LOB, responsible for designing, developing and building software solutions to effectively manage MCS customers. We also build new services to drive OCI consumption and works on enhancing customer’s experience. Service engineering constantly improves operations by conducting system analysis and recommending changes in policies and procedures for MCS customers.


***About The Job***

A unique opportunity to join a rapidly growing world\-class team to engineer cutting edge Oracle Cloud technologies and infrastructure that make up the Oracle Cloud solutions. As part of the Service Engineering team, you will be continually challenged and have an opportunity to contribute to design, develop, troubleshoot and debug software programs for databases, Oracle Identity Manager, Oracle Service Bus, Saas based Customer portal, tools, Cloud networks etc.


Roles \& Responsibilities are to lead/collaborate cross teams across globe and design, develop software applications, collaboration with operations for debugging issue and roll out new releases. Role needs in\-depth expertise in implementation and maintenance of Oracle Identity Manager solution, Oracle Service Bus, Java, micro services, php, Oracle Database, OCI.


***Skill set and Clearance***

* Design and develop custom connectors to integrate Oracle Identity Manager with various applications and systems.
* Create and configure OIM workflows, approval policies, and entitlements.
* Develop custom UI components for OIM self\-service pages.
* Troubleshoot and resolving technical issues related to OIM implementation.
* Experience in complete cycle of OIM implementation including installation, configuration, and Implementation.
* Understanding of building workflows, OIM related objects, customisation to OIM user/admin screens.
* Developing connectors to integrate the existing directory server with OIM
* Experience in JDBC, well versed with API, Web Services and JNDI
* Experienced in Oracle Service Bus implementation
* Micro service design, development and Implementation
* Securing REST, micro services solution using
* WebLogic skills, including configuration, deployment, performance tuning, monitoring, and troubleshooting.
* Experience on Implementation of SOA composites, custom workflows and approval policies.
* Basic knowledge of Oracle Back\-end PL/SQL Development

***Good To Have Skills***

* Unix Shell scripting
* Power Shell
* Design , Test, Deployment Documentation
* DevOps process implementation
* OCI
* PHP

***Experience***

* 4\+ years of hands\-on OIM implementation
* 2\+ years in scripting and automation.
* Total of 4\+ years work experience in software life cycle management
* Work in global development model.
* Ability to take work from defining scope to successful delivery of solutions.
* Working on implementing solutions public cloud services
* 2\+Years of hands\-on OSB Implementation
* 3\+ Java / microservices experience

***Education*** 

* Bachelor’s degree in computer science or related field.

Career Level \- IC3


  
As a member of the software engineering division, you will


* Assist in defining and developing software for tasks associated with the developing, debugging or designing of software applications or operating systems.
* Involve in Design and Development of software development activities around identity governance platform.
