We’re looking for a seasoned Manager/Principal Product Designer to lead the UX/UI strategy for CashKaro and EarnKaro's marketing campaigns and digital experiences. If you have 6–7 years of hands\-on experience in product design, a sharp eye for design systems, and thrive on data\-led decisions, you’ll fit right in. Your role will be pivotal in turning user insights into delightful, high\-converting journeys that fuel business growth. **Key Responsibilities:****UX Strategy \& Ownership:**
Own the end\-to\-end UX for marketing\-led journeys across CashKaro \& EarnKaro.
Align designs with KPIs like conversions, drop\-offs, and activation.
Use data insights and lean UX methods to build hypothesis\-based experiments.
Example: For campaigns like Diwali Mega Sale, analyze drop\-offs, conduct usability tests, and redesign interfaces (e.g., real\-time savings display) to improve conversions.
 **Design Systems \& Scalability:**
Build and manage scalable design systems using atomic principles.
Standardize tokens, components, colors, and typography across platforms.
Work closely with engineering to maintain design\-dev parity.
Example: Create unified Figma\-Stoybook libraries to eliminate UI inconsistencies between mobile and web.
 **Research \& Analytics\-Led Design:**
Lead usability studies, user interviews, heuristic reviews, and surveys.
Collaborate with product/data teams to analyze funnels, session replays (e.g., Hotjar), and behavior data.
Own a performance dashboard mapping user journey to design ROI.
Example: For low EarnKaro onboarding engagement, redesign flows after Hotjar reviews \+ user interviews.
 **Innovation \& MVP Thinking:**
Drive mini R\&D sprints to test prototypes and refine UX.
Partner with product for MVP planning and feature prioritization.
Example: Ideate and test “Smart Cashback Suggestions” to increase multi\-store usage based on behavior data.
 **Retention \& Activation Optimization:**
Build user flows targeting reactivation, onboarding, and long\-term retention.
Apply gamification and milestone\-driven engagement ideas.
Example: For influencer drop\-off on EarnKaro, launch a level\-based reward system and tracker to improve motivation.
 **Team Leadership \& Mentorship:**
Mentor designers in design principles and career growth.
Set and track quarterly OKRs, and improve sprint planning via agile tools.
Example: Streamline prioritization using a task urgency\-impact matrix; assign design leads per project for ownership.
 **Competitive UX Benchmarking:**
Continuously study competitor UX flows, features, and design decisions.
Conduct teardown sessions and suggest actionable differentiators.
Example: Analyze ""instant withdrawal"" from rival apps; work with product/finance to explore UPI\-based faster payouts.
**Must\-Have Skills:**
UX Strategy \& IA: Deep experience crafting flows, user journeys, and interaction maps.
Design Systems: Strong knowledge of tokenization, modular systems, and atomic design.
Prototyping Tools: Advanced proficiency in Figma, Sketch, or Adobe XD; experience with shared libraries.
Analytics: Comfortable using Mixpanel, Google Analytics, or Hotjar to track user behavior.
Product Thinking: Strong understanding of lean UX, MVP prioritization, and outcome\-driven design.
Agile Practices: Experience with Jira, Trello, or Asana in POD\-based workflows.
Engagement Design: Working knowledge of gamification, lifecycle hooks, and retention tactics.
**Good\-to\-Have Skills:**
Motion Design: Familiarity with After Effects, Lottie, or Principle to bring interactivity and life to user flows.",,https://in.indeed.com/cmp/Cashkaro.com,Product Management
in-e8504320bbc8c138,indeed,https://in.indeed.com/viewjob?jk=e8504320bbc8c138,https://careers.wipro.com/job/Hyderabad-Developer-L3-500032/1143152855/?feedId=420455&utm_source=Indeed,Developer - L3,Wipro,"TS, IN",2025-04-10,,,,,False,"Wipro Limited (NYSE: WIT, BSE: 507685, NSE: WIPRO) is a leading technology services and consulting company focused on building innovative solutions that address clients’ most complex digital transformation needs. Leveraging our holistic portfolio of capabilities in consulting, design, engineering, and operations, we help clients realize their boldest ambitions and build future\-ready, sustainable businesses. With over 230,000 employees and business partners across 65 countries, we deliver on the promise of helping our customers, colleagues, and communities thrive in an ever\-changing world. For additional information, visit us at www.wipro.com.**Job Description**
-------------------

**Role Purpose**


The purpose of this role is to design, test and maintain software programs for operating systems or applications which needs to be deployed at a client end and ensure its meet 100% quality assurance parameters

**͏**
-----

**Do**


1\. Instrumental in understanding the requirements and design of the product/ software

* Develop software solutions by studying information needs, studying systems flow, data usage and work processes
* Investigating problem areas followed by the software development life cycle
* Facilitate root cause analysis of the system issues and problem statement
* Identify ideas to improve system performance and impact availability
* Analyze client requirements and convert requirements to feasible design
* Collaborate with functional teams or systems analysts who carry out the detailed investigation into software requirements
* Conferring with project managers to obtain information on software capabilities
**͏**
-----


2\. Perform coding and ensure optimal software/ module development


* Determine operational feasibility by evaluating analysis, problem definition, requirements, software development and proposed software
* Develop and automate processes for software validation by setting up and designing test cases/scenarios/usage cases, and executing these cases
* Modifying software to fix errors, adapt it to new hardware, improve its performance, or upgrade interfaces.
* Analyzing information to recommend and plan the installation of new systems or modifications of an existing system
* Ensuring that code is error free or has no bugs and test failure
* Preparing reports on programming project specifications, activities and status
* Ensure all the codes are raised as per the norm defined for project / program / account with clear description and replication patterns
* Compile timely, comprehensive and accurate documentation and reports as requested
* Coordinating with the team on daily project status and progress and documenting it
* Providing feedback on usability and serviceability, trace the result to quality risk and report it to concerned stakeholders
**͏**
-----


3\. Status Reporting and Customer Focus on an ongoing basis with respect to project and its execution

* Capturing all the requirements and clarifications from the client for better quality work
* Taking feedback on the regular basis to ensure smooth and on time delivery
* Participating in continuing education and training to remain current on best practices, learn new programming languages, and better assist other team members.
* Consulting with engineering staff to evaluate software\-hardware interfaces and develop specifications and performance requirements
* Document and demonstrate solutions by developing documentation, flowcharts, layouts, diagrams, charts, code comments and clear code
* Documenting very necessary details and reports in a formal way for proper understanding of software from client proposal to implementation
* Ensure good quality of interaction with customer w.r.t. e\-mail content, fault report tracking, voice calls, business etiquette etc
* Timely Response to customer requests and no instances of complaints either internally or externally
**͏**
-----

**Deliver**

**No.** **Performance Parameter** **Measure**  


1\. Continuous Integration, Deployment \& Monitoring of Software 100% error free on boarding \& implementation, throughput %, Adherence to the schedule/ release plan  


2\. Quality \& CSAT On\-Time Delivery, Manage software, Troubleshoot queries, Customer experience, completion of assigned certifications for skill upgradation  


3\. MIS \& Reporting 100% on time MIS \& report generation  


