**About Netradyne**



Founded in 2015, Netradyne is a technology company that leverages expertise in Artificial Intelligence, Deep Learning, and Edge Computing to bring transformational solutions to the transportation industry. Netradyne's technology is already deployed in thousands of vehicles; and our customers drive everything from passenger cars to semi\-trailers on interstates, suburban roads, rural highways—even off\-road.



Netradyne is looking for talented engineers to join our Analytics team comprised of graduates from IITs, IISC, Stanford, UIUC, UCSD etc. We build cutting edge AI solutions to enable drivers and fleets realize unsafe driving scenarios in real\-time to prevent accidents from happening and reduce fatalities/injuries.

  

**Job Title:** Senior AI Platform Product Manager  

**Location:** Bangalore  

**Department:** Product Management  

**Reports To:** Director


**About the Role:**  

We are seeking an experienced Senior AI Platform Product Manager to lead the development and continuous improvement of our AI\-driven platform. This role focuses on ensuring robust, consistent, and accurate AI features through close collaboration with cross\-functional teams. The ideal candidate will have a strong domain knowledge in machine learning, particularly in computer vision, and will drive initiatives to enhance our platform's AI capabilities and analytics features.


**Key Responsibilities:**


* **Safety Feature Development:** Drive the development of new AI\-driven safety features by working with both international and Indian fleet customers. Inspire innovation and align feature development with customer needs and market opportunities.
* **AI KPI Management:** Understand and measure machine learning algorithms using key performance indicators (KPIs) such as precision, recall, and false positive rate. Apply basic statistical principles to ensure unbiased and accurate performance evaluations; and collaborate with the Analytics Operations team to root cause ML observations.
* **Continuous Improvement Initiatives:** Lead ML continuous improvement (CI/CD) efforts with the ML Infrastructure team, aiming for 99%\+ model accuracy. Prioritize improvements based on current KPIs and collaboration with ML Infra Product Experts.
* **User Experience:** Work with the UX team to enhance customer interactions with video annotation, alert decoration, and feature configurations.
* **Release Management:** Manage roadmap enhancements for release cycles. Ensure proper release notes and collaborate with the technical documentation team for customer\-facing communications.
* **Compliance and Best Practices:** Review all AI Product Management PRDs to ensure they meet the platform's standards and best practices.
* **Mentorship:** Mentor junior product managers, fostering a culture of learning and collaboration within the team.


**Skills:**


* Strong analytical skills with an ability to evaluate data, assess risks, and make informed decisions.
* Excellent communication skills tailored to different audiences, including engineering, marketing, support, and leadership.
* Ability to lead cross\-functional teams and drive complex projects to completion.


**Qualifications and Experience:**


* Bachelor's degree in Computer Science, Engineering, or a related field. Advanced degree preferred.
* At least 10 years of experience in technology, with 5\+ years in Product Management focusing on AI\-driven platforms.
* Strong understanding of machine learning, computer vision, and statistical principles.
* Experience with product management tools such as JIRA, Confluence, or similar.
* Proven ability to work with international teams and flexibility to accommodate different time zones, including evening IST meetings.
* Experience in video telematics and fleet management is a plus.


We are committed to an inclusive and diverse team. Netradyne is an equal\-opportunity employer. We do not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, ancestry, national origin, religion, sex, gender, gender identity, gender expression, sexual orientation, age, disability, veteran status, genetic information, marital status, or any legally protected status.



If there is a match between your experiences/skills and the Company's needs, we will contact you directly.



Netradyne is an equal\-opportunity employer.


**Applicants only \- Recruiting agencies do not contact.**


**Recruitment Fraud Alert!**



There has been an increase in fraud that targets job seekers. Scammers may present themselves to job seekers as Netradyne employees or recruiters. Please be aware that Netradyne does not request sensitive personal data from applicants via text/instant message or any unsecured method; does not promise any advance payment for work equipment set\-up and does not use recruitment or job\-sourcing agencies that charge candidates an advance fee of any kind. Official communication about your application will only come from emails ending in '@netradyne.com' or '@us\-greenhouse\-mail.io'.



Please review and apply to our available job openings at Netradyne.com/company/careers. For more information on avoiding and reporting scams, please visit the Federal Trade Commission's job scams website.",,https://in.indeed.com/cmp/Netradyne,Product Management
