**Product Strategy:**

* Understand the overall market for the InterConnect platform, working closely with internal stakeholders and external customers
* Demonstrate deep understanding of customer needs through market research and analysis
* Lead market validation through review and testing of concepts with existing and prospective customers (voice of customer, customer advisory boards, etc.)
* Contribute to business cases and budget planning activities
* Collaborate with business unit product leaders to tie product deliverables to GTM efforts

**Product Roadmaps and Requirements:**

* Drive prioritization of strategic platform initiatives
* Lead requirements definition for product development, understanding product trade\-offs and driving alignment
* Manage market feedback efforts to drive product direction
* Assess and plan the product’s future lifecycle, to include enhancement and sunsetting
* Collaborate with product owners to break down strategic initiatives into epics and features for the platform
* Facilitate ideation and brainstorming sessions/workshops with stakeholders and your team to solve problems

**Execution:**

* Foster innovation by bringing up new problems and encouraging new ways to solve existing problems
* Define and establish objectives and track and manage multiple products through Key Performance Indicators (KPIs)
* Lead efforts to prepare for and support product releases, including capability presentations and documentation
* Drive product engagement and satisfaction and manage the product’s performance including attainment of revenue and margin objectives
* Assess monitored product adoption and usage and engage in the collection of customer feedback

### **What experience you need**

* Bachelor’s degree in Business or Computer Science (or a related field)
* 5\+ years of experience managing B2B products/platforms that drive revenue for organizations
* Ability to create and deliver effective presentations to leadership, and present product overviews (including demos when necessary) to internal and external customers
* Strong technical skills for breaking down complex business processes and data flow challenges to technology teams (knowledge of APIs, batch processing, microservices or other similar technologies)
* Comfortable working with spreadsheets to analyze product operating costs and track product investments to budget and business cases
* Experience working on Go\-to\-Market (GTM) strategies and launching products in markets

### **What could set you apart**

* MBA or Masters Degree
* Experience managing decisioning platforms, or AI/ML experience
* Experience in credit risk and/or working with large financial institutions or credit unions
* Experience managing products hosted on the cloud
* Experience managing products across multiple geographies",,https://in.indeed.com/cmp/Equifax,Product Management
