* Scrum team liaison between developers/testers/UX/Solution Architect.
* Experience in creating, refining, and grooming User stories.
* Experienced in using/incorporating Wireframes.
* Experience in understanding/leveraging historical Mainframe/CICS based applications and user interface.
* Experience with project methodology and project life cycles.
* In depth knowledge of business operations and processes with the ability to articulate these processes to others.
* Experience with analysis planning, requirements elicitation, test planning, creating test cases and test data, executing test scripts, implementation planning, and implementation execution.
* Has experience in leading projects for onshore business partners.
* Understand and apply technology as it relates to the business.
* Demonstrated ability to effectively manage multiple work assignments while being able to shift priorities to meet the current business environment needs.
* Excellent communication skills; both written and verbal.

Initiative\-taker and can work independently * \- get work done without oversight.
* Can plan and lead work efforts as needed.
* Working knowledge and experience with the financial industry
* Effective written communication skills to deliver articulate communications and concisely summarize information.
* Ability to work in a challenging environment with minimal supervision.
* Strong knowledge of the following applications:
	+ MS Visio
	+ MS Excel
	+ MS Office
	+ MS PowerPoint
	+ JIRA
	+ BlueWorks Live

**Preferred Qualifications/ Experience**

* Project related experience with financial or brokerage applications
* Experience developing and revising business processes.

**About Our Company**  

Ameriprise India LLP has been providing client based financial solutions to help clients plan and achieve their financial objectives for 125 years. We are a U.S. based financial planning company headquartered in Minneapolis with a global presence. The firm’s focus areas include Asset Management and Advice, Retirement Planning and Insurance Protection. Be part of an inclusive, collaborative culture that rewards you for your contributions and work with other talented individuals who share your passion for doing great work. You’ll also have plenty of opportunities to make your mark at the office and a difference in your community. So if you're talented, driven and want to work for a strong ethical company that cares, take the next step and create a career at Ameriprise India LLP.


Ameriprise India LLP is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, sex, genetic information, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, disability, veteran status, marital status, family status or any other basis prohibited by law.

