* Full\-stack development skills, including frontend development with React/JavaScript, building and maintaining RESTful APIs, and understanding web architecture and microservices
* Experience with AWS services, cloud\-native architectures, scalable and secure deployment patterns, and familiarity with monitoring and observability tools
* Ability to handle large\-scale datasets, data engineering principles, and knowledge of automated workflow design and implementation

**What we will look for in an ideal candidate:**

* Engineering (B.E./ B. Tech.) graduate or Masters (Stats, Quant, Mathematics, etc.) from a well\-recognized institute.
* Strong problem\-solving abilities and analytical mindset
* Excellent communication skills with technical and non\-technical stakeholders
* Demonstrated ability to work in fast\-paced, agile environments
* Comfort working with globally distributed teams

**Preferred Additional Experience**:

* Financial services or investment management background
* Experience with web scraping and data extraction techniques
* Open\-source contributions or side development projects

**About Our Company**  

Ameriprise India LLP has been providing client based financial solutions to help clients plan and achieve their financial objectives for 125 years. We are a U.S. based financial planning company headquartered in Minneapolis with a global presence. The firm’s focus areas include Asset Management and Advice, Retirement Planning and Insurance Protection. Be part of an inclusive, collaborative culture that rewards you for your contributions and work with other talented individuals who share your passion for doing great work. You’ll also have plenty of opportunities to make your mark at the office and a difference in your community. So if you're talented, driven and want to work for a strong ethical company that cares, take the next step and create a career at Ameriprise India LLP.


