Job Description
We are seeking a highly experienced Senior Data Analyst with expertise in Power BI and Dimensional Modelling to assist in data analysis initiatives and drive actionable insights for our organization. As a senior member of the data team, you will be responsible for developing complex reports, implementing efficient data models, and working closely with business leaders to ensure data\-driven decision\-making. Your role will also involve collaborating with cross\-functional teams to ensure data integrity and optimal reporting solutions.


**Key Responsibilities:**

* **Advanced Data Analysis \& Reporting:**
	+ Lead the development, design, and maintenance of advanced reports and dashboards using Power BI.
	+ Perform in\-depth data analysis to uncover key business insights and trends.
	+ Collaborate with business stakeholders to define reporting requirements and develop solutions that support business objectives.
	+ Ensure the accuracy and timeliness of reports, identifying and correcting data discrepancies.
* **Dimensional Modelling \& Data Architecture:**
	+ Assist in the design and implementation of dimensional models that support efficient reporting and data analysis.
	+ Work with data engineers to build and maintain data models that ensure optimized performance and scalability.
	+ Manage and improve existing data models to ensure they align with evolving business needs and reporting requirements.
* **Power BI Expertise:**
	+ Develop complex data visualizations and interactive reports in Power BI to drive insights and inform decision\-making.
	+ Write and optimize DAX calculations for advanced data manipulation and performance tuning.
	+ Train and mentor junior team members in Power BI best practices and report development techniques.
	+ Familiar with Power BI Deployment Pipelines and Version Control
* **Data Strategy \& Governance:**
	+ Ensure data quality, consistency, and integrity across various data sources and reports.
	+ Implement and enforce data governance policies, ensuring adherence to data security, privacy, and compliance standards.
	+ Develop and maintain data documentation, including data dictionaries and metadata.
**Job Qualifications:**

**Key Qualifications:**

* Bachelor’s degree in Data Science, Computer Science, Information Technology, or a related field;
* **Experience:**
	+ 5\+ years of experience as a Data Analyst or in a similar role, with at least 2 years in a senior or leadership position.
	+ Extensive hands\-on experience with Power BI, including DAX, Power Query, and complex data visualizations.
	+ Proven experience in designing and implementing dimensional models (e.g., star and snowflake schemas).
* **Technical Skills:**
	+ Advanced proficiency in SQL for data extraction, manipulation, and performance tuning.
	+ Strong understanding of ETL processes, data warehousing principles, and database architecture.
	+ Experience with cloud platforms (e.g., Snowflake, Azure, AWS)
* **Soft Skills:**
	+ Excellent analytical and problem\-solving skills with a strong attention to detail.
	+ Ability to lead, mentor, and develop junior analysts.
	+ Strong communication and presentation skills, with the ability to explain complex data to non\-technical stakeholders.
	+ Ability to manage multiple projects and priorities in a fast\-paced environment.

**Cotality's Diversity Commitment:**

Cotality is fully committed to employing a diverse workforce and creating an inclusive work environment that embraces everyone’s unique contributions, experiences and values. We offer an empowered work environment that encourages creativity, initiative and professional growth and provides a competitive salary and benefits package. We are better together when we support and recognize our differences.  



**Equal Opportunity Employer Statement:**

Cotality is an Equal Opportunity employer committed to attracting and retaining the best\-qualified people available, without regard to race, ancestry, place of origin, colour, ethnic origin, citizenship, creed, sex, sexual orientation, record of offences, age, marital status, family status or disability. Cotality maintains a Drug\-Free Workplace.  



Please apply on our website for consideration.


Privacy Policy


Global Applicant Privacy Policy


By providing your telephone number, you agree to receive automated (SMS) text messages at that number from Cotality regarding all matters related to your application and, if you are hired, your employment and company business. Message \& data rates may apply. **You can opt out at any time by** **responding STOP or UNSUBSCRIBING and will automatically be opted out company\-wide.**

