Now is the time to bring your expertise to Insight. We are not just a tech company; we are a people\-first company. We believe that by unlocking the power of people and technology, we can accelerate transformation and achieve extraordinary results. As a **Fortune 500 Solutions Integrator** with deep expertise in cloud, data, AI, cybersecurity, and intelligent edge, we guide organizations through complex digital decisions

 **About the role**  

As a **AI ML Technical Lead** with Insight , we are seeking a highly skilled AI/ML led engineer to join our team and contribute to lead, design, development, and deployment of artificial intelligence solutions. As a Team Lead, you will be responsible for overseeing the end\-to\-end lifecycle of AI/ML projects, mentoring engineers, and collaborating with cross\-functional teams to drive innovation and business impact.


The ideal candidate will have a strong background in machine learning, deep learning, NLP and computer vision and data science, with the ability to build and integrate AI models that solve complex business problems.

  

About the team


Join us at the Data \& AI Division, where we're not just another tech Division—we're the driving force behind empowering businesses to unlock the full potential of their data. Our mission is crystal clear: to harness the power of data through scalable solutions and repeatable processes, revolutionizing decision\-making and problem\-solving across industries.


What We Do:


Dynamic Data Insights: Delve into the realm of data analytics and gain invaluable insights that fuel informed decision\-making, empowering businesses to tackle challenges faster and more effectively.


Cutting\-Edge Platforms: Step into the forefront of innovation with our modern data platforms, cloud solutions, and infrastructure, laying the groundwork for unleashing untapped business potential and maximizing ROI.


AI\-Powered Advancements: Embrace the future with predictive analytics and AI\-driven trend forecasting, equipping organizations to seize new opportunities and gain a competitive edge in today's fast\-paced markets.


Automation Revolution: Lead the charge in automation solutions, revolutionizing workflows and boosting productivity, enabling teams to concentrate on high\-value tasks and propel business growth.


Optimization Expertise: Harness our advanced analytics capabilities to optimize processes and elevate performance, ensuring steadfast operations and continual improvement.


Comprehensive Business Intelligence: Provide comprehensive views of data through our business intelligence solutions, empowering organizations to address critical questions and navigate a path toward future success.


Join our team and be part of a transformative journey where your contributions will shape the future of AI integration, driving real\-world impact and propelling businesses toward success.

 **Key Responsibilities:**

* Lead and mentor a team of AI/ML engineers, ensuring best practices in model development and deployment.
* Design, develop, and implement scalable machine learning models and AI\-driven solutions.
* Collaborate with data scientists, software engineers, and product managers to integrate AI models into applications.
* Optimize and fine\-tune machine learning models for performance, accuracy, and efficiency.
* Stay up\-to\-date with the latest advancements in AI/ML technologies and incorporate them into the team’s workflow.
* Conduct code reviews, provide technical guidance, and improve development processes.
* Manage project timelines, deliverables, and ensure alignment with business objectives.
* Work with cloud\-based and on\-premises AI/ML platforms to deploy and monitor models in production.
* Ensure compliance with ethical AI principles, data privacy regulations, and best security practices.
* Collaborate with DevOps teams to ensure seamless integration of AI models into existing systems and workflows.
* Document AI processes, model architectures, and development practices to ensure knowledge sharing and scalability.
* Provide technical leadership and mentorship to junior AI engineers and data scientists.

  

  

**Be Ambitious**: This opportunity is not just about what you do today but also about where you can go tomorrow. As a AI ML Lead, you are positioned for swift advancement within our organization through a structured career path. When you bring your hunger, heart, and harmony to Insight, your potential will be met with continuous opportunities to upskill, earn promotions, and elevate your career.

 **Required Skills and Qualifications:**

* Bachelor’s or master’s degree in computer science, Artificial Intelligence, Machine Learning, Data Science, or a related field.
* 8 to 12 years of experience in AI, machine learning, or data science roles, with a strong portfolio of successfully deployed AI solutions along with at least 2 years in leading the AI/ML team.
* Strong proficiency in Python, TensorFlow, Py\-Torch, Py\-Spark and other ML frameworks.
* Strong understanding of machine learning algorithms, deep learning architectures (e.g., CNNs, RNNs, GANs), NLP, Computer Vision, Generative AI and AI model development.
* Knowledge on MLOps practices and tools for model deployment, monitoring, and scaling.
* Experience with data preprocessing, feature engineering, and working with large datasets in cloud environments (e.g., AWS, Google Cloud, Azure).
* Familiarity with data visualization tools (e.g., Matplotlib, Seaborn, Power BI or Tableau) and experience in interpreting and communicating model results.
* Strong problem\-solving skills, with the ability to translate business requirements into AI solutions.
* Excellent communication skills, with the ability to explain complex technical concepts to non\-technical stakeholders.
* Experience with version control systems (e.g., Git) and Agile development practices.

**Other Skills:**

* Experience with reinforcement learning, and Agentic AI will add advantage.
* Knowledge of ethical AI practices and considerations in AI model development.
* Experience with containerization and orchestration tools (e.g., Docker, Kubernetes) for AI model deployment.

 **What you can expect**


We’re legendary for taking care of you, your family and to help you engage with your local community. We want you to enjoy a full, meaningful life and own your career at Insight. Some of our benefits include:

* Freedom to work from another location—even an international destination—for up to 30 consecutive calendar days per year.
* Medical Insurance
* Health Benefits
* Professional Development: Learning Platform and Certificate Reimbursement
* Shift Allowance

  

But what really sets us apart are our core values of Hunger, Heart, and Harmony, which guide everything we do, from building relationships with teammates, partners, and clients to making a positive impact in our communities.

 **Join us today, your ambitious journey starts here.**

 *Insight is an equal opportunity employer, and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, sexual orientation or any other characteristic protected by law.*

*When you apply, please tell us the pronouns you use and any reasonable adjustments you may need during the interview process.*  

*At Insight, we celebrate diversity of skills and experience so even if you don’t feel like your skills are a perfect match \- we still want to hear from you!*  

  

**Today's talent leads to tomorrow's success. Learn more about Insight:**  

**https://www.linkedin.com/company/insight/**

  

Insight is an equal opportunity employer, and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, sexual orientation or any other characteristic protected by law.

  

