gd-1009699814565,glassdoor,https://www.glassdoor.co.in/job-listing/j?jl=1009699814565,,Analyst- Quantitative Analytics,JPMorganChase,Bengaluru,2025-04-06,,830000.0,900000.0,INR,False,"**JOB DESCRIPTION**  

The Corrections and Remediations Analytics \- Center of Excellence (CoE) performs data analysis to identify customers impacted by process or operational breaks throughout the firm. This CoE supports Auto Finance, Business Banking, Consumer Banking, Credit Card, Merchant Services, and Wealth Management. Analysts benefit from unique exposure to various products and teams across J.P. Morgan Chase.


Job Summary:

* As a Quantitative Analytics Analyst on the Remediation \& Corrections team, you will be crucial in identifying, classifying, and resolving customer impacts stemming from business process or operational disruptions at JP Morgan Chase.
* This role involves addressing affected customers by recalculating and crediting finance charges, fees, and processing account adjustments to rectify account issues.
* To succeed, you must be highly motivated, analytical, detail\-oriented, and an outstanding problem solver who takes pride in managing customer issues comprehensively and delivering exceptional service.


Job Responsibilities

* Use SAS \& SQL skills to query databases and research to identify correction population, financials and create execution files using accounts, customer, and transaction level data.
* Ensure analytics steps are accurate through attention to detail and supporting the independent validation team with understanding case requirements and code.
* Use SAS macros or another tool to automate analytics steps which are repetitive between cases.
* Develop skills continuously and upskill to languages like Python etc. and deepen data knowledge to support closure of projects, ensure correct data is being supplied to stakeholders, deliver analytical requirements per the “requirements documents” and provide best\-in\-class analytics.
* Collaborate with key stakeholders like Project Managers, Business Analysts etc. across the firm to understand the context of cases including the issue and then use analytic techniques to carry out requirements (which requires translating high\-level requirements into steps) and drive Analytics and Insights.

  

Required qualifications, capabilities and skills

* Minimum 3 years of related experience, Bachelor’s Degree in Math, Statistics, Software Engineering, Computer Science, Engineering, or similar field
* Prior experience with SAS and another programming language, e.g. Python, R, SQL, Java
* Data Wrangling: Able to query data from multiple sources with considerations for null values or required manipulations/aggregation
* Data Mining: Identify insights and anomalies within data
* Logical reasoning – translating plain English requirements into codes and driving analytical insights out of it

Preferred qualifications, capabilities and skills

* Proficiency with standard MS Office tools (Excel, Word, PowerPoint, etc.)
* Flexible individual who can easily and efficiently transition across topics and disciplines.
* Adept at multi\-tasking and meeting deadlines in high\-pressure environment.
* Demonstrates personal dedication and strong work ethic, sets high standards for self with a strong willingness to learn and take feedback.
* Strong verbal and written communication skills with the ability to synthesize data and information into executive summaries, briefs and/or reports.
* Understanding of data infrastructure in a financial services organization will be a plus. JPMC Product or Database knowledge and experience preferred.


**ABOUT US**  

JPMorganChase, one of the oldest financial institutions, offers innovative financial solutions to millions of consumers, small businesses and many of the world’s most prominent corporate, institutional and government clients under the J.P. Morgan and Chase brands. Our history spans over 200 years and today we are a leader in investment banking, consumer and small business banking, commercial banking, financial transaction processing and asset management.  

  

We recognize that our people are our strength and the diverse talents they bring to our global workforce are directly linked to our success. We are an equal opportunity employer and place a high value on diversity and inclusion at our company. We do not discriminate on the basis of any protected attribute, including race, religion, color, national origin, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, age, marital or veteran status, pregnancy or disability, or any other basis protected under applicable law. We also make reasonable accommodations for applicants’ and employees’ religious practices and beliefs, as well as mental health or physical disability needs. Visit our FAQs for more information about requesting an accommodation.

  

  

  

**ABOUT THE TEAM**  


Our Consumer \& Community Banking division serves our Chase customers through a range of financial services, including personal banking, credit cards, mortgages, auto financing, investment advice, small business loans and payment processing. We’re proud to lead the U.S. in credit card sales and deposit growth and have the most\-used digital solutions – all while ranking first in customer satisfaction.  

  

The CCB Data \& Analytics team responsibly leverages data across Chase to build competitive advantages for the businesses while providing value and protection for customers. The team encompasses a variety of disciplines from data governance and strategy to reporting, data science and machine learning. We have a strong partnership with Technology, which provides cutting edge data and analytics infrastructure. The team powers Chase with insights to create the best customer and business outcomes.",,https://www.glassdoor.co.in/Overview/W-EI_IE5224839.htm,Data Science
gd-1009700028491,glassdoor,https://www.glassdoor.co.in/job-listing/j?jl=1009700028491,,"Lead, Data Science",Kenvue,Bengaluru,2025-04-06,,,,,False,"Description **Who We Are**



At Kenvue, we realize the extraordinary power of everyday care. Built on over a century of heritage and rooted in science, we’re the house of iconic brands \- including NEUTROGENA®, AVEENO®, TYLENOL®, LISTERINE®, JOHNSON’S® and BAND\-AID® that you already know and love. Science is our passion; care is our talent. Our global team is made by 22,000 diverse and brilliant people, passionate about insights, innovation and committed to deliver the best products to our customers. With expertise and empathy, being a Kenvuer means to have the power to impact life of millions of people every day. We put people first, care fiercely, earn trust with science and solve with courage – and have brilliant opportunities waiting for you! Join us in shaping our future–and yours.


**What You Will Do**



The Data Scientist will lead the Data Science/AI/ML work, drive advanced analytics initiatives, and contribute to the strategic vision of data\-driven decision\-making within the organization. You will collaborate with cross\-functional teams, including data engineers, business analysts, and product managers, to develop innovative data solutions and insights that impact business outcomes positively. With a focus on applying operations research techniques to solve business problems, you will be a hand\-on contributor for the data science team, driving advanced analytics initiatives to deliver innovative solutions.


**Responsibilities:**


* Technical contribution: Provide technical expertise to the data science team collaborating with data scientists on projects and methodologies. Lead and manage complex data science projects from ideation to implementation, ensuring timely delivery and high\-quality outcomes.
* Modeling and Analysis: Develop and deploy sophisticated simulation and optimization model using open source and commercial solvers.
* Data Exploration: Conduct in\-depth exploratory data analysis to understand patterns, trends, and anomalies that can lead to valuable business insights.
* Algorithm Selection and Analytic formulation: Identify and recommend appropriate machine learning algorithms and techniques for specific business problems.
* Innovation and Research: Stay up\-to\-date with the latest advancements in Operations Research and apply cutting\-edge techniques to enhance analytical capabilities.
* External partner engagement: Evaluation and selection of external vendors partners for data science and machine learning. Working closely with the selected partner to oversee the technical and business outcomes.
* Collaboration: Collaborate with stakeholders to understand business challenges, align data science initiatives with business goals, and communicate results effectively.
* Data Governance and Ethics: Ensure compliance with data governance policies, privacy regulations, and ethical considerations related to data science projects.
* Continuous Improvement: Promote a culture of continuous learning and improvement within the data science team, encouraging the adoption of best practices and innovative approaches.


**Key Accountabilities:**


* Collect and clean data
* Build and train models
* Interpret and communicate results
* Work with stakeholders to understand their needs
* Deploy models into production
* Maintain and improve models
* Developing data pipelines
* Building data visualizations
* Writing data science reports
* Presenting data science findings to stakeholders
* Collaborating with other data scientists and engineers
* Creating data mining architectures/models/protocols, statistical reporting, and data analysis methodologies to identify trends in large data sets
* Analysis may be applied to various areas of the business (e.g., Market Economics, Supply Chain, Marketing/Advertising, Scientific Research, etc.)
* Researching and applying knowledge of existing and emerging data science principles, theories, and techniques to inform business decisions


**What We Are Looking For**


**Required Qualifications:**


* Strong knowledge and understanding of Probability \& Statistics
* University/Bachelor's degree in Computer Science, Statistics, or a related field.
* 7\-9 years of experience in data analysis, machine learning, or a related field.
* Proven experience (typically 6\+ years) in Data Science/AI/ML, with a strong track record of leading and delivering successful Data Science/AI/ML projects.
* Sound knowledge of Data Science/AI/ML concepts and techniques from Regression, Clustering, Classification, Time series, Deep learning, Gen AI, Statistics and Probability
* Proficiency in at least one commonly used coding language preferably Python.
* Experience with big data technologies and frameworks (e.g., Spark) is a plus.
* Excellent problem\-solving and analytical skills, with a keen eye for identifying patterns and insights in complex datasets.
* Strong communication skills and the ability to present technical findings to both technical and non\-technical stakeholders.
* Business acumen and the ability to align data science projects with organizational goals and objectives.

Qualifications **Desired Qualifications:**


* Proficiency in one of the following areas: Linear Algebra, Calculus, preferably from Retail, eCommerce or CPG industry
  


Primary Location Asia Pacific\-India\-Karnataka\-Bangalore
Job Function Digital Product Development",,https://www.glassdoor.co.in/Overview/W-EI_IE8265614.htm,Data Science
