**Job Description \& Summary**

At PwC, our people in data and analytics focus on leveraging data to drive insights and make informed business decisions. They utilise advanced analytics techniques to help clients optimise their operations and achieve their strategic goals.
  

  

In business intelligence at PwC, you will focus on leveraging data and analytics to provide strategic insights and drive informed decision\-making for clients. You will develop and implement innovative solutions to optimise business performance and enhance competitive advantage.
\*Why PWC


At PwC, you will be part of a vibrant community of solvers that leads with trust and creates distinctive outcomes for our clients and communities. This purpose\-led and values\-driven work, powered by technology in an environment that drives innovation, will enable you to make a tangible impact in the real world. We reward your contributions, support your wellbeing, and offer inclusive benefits, flexibility programmes and mentorship that will help you thrive in work and life. Together, we grow, learn, care, collaborate, and create a future of infinite experiences for each other. Learn more about us .


At PwC, we believe in providing equal employment opportunities, without any discrimination on the grounds of gender, ethnic background, age, disability, marital status, sexual orientation, pregnancy, gender identity or expression, religion or other beliefs, perceived differences and status protected by law. We strive to create an environment where each one of our people can bring their true selves and contribute to their personal growth and the firm’s growth. To enable this, we have zero tolerance for any discrimination and harassment based on the above considerations. ""


**Job Description \& Summary –** Business Solutions Analyst


**Responsibilities:**

**Employment Type:** Full\-Time


PwC Advisory is seeking a dynamic and strategic Associate Director/Director to lead our BFSI Business Analysis practice. This senior leadership role will focus on driving transformative solutions for clients in the Banking, Financial Services, and Insurance sectors. The successful candidate will combine deep industry expertise with innovative problem\-solving value propositions to deliver measurable value, strengthen client relationships, and contribute to PwC’s market\-leading position in advisory services.


Lead the development and execution of business strategies for BFSI clients along with associated value solutions, addressing challenges such as digital transformation, regulatory compliance, risk management, and operational efficiency leveraging Data and Analytics functions including AI, Gen AI and emerging technologies.


Oversee a portfolio of high\-impact advisory projects, ensuring exceptional delivery and alignment with client goals. Build and maintain strong relationships with C\-suite executives and key stakeholders, acting as a trusted advisor. Direct a team of consultants and analysts, providing mentorship, fostering collaboration, and driving professional excellence. Identify new business opportunities, lead pursuits, and contribute to proposals that expand PwC’s footprint in the BFSI sector in close collaboration with the assigned D \& A partner.


Leverage data\-driven insights and advanced technologies (e.g., AI, cloud, blockchain) to design innovative solutions tailored to client needs. Collaborate with cross\-functional PwC teams, including technology, risk assurance, and tax, to deliver integrated advisory services.


Stay ahead of industry trends, regulatory changes, and competitive dynamics to position PwC as a thought leader in BFSI. Represent PwC at industry events, conferences, and forums to enhance brand visibility and thought leadership and also work towards publication of associated journals and concept papers to propagate PwC’s point of view on the related subject of interest.


**Qualifications \& Experience:**

MBA or equivalent in Business Administration or associated subjects from a reputed institute with bachelor’s degree in STEM, Finance, Business Administration, Economics, or a related field. Relevant certifications (e.g., CFA, FRM, or PMP) are advantageous but not required.


12\+ years of experience in consulting or industry roles within BFSI, with a focus on business solutions, strategy, or transformation.


**Leadership Attributes:**

Proven leadership experience managing teams and delivering complex, client\-facing projects (Big 4 or similar consulting experience is highly desirable). Deep knowledge of BFSI domains, including banking operations, insurance processes, wealth management, or capital markets. Strong analytical skills with proficiency in tools such as like Hyperscaler, Python, SAS, AI \& Gen AI or advanced Excel; familiarity with fintech innovations is a plus.


Exceptional communication and interpersonal skills, with a track record of influencing senior executives and driving consensus. Demonstrated ability to manage large\-scale engagements, budgets, and client expectations in a fast\-paced environment.


**What We Offer:**

Competitive compensation package, including performance bonuses and equity opportunities. Comprehensive benefits, including health, wellness, and retirement programs. A collaborative, inclusive culture with access to global resources and continuous learning opportunities. Career advancement within PwC’s renowned Advisory practice, with exposure to diverse industries and geographies.


How to Apply:


Please send your resume to PwC employment portal.
 

PwC is committed to fostering a diverse and inclusive workplace where all voices are valued.


