gd-1009690423161,glassdoor,https://www.glassdoor.co.in/job-listing/j?jl=1009690423161,,Data Scientist - Generative AI,Smart Capital Center,,2025-03-31,,,,,True,"We are seeking a talented and driven Data Scientist \- Generative AI Engineer to join our AI Research and Development department. In this role, you will work with advanced AI models to design, implement, and enhance generative AI solutions. You will help improve the accuracy, scalability, and overall performance of models that drive decision\-making for high\-stakes real estate investment and financing.  
Key Responsibilities:

* Generative AI Model Development: Build, train, and fine\-tune large generative models (LLMs, GPT, BERT, etc.) for various applications within real estate and finance.
* AI Agents \& Retrieval\-Augmented Generation (RAG): Develop AI agents and implement RAG techniques to enhance generative model capabilities. Work with LangGraph, LangChain, and similar frameworks for advanced AI applications.
* Data Analysis \& Integration: Analyze large, complex datasets and integrate relevant data into generative models for improved outcomes and performance. Develop scalable AI solutions using Python, TensorFlow, PyTorch, or similar frameworks.
* Model Testing \& Optimization: Evaluate and optimize the performance of generative models, ensuring accuracy, stability, and efficiency in production environments.
* Collaboration: Work closely with cross\-functional teams to align AI solutions with broader business and AI development goals.
* Prompt Engineering: Contribute to prompt design and refinement for LLMs to ensure they are optimized for real\-world use cases.
* Research \& Development: Stay current with the latest advancements in generative AI, deep learning, and AI agent frameworks, applying cutting\-edge techniques to enhance AI\-driven decision\-making processes.
* Documentation: Maintain detailed documentation of model architecture, design decisions, testing protocols, and results to facilitate ongoing improvements.
* Qualifications:
* Experience: Minimum 4 years of professional experience in AI, machine learning, or data science roles.
