The AI \& Analytics Engineer will have a strong background in data engineering, data architecture, and data pipeline development. The AI \& Analytics Engineer will play a crucial role in designing, building, and maintaining the infrastructure required for optimal extraction, transformation, and loading (ETL) of data from a wide variety of data sources to support the development of AI and analytics models and insights. In this role, the AI \& Analytics Engineer will be responsible for collecting, cleaning, and preprocessing large datasets from various sources to ensure data quality and integrity. This role will develop and implement robust data pipelines and workflows to support data science and AI initiatives. This work will involve close collaboration with AI developers and data scientists to understand their requirements and translate them into scalable and efficient data solutions and visualizations. This role will perform exploratory data analysis to identify trends, patterns, and anomalies, and ensure that the data infrastructure supports the development and deployment of machine learning models. The ability to communicate findings and insights through data visualizations, reports, and presentations will be essential in driving informed decision\-making across the organization. Additionally, the AI \& Analytics Engineer will stay up\-to\-date with the latest advancements in data engineering, big data technologies, and cloud platforms, ensuring that our methodologies and tools remain cutting\-edge. Your contributions will be vital in maintaining the integrity of our data throughout its lifecycle and in fostering a culture of continuous learning and innovation within the team.

