in-d019a7bacfb71274,indeed,https://in.indeed.com/viewjob?jk=d019a7bacfb71274,https://pfizer.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/en-US/PfizerCareers/job/India---Chennai/Senior-Associate---Data-Science--Manufacturing-Intelligence_4933893,"Associate Manager - Data Science, Manufacturing Intelligence",Pfizer,"TN, IN",2025-04-03,fulltime,,,,True,"Join our dynamic Manufacturing Intelligence and Global Automation (MIGA) team as a Senior Associate \- Data Science, where you will leverage cutting\-edge data science and AI technologies to drive innovation and optimize manufacturing processes. MIGA propels Pfizer Global Supply (PGS) towards Industry 4\.0 capability by collaborating with manufacturing sites and Digital/IT teams in developing, implementing, and replicating high\-value Manufacturing Intelligence solutions.
This role comes with the flexibility to work remotely.
Responsibilities* Develop and implement text analytics models to extract meaningful insights from unstructured data, facilitating improved decision\-making and operational efficiency.
* Design and deploy anomaly detection systems to identify deviations in manufacturing processes, ensuring process robustness and minimizing downtime.
* Leverage machine learning algorithms to recommend optimization of manufacturing process parameters for enhanced product quality and yield.
* Collaborate with cross\-functional teams, including process engineers, IT/digital specialists, and management, to integrate data\-driven solutions into the manufacturing environment seamlessly.
* Continuously monitor and refine machine learning models, ensuring their accuracy and relevance over time, and provide regular updates to key stakeholders on project progress and outcomes.
* Perform model and code testing, validation and documentation required for GxP / non\-GxP deployment of solutions.


Basic Qualifications* A PhD/Master’s degree in relevant engineering major, statistics, or computer science is preferred.
* Minimum 3 years hands\-on data science, machine learning work experience.
* Strong Proficiency on Python and SQL programming, writing modularized code, hands\-on with libraries like numpy, pandas, shap, scikit\-learn, matplotlib, seaborn, plotly
* Hands\-on experience with Natural Language Processing (NLP), Text mining, word embedding techniques, knowledge of pre\-trained networks, fine\-tuning of pre\-trained models, named entity recognition and text classification
* Advance proficiency on data wrangling, pre\-processing and data visualization
* Multivariate modeling; Machine Learning; Anomaly detection techniques, deep learning frameworks like PyTorch/Tensorflow
* Experience of developing and deploying ML solutions in AWS or similar environments, familiarity with model version control and ML pipeline
* Track record in applying data science and machine learning methodologies to real\-world data to generate insight and support decision making (not just academics/training projects).


Preferred Qualifications  

* Chemical or Bioprocess engineer/professional with understanding of unit operations and processes in Biopharmaceutical Manufacturing.
* Experience of deploying Interpretable Machine Learning or Explainable AI and knowledge of Shapley values and plots
* Hands\-on project experience in developing and deploying GenAI solutions for Retrieval\-Augmented Generation (RAG) and agentic applications.
* Demonstrated experience of storytelling with interpretability tools usable by technical experts and non\-technical stakeholders
* Independent, self\-motivated personality with excellent oral and written communication skills
  

  

Work Location Assignment: Remote  

Pfizer is an equal opportunity employer and complies with all applicable equal employment opportunity legislation in each jurisdiction in which it operates.
