in-600c60ec54eff7a7,indeed,https://in.indeed.com/viewjob?jk=600c60ec54eff7a7,https://jobs.exxonmobil.com/ExxonMobil/job/Bengaluru-Wells-Analytics-Engineer-KA/1246707600/?feedId=204100&utm_source=Indeed&utm_campaign=XOM_Indeed,Wells Analytics Engineer,ExxonMobil,"KA, IN",2025-04-02,,,,,False,"**About us**

  

At ExxonMobil, our vision is to lead in energy innovations that advance modern living and a net\-zero future. As one of the world’s largest publicly traded energy and chemical companies, we are powered by a unique and diverse workforce fueled by the pride in what we do and what we stand for.

  

The success of our Upstream, Product Solutions and Low Carbon Solutions businesses is the result of the talent, curiosity and drive of our people. They bring solutions every day to optimize our strategy in energy, chemicals, lubricants and lower\-emissions technologies.

  

We invite you to bring your ideas to ExxonMobil to help create sustainable solutions that improve quality of life and meet society’s evolving needs. Learn more about **our What and our Why** and how we canwork **together**.

**What role you will play in our team**
---------------------------------------

  

We are looking for minimum 3 years experienced engineers with an emphasis on data engineering and analytics using visualization tools to provide wells engineering support across ExxonMobil’s global portfolio. This position will also require interaction with the broader data science and analytics career community in ExxonMobil India to share best practices and upskill on various technologies (Snowflake, Databricks, many others).

  

ExxonMobil is a long\-term career orientated company where you will have opportunities to develop your skills, while working across different projects and business functions on a global scale.

**What you will do**
--------------------

  

* Create intuitive and effective visualizations of drilling, completion, and production data from multiple repositories to provide immediate insights.
* Work in teams on data visualization projects using Spotfire /Power BI to solve complex engineering and business problems.
* Develop data models on Wells – drilling, completion and production data.
* Collaborate with cross functional teams to integrate data from various sources (PI, SAP, EC, CORVA etc.)
* Identify and collaborate with various teams to resolve data quality issues.
* Provide engineering recommendations in drilling, completions, and well performance area to ExxonMobil Wells teams based on data modeling and analysis
* Create tutorials, SOP documentation, training material pertaining to data modeling and analysis if required.
* Engage with stakeholders to meet expectations by valuable and actionable insights.
* Develop custom visuals to deliver effective and accurate insights.
* Develop automated reports using Visualization tools.
* Contribute to various stages of analytics, model deployment and model maintenance.
**About You**
-------------

 **Skills and Qualifications**

  

* Bachelor’s or Master’s degree from a recognized university in data engineering, data visualization, petroleum engineer, chemical engineer or computer graphics design with minimum GPA of 7\.5
* Minimum 3 years of work experience in Data analytics and visualization in the upstream oil and gas industry.
* Strong analytical skills to evaluate critical design \& operating parameters through data and trend analysis.
* Experience in creating visualizations on Spotfire/Power BI is preferred.
* Experience in data extractions from different kinds of database like common O\&G database, SQL server, oracle server etc.
* Data Modelling for variety of data including real time data. Knowledge of Databricks and GitHub is preferred.
* Knowledge of SQL and Python (PySpark) programming is preferred.
* Experience preferred in well design, well performance monitoring, troubleshooting, or optimization of well performance and well management preferred
* Experience in data collation preferred
* Experience in programming languages such as Java will be an advantage
**Preferred Qualifications / Experience**
-----------------------------------------

* Strong communication skills
* Ability to cooperate effectively in a team environment
* Flexibility to work in shifts, with opportunities to leverage flexible work hours
* Position is Bangalore\-based with potential for international travel
**Your benefits**
-----------------

  

An ExxonMobil career is one designed to last. Our commitment to you runs deep our employees grow personally and professionally, with benefits built on our core categories of health, security, finance and life. We offer you:

  

* Competitive compensation
* Medical plans, maternity leave and benefits, life, accidental death and dismemberment benefits
* Retirement benefits
* Global networking \& cross\-functional opportunities
* Annual vacations \& holidays
* Day care assistance program
* Training and development program
* Tuition assistance program
* Workplace flexibility policy
* Relocation program
* Transportation facility

  

Please note benefits may change from time to time without notice, subject to applicable laws. The benefits programs are based on the Company’s eligibility guidelines.

**Stay connected with us**
--------------------------

  

* Learn more about ExxonMobil in India, visit **ExxonMobil India** and **Energy Factor India****.**
* Follow us on **LinkedIn** and **ExxonMobil (@exxonmobil) • Instagram photos and videos**
* Like us on **Facebook**
* Subscribe our channel at **YouTube**
**EEO Statement**
-----------------

  

ExxonMobil is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin or disability status.

**Business solicitation and recruiting scams**
----------------------------------------------

  

