in-172d1fec9d26c0fb,indeed,https://in.indeed.com/viewjob?jk=172d1fec9d26c0fb,http://in.indeed.com/job/data-scientist-llm-specialist-172d1fec9d26c0fb,Data Scientist – LLM Specialist,citriot solutions pvt tld,"KA, IN",2025-04-02,fulltime,,,,False,"**Position: Data Scientist – LLM Specialist**

**Location:** Bangalore (On\-Site)  
**Experience Level:** 3\+ years in AI/ML with expertise in Large Language Models (LLMs)  
**Employment Type:** Full\-time

**About Citriot**

Citriot (https://www.citriot.ai/) is at the forefront of AI\-driven solutions, specializing in developing state\-of\-the\-art machine learning and deep learning models to solve real\-world challenges. We are now expanding our expertise into **Large Language Models (LLMs)** to drive AI innovation across industries.

**Key Responsibilities :\-**

**LLM Model Development \& Optimization**

* Design, fine\-tune, and deploy **large\-scale language models** (GPT, LLaMA, Mistral, etc.) for real\-world applications.
* Develop **custom LLM solutions** for NLP tasks such as text generation, summarization, question answering, and conversational AI.
* Implement **prompt engineering** and retrieval\-augmented generation (RAG) techniques to enhance LLM capabilities.
* Optimize model performance with **quantization, pruning, and knowledge distillation** to reduce computational overhead.

**LLM Deployment \& MLOps**

* Deploy LLMs on **cloud (AWS, Azure, GCP)** and **on\-prem infrastructure** with optimized inference pipelines.
* Utilize **vector databases (e.g., FAISS, Pinecone, Chroma DB)** for efficient retrieval\-augmented generation.
* Implement **API\-based LLM services** and integrate them with business applications.
* Monitor model drift and performance, ensuring continuous improvement using **MLOps frameworks (MLflow, Kubeflow, SageMaker).**

**Research \& Experimentation**

* Stay updated with the latest advancements in **open\-source LLMs (Meta AI, OpenAI, Cohere, etc.)**.
* Experiment with **fine\-tuning techniques** such as **LoRA, PEFT (Parameter Efficient Fine\-Tuning),** and **adapter layers.**
* Conduct **benchmarking studies** on different LLM architectures and optimize for specific use cases.

**Performance \& Scaling**

* Implement **distributed training strategies** for large\-scale LLMs on multi\-GPU and TPU clusters.
* Work with **NVIDIA GPUs (A100, H100, Jetson)** and optimize inference using TensorRT, ONNX, and DeepSpeed.
* Ensure **low\-latency model serving** by leveraging **LLM optimization libraries** like vLLM and TGI (Text Generation Inference).

**Qualifications Required:**

* Bachelor’s or Master’s in **Computer Science, Data Science, AI, or related fields.**
* **3\+ years of AI/ML experience**, with at least **2\+ years of hands\-on experience** working with LLMs.
* Proficiency in **Python** and frameworks like **PyTorch, TensorFlow, and Hugging Face Transformers**.
* Experience in **training, fine\-tuning, and deploying LLMs on cloud and on\-prem infrastructure**.
* Strong understanding of **LLM architectures**, transformer models, and generative AI techniques.
* Experience with **vector databases (FAISS, Pinecone),** and retrieval\-augmented generation (RAG).
* Hands\-on experience in **MLOps (MLflow, Kubeflow, SageMaker)** for model lifecycle management.

**Preferred:**

* Experience in **LLM optimization** (DeepSpeed, LoRA, Flash Attention, GPTQ).
* Familiarity with **NVIDIA TensorRT, ONNX, vLLM, or TGI** for optimized inference.
* Knowledge of **distributed computing frameworks** (Ray, Dask) for scaling LLM workloads.
* Prior contributions to **open\-source LLM projects** or research publications in NLP/AI conferences.

**Why Join Us?**

* Work on cutting\-edge **LLM projects** shaping the future of AI.
* Collaborate with a team of **top AI/ML engineers** and researchers.
* Competitive salary, benefits, and opportunities for professional growth.

