in-87c7b9ab3b422adb,indeed,https://in.indeed.com/viewjob?jk=87c7b9ab3b422adb,https://eltropy.bamboohr.com/careers/203?source=indeed&src=indeed&postedDate=2025-04-01,NLU Engineer – Conversational AI & NLP,Eltropy,"KA, IN",2025-04-01,fulltime,,,,True,"**About the Role**



We are seeking an NLU Engineer to design, develop, and optimize conversational AI systems. You will be responsible for intent recognition, entity extraction, and dialogue management to enhance AI\-driven user interactions.  

  

**Responsibilities:**


* Develop and optimize NLU pipelines using frameworks like Rasa, spaCy, or Hugging Face Transformers.
* Implement and fine\-tune text classification, named entity recognition (NER), and semantic parsing models.
* Train and deploy language models (LLMs) tailored for specific domains.
* Enhance multilingual NLU capabilities by integrating diverse language datasets.
* Preprocess and analyze large\-scale textual datasets to improve model accuracy.
* Conduct A/B testing and model evaluation using metrics like F1\-score, accuracy, and perplexity.
* Deploy NLU models into production environments using cloud\-based AI services like AWS, Azure, or Google Cloud.
* Develop and maintain NLU training datasets and oversee continuous model retraining.


 **Requirements:**


* Proficiency in Python and experience with NLP libraries like spaCy, NLTK, Hugging Face, or Rasa.
* Hands\-on experience with deep learning frameworks (TensorFlow, PyTorch) for NLP tasks.
* Has knowledge of LLM frameworks such as langchain, langGraph, OpenAI realtime APIs
* Familiarity with transformer\-based models (BERT, GPT, T5, etc.).
* Understanding of speech\-to\-text (STT) and text\-to\-speech (TTS) technologies.
* Experience with vector databases and retrieval\-augmented generation (RAG).
* Strong problem\-solving skills and ability to optimize NLU models for real\-world applications.


 **Preferred Qualifications:**


* Experience in LLM fine\-tuning and prompt engineering.
* Knowledge of knowledge graphs and ontologies for improved intent handling.
* Familiarity with cloud AI services and deployment best practices.
  


**About Eltropy:**



Eltropy (www.eltropy.com) is on a mission to disrupt the way people access financial services. Eltropy enables financial institutions to digitally engage in a secure and compliant way. Using our world\-class digital communications platform, community financial institutions can improve operations, engagement and productivity. CFIs (Community Banks and Credit Unions) use Eltropy to communicate with consumers via Text, Video, Secure Chat, co\-browsing, screen sharing and chatbot technology — all integrated in a single platform bolstered by AI, skill\-based routing and other contact center capabilities.

 **Eltropy Values:**



 Customers are our North Star



 No Fear. Tell the truth.



 Team of Owners

  


Eltropy is an equal opportunity employer. All applicants will be considered for employment without attention to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, veteran or disability status.",,https://in.indeed.com/cmp/Eltropy,Data Science
in-ad97f1b90a123ffb,indeed,https://in.indeed.com/viewjob?jk=ad97f1b90a123ffb,https://careers.agcocorp.com/job/Pune-Manager%2C-Smart-Pricing-Data%2C-Global-Parts-MH/1257753100/?feedId=28200&utm_source=Indeed&utm_campaign=AGCO_Indeed,"Manager, Smart Pricing Data, Global Parts",AGCO Corporation,"MH, IN",2025-04-01,,,,,False,"Do you want to help solve the world's most pressing challenges? Feeding the world's growing population and slowing climate change are two of the world's greatest challenges. AGCO is a part of the solution! Join us to make your contribution.

  

AGCO is looking to hire candidates for the position of **Manager, Smart Pricing Data, Global Parts**.

  

This role will be responsible for proactively identifying data gaps, analyzing and automating market trends, and supporting price decisions to maximize opportunities.

* AI/ML Learning: leverage new and innovative solutions to automate pricing processes, data validation and price decision optimization.
* Proactively leverage advanced analytical tools to support global pricing initiatives and opportunities bringing skills to provide best in class guidance for achieving strategic growth.
* Competitive intelligence: analyze and disseminate information about industry, competitors and customers. Monitors competition to identify areas for improvement and differentiation. Keep track of industry trends and developments.
* Market intelligence: Analyze and disseminate information about markets across the 4 Regions to identify opportunities.

 **Your Impact**

* Leverage intelligence tools and applications to analyze internal and external data sources and develop learning models providing insights to support key decision making and recommendations.
* Proactively provide coherent recommendations from analytical models while clearly defending and explaining the data to management and other sponsors.
* Proactively build strategies to learn competitor pricing (using as an example web scraping solutions) and distribution partners and customer behavior. Adjust strategies and modeling accordingly in close collaboration with stakeholders.
* Support analysis of financial implications of pricing changes, including impacts on margins, revenues, and market share.
* Proactively develop and enhance pricing analytics tools and applications to support the pricing activities and strategies globally.

 **Your Experience and Qualifications**

* Master's Degree in Data Science or comparable.
* 5\+ years' experience in an advanced data analytics role, preferably in aftersales parts, consulting or pricing context.
* Proven experience developing and defending machine learning models.
