What you do at McKesson matters. We foster a culture where you can grow, make an impact, and are empowered to bring new ideas. Together, we thrive as we shape the future of health for patients, our communities, and our people. If you want to be part of tomorrow’s health today, we want to hear from you.

**Current Need**


We are looking for Sr Director, AI Strategy \& Transformation to lead the AI Big Bets program strategy and delivery, aimed at accelerating modernizing our enterprise operations, primarily focused on supply chain, cash management, pricing, and document/contract digitization and optimization.


This role will drive enterprise\-wide transformation by leveraging AI to enhance operational efficiencies and business value, co\-leading with the AI/ML experimentation leader to identify, validate, and capitalize on strategic opportunities.

**Key Responsibilities:**

**Strategic Leadership \& Transformation**

* Develop and lead the strategic AI experimentation process to identify high\-impact opportunities across the enterprise focused on modernizing our operations
* Collaborate with AI/ML experimentation leader to design and execute experiments that demonstrate incremental business value, guiding prioritization and resource allocation.

**End\-to\-End Value Realization**

* Ensure seamless integration of AI solutions across business units by partnering with advanced analytics, data science, and operational teams.
* Oversee the full lifecycle of AI initiatives from ideation through to implementation and value capture, ensuring alignment with business unit and enterprise objectives.

**Establish High\-Performance Delivery Structure**

* Lead enterprise level program with a team of AI experts and data scientists, promoting a culture that embraces agility, innovation, and strategic risk\-taking to stay ahead in AI advancements
* Establish an environment that balances speed with thoroughness, encouraging calculated risk\-taking and viewing failures as learning opportunities
* Help design flexible team frameworks that enable rapid adaptation to diverse business challenges, ensuring the team can pivot efficiently across domains.
* Navigate and lead within a matrix organization by fostering collaboration and alignment with cross\-functional stakeholders, driving AI initiatives that align with strategic business goals.

**Change Management \& Communication**

* Develop and execute change management strategies to facilitate the adoption of AI technologies across the enterprise, engaging senior executives directly
* Drive shared accountability between technology and business teams, engaging directly with senior technology leaders as well as BU function heads
* Foster a culture of innovation and continuous improvement across the organization.

**Facilitate Knowledge Transfer \& Scaling**

* Develop processes to transition successful experiments to production implementation teams
* Create knowledge repositories and documentation standards to capture learnings from all experiments
* Establish communities of practice to share techniques and insights across the organization

**Measure \& Communicate Impact**

* Implement metrics to track experimental throughput, success rates, and business impact
* Leverage compelling narratives and visualizations to communicate complex findings to executives
* Create transparent reporting on the experimentation pipeline and portfolio performance

**Minimum Requirements**


Typically requires 13\+ years of professional experience and 6\+ years of diversified leadership, planning, communication, organization, and people motivation skills (or equivalent experience).

**Critical skills**

* 13\+ years in leading strategy and delivery of data science and advanced analytics initiatives, with extensive experience in digital transformation initiatives.
* Proven expertise in building and leading high\-performance teams, fostering a culture of agility and innovation. Ability to ensure team alignment and delivery on strategic AI initiatives across diverse business challenges.
* Demonstrated ability to engage and influence cross\-functional stakeholders, ensuring strategic alignment of AI initiatives with enterprise goals. Proficient in translating complex technical concepts into actionable insights for business leaders.
* Extensive experience driving enterprise\-wide transformation through AI, with a focus on modernizing operations and enhancing operational efficiencies.
* Strong technical foundation in AI/ML with the ability to evaluate feasibility and impact of AI solutions. Experience in designing experimentation frameworks that balance speed, quality, and compliance.
* Skilled at identifying high\-value AI/ML opportunities and translating them into measurable business outcomes. Experience in end\-to\-end management of AI initiatives from ideation to implementation and value realization.
* Excellent communication skills to articulate complex findings and foster buy\-in from executives. Ability to create compelling narratives and visualizations to communicate AI impacts.
* Proven track record of transitioning successful AI experiments into production, establishing knowledge repositories, and fostering communities of practice to drive continuous learning.

**Working Conditions:**


Environment (Office, warehouse, etc.) –

* Traditional office environment.
* Large percent of time performing computer based work is required

**Education**

Bachelor’s degree required in a quantitative field such as Statistics, Computer Science, Economics, Operations Research, Engineering, Applied Mathematics or related field. MBA or Master’s degree in a quantitative field preferred OR equivalent experience.


