**About the Role:**

Are you passionate about building AI\-driven solutions? We are looking for an experienced Senior Data Scientist / AI Engineer to join our team and play a key role in developing an AI\-enabled ERP solution. You will work on designing scalable AI models, implementing ML pipelines, and exploring cutting\-edge AI technologies to drive innovation. Additionally, this role will include managing and mentoring a team of data scientists and AI engineers, providing leadership and guidance to foster a collaborative and efficient work environment.

**Key Responsibilities:**

* AI \& ML Development: Design and build AI models from scratch, optimize machine learning algorithms, and integrate them into our ERP solution.
* AI Pipeline \& Infrastructure: Develop and maintain an AI development and deployment pipeline using cloud and containerized solutions.
* Research \& Innovation: Conduct R\&D activities to identify opportunities for AI\-driven automation and efficiency.
* NLP \& Computer Vision: Work on sentiment analysis, NLP, and computer vision tasks to enhance product capabilities.
* Model Deployment \& APIs: Deploy ML models, create APIs, and ensure seamless integration into production systems.
* Collaboration \& Strategy: Work closely with product teams to explore AI’s impact and align AI strategies with business objectives.
* Team Management: Lead and mentor a team of data scientists and AI engineers. Provide guidance, training, and career development support to junior team members.
* Leadership: Foster a collaborative team culture, ensure timely delivery of projects, and contribute to the overall technical growth of the team.

**Required Skills \& Experience:**

* 8\-10 years of experience in AI, Machine Learning, or Data Science roles.
* Expert\-level proficiency in Python and ML frameworks (scikit\-learn, TensorFlow, Keras, PyTorch).
* Strong understanding of ML algorithms (classification, regression, clustering, optimization).
* Experience with deep learning architectures (ANN, CNN, RNN, LSTM).
* Hands\-on experience with NLP (NLTK, spaCy) and computer vision (OpenCV, PIL).
* Experience deploying AI models using Flask APIs, Docker, Kubernetes.
* Strong problem\-solving skills and ability to articulate AI concepts effectively.
* Leadership and team management experience, with the ability to guide and develop junior members.

**Preferred/Optional Skills:**

* Knowledge of Java and experience with software development best practices.
* Understanding of SDLC, version control (Git), and CI/CD pipelines.
* Experience with Big Data technologies (Spark, Hadoop, Data Engineering concepts).
* Ability to interact with clients and communicate AI\-driven solutions effectively.

If you are excited about working with AI\-driven products and solving real\-world challenges, we would love to hear from you!

Job Type: Full\-time

Pay: Up to ₹1,200,000\.00 per year

Application Question(s):

* Have you worked on AI model deployment or building AI Pipelines?
* Do you have experience managing or leading AI/ML teams?

Experience:

* AI/ ML: 8 years (Required)

Work Location: In person",,https://in.indeed.com/cmp/Pinnacle-Software-and-Services-Pvt-Ltd,Data Science
